ineteenth century?", "answer": "Oxford Movement", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American author lends his name to a subgenre of horror fiction exemplified by the 1927 short story \"The Colour Out of Space\"?", "answer": "H. P. Lovecraft", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who wrote a novel named after the most famous peak in the Great Balsam Mountains?", "answer": "Charles Frazier", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which public university located on 355\u00bd acres (1.4 km\u00b2) in unincorporated Prince George's County did  Maryland Route 197 provided access to ", "answer": "Bowie State University", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who distributed the 2013 superhero film in which Ken Yamamura plays the young Ichir\u014d Yashida?", "answer": "20th Century Fox", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A famous sexual harassment class-action lawsuit of the 1980s occurred in what ore mining district in 1866?", "answer": "Mesabi Range", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Rigid frame airships were used by Germany to fly bombing raid over Great Britian in what war?", "answer": "World War I", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were Clarence G. Badger and A. Edward Sutherland both film directors?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What country of origin does The Hard Goodbye and Sin City have in common?", "answer": "American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Out of all of the cities that The Shoshone between, which one of these cities was the largest city in the state of Montana?", "answer": "Billings, Montana", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was the Olympics held where Hans Rinn won his first gold medal?", "answer": "Innsbruck, Austria", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What state in East Asia is the city Taitung located?", "answer": "Taiwan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "While the Newcastle 500 is a motor racing event for Supercars, the Supercars Championship is what?", "answer": "touring car racing category based in Australia", "type": "bri