s, or other special needs", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Harrelson Boulevard runs near the second-largest mall in what state?", "answer": "South Carolina", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In between Twenty One Pilots and Man or Astro-man?, which one was formed in Auburn, Alabama, in the early 1990s?", "answer": "Man or Astro-man?", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What UMTS-based mobile phone networks and Broadband internet Providers does Vidiator produce?", "answer": "the Hutchison 3", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Agona Nkwanta is the capital of Ahanata west district in what region?", "answer": "Ghana", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American film director, producer, screenwriter co-founded Troma Entertainment film studio, Lloyd Kaufman or Joseph Ruben?", "answer": "Joseph Porter Ruben", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the name of the three act opera that had a role created by William McAlpine ?", "answer": "Gloriana", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Cain-Sloan Co. was a department store that could be found in what Goodlettsville, Tennessee mall?", "answer": "Rivergate Mall", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The content of the Mishnat ha-Middot resembles the work of this 1st Century AD Egyptian mathematician.", "answer": "Hero of Alexandria", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which star of The Family Tree is known for his roles in the films \"Young Guns\", \"Samantha\", \"Where the Day Takes You\", \"My Best Friend's Wedding\", \"The Last Outlaw\", \"About Schmidt\" ?", "answer": "Dermot Mulroney", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Edit referenced the Paul and Linda McCartney hit that came from which album?", "answer": "Ram", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When is the American football quarterback who is a notable players for the USC Trojans in 2002 born", "answer": "May 17, 1982", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the loose sequel that came years after Return to Castle Wolfenstein was released?", "answer": "Wolfenstein", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Andrzej Seku\u0142a shot the first two feature films by which acclaimed cult director?", "answer": "Quentin Tarantino", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Striding Lion, a wall relief made from polychrome glazed, fired bricks, is one of the most iconic objects on display at the Royal Ontario Museum, Toronto, it is one of many such reliefs that decorated the walls of the palace's ceremonial hall and very similar to the lions that line the processional way from the Ishtar Gate to which temple? ", "answer": "Marduk", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Biloxi Bay Bridge is over a city in Jackson County which has a population of how many in 2000?", "answer": "17,225", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What ethnic group does the incumbent who was challenged by R.J. Harris in the 2010 for the  Republican Party nomination  in the primary election for Oklahoma's 4th congressional district?", "answer": "Native Americans", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which band debuted first, Fake Problems or L'Arc-en-Ciel?", "answer": "L'Arc-en-Ciel", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Can\u2019t is Not an Option is an autobiography by a politician that served as governor of South Carolina between which years ?", "answer": "January 2011 to January 2017", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Los-Angeles-based rock band did session work with Ian Fraser Kilmister?", "answer": "Mother Superior", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " \"A Subtlety\" is a piece of installation art by an artist currently serving a five-year term as Tepper Chair at what university?", "answer": "Rutgers University", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the right wing of the West Coast Express born?", "answer": "1975", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The man whose email's were hacked in the Pizzagate scandal was born on what day?", "answer": "January 8, 1949", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which artist recorded the track \"Let Me KNow (I have a Right)\" and \"I am What I am\"?", "answer": "Gloria Gaynor", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the singer who collaborated with Aesop Rock on \"Hokey Fright\" born?", "answer": "1972", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Alfred Hitchcock film Under Capricorn, which was preceeded by Rope, was adapted to the screen by which person?", "answer": "Hume Cronyn", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the lead singer of the band Roger O'Donnell has performed with that was founded in London in February 1977?", "answer": "Richard Butler", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Norwegian heiress, is the daughter of the owner of Norwegian holding company Ferd?", "answer": "Alexandra Gamlemshaug Andresen", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Aviron Pictures was directed by Luis Prieto?", "answer": "Kidnap", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Danish actress played Nicole 'Pumpkin' Truchaut in a film adapted from the novel \"The Death of Napoleon\"?", "answer": "Iben Hjejle", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which song, named the number 1 song of the decade of 2000's on the Adult Pop Charts by \"Billboard\" magazine, was on The Calling's debut album, Camino Palmero?", "answer": "Wherever You Will Go", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is The Royal Governor and American-born attorney in the 1700s?", "answer": "William Franklin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Do You Believe Me Now is the second studio album of American country music singer Jimmy Wayne, the album is also Wayne's first album in five years and his debut for Valory Music Group, a subsidiary of which independent American record label specializing in country and pop artists, and  based on Music Row in Nashville, Tennessee, and is distributed by Universal Music Group (UMG)?", "answer": "Big Machine Records, LLC", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Da'Vine Joy Randolph was in \"Ghost the Musical,\" a book and lyrics written by whom?", "answer": "Bruce Joel Rubin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Tam\u00e1s L\u00e1szl\u00f3