arison"}, {"question": "Kumail Nanjiani starred on the comedy that was a spin off of what other Adult Swim series?", "answer": "Childrens Hospital", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Georges Ladoux was famous for recruiting which exotic dancer as a French spy?", "answer": "Mata Hari", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which film featured footage of interviews and a punk band, Night Mail or There Is No Authority But Yourself", "answer": "There is No Authority But Yourself", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Scott Harris worked with which EDM-pop duo and reached #1 on the US Mainstream Top 40 chart in 2016?", "answer": "The Chainsmokers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When did the author of Bell Atlantic Corp. v. Twombly start serving on the Supreme Court?", "answer": "October 1990", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What hip-hop music group was one of several notable groups from the Danish modern pop and rock scene?", "answer": "Outlandish", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Hiroshi Inagaki and Salma Hayek are both known for being involved in what industry?", "answer": "film", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Om Prakasj Sharma received the National Award for Painting by what commander-in-chief of the Indian Armed Forces?", "answer": "President of India", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which band has had more members, Ubiquitous Synergy Seeker or Super Furry Animals?", "answer": "Super Furry Animals", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What leaves are often referred to as cilantro in North America, Centranthus or Coriandrum ?", "answer": "Coriandrum", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which 2006 documentary film tells the stories of three Jehovah's witnesses who, amongst other Witness teachings, claim the right to refuse to perform military service on the grounds of freedom of religion?", "answer": "Knocking", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " How far is the major building in the parish Hoghton, located to the east of the village of Hoghton, Lancashire, England?", "answer": "0.7 mi", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the film that premiered at The Bagdad Theatre in 1975?", "answer": "Milo\u0161 Forman", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jason Mulgrew was named one of the  50 Hottest Bachelors of 2005 in what magazine that  has the largest audience of any American magazine", "answer": "People", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which country contains both the Maiden's Tower and the Te\u015fvikiye Mosque?", "answer": "Turkey", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Sherri Lou Ellis was portrayed by Cher in the 1983 film \"Silkwood.\" Which actress portrayed her roommate?", "answer": "Meryl Streep", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "This lady was wife to Ralph the Timid and Queen Consort of which three Countries?", "answer": "England, Denmark, and Norway", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How Wonderful You Are is a 2001 song by Gordon Haskell, it was the Christmas number-two in 2001, behind Robbie Williams and Nicole Kidman's, that is which song written by C. Carson Parks", "answer": "Somethin' Stupid", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Disney film came first Amy or The Big Green?", "answer": "Amy", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Kyle Chandler had a starring role in the 2012 drama film directed by whom?", "answer": "Ben Affleck", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The DePaul Blue Demons are a member of a collegiate athletic conference that competes in NCAA Division I in all sports except what?", "answer": "football", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which was made first,  Prince Among Slaves or The Seafarers?", "answer": "The Seafarers", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which magazine, Me Naiset or Peg's Paper still publishes magazines today?", "answer": "Me Naiset", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What Wes Anderson film is about a fox who steals food from wealthy farmers?", "answer": "Fantastic Mr. Fox", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who represents the group sometimes considered Albanized Romani in the Assembly of Kosovo?", "answer": "Veton Berisha", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Aside from the series that ranges from atomic numbers 89 to 103, what series is an exception to the rule that the number of valence electrons ranges from 0-8 electrons?", "answer": "Lanthanide", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How far south-west of Inverness is the castle of which Robert Lauder of Quarrelwood was Captain located?", "answer": "21 km", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year was \"The Christmas Truce\" during the World War I?", "answer": "1914", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who won the Kool Championship in the 1997 race utilizing Toyota's in-house engines?", "answer": "Alex Barron", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Dennis Nicolaas Maria Bergkamp was described as a \"dream for a striker\" by a French professional footballer who spent eight years at a club where he is their all-time record what?", "answer": "goalscorer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What are Palio and Seal Island?", "answer": "documentary film", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": " Eurardy Reserve is located 530 km north of a city that had how many inhabitants as of 2017 ?", "answer": "1.94 million", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which National Basketball Association team does this American business entrepreneur, to whom Richard Carr sold his shares of Arsenal in 2008, own?", "answer": "Denver Nuggets", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which film director was born first, John English or Jason Reitman?", "answer": "John Wilkinson English", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Josh Howard is a columnist for a magazine about what type of publication?", "answer": "comic books", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Near which village, civil parish and post town in North Lincolnshire, England is Thornton Abbey located?", "answer": "Ulceby", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who worked more behind the camera, Nora Ephron or Nadine Labaki?", "answer": "Nora Ephron", "type": "comparison"}, {