er": "Marlon Brando Jr.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which tennis player won more Olympic gold medals, Tony Roche or Marc Rosset?", "answer": "Marc Rosset", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which film came first Earth or Babes in Toyland?", "answer": "Babes in Toyland", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Frederick E. Turneaure became an instructor at the university founded in what year and named after the first President?", "answer": "1853", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the singer who released \"Partytime!\" born?", "answer": "1957", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "While some traditions have wide-ranging campus support, others are officially discouraged by the administration, many traditions are paralleled at peer schools, such as which collegiate athletic conference comprising sports teams from eleven schools, which are ten small liberal arts colleges and one medium-sized research university?", "answer": "New England Small College Athletic Conference (NESCAC)", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Beno\u00eet Ferreux is best known internationally for his role in a film directed by who?", "answer": "Louis Malle", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which country music duo was founded in 1990?", "answer": "Brooks & Dunn", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which movie showcasing the voice of  Ben Wishaw was awarded the Empire Award for Best Comedy?", "answer": "Paddington", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which band is based closer to Australia, Flight of the Conchords or Fake Problems ?", "answer": "Flight of the Conchords", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The 1999 Munster Senior Hurling Championship Final was a hurling match, played on Sunday 4 July 2000 at Semple Stadium, Thurles, County Tipperary, sponsored by Guinness ( ) is an Irish dry stout that originated in the brewery of Arthur Guinness (1725\u20131803) at St. James's Gate brewery in which capital city of Ireland?", "answer": "Dublin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Die Mutter is an East German film adopted from a play by a poet who was married to which actress ?", "answer": "Helene Weigel", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What county of Scotland is the Scottish Police College based in?", "answer": "Fife", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the opera scheduled to premier in 2018 written by Rufus Wainwright, the composer of Prima Donna?", "answer": "Hadrian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What country where Dysoxylum gotadhora is native to is officially a Kingdom?", "answer": "Bhutan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many Primetime Emmy Awards did Susan Silverman's sister win?", "answer": "two", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Major League Baseball (MLB) team has the home stadium where \"Under Armour All-America Game\" takes place annually?", "answer": "Tampa Bay Rays", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The documentary \"Freedom Downtime\" focuses on a computer hacker arrested in what year?", "answer": "1995", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What navigable canal crosses the border between England and Wales and contains the Trevor basin?", "answer": "The Llangollen Canal", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was the person who hosted the 2004 Teen Choice Awards with Nicole Richie born ?", "answer": "New York City", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Simon Henwood is best known for directing a Kanye West song released on which day ?", "answer": "September 18, 2008", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both Lambert Hillyer and Charles Shyer American film directors?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The 1975 NHL Amateur Draft had a number-one selection made by the team in what Division of the Eastern Conference?", "answer": "Metropolitan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who did the singer of That's My Pa play in High Noon?", "answer": "Ben Miller", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Austrian colonization of Nicobar Islands was a short-lived and unsuccessful attempt of Habsburg Monarchy to make a colony of Nicobar Islands, this had previously been a Danish colony and Austria established it with the mistaken assumption that Denmark had abandoned its claims to the islands, which term denotes the colonies that Denmark-Norway possessed from 1536 until 1953, and,Denmark alone after 1814?", "answer": "Danish colonial empire", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Early Slavs lived during which time of widespread movements of mainly Germanic peoples?", "answer": "Migration Period", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In the siege of Mons, the forces of the Grand Alliance were under the command of a king known in Northern Ireland and Scotland as King what ?", "answer": "King Billy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the population in 2010 of the county in which the city of Greenwood is located ?", "answer": "1,152,425", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Floating Power was a technology developed by an automobile firm headquartered in what MIchigan city?", "answer": "Auburn Hills", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What  prominent Indian dance choreographer in Hindi cinema provided assistance for the 1963 Indian social film directed by Nitin Bose?", "answer": "Saroj Khan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Lorraine Campaign and Operation Undertone both occurred during which war?", "answer": "World War II", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Many Heisman winners were unsuccessful at the professional level, including, among others, Jason White, an American former college football quarterback who played for what university?", "answer": "the University of Oklahoma", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Kyle MacLachlan's role as Dale Cooper was featured on what network in 2017? ", "answer": "Showtime", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ignoreland is the eighth track from what R.E.M. album that was released on October 5, 1992?", "answer": "Automatic for the People", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What second most populous city in the United States is chstistian musician Bob Ayala from?", "answer": "Los Angeles", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the middle name of the man who coached the 2014 Washington State Cougars?", "answer": "Charles", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "what year did the winner of the 1992 South African Grand Prix with the CART Indy Car World Series?", "answer": "1993", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Betty Jane Willis designed what Las Vegas landmark funded in May 1959 and erected soon after by Western Neon?", "answer": "Welcome to Fabulous Las Vegas sign", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the first naval recipient of the Medal of Honor in World War II shot down?", "answer": "27 November 1943", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the nationality of the MVP of The 2003 FIBA Under-19 World Championship ?", "answer": "Australian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which county is the John Sprunt Hill House located?", "answer": "Durham County", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What sport did both  Mary Carillo and T\u00edmea Babos play?", "answer": "tennis player", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Rosario Castellanos and Maurice Blanchot, have which similar occupation?", "answer": "writer", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What place is a town in Hancock County, Maine, United States with a summerhouse designed by the partnership of Fred L. Savage and Milton W. Stratton, located at ?", "answer": "Mount Desert Island", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which district did James Comer represent before becoming the Agriculture Commissioner of Kentucky in 2012?", "answer": "53", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "On 1 July 1943 the 3rd Government of Ireland was officially appointed and the new Fianna F\u00e1il government was led by a prominent politician and statesman whose politica career spanned over half a what?", "answer": "century", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The duo of music directors Manoj Saran and Gyan Varma composed musical score for which 1987 film produced by A. S. I