ison established in 1851 in Coburg, Victoria?", "answer": "Gregory David Roberts", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In the 2003-04 season, Toronto Raptors drafted a future All-Star forward born in which year ?", "answer": "1984", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "So Fly was a song co-produced by the rapper who began her career with what R&B group?", "answer": "Sista", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What nationality was the female composer who came before Shirley Anne Walker?", "answer": "Italian American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Lindsay Frimodt is an American model whos advertisements include an American sportswear fashion designer who was the first women\u2019s ready-to-wear designer for who?", "answer": "the French house Celine", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the full name of the street in New York where Richard Serra lives?", "answer": "Triangle Below Canal Street", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which European tale or movie had frequent  plot of a cat that talks and wears magical boots?", "answer": "\"Puss in Boots\" about a cat who talks and walks on his hind legs while wearing magical boots.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the nickname for the player who won the 2008 World Matchplay?", "answer": "The Power", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was Francisco Rodr\u00edguez Araya's Swiss international older brother born?", "answer": "1992", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Dorton, Kentucky is located along a US highway that runs between Jacksonville, Florida and what Michigan city?", "answer": "Mackinaw City", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "West Meets East, Volume 2 starred Ravi Shankar, a Bengali Indian musician, was a virtuoso of which instrument?", "answer": "sitar", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The film Cold Mountain stars what actress who was born in 1984?", "answer": "Jena Malone", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which poet's work has Lori Saint-Martin translated into French and has published seven autobiographies?", "answer": "Maya Angelou", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "For which university is the coach of the 2004 Arizona Wildcats football team currently defensive coordinator?", "answer": "University of Oklahoma", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Shin Hye-sung and Trent Reznor, have which mutual occupations?", "answer": "singer, songwriter", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In what genre of film are both Meet the Patels and Tintin and I?", "answer": "documentary", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What does the structure whose operation was engaged by Great Wheel Corporation consist of? ", "answer": "rotating upright wheel", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born first, James Agee or Robert Pinsky?", "answer": "James Rufus Agee", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "when was the  American football coach who led  2015 East Carolina Pirates football team born ", "answer": "October 8, 1958", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the director of the 1991 film Naked Lunch born?", "answer": "March 15, 1943", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What genre is the movie High Fidelity directed by Stephen Frears?", "answer": "American romantic comedy-drama film", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what film did British comedian Eddie Izzard have a starring role?", "answer": "The Riches", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Eastern District of Taipei, refers to the newly developed area in eastern Taipei, Taipei City Hall, Taipei City Council and Taipei 101 are all located in this district, TAIPEI 101 , formerly known as the Taipei World Financial Center \u2013 is a landmark supertall skyscraper in Xinyi District, Taipei, in which country?", "answer": "Taiwan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the population of the borough Burnley High School is in?", "answer": "87,500", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was college at which Thomas Balaton was educated after Eton founded ?", "answer": "1379", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Boxer Sam Rukundo was born in a city that is divided into how many boroughs?", "answer": "five", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "La Casa Pacifica was a mansion that was used by the President who was a Senator from what state?", "answer": "California", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the name of the man who Carol Kane played the wife of who was a lovable-but-goofy mechanic in a television series?", "answer": "Latka Gravas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Between Les Claypool and Dennis Locorriere, who had more diverse job experiences?", "answer": "Leslie Edward \"Les\" Claypool", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which band was formed in Edinburgh and had the genre influenced by the music of Appalachia?", "answer": "Swamptrash", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The grandfather of  Duke Peter Alexandrovich was the Duke of what European dynasty of North German Origin", "answer": "House of Oldenburg", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which player from \"Fergie's Fledglings\" was co-owner of Salford City?", "answer": "Gary Neville", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Salutation was a modern dance solo choreographed by Martha Graham whose style, known as what, reshaped American dance and is still taught worldwide?", "answer": "the Graham technique", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The play Peter and Alice features a meeting between Alice Liddell and Peter Llewelyn Davies, best known as the source of the name for the title character in what play?", "answer": "Peter Pan, or The Boy Who Wouldn't Grow Up", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What does the Multnomah tribe call this region, which is near the northern range of this plant Lilium washingtonianum?", "answer": "Wy'east", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What do Alan Crosland and Leopold Wharton have in common?", "answer": "film director", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which Australian network featured a miniseries on the motor racing driver known as \"The King of the Mountain\"?", "answer": "Network Ten", "type": "b