r 1,000,000", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What type of brand are Schweppes and Frescolita?", "answer": "beverage", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which Civil Rights Movement leader, who was born in 1908, did Samuel Bowers murder?", "answer": "Vernon Dahmer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Hail Mary\" is a single by American rapper Tupac Shakur, who died on September 13, of which year?", "answer": "1996", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which film was released first, Old Yeller or Flight of the Navigator?", "answer": "Old Yeller", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "On what date did Farshid Karimi's younger brother play his last game of football?", "answer": "11 April 2014", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What prize in Physics has the inventor of the heterotransistor, who is the head of the St Petersburg Academic University won?", "answer": "Nobel Prize in Physics", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many model generations did the car Bill Elliott won the 1985 Daytona 500 in have?", "answer": "eleven", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which First World War survivor was commemorated in a speech given by the 46th vice president in 2005?", "answer": "Howard Verne Ramsey", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Desert Sands was a film that starred the stage and television actor who first rose to fame for his role in what late 1940s Broadway production?", "answer": "Mister Roberts", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which compact luxury crossover SUV is the new BMW X2 modeled after?", "answer": "BMW X1", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Embassy of Colombia in Vienna is located near the city hall that was constructed from what year?", "answer": "1872 to 1883", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the population at the 2010 census of the village where the 2014 Cheez-It 355 at The Glen was held?", "answer": "1,859", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which little bearded man in Irish folklore is most akin to the Dutch Kabouter?", "answer": "Leprechaun", 