d primarily to a younger audience, 2600: The Hacker Quarterly or Tiger Beat?", "answer": "Tiger Beat", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What Roller coaster appeared in an American disaster-suspense film starring George Segal?", "answer": "The Rocket", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Andi Kravljaca and Rob Zombie, are Swedish?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What band has released more albums, Bodyjar or The Stranglers?", "answer": "The Stranglers", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Works by what man, who was part of the duo Simon & Garfunkel, were included in the 1967 Joan Baez album, Joan?", "answer": "Paul Frederic Simon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What drummer, whose career spans more than 30 years, played with the British Rock Symphony, The Who, and Oasis?", "answer": "Zak Starkey", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who won at Wimbledon first Jean-Julien Rojer or Leo\u0161 Friedl?", "answer": "Leo\u0161 Friedl", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which DJ best known for his role in the 1970s Disco music scene held residence at the club Studio 54 which is currently a Broadway theatre?", "answer": "Tom Savarese", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Adam Adamowicz is known for his work at a game developer which is lead by who?", "answer": "Todd Howard", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the nickname of the railroad executive that stayed at the Travelers Hotel?", "answer": "The Empire Builder", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Lynda Bird Johnson Robb is the oldest living child of a U.S. President following the death of a United States Army officer who served as the United States Ambassador to where?", "answer": "Belgium", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the romantic comedy film that stars an actor that played Peter Waters and was born September 8, 1975?", "answer": "Matty Rich", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "T. K. Kurien was the Executive Vice Chairman of a corporation headquartered in what city?", "answer