ital of the island on which Wickham Heights are located ?", "answer": "Stanley", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Angelo Henna masterminded the murder of an American mobster born in what year?", "answer": "1892", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Book of Artifacts (abbreviated as BoA) is a supplemental sourcebook to the core rules of the second edition of the \"Advanced Dungeons & Dragons\" fantasy role-playing game, the book had some additional design by Wolfgang Baur, an American game designer, best known for his work with \"Dragon\" magazine, born in which year?", "answer": "1968", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which documentary was released first, Takin' Place or Lake of Fire?", "answer": "Lake of Fire", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "A. J. Iversen collaborated with architects and designers to create a style of furniture development in what nation?", "answer": "Denmark", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Shot in the Dark\" is a single from an album released by which record label ?", "answer": "Roadrunner Records", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the home stdium of Scott Crichton's college football team?", "answer": "Reser Stadium", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Madhusudhan Rao appeared in which Tamil-language fantasy comedy film of 2016?", "answer": "Kaashmora", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "30 Hudson Yards and Bank of America Tower are both located in which city?", "answer": "Manhattan", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "When was the award created that was won five times by Adri\u00e1n Beltr\u00e9?", "answer": "1957", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jackson is what south of a small town in Beaverhead County, Montana, United States?", "answer": "unincorporated community", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who appeared in 1965 \"The Hill\" and born on December 18th?", "answer": "Ossie Davis", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the 1980 American teen musical drama film directed by Alan Gore, which was remade in 2009