as the assignment of Kevin and Pat Tillman?", "answer": "The 75th Ranger Regiment", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What novel spawned a film and a film based on the search for the right actress for the film?", "answer": "\"Gone with the Wind\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How far from the White House is the hotel where the Peace Conference of 1861 occurred?", "answer": "two blocks", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "what year did the shopping mall adjacent to Albert Campbell Square open?", "answer": "1973", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 2010 Washington Redskins began by having the selection of which offensive tackle who played at Oklahoma?", "answer": "Trent Williams", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Richard S. Westfall  is best known for his biography of a mathematician who was a key figure in what?", "answer": "the scientific revolution", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Road to Freedom was a monthly anarchist political journal published by Hippolyte Havel, the journal is known as the successor to Mother Earth\" by which anarchist political activist and writer?", "answer": "Emma Goldman", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Between E. Howard Hunt and Karen Joy Fowler, who had a more diverse career?", "answer": "E. Howard Hunt", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which American writer lived longer, pediatrician Benjamin Spock or Alex Haley?", "answer": "Benjamin McLane Spock", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What actress and singer appeared in a musical with music by Alan Menken, lyrics by Howard Ashman and Tim Rice, and book by Linda Woolverton?", "answer": "Brooke Elliott", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Gackt and Phil Mogg from the same country?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What country does Bugzy Malone and Grime have in common?", "answer": "UK", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The host of the 1988 Soul Train Music Awards became an United Nations Global Ambassador for what organization?", "answer": "Food and A