n Take It!", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The english singer, dancer, and model, who has worked with n American electronic dance music duo consisting of uncle and nephew Redfoo and SkyBlu, is best known as a member of what?", "answer": "G.R.L.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The actor that played the title role in the series \"Merlin\" also appeared in a 2014 2014 British film based on the First World War memoir by what author?", "answer": "Vera Brittain", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "James Martin Pacelli McGuinness, was an Irish republican and Sinn F\u00e9in politician who from May 2007 to January 2017, who had a titled partial position, are the joint heads of the Northern Ireland Executive and have overall responsibility for the running of the Executive Office?", "answer": "First Minister and deputy First Minister", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which is an alternative rock band, Galaxie 500 or Juliette and the Licks?", "answer": "Galaxie 500", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which band lasted the longest, New Model Army or The Von Bondies?", "answer": "New Model Army", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In which American state in the New Engand region does Quebec Route 243 become Vermont Route 243?", "answer": "Vermont", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Thorvald Eiriksson was the brother of an explorer who is believed to be the first known European to discover what continent?", "answer": "North America", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which theatre that had a catastrophic fire on December 5, 1876 was formerly known as the Park theatre?", "answer": "Brooklyn Theatre", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What investment company owns the North American vacuum company Hoover?", "answer": "Techtronic Industries", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Gift of Screws was the fifth solo album released by Lindsey Buckongham who released how many solo albums?", "answer": "six", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Of the two plants, Dictyosperma and Lepidozamia, which has been farmed to extinction in its native climates", "answer": "Dictyosperma", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Orson Welles's production of \"Julius Ceasar\" was a success at what theatre that reopened in 1937 after the depression?", "answer": "Mercury Theatre", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Saumarez Homestead maintained by the National Trust of Australia is located in which city approximately halfway between Sydney and Brisbane?", "answer": "Armidale", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many episodes were in the seaon of \"South Park\" which had the episode \"Big Gay Al's Big Gay Boat Ride\"?", "answer": "13", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Worker: Which opera original produces in 1831 by Vincenzo Bellini?", "answer": "Norma", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In 1994, Tinny starting performing at an amusement park in what city?", "answer": "Nashua, New Hampshire", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Innocent Age is the seventh album by American singer-songwriter Dan Fogelberg, released in which year, the album also includes his song \"Times Like These\" from the 1980 \"Urban Cowboy\" soundtrack?", "answer": "1981", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "WHo is the person who wrote many novels about Reginald Ashley Caton's child?", "answer": "Martin Amis", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Lance Armstrong consistently denied allegations of doping until a partial confession during a broadcast interview with a talk show host born in which year ?", "answer": "1954", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Warsaw was the planned debut album by which English post-punk band, formed in 1976 in Salford, Greater Manchester?", "answer": "Joy Division", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American actor, director, and comedian played the character Niles Crane on Frasier?", "answer": "David Hyde Pierce", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What elevation does Malangutti Sar and Dhaulagiri have in common?", "answer": "mountain", "type": "comparison"}, {"question"