.6 billion bridge and tunnel project?", "answer": "southern end of the Wanshan Archipelago", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When did Sobrante Park, Oakland, California witness a large migration of white residents? ", "answer": "mid to late 50's", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which singer who sang a version of \"Thakita Thadimi\" has the title of \"Bhava Gayakan\"?", "answer": "P. Jayachandran", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Meet Corliss Archer is an American television sitcom that aired on CBS, and later in syndication via which company, that produced syndicated radio and television programs in the United States?", "answer": "Frederic W. Ziv Company", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the American Theater Hall of Fame founded?", "answer": "The American Theater Hall of Fame in New York City was founded in 1972.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what Olympics did the greatest Great British yachtsman since Sir Aineslie, CBE, win silver?", "answer": "1976 Montreal Olympics", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which is a public research facility, University of Texas System or University of California, Los Angeles ?", "answer": "University of California, Los Angeles", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "James Dodds McClelland was born in what city in Westchester County, New York, that is immediately to the north of what borough?", "answer": "the Bronx", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"With a Flair\" is a song written for which 1971 Walt Disney musical film based upon the books \"The Magic Bedknob; or, How to Become a Witch in Ten Easy Lessons\" and \"Bonfires and Broomsticks\"?", "answer": "Bedknobs and Broomsticks", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which game has been nominated for a prize at Cannes, Concept or Roulette? ", "answer": "Concept", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Neil Hudson won what premier motocross championship in 1981?", "answer": "Motocross World Championship", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 2011 Euroleague Final Four games were held in an arena designed by whom?", "answer": "Arata Isozaki", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Rakesh Kr Yadav specializes in what throing event in regular track and field competition that consists of a metal ball attached by a steel wire to a grip?", "answer": "hammer throw", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Thomas Merton and Jane Urquhart, are in the writing industry?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which media and animation company do \"Cars\" and \"The Little Mermaid\" have in common?", "answer": "Disney", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What type of media does When the Levees Broke and Mala Mala have in common?", "answer": "film", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which film director was also a cinematographer, Edwin Greenwood or Nicolas Roeg?", "answer": "Nicolas Jack Roeg", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "who sang the song produced by the songwriter who developed the wall of sound?", "answer": "Curtis Lee", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Halma and Nine Men's Morris both strategy board games?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Tim Robbins play \"Embedded\" pokes fun of which former Deputy Chief of Staff during the George W. Bush administration?", "answer": "Karl Rove", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The author of Girl Guides, and the first Chief Scout of the Boy Scouts Association, was also the man who signed the charter to allow international scouts in which year? ", "answer": "1925", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What seaside resort area is the Mechanics' Institute located in?", "answer": "Sorrento, Victoria", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Happy Feet Two includes new characters that are voiced in part by an American actor who is known for voicing Moe Szyslak in what television sitcom?", "answer": "The Simpsons", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Did Tom Nijssen and Robert Seguso play the same sport professionally?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The