rn?", "answer": "1 January 1933", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which team has as its home stadium the venue for the 2019 UEFA Champions League Final  ?", "answer": "Atl\u00e9tico Madrid", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Matthew Ryan has been descrbed as part Westerberg and part an American singer-songwriter who is nicknamed \"The Boss\" and is known for his work with what band?", "answer": "E Street Band", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Lazard and RHB Bank, are both in which type of industry?", "answer": "financial", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which of the following, Tom Robinson or Kevin Woo, is a British singer-songwriter, bassist, radio presenter and long-time LGBT rights activist?", "answer": "Thomas Giles \"Tom\" Robinson", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Imagine was filmed at which Grade II listed house?", "answer": "Tittenhurst Park", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the  English poet who created Johannes Agricola in Meditation born?", "answer": "7 May 1812", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Jamican National Premier League soccer team shares the same name as a Jamaican beer brewed by Desnoes & Geddes?", "answer": "Red Stripe", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Alexander Ivanovich Mikhailov and Nikolay Mitrofanovich Krylov both Russian?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who is the award-winning English soap opera actress noted for her on-screen relationship with Joe Dutine?", "answer": "Sally Dynevor", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what neighborhood was the 1962 Pro Bowl played?", "answer": "Exposition Park", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American reality competition television series  was Davenport  best known as a contestant on the second season", "answer": "RuPaul's Drag Race", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was the founder of the organization originally known as Center for Reproductive Law and Policy born?", "answer": "Detroit Lakes, Minnesota", "type": "bridge"}, {"questi