ined a decisive victory against the Austrian army and where Louis Jean Nicolas Abbe, a French general led a brigade?", "answer": "Napoleonic Wars", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Following the 1970 NFL season, Billy Truax was traded by the Rams to the Cowboys for a wide receiver that played football at what college? ", "answer": "University of Oklahoma", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Counterpoints was an album that was without which English drummer?", "answer": "Robert John \"Bob\" Henrit", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Inger! was released by a company which was founded and named for an American who was born and raised where?", "answer": "Greenup County, Kentucky", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When did the first captain of the Karachi Kings in 2016 announce his retirement from Test cricket?", "answer": "On 3 November 2015", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the host of A-List Listings who is known for dating and later marrying Neil Patrick Harris?", "answer": "David Burtka", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What county in Kansas was Helen T. Parsons born in?", "answer": "Cowley County", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Greg McDermott (born November 25, 1964) has served as the head coach of the Creighton University Bluejays men's basketball team since April 26, 2010, he's the father of Douglas Richard McDermott, is an American professional basketball player for the New York Knicks, of which organization?", "answer": "National Basketball Association (NBA)", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "James Howard Mitcham was known for specializing in what potato-based cuisine?", "answer": "cook best known for his books on Louisiana's Creole and Cajun cuisines and that of New England, with an emphasis on seafood.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Hilo International Airport and Columbia Metropolitan Airport in the same state?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the \"Say Good NIght To Illiteracy\" book series publisher's original 