n that was born in what year?", "answer": "1946", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was this NHL goaltender who had a species of wasp named after him born?", "answer": "10 March 1987", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Bipasha Basu earned her first Filmfare Award nomination for Best Actress in film by what director?", "answer": "Vikram Bhatt", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Brenno Ambrosini has lauded the work of which former Soviet composer and pianist?", "answer": "Boris Ivanovich Tishchenko", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the second profession of the Mexican ballerina best known for the Tchaikovsky ballet that initially failed?", "answer": "Architect", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Brigitte and Essence both magazine publications?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What kind of group does Maid of Orleans and Mull of Kintyre have in common?", "answer": "band", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "essie is an American 1984 ABC television police drama series starring Lindsay Jean Wagner, is an American film and television actress, model, author, singer, acting coach, and adjunct professor, born on which date?", "answer": "June 22, 1949", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "James Poe worked on the 1956 movie that starred which actors?", "answer": "Cantinflas and David Niven", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Marc Pedraza Sarto plays professional football for a team founded in what year?", "answer": "1916", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 2006 Boise State Broncos football team represented Boise State University in the 2006 NCAA Division I FBS football season, became only the second team from outside the Bowl Championship Series (BCS) to play in a BCS bowl game when they faced Oklahoma in which college football bowl game played as part of the 2006\u20132007 Bowl Championship Series (BCS) of the 2006 NCAA Division I FBS football season?", "answer": "2007 Tostitos Fiesta Bowl", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the 2009 po