e off against a Dutch martial artist at?", "answer": "Invicta Fighting Championships", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which sound editor was nominated for an academy award at the ceremony hosted by Jimmy Kimmel?", "answer": "Mildred Iatrou Morgan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which gas-operated (short-stroke gas piston) self-loading rifle with a rotating bolt is developed by the Tangodown company?", "answer": "FN SCAR", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the featured singer in Katy Perry's song \"E.T.\"?", "answer": "Kanye West", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the train who's line goes through the small village of Miralago?", "answer": "Bernina Express", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were J. P. Donleavy and Imre Kert\u00e9sz both authors?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In what month was the woman who published Comedy 23/6 born?", "answer": "July", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jyoti Hegde is an artist who performs on the instrument typical of what genre?", "answer": "Hindustani classical music", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which tennis player won numerous doubles titles, Rika Hiraki or Franti\u0161ek \u010cerm\u00e1k?", "answer": "Franti\u0161ek \u010cerm\u00e1k", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which 2008 Swedish Romantic horror film featured a Swedish actress best known for her work in children's television shows?", "answer": "Let the Right One In", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the award for scientific acomplishments won by Soviet scientist Mikhail Borisovich Golant and named after an infamous Soviet ruler created?", "answer": "June 23, 1925", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The football tournament that was won by Australia was held in what country?", "answer": "Russia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What does William John Howey and Bok Tower Gardens have in common?", "answer": "Florida", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who did Any Holligan challenge for light welterweight title under one of the four major boxing organizations?", "answer": "Julio C\u00e9sar Ch\u00e1vez", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Chungking Mansions is a building located at 36\u201344 Nathan Road in Tsim Sha Tsui, Kowloon, Hong Kong, the unusual atmosphere of the building is sometimes compared to that of the former Kowloon Walled City, Kowloon Walled City was a largely-ungoverned densely-populated settlement in Kowloon City in which region?", "answer": "Hong Kong", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are the genuses Michelia and Stenomesson in the same family?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who was the \"The X Factor\" runner up to the winner whose single, \"Impossible\", has gone on to sell over 1.4 million copies in the UK?", "answer": "Jahm\u00e9ne Aaron Douglas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which two-generation compact automobile was the foundation for the race-class Fitch Sprint?", "answer": "Chevrolet Corvair", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Did Hayley Mills star in Tonka and Summer Magic?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Missionary is a 1982 British comedy film starring an English actress born in what year?", "answer": "1934", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What person does Airstream and Spirit of St. Louis have in common?", "answer": "Charles Lindbergh", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Mark Rylance won a BAFTA for his portrayal of which Soviet intelligence officer in the 2015 movie \"Bridge of Spies\"?", "answer": "Rudolf Ivanovich Abel", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the writer of such songs as \"New Orleans\" and \"Georgia on my Mind\"?", "answer": "Hoagy Carmichael", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The song \"What the Water Gave Me\" was written by a singer born in what year?", "answer": "1986", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which band is English, The Stranglers or Iamamiwhoami?", "answer": "The Stranglers", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which of these is based off of an MTV series: Jackass Number Two or Great West End Theatres?", "answer": "Jackass Number Two", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What was the nationality of the winner of the 2007 Masters of Formula 3?", "answer": "German", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Which tennis player was born first, Pavel Slo\u017eil or Svetlana Kuznetsova?", "answer": "Pavel Slo\u017eil", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who appeared in a 2012 epic musical drama film directed by Tom Hooper?", "answer": "Caroline Sheen", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Th\u00e9ophile Bader, was a French businessman, he was the co-founder of which upmarket French department store chain?", "answer": "Galeries Lafayette", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the person, who was executed a day after William Joyce was hanged for treason in 1946, born? ", "answer": "5 May 1918", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Karen Harris Wheaton Towe is an American Pentecostal preacher, Gospel music singer and recording artist based in Hamilton, Alabama, she has toured throughout the U.S. performing at events that also featured preachers and Christian artists such as Toufik Benedictus \"Benny\" Hinn, an Israeli televangelist, best known for his regular \"Miracle Crusades\"\u2014revival meeting or faith healing summits that are usually held in stadiums in major cities, which are later broadcast worldwide on which television program?", "answer": "This Is Your Day", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which newspaper is owned by Sheldon Adelson and distributed with the \"Las Vegas Sun\"?", "answer": "Las Vegas Review-Journal", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Tom Walls and The Wachowskis, share which occupations?", "answer": "producer and director", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "When was the label for brooks & Dunn formed?", "answer": "1989", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the remixed version of the song released which is by Taylor Swift featuring Kendrick Lamar from her fifth studio album \"1989\" ?", "answer": "May 17, 2015", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "De Beneficiis and the series regarding \"the happy life\" translate to what Greek concept?", "answer": "eudaimonia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What title does this American white supremacist who promoted the term \"Alt-right\" in 2010 prefer to go by?", "answer": "identitarian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Medici and Senet both board games?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Eugeniusz Bodo and Chris Buck both shared what occupation?", "answer": "film director", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Of the two Disney films, Perri or Beauty and the Beast, which is True-Life Fantasy?", "answer": "Perri", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are Delmer Daves and Patrick Bokanowski both nationals of the same country ?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Danziger Echo was a newspaper that was published in the city state that existed between which years?", "answer": "1920 and 1939", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American operatic baritone and actor sung in Porgy and Bess album ", "answer": "Robert Merrill", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What roller coaster located in North Rhine-Westphalia, Germany is designed in a western style?", "answer": "Colorado Adventure", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which film released on 11 May 2007 was Harold Perrineau an actor?", "answer": "28 Weeks Later", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which country\u2018s show is the series ITV show that Nadia Forde participated present ", "answer": "UK", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Giant was created by which director and screenwriter?", "answer": "David Keith Lynch", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When did the railway line servicing Exeter and a suburb 14 km north-west of Adelaide close?", "answer": "1978", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What band wrote the album The Stage and the song The Stage?", "answer": "Avenged Sevenfold", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which film maker is more awarded Su Friedrich or Rob Nilsson?", "answer": "Rob Nilsson", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What sportcaster born in 1962 and currently employed by ESPN also served on the sports staff of WAER (88.3 FM)?", "answer": "Sean McDonough", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the era of the castle located in the vicinity of Coalford, Scotland?", "answer": "16th-century", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the 2006 Spanish-Mexican dark fantasy film that won an award for Makeup done by David Marti?", "answer": "Pan's Labyrinth", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "This Is Serious is the second solo studio album by a singer best known for what 1985 duet?", "answer": "Separate Lives", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Northern States Power Company is now a subsidiary of what utility holding company based in Minneapolis, Minnesota?", "answer": "Xcel Energy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the film that \"Homesick\" lost out to be Norway's submission for the Academy Award for Best Foreign Language Film at the 88th Academy Awards?", "answer": "Roar Uthaug", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the United Football League team for which former NFL player Edgerton Hartwell payed?", "answer": "Las Vegas Locomotives", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the Irish name for the mountain range which contains Slieve Meelmore?", "answer": "na Beanna Boirche", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What album took over two years to create and contained a song written with the help of Julia Michaels?", "answer": "Purpose", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was the co-writer of In My Blood born and raised?", "answer": "Albany Creek, Queensland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The WEMF AG f\u00fcr Werbemedienforschung collects figures on what in Switzerland?", "answer": "media usage", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What championship did the North Carolina Tar Heels football team win in 2015 under the guidance of former University of South Mississippi coach Larry Fedora?", "answer": "ACC Coastal Division Championship", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the movie that Joseph E. Levine was involved and starred Brigitte Bardot released? ", "answer": "1963", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The town of Essam and Bia District are both in which African country?", "answer": "Ghana", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the event held that \"Sieranevada\" was selected to compete for the Palme d'Or at?", "answer": "from 11 to 22 May 2016", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What song, co-produced by a man who currently resides in New York City, released on September 10 and in the song Rihanna demands physical attention from her lover?", "answer": "Only Girl", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What state in Somalia does Taleh belong?", "answer": "Somaliland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What river is the namesake of the city that sports club Boca R\u00edo Gallegos is located in?", "answer": "Gallegos River", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What company marketed and sold the Lincoln Continental Mark V?", "answer": "Lincoln Motor Company", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What famous Indian film actor stars in En Kelvikku Enna Bathil?", "answer": "Rajinikanth", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Moon Hee-joon and Jesse Michaels, share which occupations?", "answer": "singer-songwriter", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "When Vladimir Kashpur portrayed Baba Yaga she was one of how many sisters?", "answer": "trio of sisters", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Which board game, Java or Twin Tin Bots, was designed by Philippe Keyaerts and published by Flatlined Games?", "answer": "Twin Tin Bots", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "When did the Liberal member for the House of Representatives start serving as the Minister of Defense Industry?", "answer": "19 July 2016", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the agreement used in the Universal Metric to Flow operation and is a commitment between service provider and customer?", "answer": "service-level agreement", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What area managed by the Bureau of Land Management is easily seen from a strip south of the Las Vegas city limits? ", "answer": "Red Rock Canyon National Conservation Area", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Little Western Wall, also known as HaKotel HaKatan (or just Kotel Katan) and the Small Kotel, is a Jewish religious site located in the Muslim Quarter of the Old City of Jerusalem, it is the continuation of the larger part of the Western Wall and almost exactly faces the Holy of Holies, a term in the Hebrew Bible which refers to the inner sanctuary of the Tabernacle, where who dwelt?", "answer": "God", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What other name did the missle, which was mounted to a small, lightweight, four wheel drive vehicle that served the Swedish and Swiss armies, go by?", "answer": "Robot 53", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which was based on a Disney theme park attraction, The Country Bears or Jungle Cruise?", "answer": "The Country Bears", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Where was the starting city of the concert tour for Taylor Swift's studio album that followed her album \"Speak Now\"?", "answer": "Omaha, Nebraska", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was in the copyright with David McKenzie for the game system which is the base of Living Steel?", "answer": "Barry Nakazono", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The first medal ever won in the winter Olympics for Ukraine was won by an athlete born in which year ?", "answer": "1977", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Eoghan Casey has an M.A. in Educational Communication and Technology from a university founded in which year ?", "answer": "1831", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which actress composed two Vaishnava devotional albums namely \"\"Azhagu\"\" and \"\"Thirupathi Thirukudai Thiruvizha and acted in (Tamil: \u0b9a\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb0\u0bc8 \u0ba4\u0bc7\u0bb5\u