 the Disney Channel comedy series \"Lizzie McGuire\"?", "answer": "September 9, 2008", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Valery Lagunov is the teacher of the dancer in what famous ballet troupe?", "answer": "Bolshoi Ballet", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was one producer for Teen Angel, ALF and The Tonight Shoe Starring Johnny Carson from?", "answer": "Detroit, Michigan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What country of origin does Operation Spark and Henning von Tresckow have in common?", "answer": "German", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which two cities does the motorway, which intersects Sheffield Parkway at junction 33, connect?", "answer": "London to Leeds", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 1986-87 FC Bayern Munich season was the last under a manager of what nationality?", "answer": "German", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What news company does the opponent of Chris Koster in 2012 work as contributor for?", "answer": "CNN", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which former shopping center is now partly occupied by a store that is headquartered in Chesapeake, Virginia?", "answer": "The Shoppes at Trexler", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who wrote the screenplay for the film which inspired the film  De Dhakka ?", "answer": "Michael Arndt.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What song did Collect-12\" Mixes Plus remix?", "answer": "compilation album", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Erling Christian Foss was a Danish civil engineer, famous for his contributions to the underground insurgency to resist which nation's occupation of Denmark?", "answer": "German", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which plant species, Emmenopterys or Olea, is considered an Evergreen?", "answer": "Olea", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What career did the older brother of Ailes Gilmour have?", "answer": "artist and landscape architect", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which university is longer established: Duke University in North Carolina, or Lehigh University in 