ilms such as which 2003 drama film directed by Robert Altman and starring Neve Campbell, who co-wrote and co-produced the film?", "answer": "The Company", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which country did the subject of Mao II govern? ", "answer": "People's Republic of China", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The movie Into Thin Air: Death on Everest was based on what book by Jon Krakauer?", "answer": "\"Into Thin Air\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many students does Delphi Community High School serve in Indiana?", "answer": "500", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the third race after European and African that describes this multi-racial people for whom Vardy Community School provided education to in the  late-19th and early-20th centuries?", "answer": "Native American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Wilmington Trust was founded by an American engineer and politician who serves as a United States Senator from what state?", "answer": "Delaware", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The phenomenon known as Beatlemania originated in the United Kingdom, birthplace of the Beatles, when the band first realised enormous popularity there in 1963, the Beatles achieved a commercial breakthrough with their second UK single release, \"Please Please Me\", a song and the second single released by English rock group the Beatles in the United Kingdom, and the first to be issued, in which country?", "answer": "United States", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The War of the Roses is partly adapted from a Shakespeare play that culminates in which opening battle of the war?", "answer": "First Battle of St Albans", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Alexander Campbell, was a tavern owner, who, with three other convicted, was hanged for the murders of two mine operatives, which  Irish 19th-century secret society active in Ireland, Liverpool and parts of the eastern United States, best known for their activism among Irish-American and Irish immigrant coal miners in Pennsylvania?", "answer": "Molly Maguires", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Mikky Ekko featured song is used on the third-season finale of the TV Show Younger?", "answer": "Stay", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was an expatriate, Paul Bowles or Lawrence Durrell?", "answer": "Paul Frederic Bowles", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are both Henry Grantland Rice and David Guterson American writers?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Nathan Drake,  the protagonist of the \"Uncharted\" video game series, who was the voice and motion capture artist, that played him? ", "answer": "Nolan Ramsey North", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the operational conversion unit of the aerial warfare branch of the Australian Defence Force formed?", "answer": "December 1941", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which did Michael Rosen finish last, Forever More or Children's Laureate?", "answer": "Children's Laureate", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Among two literary figures, Robert Stone and Paul Heyse, who was born earlier?", "answer": "Paul Johann Ludwig von Heyse", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Where did the prince whose name means \"fortunate\" sailed to in 1170?", "answer": "America", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Everything Is Racist is the sixth album by a comedy artist born in what year?", "answer": "1987", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Cassius M. \"Cash\" Hollister (December 7, 1845 \u2013 October 18, 1884) was a 19th-century American law enforcement officer and deputy U.S. marshal who served as mayor and sheriff of which city in Kansas, during his career, he worked with several well-known lawmen including Henry Newton Brown (1857 \u2013 April 30, 1884) was an American Old West gunman who played the roles of both lawman and outlaw during his life?", "answer": "Caldwell", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What song did John Lennon write in his house at Menlove Avenue that lead The Beatles to a commercial breakthrough prior to th