": "William A. Fowler", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Erik Andreas Colban worked with the Secretary-General of the United Nations who earned a reputation as what?", "answer": "a pragmatic, determined politician", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which restaurant is themed and was first opened in the Mall of America?", "answer": "Rainforest Cafe", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which United States Navy ship was named for a man who was both Secretary of the Navy and a New Hampshire senator?", "answer": "USS \"Chandler\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which member of the LIGO Scientific Collaboration is an expert on gravitational waves?", "answer": "Barry Barish", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the middle name of the author of the novella Riding the Bullet ?", "answer": "Edwin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which moutain is higher, Gasherbrum I or Broad Peak?", "answer": "Gasherbrum I", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Scott Dean Boras, is an American sports agent, specializing in baseball, Boras has brokered many record-setting contracts since 1982, and many of his clients, including Jacoby McCabe Ellsbury, an American professional baseball center fielder for the New York Yankees, of which organization?", "answer": "Major League Baseball (MLB)", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the eastern terminus of the historical railroad that ran 98.77 miles through towns including a Middlesex County town with a 2010 census population of 17659?", "answer": "North Cambridge Junction", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which classification level is both Butea and Cynoglossum?", "answer": "genus", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Hannah Norsa achieved fame appearing in an opera that was written in what year?", "answer": "1728", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What airline operates United Club as well as a regional airline?", "answer": "United Airlines", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the brewpub run by the brewing company