ard on the rock album Moonlight Shadows?", "answer": "pop, rock, surf rock and ballads with a jazz influence", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which landlocked country in South Asia and one of the region's least populous nations has only four airports?", "answer": "Bhutan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year was the brewery founded that sponsored the 1994\u201395 English Premiership ?", "answer": "1787", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "An American actor who starred in the 1981 American drama film starring Harry Hamlin also starred with which famous actor in \"Rebel Without a Cause\"?", "answer": "James Dean", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which contributor to Padr\u00f3n Real was the first to demonstrate that Columbus' conjecture about Asia's eastern outskirts was wrong?", "answer": "Amerigo Vespucci", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Melbourne, Australia street gang founded by members of Victoria's South Sudanese community fought a rival gang made up of youths from a South Pacific background in March 2016 after the Moomba parade.   ", "answer": "Apex", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What position does the footballer who scored the only goal in the 2017 FIFA U-20 World Cup Final play?", "answer": "forward", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the national movement of the Jewish people did Samuel Gruber \"aka\" Mieczyslaw Gruber belong to?", "answer": "Zionism", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What network did Katherine Cassidy star as Ruby on?", "answer": "The WB", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Vice Versa and Mothering were both what?", "answer": "Magazine", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which fell in the English Lake District is home to Honister Hause?", "answer": "Green Gable", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was St. Augustine's nickname for a 2nd Century AD story whose characters appeared in Greek art in the 4th century BC?", "answer": "The Golden Ass", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the group that 