ian?", "answer": "Jerry Clower", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What mid-level retailer that can be found at Square One Shopping Centre was founded in 1977?", "answer": "American Eagle Outfitters", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many career goals did Arthur Hudgell, the English former football player, have against Blackburn Rovers Football Club that competes in League One, the third tier of the English football league?", "answer": "no goals", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both Candy Flip and Loop names of bands?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In the \"Lost\" episode \"The Variable\" Dr. Burke is being chased by whom?", "answer": "the Dharma Initiative", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "RatPac-Dune Entertainment was co-founded by the billionaire of what nationality?", "answer": "Australian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which school has a longer name under which it was founded, Brown University or Columbia University?", "answer": "Brown University", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which writer is English, Anthony Burgess or Conrad Aiken?", "answer": "Anthony Burgess", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which director was also a musician, Emir Kusturica or Elia Kazan?", "answer": "Emir Kusturica", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who founded Green Ronan Publishing in 2000, known for it\u2019s role playing games such as A Song Of Fire And Ice?", "answer": "Chris Pramas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Fabulous Faker Boy\" is the 20th episode of the 24th season of \"The Simpsons\", it originally aired on the Fox network in the United States, on which date?", "answer": "May 12, 2013", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "John Bassett (born 1934) is the person credited with putting together the talent for the Edinburgh International Festival revue, \"Beyond the Fringe\", a British comedy stage revue written and performed by Peter Cook, Dudley Moore, Alan Bennett, and Jonathan Miller, first started in which year?", "an