idge"}, {"question": "What is the birthdate of this soprano singer in opera and musical theater, who sang her first solo guided by this Dutch violinist and conductor best known for creating the waltz-playing Johann Strauss Orchestra?", "answer": "1 March 1978", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Unique archaea bacteria were found by Brett Baker's lab at the University of California Berkely at a mine which has been geologically classified as what?", "answer": "\"massive sulfide ore deposit\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Once a Day\" is a song written by Bill Anderson and recorded as the debut single by American country artist Connie Smith, it was the first debut single by a female country artist to reach number one, and held the record for the most weeks spent at number one by a female country artist until it was surpassed by which song recorded by American singer-songwriter Taylor Swift for her fourth studio album, \"Red\" (2012)?", "answer": "We Are Never Ever Getting Back Together", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which soap opera, did the singer whose 1990 album was, Rhythm of Love, star ?", "answer": "Neighbours", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the name of the city founded by the man who conquered the Incan Empire?", "answer": "Jauja", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are MedStar Georgetown University Hospital and MedStar Washington Hospital Center both located in Washington DC?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Herbert Parker was born in which English town that is commonly abbreviated by locals to \"Accy\"?", "answer": "Accrington", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Allan Smart played as what position for Burscough Football Club?", "answer": "Striker", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The ;largest mall in Windsor, Ontario is served by what bike trail?", "answer": "Devonwood Bike Trail", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Northern Cheyenne warrior Wooden Leg fought at the Battle of the Little Big Horn against a Union g