ndence structure, which is just behind the Parliament House of Ghana, was commissioned by Dr. Kwame Nkrumah, the first President of Ghana, in what year, and serves as the official seat of the Speaker of Parliament of the country?", "answer": "1965", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were both Bryan Singer and Stuart Paton actors and directors?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Bytham River was one of the great Pleistocene rivers of central and eastern England until it was destroyed by the extreme Anglian Glaciation around 450,000 years ago, it is named after which village and civil parish of around 300 houses in South Kesteven, Lincolnshire, England?", "answer": "Castle Bytham", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "On what date was Rihanna's album containing the song \"Half of Me\" released?", "answer": "November 19, 2012", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which conference does the team, for which Willie Warren played college basketball, play?", "answer": "Big 12 Conference", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " The husband of Susan Lynch beat what incumbent for governor in 2004?", "answer": "Craig Benson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which author won more awards for their writing, Nevil Shute or Melissa Bank? ", "answer": "Melissa Bank", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In 2014, the registrar DNV GL acquired which marine control company, founded by Thor Inge Fossen?", "answer": "Marine Cybernetics", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were Jerry Belson and Larry Clark both film directors?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which magazine was founded first, Better Homes and Gardens or Human Rights Quarterly?", "answer": "Better Homes and Gardens", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which magazine, Wired or Reason, have had more international spinoffs?", "answer": "Several spin-offs have been launched", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "John Benedict Hillerman, is an American actor, known for his starring role as t