t?", "answer": "Mong Kok", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What plant genus, Kigelia or Rumohra, occurs throughout tropical Africa?", "answer": "Kigelia", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Diane Keaton made her name acting in several Woody Allen films. In which one did she perform the song \"You'd Be So Nice to Come Home To\"?", "answer": "Radio Days", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What city is the company Allan Lester Schuman was formerly a CEO at headquartered in?", "answer": "St. Paul, Minnesota", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed a 2015 American comedy film an actor who played Kim Hyde in Home and Away starred in?", "answer": "Jonathan Goldstein", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "New Hampshire's 2nd congressional district covers the western and northern parts of New Hampshire, it is currently represented in the United States House of Representatives by which Democrat, an American politician and author who has been the U.S. Representative for New Hampshire 's 2 congressional district since 2013?", "answer": "Ann McLane Kuster", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the full name of the man that inspired the Stand by me", "answer": "Samuel Dale \"Sam\" Cook", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is another name for the mountain that The Peak Galleria is near the summit of?", "answer": "Mount Austin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Babas\u00f3nicos is a band that is mostly native to what language?", "answer": "Spanish", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What do The Joy Formidable and Morning Parade have in common?", "answer": "rock band", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "how is Laiwu and Ningbo connected?", "answer": "China", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which airport is located in the largest estuary in North America?", "answer": "Tangier Island Airport", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Bengali political film was censored by one of the most powerful film censor boards in the world?", "answer": "Kangal Malsat", "type": "bri