e Buckeyes lost to during the 2007 BCS National Championship Game?", "answer": "Ben Hill Griffin Stadium", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which star of the movie \"Yogi Bear\" was born on November 29, 1976?", "answer": "Anna Faris", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Purple Rain-Union\" is the sixth episode of the fourth season of the animated comedy series \"Bob's Burgers\" and the overall 51st episode, the title of the episode is a reference to the song, film, and which sixth studio album by American recording artist Prince, the first to feature his band The Revolution, and is the soundtrack to the 1984 film of the same name?", "answer": "Purple Rain", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which company published a book by an author who writes about political conservatism?", "answer": "Regnery Publishing", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Nerine and Aichryson names of plant genera?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "A Myocardial infarction is also known as what?", "answer": "heart attack", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which waterfall in Africa is known as \"The Smoke that Thunders\" and is located within the Kavango-Zambezi Transfrontier Conservation Area (KAZA)", "answer": "Victoria Falls", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are the Nepenthes and Carpobrotus both carnivorous plants?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who is the former cricket player on the cast of the show Cannonball?", "answer": "Andrew \"Freddie\" Flintoff", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Dyro has remixed the track that was released by Rihanna on what 2012 album?", "answer": "Unapologetic", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Benahavis is a Spanish mountain village between Estepona, Ronda, and a city that is head of the judicial district that bears its name, and is the headquarters of what?", "answer": "Association of Municipalities of the region", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which documentary was released first, The Cats of Mirikitani or The Climb?", "answer": "The Cats of Mirikitani", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Pepsi Orange Streak roller coaster is located in what Minnesota city?", "answer": "Bloomington", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What air raid shelter was the venue for Hitler's wedding?", "answer": "F\u00fchrerbunker", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Pakistan Idol included a singer and philanthropist who has performed at what British landmark?", "answer": "Royal Albert Hall", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Tina Turner and Lukas Rossi, were raised in the Southeastern United States?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the capital of the district that is north of Ketu South Municipal District?", "answer": "Dzodze", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Both Blue Lacy and Seskar Seal Dog are examples of breeds of what animal?", "answer": "dog", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What was the population in 2014 of the city that Jean-Michel Severino was born in?", "answer": "4.7 million", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American politician and attorney from the state of Missouri did General Chris Koster won re-election for a second full term against", "answer": "Edward Robert Martin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "HCF CATCH is an industry led, not-for-profit, training facility located in a village and civil parish that is where?", "answer": "North East Lincolnshire, England", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What kind of show is widely heralded as both a parody and a pastiche of heavy metal culture, and  was developed by Titmouse ,Inc?", "answer": "American adult animated television series", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "From what town is the actor from who played Denham in the 1967 film directed by James Clavell?", "answer": "Southmoor, Berkshire, England", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When did the series premier in which Blake Lee plays Josh Novak?", "answer": "October 1, 2017", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which famous London landmark served as the opening logo for London Films Productions movies?", "answer": "Big Ben", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the film Karidja Tour\u00e9 is best known for starring in?", "answer": "C\u00e9line Sciamma", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When did Margaret Georgiana Spencer's husband die?", "answer": "31 October 1783", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the autobiography written about a Queen that governed as regent from 1406 until 1418 during the minority of her son?", "answer": "Memorias", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Synod of Chester led to a battle with a victory for who?", "answer": "Anglo Saxons", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Is Willsboro Congregational Church on a highway that runs east-west, or north-south?", "answer": "north\u2013south", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Rags to Riches\" is a 1953 popular song by Richard Adler and Jerry Ross, the best-known version of the song, recorded by Tony Bennett with which Canadian bandleader, orchestrator, composer and conductor, known for his lush arrangements of pop and Christmas standards?", "answer": "Percy Faith", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Docteur Jekyll et les femmes stars a Northern Irish actor known for creating what role in \"Marat/Sade\"?", "answer": "Marquis de Sade", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What role do Paul McCartney and Tanya Donelly share in common in terms of their artistic profession?", "answer": "singer-songwriter", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What city did the book for which the Democratic candidate in  the 1934 California gubernatorial election was known took place?", "answer": "Chicago", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Between The Del Fuegos and Spoon, which band releases more diverse style music?", "answer": "Spoon", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Lauren Lapkus has made appearances on the sitcom about a middle-class family in what state?", "answer": "Indiana", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Turkish city between t