in or Vladimir Levenshtein?", "answer": "Lev Semyonovich Pontryagin", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are both American Hairless Terrier and Northern Inuit Dog native to the same country?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is a movie that Rita Wilson played in, besides Now and Then?", "answer": "\"Sleepless in Seattle\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the host of Dirty Dancing born?", "answer": "1969", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was Animal Rights released internationally?", "answer": "6 December 2010", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Friars Club of Beverly Hills had a member named Billy Crystal who played Jodie Dallas on which ABC sitcom?", "answer": "Soap", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Do Macropidia and Crescentia only produce flowers?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What city in the Lerma Valley in the northwest part of Argentina was home to Miguel \u00c1ngel Biazzi for twenty years?", "answer": "Salta", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of this public copyright license that may be used by tabletop role-playing game developers, in which Dawning Star is published under it?", "answer": "Open Game License", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Mad girl's love song is a poem by Sylvia Plath who also wrote?", "answer": "The Bell Jar", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Say Goodbye is featured in what 2006 American romantic dance film that was directed by Anne Fletcher?", "answer": "Step Up", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the court painter of the Queen that was also the Grand Duchess of Lithuania from 1575-1586?", "answer": "Martin Kober", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the largest island south of the most northerly of the abstract five major circles of latitude shown on maps of the Earth?", "answer": "Hitra", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What band formed earlier, Middle Class Rut or Superchunk?", "answer": "Superchunk", "type": "comparison"}, 