ompany?", "answer": "Vall\u00e9e de Joux", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both Parsley and Stangeria considered species in the classification system?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Where did the man who rushed 16 times for 129 yards in the 2008 Pro Bowl play college football?", "answer": "Oklahoma", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Nkroful is a village in a district that was inaugurated on what date?", "answer": "29 February 2008", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Guinea is home to 1 million people and which species of dragonfly in the Libellulidae family?", "answer": "Malgassophlebia bispina", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who created the political drama in which Jorja Fox played recurring character Secret Service Agent Gina Toscano?", "answer": "Aaron Sorkin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who became Englands's poet laureate in 1692 and created an adaptation of one of Shakespeare's works, debuting in 1681?", "answer": "Nahum Tate", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Gary Cornish and Anthony Joshua engage in what combat sport? ", "answer": "professional boxer.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Was The Devil and Max Devlin or Do Dooni Chaar released first?", "answer": "The Devil and Max Devlin", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which cousin of Joan of Lancaster's father was deposed with her father's help?", "answer": "King Edward II", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A Song of Ass and Fire is the 245th episode of South Park, it is the second part of a three-episode story arc. What is the name of the first part?", "answer": "Black Friday", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Sempringham is near the civil parish in which district of Lincolnshire?", "answer": "South Kesteven", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Max Abramson is a former Libertarian member of the New Hampshire House of Representatives, representing Rockingham District number what, for Seabrook, in Hampton Falls, a New England town in Rockingham County, New Hampshire, Un