at year?", "answer": "2006", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What band was the author of Out of Sync known for being a part of?", "answer": "NSYNC", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Circa Waves and The Gandharvas, have what in common?", "answer": "rock band", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which debut novel by Native American novelist James Welch was produced by another Native American author Sherman Alexie?", "answer": "Winter in the Blood", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Mike York played two seasons of Major League Baseball for the Cleveland Indians, and a team that is often referred to as the Bucs or what?", "answer": "Buccos", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Obafemi Martins scored one goal in in Birmingham City F.C.'s 2011 final win against Arsenal, what is the nationality of the other goal-scorer?", "answer": "Serbian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is the headquarters of a company that produced a documentary on Amanullah Nezami?", "answer": "Lucknow, India", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What awards show held on Friday, March 17, 1989 did Raquel Welch, an American actress and singer appear as a guest?", "answer": "31st Annual TV Week Logie Awards", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which company has pizza restaurants in more states, Pacpizza or Fox's Pizza Den?", "answer": "Fox's Pizza Den", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Wild Horse, Nevada is a community in the county whose population is what?", "answer": "48,818", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Elizabeth Claire Kemper plays the role of Kimmy Schmidt on what network", "answer": "Netflix", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the precious owner of \"Middlewick House\" born? ", "answer": "27 December 1939)", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Dolores Cross became the first female president of Chicago State University and a college affiliated with what church?", "answer": "African Methodist Episcopal Church", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which film was released earlier, Little