sed on which day ?", "answer": "21 August 1997", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Kevin \u00c1lvarez represented Honduras in an olympic competition held in this country?", "answer": "Brazil", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In 1979 AC/DC paired with producer Lange and recorded their international breakthrough that would be the last album featuring which lead singer?", "answer": "Bon Scott", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What major city was Eastern Condors, an action film co-starring the winner of Miss Hong Kong 1984, filmed in?", "answer": "Hong Kong", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which city is this German video game and software developer founded in another city in 1999 based, which absorbed workers from the disbanding of Carbonated Games?", "answer": "Frankfurt, Germany", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Eva Anna Paula Hitler, was the longtime companion of Adolf Hitler and, for fewer than 40 hours, his wife, she was a key figure within Hitler's inner social circle, mid-1944, when her sister Gretl married which high-ranking commander in the Waffen-SS of Nazi Germany?", "answer": "Hermann Fegelein", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the composer of the music for \"The Great Maratha\" better known as?", "answer": "Khayyam", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year was the actress who stared in \"Surviving Evil\" and \"Hotel Babylon\" born in?", "answer": "1978", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The namesake of Robbinsdale Armstrong High School served in what war?", "answer": "the Korean War", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which musical genre do the bands Eleventh Dream Day and Verona both play?", "answer": "rock", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What type of shows are Punch and Judy and The Beggar's Opera?", "answer": "opera", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Music for an Accelerated Culture is the debut album from new rave/grindie band Hadouken!, the title is thought to be a reference to both Douglas Coupland's book and Music for the