al also sang in Armenian, Turkish, and Assyrian, Pete Mangurian or John Bilezikjian? ", "answer": "John Bilezikjian", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Stormborn is an episode whose title refers to the character in whose novels?", "answer": "George R. R. Martin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Welsh rock band, formed in 1992, released their ninth studio album, \"Keep the Village Alive\" in 2015? ", "answer": "Stereophonics", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "what does Haberlandia odzalaensis and Cameroon have in common?", "answer": "Congo", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Goh Choon Pong is the chief executive officer of what company with its head office on the fifth floor of the SATS Airfreight Terminal 5 at Singapore Changi Airport?", "answer": "Singapore Airlines Cargo", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "El Prado is an unincorporated suburb of Taos, in Taos County, New Mexico, it is bounded on the east by the town of Taos, and to the north by lands of which ancient pueblo belonging to a Tiwa-speaking Native American tribe of Puebloan people?", "answer": "Taos Pueblo", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Jameh Mosque of Tabriz is next to what place that is defined asa permanently enclosed marketplace or street where goods and services are exchanged or sold?", "answer": "the Grand Bazaar of Tabriz", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Joseph Robinette \"Beau\" Biden III, was an American attorney, officer in the Army Judge Advocate General's Corps, and politician from Wilmington, Delaware, and was the eldest of three children from the marriage of former U.S. Vice President Joe Biden and his first wife, Neilia, Joe Biden is an American politician, who was the 47th Vice President of the United States, during which time period?", "answer": "2009 to 2017", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is Anthony Stark trying to do with Amahl Farouk?", "answer": "set up an alliance", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was the 1976 European Cup Final ,which featured Dominique Rocheteau, played at?", "answer": "Hampden Park, Glasgow", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the second largest city in the country 8958 sq mile country located on the Horn of Africa?", "answer": "Ali Sabieh", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Bastard of Istanbul was written by this Turkish author born in what year?", "answer": "1971", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Symphony No. 6 in B minor was first performed in Moscow on 4/16 December, conducted by  Russian pianist, teacher, conductor and composer also known as who?", "answer": "Wassily Safonoff", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "C. David Cush was the CEO of the airline founded in what year?", "answer": "2004", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which month does this major tennis tournament take place, which was once called Australasian Championships?", "answer": "January", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which player who has recorded the most hits of any foreign-born player in MLB won the Japan Professional Sports Grand Prize?", "answer": "Ichiro Suzuki", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of the \"Golden Three\" composers was born October 28, 1825?", "answer": "Dmytro Bortniansky", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How long was the male co-writer of \"Pools of Darkness\" employed by TSR, Inc? ", "answer": "more than 20 years", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Name the Swiss born Italian record producer, composer, musician and DJ, best known for his compostion 'Children' and who has worked with Frank Musker, the British songwriter and composer for artists such as Sheena Easton, Bucks Fizz and Lisa Stansfield?", "answer": "Robert Miles", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What wrestler besides Kairi Hojo and \u5ca9\u8c37 \u9ebb\u512a is known as part of the three best wrestlers in the world?", "answer": "Io Shirai", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Austro-Hungarian U-boat fleet during the First World War, mainly consisted of German manufactured units transported by rail from Germany'