: "United States", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Of the two rock bands, Okkervil River or H\u00fcsker D\u00fc, which began as a trio made up of Shef and friends?", "answer": "Okkervil River", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Aunt Bam's Place is a 2011 American musical play created, written, produced, and directed by Tyler Perry, an American actor, comedian, filmmaker, writer, and songwriter, specializing in which genre?", "answer": "gospel", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "John Haase, is an English gangster, drug dealer and associate of Curtis Warren, an English gangster, who as Britain's most notorious drugs trafficker was formerly Interpol's Target One, and once listed on what?", "answer": "Sunday Times Rich List", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the co-star of a Hong Kong actress raised in Britain and Hong Kong in the comdey film What a Hero! ?", "answer": "Andy Lau", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which was built first the Time Warner Center or the Woolworth Building?", "answer": "The Woolworth Building", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Novelists Gerhart Hauptmann and Mario Vargas Llosa both won the Nobel Prize in Literature but in which year did Llosa most recently accomplish it?", "answer": "2010", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the Informe Robinson who was hosted by a Former Republic of Ireland football player Michael Robinson who also played as a striker?", "answer": "is a monthly Spanish sports magazine programme broadcast", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year was the actor born that stared in a 1985 American Comedy Head Office?", "answer": "1948", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who wrote the 1966 Beatles song that went on to number one in seven countries?", "answer": "Paul McCartney and John Lennon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many Saturn Award nomination does one of the stars of the film Hong Kong 97 have ?", "answer": "four", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When does one of the founder of Beacon Global Strategies born who was also an American political consultant?", "answer": "November 25, 1969", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Les deux journ\u00e9es, ou Le porteur d'eau (\"The Two Days, or The Water Carrier\") is an opera in three acts by Luigi Cherubini, with a libretto by Jean-Nicolas Bouilly, Bouilly claimed he took the story from a real life incident during the French Revolution but, for fear of censorship, he moved the action back to 1647 and the time of Cardinal Jules Raymond Mazarin, Duke of Rethel, Mayenne and Nevers, was an Italian cardinal, diplomat, and politician, who served as the Chief Minister to the kings of France Louis XIII and Louis XIV from 1642 until his death, in what year?", "answer": "1661", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "This book was an overview of the history of computer science and the Digital Revolution written by an American writer and journalist who is the president and CEO of what organization?", "answer": "Aspen Institute", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Enemy at the Gate was dedicated to the actor known for playing which character on Stargate SG-1?", "answer": "General Hammond", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many academy awards has the actor who starred in Cheers and the Hunger Games been nominated for", "answer": "two-time", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the name of the 1975 American thriller film directed by and starring Clint Eastwood, co-starring American actor Jack Cassidy?", "answer": "The Eiger Sanction", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of the following films explores the careers of prominent rock musicians: It Might Get Loud or Kon-Tiki?", "answer": "It Might Get Loud", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Tom Brower is a member of the House of Representatives from a district that includes which third-largest Hawaiian island?", "answer": "Oahu", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the current job of the player who broke Buzz Arlett's minor league home run record ?", "answer": "hitting coach for the West Michigan Whitecaps.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Born June 30, 1983 who fronted the second series of the British reality television series Hair?", "answer": "Katherine Ryan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which film came out earlier, \"Comandante\" or \"The Judge and the General\"?", "answer": "Comandante", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Maggie Lau had a small part in which 2005 Hong Kong movie?", "answer": "The Myth", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Did Michael Shaara and Michel Foucault have the same nationality ?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What street runs parallel to the street at the heart of the Arbat District of Miscow?", "answer": "Sivtsev Vrazhek", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year did the man that the Freedom Festival is named after become an Evangelical Christian?", "answer": "1785", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Benjamin Randell Harris served during the major conflicts led by which French leader?", "answer": "Napoleon I", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year did the current Attorney General of Missouri run against Kurt Schaefer?", "answer": "2016", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the nickname of the jazz artist featured on the cover of J-Live's second studio album?", "answer": "Trane", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who  played for a football club that was based in Leeds, West Yorkshire, England?", "answer": "Albert Sissons", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Walter Flanagan, is a comic book store manager, reality television personality, podcaster, and comic book artist, and a long-time friend of who, an American filmmaker, actor, comic book writer, author, and podcaster, and came to prominence with the low-budget comedy film \"Clerks\" (1994)?", "answer": "Kevin Smith", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What compilation series contains the album A Very Special Acoustic Christmas and features artists such as Tom Petty and the Heartbreakers? ", "answer": "A Very Special Christmas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is the company The Thompson/Center Contender  based?", "answer": "Springfield, Massachusetts", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which subdivisions of the University of Massachusetts is  Philip H. Melanson a Chancellor Professor of Policy Studies at ", "answer": "The University of Massachusetts Dartmouth", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The producer of an action-adventure video game developed by Clover Studio and published by Capcom and released in 2008 is now the head producer at what company?", "answer": "PlatinumGames", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the only survivor of the JAT Yugoslav Airlines Flight 367 and holds the Guinness world record for surviving the highest fall without a parachute? ", "answer": "Vesna Vulovi\u0107", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which software was used to create the film that became source material for \"Yo Frankie!?\"", "answer": "Blender", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Yoo Ha, is a South Korean film director, screenwriter and a contemporary poet, he directed the critically acclaimed film,  \"Once Upon a Time in High School\" (2004), is a South Korean drama film, the background of the film is set in a high school in which country?", "answer": "South Korea", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Cake and The Darling Buds both from America?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "what is the best player from the strongest Mexican football side to compete in Copa Libertadores, is famously known as?", "answer": "Bofo", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Hispaniola was found by the same person who alerted Europe of which unknown continent?", "answer": "Americas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the actor who starred in the 1989 comic science fiction film directed by Joe Johnston doing now?", "answer": "film acting hiatus", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is a genus of about 57 species of succulent subtropical plants of the family \"A