nt to the town that boasts itself as the location of  Everglades Gardens property?", "answer": "Katoomba", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is a 1988 romantic comedy-drama film directed by Mike Nichols and written by Kevin Wade, that stars an American actress which earned her a nomination for the Academy Award for Best Actress and won her a Golden Globe?", "answer": "Working Girl", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the first band fronted by Henry Lawrence Garfield?", "answer": "State of Alert", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Corey Taylor and Buffalo Tom both American-based musicians?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "George E. Hyde wrote about which Indian tribe that was also known as Dakota?", "answer": "Sioux", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What American singer, songwriter, dancer and actress, born May 16, 1966, is featured in the video Janet: Live in Hawaii?", "answer": "Janet Jackson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which is from farther west, Moscow Watchdog or Shetland Sheepdog?", "answer": "Shetland Sheepdog", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Lambada starred what actor who died in October 13, 2002?", "answer": "Keene Curtis", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which has a larger population, Hays, Kansas or Ellis County, Kansas?", "answer": "Ellis County, Kansas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the album containing \"Soft Touch\" released? ", "answer": "February 1979", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of the following skyscrapers has 49 floors: 101 Park Avenue or 126 Madison Avenue?", "answer": "101 Park Avenue", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What's the name of the american composer, conductor and arranger who was also one of the producers of the Beach Boys'?", "answer": "Henry Mancini", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Josie Cotton is best known for Johnny Are You Queer, which was used in the soundtrack for what 1983 American romantic comedy film that was directed by Martha Coolidge?", "a