ctor, and photographer who was raised in Baldwin, New York?", "answer": "Pacify Her", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 2001 Rockingham 500 was a Championship Auto Racing Teams (CART) motor race held on 22 September 2001 at the Rockingham Motor Speedway in Corby, Northamptonshire, England, which Swedish former race car driver, finished second for Team Rahal?", "answer": "Kenny Br\u00e4ck", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Is Orlando Sanford International Airport or East Texas Regional Airport further West?", "answer": "East Texas Regional Airport", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Chris Berman works for what network?", "answer": "ESPN", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the Marine Corp equivalent of the military award Eugene Mead Caffey received for his heroism in World War II?", "answer": "Navy Cross", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which professional basketball team with the home stadium Philips Arena did the retired American professional basketball Roshown McLeod play for?", "answer": "Atlanta Hawks", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the most important element of step dance, a style performed by Ira Bernstein?", "answer": "the footwork", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "between Michael Winner and Bo Widerberg, which person was born before the other?", "answer": "Bo Gunnar Widerberg", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Where was the main character in the film Bronson detained in high-security psychiatric hospitals?", "answer": "He has spent periods detained in the Rampton, Broadmoor and Ashworth high-security psychiatric hospitals.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "No. 1 Commando carried out a series of small scale cross channel raids and spearheaded what invation which started on 8 November 1942.", "answer": "Operation Torch", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were the films \"The Boatniks\" and \"College Road Trip\" both made by Walt Disney?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which was founded first, University of M