ed by the film \"Lone Wolf McQuade\"?", "answer": "Walker, Texas Ranger", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The organic compound with formula C3H8O2 is mainly used as a what that can can be formed by the nucleophilic attack of methanol on a  colorless and flammable gas with a faintly sweet odor?", "answer": "a solvent", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What television series based on a 1988 novel featured Marissa Lee Neitling as Kara Foster?", "answer": "\"The Last Ship\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What episode was played first, Truth and Advertising or PC Principal Final Justice?", "answer": "Truth and Advertising", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Is Yangzhong or Cenxi located in the east of Guangxi, People's Republic of China?", "answer": "Cenxi", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Odense Steel Shipyard was best known for building container ships for its parent group the largest container ship and supply vessel operator in the world since what year?", "answer": "1996", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "what type of liquor is used in a Bananarita that a Manhattan leaves out", "answer": "banana liquor", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The F Word was a romantic comedy film that starred the actor of what nationality, known for a role in \"Life of Pi\"?", "answer": "English", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which nationality is the mathematical physicist who invented a crackpot index to give an idea of what sort of claims and rhetoric were commonplace among pseudophysics proposals he had come across", "answer": "American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Peg's Paper and WomenSports are both what?", "answer": "magazine", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What non-alcoholic beverage was produced a regional division of the world's third-largest brewing company?", "answer": "Coors Cutter", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who, Kenneth Webb or Buster Keaton, was best known for his silent films?", "answer": "Joseph Frank \"Buster\" Keaton", "type": "compa