n", "answer": "Westpac Banking Corporation", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "On the Strength is the 2nd and final album by which American hip hop group formed in the South Bronx in 1976?", "answer": "Grandmaster Flash and the Furious Five", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The IRA Army Council is or was the decision-making body of the Provisional Irish Republican Army, more commonly known as the IRA, a paramilitary group dedicated to bringing about the end of the Union between Northern Ireland and Great Britain, the Council said to have included which Irish republican politician who is the president of the Sinn F\u00e9in political party, and a Teachta D\u00e1la ?", "answer": "Gerard \"Gerry\" Adams", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which dog breed is created from the cross of two other dog breeds, the Plummer Terrier, the Pudelpointer, or both?", "answer": "Pudelpointer", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are Huai'an and Ulanqab both located in China?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are Daniel McNicoll and Vinko Bre\u0161an both directors?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who won the Sawamura Award in 2007 and is a starting pitcher for the Los Angeles Dodgers?", "answer": "Yu Darvish", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the title of the film staring a golden award winner that premiered at the 1998 Sundance Film Festival ? ", "answer": "Dead Man's Curve", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Godlike: Superhero Roleplaying in a World on Fire, 1936-1946 is an alternate history World War II era Superhero role-playing game, is the first game released using the One-Roll Engine (O.R.E.) gaming system, a dice pool system where matched die results determine success, The One-Roll Engine (or O.R.E.) is a generic role-playing game system developed by who for the alternate history superhero roleplaying game \"Godlike\"?", "answer": "Greg Stolze", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Bemidji Axemen play in what state?", "answer": "Minnesota", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which cliff juts horizontally and is east of Tyssedal, Norway?", "answer": "Trolltunga", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Tim Webber is an English visual effects supervisor, he is known for his work on The Dark Knight, a 2008 superhero film directed, co-produced, and co-written by who?", "answer": "Christopher Nolan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jouji Nakata voiced Hellsing's Alucard which was written by which Japanese manga artist?", "answer": "Kouta Hirano", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What person heavily influenced a minister and close friend of Martin Luther King Jr.?", "answer": "Myles Falls Horton", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which significant Ukrainian Soviet modernist composer was taught by Arkady Abaza?", "answer": "Nikolai Roslavets", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A narrative ballet or story ballet, is a form of ballet that has a plot and characters, Plot refers to the sequence of events inside a story which affect other events through the principle of what?", "answer": "cause and effect", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are James Kerwin and Danny Boyle both film directors ?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Under what president did William Cohen serve as Secretary of Defense in the years following the death of Esequiel Hern\u00e1ndez Jr.?", "answer": "Bill Clinton", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the castle where Michael Gottlieb is located built?", "answer": "the 19th century", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who plays Elliot Alderson and was born on May 12, 1981?", "answer": "Rami Malek", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was a featured rap artist on Brighter Daze from?", "answer": "North Carolina", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who replaced the producer, born in 1971, who worked with the band on their studio album \"Room on Fire?\"", "answer": "Gordon Raphael", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many people were killed when the ocean liner