ional concentration of pueblos in the American Southwest?", "answer": "Pueblo Bonito", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which technique where the roller coaster is allowed to coast through the ride's circuit through the force of gravity is used in Adventure World since 1991?", "answer": "chain lift hill", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Peninsula Players is a program that reuses stock scenery and?", "answer": "costumes.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the population in 2016 of the city that includes Callala Beach?", "answer": "99,650", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year was the writer of the short story collection Cathedral born?", "answer": "1938", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What part of Idaho is covered by the the sister station of KREM-TV?  ", "answer": "North Idaho", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jan Smuts and a British Transvaal was given which award that recognizes distinguished service in the armed forces?", "answer": "Order of Merit", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the stadium of the football club for which Stefano Maler plays?", "answer": "Sparda Bank Hessen Stadium", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which one of Bill Watterson's comic strips was cited as \"the last great news paper comic?\"", "answer": "Calvin and Hobbes", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What NBC president created \"The Steven Banks Show\"?", "answer": "Brandon Tartikoff", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Russian advance during the start of the Battle of Kostiuchn\u00f3wka was also known as what?", "answer": "June Advance", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the population in 2010 for the town that holds Newfound Lake?", "answer": "1,613", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Teatro Avante is a nonprofit theater organization located in a neighborhood named after a city in what country?", "answer": "Cuba", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born first Dohonna Malik Scott or Elise \"Alex\" Leapai?", "answer": "Elise \"Alex\" L