h David Byrne and Emily Haines a songwriter?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": " Both Roulette and Game of the Goose are what?", "answer": "game", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What actor from the TV series \"Reaper\" also played a character named Sam Sullivan?", "answer": "Bret Harrison", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who, born in 1973, is the son of actor Jon Voight's former wife?", "answer": "James Haven", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In The Loop, starring Peter Capaldi, is the film based on which award-winning satirical TV series?", "answer": "The Thick of It", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Evil Dead 2: Dead by Dawn is the sequel to a film which used a prototype to build the interest of investors which was called what?", "answer": "\"Within the Woods\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Anne Hathaway appeared in what 2002 film based on a book by Charles Dickens?", "answer": "Nicholas Nickleby", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When Atarshumki I was king of Bit Agusi what was the name of the capital?", "answer": "Arpad", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which acquaintance of Kerry Wendell Thornley, who shot and killed Kennedy, is featured in the 1962 manuscript, \"The Idle Warriors\"?", "answer": "Lee Harvey Oswald", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The notable football player for Brookhaven High School was a wide receiver in the National Football League (NFL) for how many seasons?", "answer": "12", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What movie starred an actor born on 4 July 1981 in a role where he is an imprisoned petty criminal?", "answer": "A Prophet", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What actress, born July 2, 1986, who made her motion picture debut in Disney's commercially and critically successful 1998 remake of \"The Parent Trap\" also starred as Elizabeth Taylor in the 2012 film Liz & Dick?", "answer": "Lindsay Lohan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ministry of Sound Sessions Six includes remixes of tracks by many artists, including what English indie pop duo from Salford, Greater Manchester?", "answer": "The Ting Tings", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What chain was the largest direct competitor to Blockbuster Video, that was a retailer for United States computer software company which produces a human resources software line claimed to aid companies in evaluating job applicants and their suitability for particular positions by giving them personality tests?", "answer": "Hollywood Video", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year did the author of Facundo die?", "answer": "1888", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born first Scott Pembroke or Andr\u00e9 Cayatte?", "answer": "Scott Pembroke", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which of the airport close to Robert's Lounge is the busiest international air passenger gateway into North America, the fifth busiest airport in the United States and the busiest airport in the New York City airport system, handling just under 59 million passengers in 2016?", "answer": "John F. Kennedy International Airport", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Fernilee Reservoir is owned and operated by a company founded in what year?", "answer": "1995", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the 2016 population of the city in which the Murder of Constable Thomas King took place?", "answer": "246,376", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what direction does the U.S. highway that connects Florence, Souther Carolina and the county seat of Richland County run?", "answer": "east\u2013west", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What  large family car produced by by the German automaker Volkswagen, is the middle of two other cars one being  small family car marketed worldwide across seven generations, in various body configurations and under various nameplates ?", "answer": "Volkswagen Passat", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year was the man who discovered Palomar 4 born?", "answer": "1889", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ridgedale Center is an enclosed shopping mall in a suburban city which at the 2010 census had a population of what?", "answer": "49,734", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "En Iniya Enthira was written as a series in a magazine published from which Indian city ?", "answer": "Chennai", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which Lawrence Hazard film did German actress Marlena Diedrich star?", "answer": "The Spoilers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Which of the bands, Portishead or The Pillows, is named for a nearby town?", "answer": "Portishead", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "who is the coach for ND \u010crnu\u010de in 1994 who was born 27 May 1947 ? ", "answer": "Branko Oblak", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American singer, actress, dancer, activist, and comedian was featured on the soundtrack to the 2000 Disney film The Emperor's New Groove?", "answer": "Eartha Kitt", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Joplin Regional Airport and Antonio Rivera Rodr\u00edguez Airport both located on the US mainland?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The character and persona, Pandemonia, was brought to life as an inflatable created by an American artist known for working with popular culture subjects and his reproductions of banal objects, born when?", "answer": "January 21, 1955", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was a bassist for Panic! at the Disco and lead vocalist for the Brobecks?", "answer": "Dallon Weekes", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Stan Zimmerman produced the show \"Rita Rocks\" whose lead actress also appeared in the TV shows Martin and what ABC sitcom?", "answer": "My Wife and Kids", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What movie in 2005 starring Lee Young-ae deals with the themes of revenge, violence, and salvation? ", "answer": "Lady Vengeance", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which British singer now signed to Epic Records placed ahead of English pop/R&B boy band JLS on the fifth series of The X Factor? ", "answer": "Alexandra Burke",