ublic of Kazakhstan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "From 1862 to 1874 George W. Hough was the director of an observatory chartered on February 11, 1852 by what group?", "answer": "the New York State Senate", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Politics of Libya is in uncertain state due to the war of Libyan government with whom?", "answer": "National Salvation Government", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What other punch besides the \"power-punches\" is used in traditional boxing?", "answer": "jab", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What type of audience are Cosmopolitan and Bella both aimed at?", "answer": "women", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Dunbarton was a town in Barnwell County, South Carolina, United States, in 1951, it was acquired by the U.S. Atomic Energy Commission as part of a site for which nuclear reservation in the United States in the state of South Carolina, located on land in Aiken, Allendale, and Barnwell counties adjacent to the Savannah River, 25 mi southeast of Augusta, Georgia?", "answer": "Savannah River Site", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both Racing Extinction and Football Under Cover documentaries?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Were Satyajit Ray and Richard Boleslawski in the ame industry?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Vice-Admiral Frederick Spencer, 4th Earl Spencer was made a Knight of the Garter, an order of chivalry founded by whom?", "answer": "Edward III", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where most notably did the Chancellor who's death resulted in the first election for Oxford Chancellor, held several senior ministerial posts? ", "answer": "Viceroy of India", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which 2009 English-Danish Film won the award for Best Danish film at the 63rd Bodil awards?", "answer": "Antichrist", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Mysterious Origins of Man included material by the man who goes by what devotional name?", "answer": "Drutakarm\u0101 d