d for those troops that were engaged in a war that took place in which part of Africa ?", "answer": "West Africa", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which star of Into the Badlands was born on June 15, 1963 ?", "answer": "Helen Hunt", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ziegfeld Follies stars an American film actress and dancer that was born on February 21st of what year?", "answer": "1917", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The composer of \"Paluke Bangaaramaayena\" lived in what Indian village?", "answer": "Nelakondapalli", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the name of the debut album released by the Brighton hip hop duo whose one member appeared on the UK's largest rap battle league?", "answer": "Stereo Typical", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Khet and Nine Men's Morris strategy games?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who is older, Pete Docter or Patrice Leconte?", "answer": "Patrice Leconte", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What BRitish company manufactured an alternative to the Caterham 21?", "answer": "Lotus Cars", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The actor who played the part of Gram Parsons in Grand Theft Parsons was born in what year ?", "answer": "1972", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the family relationship between the two writers of \"Woman in Love\"?", "answer": "brothers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who coined the alternative name regarding a geological concept of the orogenic belt that was active in Gondwanaland?", "answer": "Alexander du Toit", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the title of the song by Migos that appears on their second studio album and is their second highest-charting song of their career? ", "answer": "T-Shirt", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are ESPN The Magazine and Military Heritage both published in Virginia?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Samoyed dogs and Smooth Collie's are both what type of working dogs.", "answer": "herding", "type": "com