ision series starring which South Korean actress and singer?", "answer": "Seo Hyun-jin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Has Judy Blume or Sandra Dallas written more non fiction books?", "answer": "Sandra Dallas is an award-winning American author of 13 adult novels, 2 children's novels, and 7 non-fiction books.", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "New York State Route 157 (NY 157) is a state highway in Albany County, New York, it runs from an intersection with NY 156 near the hamlet of Berne to a junction with NY 85 in the hamlet of New Salem, New York State Route 156 (NY 156) is a state highway in Albany County, New York, all are within which country?", "answer": "United States", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many employees did the oilfield services company which has B. Clark Burchfiel as a professor have? ", "answer": "100,000 people", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Gilbert William Barker was an Australian rules footballer who played for a club formed in what year?", "answer": "1883", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Tom McAlpin was the president of the company that was incorporated in 1996 as what?", "answer": "Magical Cruise Company Limited", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jin Kyung won an award at the Baeksang Arts Awards for a remake of what 2007 Hong Kong film?", "answer": "Eye in the Sky", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Ballester\u2013Molina is a pistol designed and built by an automotive and engineering company that manufactured weaponry and parts for what?", "answer": "public works", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Skywalker is a fictional family that has capabilities related to what concept?", "answer": "the Force", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 1985 NCAA Division I-A football season ended with the team led by the coach who went on to helm what NFL team as champions?", "answer": "Dallas Cowboys", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "GQ is the second magazine released in India after which fashion and lifestyle magazine to be wholly