ivate, coeducational, 4-year college located in south central Pennsylvania that offers more than 50 baccalaureate majors in professional programs, the sciences, and humanities to its 4,600 full-time undergraduate students, Polytechnic University of the Philippines or York College of Pennsylvania?  ", "answer": "York College of Pennsylvania", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What magazine is Japanese, about new manga and video games based on popular manga,  and used the magazine Hobby's Jump as it's prototype.", "answer": "V Jump", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the vocalist of a heavy metal band formed in Las Vegas, Nevada in 2005 born?", "answer": "1975", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Jeff Buckley and Vampire Weekend both American?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What experimental work is the French physicist, born in 1947 who serves on the selection committee for the John Stewart Bell Prize established in 2009, well-known for?", "answer": "quantum entanglement", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Battle of Canusium was part of a larger offensive to narrow the base of the general who was the son of which commander?", "answer": "Hamilcar Barca", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Match Group, Inc. operates as a subsidiary of a company with brands across how many countries?", "answer": "100", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A small small twin-engine jet corporate aircraft was further developed and updated by what brand of Textron Aviation since 2014?", "answer": "Beechcraft", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the musical that included the song \"Too Darn Hot\" turned into a movie?", "answer": "1953", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which sports team did the founder of Ave Maria University own in the 1980s?", "answer": "Detroit Tigers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When did the person who awarded the title Prince of Li\u00e8ge die?", "answer": "17 February 1934", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which tenant of Melbourne Rectangular Stadium has Jess Fishlock as head coach?", "answer": "Melbourne City FC", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the artist who released the song \"Looking Good, Feeling Gorgeous\" born?", "answer": "1960", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The doll which is a fusion a white girl child with a Southern United States archetype for a black woman who worked as a nanny is dated to what year? ", "answer": "1950s", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jagdpanther had a cannon that was previously used on the German heavy tank used during what event?", "answer": "Second World War", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Adam Beach, is a Saulteaux actor, he had a role as Dr. Charles Eastman (Ohiyesa) in which 2007 television film adapted from the book of the same name by Dee Brown?", "answer": "Bury My Heart at Wounded Knee", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which author, who became the first science fiction writer to receive the MacArthur Fellowship, wrote the story, \"Bloodchild\", which won the Hugo Award?", "answer": "Octavia Estelle Butler", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "which city and an important business and cultural centre in northern Italy was Gleb Wataghin born in ", "answer": "Turin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ronnie Dunn and Jenna Sanz-Agero were both formerly part of bands in which they each acted in what role?", "answer": "singer", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "How is Firefly Estate connected to Noel Coward?", "answer": "the burial place", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is located in Pooneryn, adjacent to the Jaffna Peninsula and was captured by  a governorate established in present-day Sri Lanka by the Dutch East India Company?", "answer": "Pooneryn Fort", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the director of Theres Always Vanilla and was born February 4, 1940?", "answer": "George A. Romero", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The band that released the song \"Back to the 80's\" have sold approximately how