ey recorded which song, written and produced by Andr\u00e9 3000 for his 2003 album?", "answer": "Hey Ya!", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Adolf \u010cech led performances of operas by a composer who was active during what period?", "answer": "romantic", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "which star of Tenderness was born on 7 April 1964?", "answer": "Russell Crowe", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How are Angostura bitters and Smoking Bishop similar?", "answer": "alcoholic mixture", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Shir\u014d Hamaguchi is a Japanese anime composer, arranger and orchestrator, he is best known for composing music to the anime franchise One Piece, a Japanese manga series written and illustrated by who?", "answer": "Eiichiro Oda", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In string theory, D-branes are a class of extended objects upon which open strings can end with Dirichlet boundary conditions, after which they are named, D-branes were discovered by Dai, Leigh and which American theoretical physicist, and string theorist?", "answer": "Joseph Polchinski", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Doggerland was an area now beneath the southern North Sea that connected Great Britain to continental Europe during and after the last glacial period, it was probably a rich habitat with human habitation in the Mesolithic period, although rising sea levels gradually reduced it to low-lying islands before its final submergence, possibly following a tsunami caused by the Storegga Slide, The three Storegga Slides are considered to be amongst the largest known ?", "answer": "landslides", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Heroes of the Equinox is a volume in which science fiction series created by Pierre Christin?", "answer": "Val\u00e9rian and Laureline", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which cartridge did John Browning design that has a rim that is the same in diameter as the .50 GI?", "answer": ".45 ACP", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the British actress and children's book author, who featured in the preschool television series 'Julie's Greenroom' with Julie Andrews?", "answer": "Emma Walton Hamilton", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Shirley Breeden narrowly beat which Republican for the 2008 term Nevada United States Senate seat?", "answer": "Joe Heck", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How are the spiritual beings, of which the title character of the 1995 film \"Zazel: The Scent of Love\" is one, typically described?", "answer": "benevolent, dreadful, and endowed with wisdom", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Inspired by \"The Grey Album\", which collaborative EP by Jay-Z and Linkin Park was released in 2004?", "answer": "Collision Course", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Tyson Hesse lead the creation of a side-scrolling platform game in order to celebrate the 25th anniversary of what game that he is best known for working on?", "answer": "Sonic the Hedgehog", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which British actress was in the movie \"Shifty\"?", "answer": "Francesca Annis", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Battle for Sevastopol is a 2015 biographical war film, about which Ukrainian Red Army Soviet sniper during World War II?", "answer": "Liudmyla Mykhailovna Pavlychenko", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "On whose novel was a 1996 British-American musical fantasy for which David Thewlis did voice work for based?", "answer": "Roald Dahl", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which airport is further south, Aniak Airport or Jackson Hole Airport?", "answer": "Jackson Hole Airport", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What American actor who appeared on the twelfth episode of The Simpsons fourth season was \"The Princess Guide\" dedicated to?", "answer": "Leonard Nimoy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What else did John Morrissey, a bare-knuckle boxer do?", "answer": "Dead Rabbits gang criminal leader", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the director of the film for which Kerrie Brown was nominated for an Aca