hon event at the 2016 Summer Olympics, officially known as the Games of the XXXI Olympiad and commonly known as Rio 2016, was a major international multi-sport event celebrated in Rio de Janeiro, Brazil, from what date time span?", "answer": "5 to 21 August 2016", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What popular West End performer starred in Stage Fright?", "answer": "Alastair Sim", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Stewart O'Nan and Wilfred Owen both considered American novelists?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the island that the \"Grand Canyon of the Pacific\" known as?", "answer": "\"Garden Isle\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Crassula and Selinum, are different types of what?", "answer": "plants", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "An eight cylinder engine with the cylinders set at an angle is called what?", "answer": "V8", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the shared profession of Jack Kerouac and Dan Masterson?", "answer": "poet", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is Tom Keegan's job at the daily newspaper published in Lawrence, Kansas, United States, by The World Company?", "answer": "Tom Keegan (born March 22, 1959) is an American sportswriter and author who currently is sports editor", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What system of two galaxies had its discovery announced on a television program presented by Brian Cox and others?", "answer": "9Spitch", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "During what year was the incorporated town and deep water seaport founded?", "answer": "1936", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who best known as a founding member of Eagles, Stevie Ray Vaughan or Bernie Leadon?", "answer": "Bernard Mathew Leadon III", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which character did Frankie Russel Faison play in the Hannibal Lecter series? ", "answer": "Barney Matthews", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Belly stars what rapper who published a book of memoirs in 2003?", "answer": "DMX", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Pluralist school was a school of pre-Socratic philosophers who attempted to reconcile Parmenides' rejection of change with the apparently changing world of sense experience, it can also be said to have included which philosopher who was the earliest Greek to develop the theory of atomism\u2014the idea that everything is composed entirely of various imperishable, indivisible elements called atoms. Leucippus often appears as the master to his pupil Democritus, a philosopher also touted as the originator of the atomic theory?", "answer": "Leucippus", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which magazine is published more frequently, Watercolor Artist or Bon App\u00e9tit?", "answer": "Bon App\u00e9tit", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which band was formed first, Circus Diablo or Cave In?", "answer": "Cave In", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which of the attracted which will be replaced by DreamWorks Theatre  is a 4D film at various theme parks around the world?", "answer": "Shrek 4-D", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Josph Ames studied Fraunhofer lines during his research of which published work?", "answer": "Fraunhofer's memoirs", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which TV show starring Samuel Page is an adaptation of a BBC miniseries. ", "answer": "House of Cards", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\" The BFG\" is a 2016 American fantasy adventure film staring what actor born in 1978?", "answer": "William Thomas Hader Jr.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who created the show with an episode called \"How to Eat with Your Butt\"?", "answer": "Trey Parker and Matt Stone", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Wee Cooper O'Fife is a folk song also recorded by which folksinger that died in 2005?", "answer": "Hedy West", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Both Murray Gell-Mann and Robert Andrews Millikan received what prestigious award?", "answer": "Nobel Prize", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jack Fairbrother was an English football goalkeeper,