ed in what year?", "answer": "1890", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The city where Turkish Statistical Institute has its headquarters in has a population of what in the urban center?", "answer": "4,587,558", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "While both were born in the 18th century, which composer was born first: Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart or Giacomo Meyerbeer?", "answer": "Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which dog breed, Majorca Ratter or Yorkshire Terrier, has a grey, black, and tan coat, and the nickname \"Yorkie\"?", "answer": "The Yorkshire Terrier", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which private Roman Catholic four-year research university did Jerome Michael \"Jerry\" Trupiano graduate from?", "answer": "Saint Louis University", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which year was this American musical comedy-drama film directed by Stephen Herek, for which Tom Werman produced the music and soundtrack, released?", "answer": "2001", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many books has a winner of multiple Hugo Awards after after winning the John W. Campbell Award born in 1942 written?", "answer": "more than 60", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the state called in which the official currency of Japan is higher compared to other currencies?", "answer": "yen expensive recession", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many characters is typically used in the runic alphabet found on 30 runestones that refer to Viking Age travels to England?", "answer": "16 characters", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the rare adult male American Opera singer who is able to sing as a sopranist?", "answer": "Michael Maniaci", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year was one of the plays in which Sergey Aydarov has an acclaimed part written by William Shakespeare?", "answer": "1599", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Blue Hills Parkway runs to the north edge of a reservation in the town that was the birthplace of which former President?", "