olved in the capture of?", "answer": "Arthur Barker", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Berkheya and Valeriana both endemic to Africa?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In which season of coaching was the longer serving of the two coaches of the 2016 Auburn Tigers football team and 2016 Oklahoma Sooners football team ?  ", "answer": "18th season", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Andrea Enria studied economics at a private university in what Italian city?", "answer": "Milan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which man was older, Tim O'Brien or Erich Fromm?", "answer": "Erich Seligmann Fromm", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are The Verve and Richard Ashcroft from the same country?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who founded the company that created the Leica M6 camera?", "answer": "Ernst Leitz", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which film was shown on a double bill with the film \"Dumbo\", Saludos Amigos or Valiant?", "answer": "Saludos Amigos", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which member of the English 2010 FIFA squad was also a member of the Tampa Bay Rowdies? ", "answer": "Joe Cole", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which German Prince, born in 1818, composed Diana von Sloange?", "answer": "Ernst II of Saxe-Coburg-Gotha", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the Australian state in which Fernando de Moraes last played with the South Melbourne FC?", "answer": "Victoria", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American band was involved in a 2005 legal battle against N.W.A. for unauthorized sampling of a song?", "answer": "Funkadelic", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the last monarch under which Robert Waterton was a trusted servant of the House of Lancaster born?", "answer": "1421", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Kyra Nijinsky was the daughter of a Russian ballet dancer who was admired for his what?", "answer": "seemingly gravity-defying leaps", "type": "bridge"}, {"ques