h recently demolished stadium was home to the first British football club to win a major European tournament?", "answer": "White Hart Lane", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Mark Eugene Gray was a member of a country pop band that started by playing local clubs which led to touring with what?", "answer": "Dick Clark's Caravan of Stars", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both The Kooks and The Deadly Syndrome from Los Angeles?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What, established in 1754, is a private Ivy League research university in Upper Manhattan, New York City, was the Alva professor Emeritus of Human Genetics in the Faculty of Medicine of McGill University awarded the prestigious Pollin Prize for Pediatric Research?", "answer": "Columbia University", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of the cult shows created by Eric Fogel was produced by Tornante Animation in association with Cuppa Coffee Studios and Rogers Communications?", "answer": "Glenn Martin, DDS", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which part of England has the same accent as the accent that Jim Burke performs \"chap hop\" in? ", "answer": "the south of England", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ruby Modine will co-star in an American slasher film directed by who?", "answer": "Christopher B. Landon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the king whose mistress was El\u017cbieta Branicka criticized of as the last king of the Commonwealth?", "answer": "failure to stand against the partitions, and thus to prevent the destruction of Poland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Paul Pumphrey went to high school with a former WWE wrestler who was born in what year?", "answer": "1974", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How did Dunkin' Donuts, a global donut company and coffeehouse, help propell Japanese actor and model Ryohei Otani into Korean entertainment in 2003?", "answer": "a commercial", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Kurt Jetta has studied data about which chain of discount 