arie", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Roy Emerson and Frew McMillan played what sport?", "answer": "tennis", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "When was the author of One Hand Clapping born?", "answer": "25 February 1917", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Soviet politician served under the First Secretary of the Communist Party of the Soviet Union?", "answer": "Nikolai Alexandrovich Bulganin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What artist was knighted in 2016 and did the vocals for the band Python Lee Jackson?", "answer": "Rod Stewart", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year did the director of the family drama film, Two Brothers, begin an acting career?", "answer": "2002", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the pilot that broke the speed of sound in 1947 that was interviewed for the book by Tom Wolfe?", "answer": "Chuck Yeager", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What school did Idaho Vandals' head coach go to after hiring Robb Akey?", "answer": "Arizona State University", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both Samuel R. Delany and Neil Simon American?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What author, who was educated in Russia before moving to the United States in 1926, included novelist Erika Holzer in her inner circle?", "answer": "Ayn Rand", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What nationality is actor that plays the philandering NYC illustrator in Loving?", "answer": "American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Do Mark Joffe and Suresh Bhardwaj share the same nationality?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are the Rahmi M. Ko\u00e7 Museum and the Milion located in the same country?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which British national museum holds Over The Top and banches at five locations in England?", "answer": "Imperial War Museum", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Japanese computer-generated anime series, Midnight Horror School, was created by what person that also created the 3