ear?", "answer": "1952", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Beasts of The Southern Wild was directed by whom?", "answer": "Benh Zeitlin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What company released the first movie directed by actress Cheryl Hines?", "answer": "Magnolia Pictures", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Tornjak and Dunker are both what?", "answer": "breed of dog", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which game, RoboRally or Plateau, was rereleased in 2016 by Wizards of the Coast?", "answer": "RoboRally", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Kajra Re is a song that features the Indian actress who won which pageant?", "answer": "Miss World 1994", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which editor of Progress in Materials Science also taught metallugy at Harvard University?", "answer": "Bruce Chalmers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which institution has the most campuses, Rice University or the University of Tennessee system?", "answer": "University of Tennessee system", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the name of this faction of the Marxist Russian Social Democratic Labour Party, which split from the Menshevik faction and who killed Alexander Bagration of Mukhrani?", "answer": "Bolsheviks", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Mistrial is the fourteenth solo studio album by American recording artist Lou Reed, A music video was created for the song \"No Money Down\" that featured an animatronic Lou Reed, Animatronics refers to the use of which type devices, to emulate a human or an animal, or bring lifelike characteristics to an otherwise inanimate object?", "answer": "robotic", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Sara Lee has worked with which folk rock music duo?", "answer": "Indigo Girls", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The person Cvjetko Popovi\u0107 was involved in the assassination of became heir presumptive to the Austro-Hungarian throne in what year?", "answer": "1896", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jawani Phir Nahi Ani stars the actor who is known