ere is the serial killer, that the Mothers of Murdered Offspring were instrumental in bringing to justice, being held ? ", "answer": "Central Prison in Raleigh.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both Matt and Kim and Jem Welsh musicians?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Raleigh\u2013Durham International Airport, is the main airport serving Raleigh, Durham, and the surrounding Research Triangle region of North Carolina, the airport  is a crew base for which regional airline carrier, owned by Trans States Holdings and is headquartered in Bridgeton, Missouri?", "answer": "Trans States Airlines", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Hawaiian Poi Dog and Field Spaniel, are a breed of what?", "answer": "dog", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Did Krzysztof Zanussi and Sebastian Gutierrez have the same profession?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is this community website created by Drew Curtis that allows members to comment on a daily batch of news articles and other items from various websites that the Slashdot effect is associated with?", "answer": "Fark", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What actor who received four Academy Award nominations starred with Sally Field in Back Roads?", "answer": "Tommy Lee Jones", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Samuel Hirsch was a major religious philosopher for a religion whose greatest center today is where?", "answer": "North America", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What two-level shopping mall was the largest in Greater Pittsburg until Monroeville Mall owned by CBL & Associates Properties, Inc., opened?", "answer": "South Hills Village", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Yoshinori Imaizumi is known for describing a subspecies that has been listed as critically endangered on the IUCN Red List since which year ?", "answer": "2008", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jonathan Corey Crowder was born in what county?", "answer": "Carroll County", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The ABS tv station's transmmitter is located on a mountain that is how many metres tall?", "answer": "727", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Both Wynn Resorts and Wynn Macau share who as their CEO?", "answer": "Steve Wynn", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Corridor of Mirrors was the first film for the character actor of what nationality?", "answer": "English", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was the instrument maker working in the 60s that reasoned that a viola played vertically could be made larger born?", "answer": "Springfield, Massachusetts.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is the carrier who inaugurated flights from Chennai to Mysore based?", "answer": "Hyderabad", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Dragon Ball Z: Bojack Unbound, was released in Japan on July 10, 1993, the antagonist Bojack was designed by the series creator, who is this Japanese manga and game artist called?", "answer": "Akira Toriyama", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Acinos and Cryptocarya both evergreen genii?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Heeb and Who Put the Bomp, are media of what type?", "answer": "magazine", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In which city did the brother of Karan Kapoor run the Prithvi Theatre?", "answer": "Mumbai", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the a particular focus of the organization for which Andrew A. Snelling works?", "answer": "promotion of young Earth creationism", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which founder of the Porsche company had Karl Rabe's help in developing his cars' transmissions?", "answer": "Ferdinand Porsche", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Did Paul Heyse and Joyce Carol Oates live during the same time?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who became famous for the work he did in establishing the fine arts program at a state-supported military college in Lexington, Virginia?", "answer": "William Dickinson Washington", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what capacity did the