s spanning over five seasons?", "answer": "The Dick Van Dyke Show", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "On what network and in what country did The Simpsons episodes \"Half-Decent Proposal\" and \"The Way We Was\" air?", "answer": "Fox network in the United States", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year was Urby Emanuelson's manager at Ajax Youth Academy born?", "answer": "1956", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What do Kino and Porcupine Tree have in common?", "answer": "rock band", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which has the highest peak, Sunanda Devi, India's second highest mountain, or Khartaphu?", "answer": "Khartaphu", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are Jules Massenet and Dmitri Shostakovich both from France?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which writer was Russian, James Gould Cozzens or Aleksandr Solzhenitsyn?", "answer": "Aleksandr Isayevich Solzhenitsyn", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the name of the designer of the casino, in which the Guggenheim Hermitage Museum was located?", "answer": "KlingStubbins", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Elymus and Nicandra, are types of what?", "answer": "plants", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which company owns the logo that appears on Air Jordan Retro XIIs?", "answer": "Nike", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where did The Black Eyed Peas song that followed \"Alive\" peak on the \"Billboard\" Hot 100?", "answer": "number seven", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Need You\" is a 1967 single by Sonny James, James Hugh Loden, known professionally as Sonny James, was an American country music singer and songwriter best known for his hit, \"Young Love\", released in which year?", "answer": "1957", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Newmarket was the home of the royal who was king of Scotland from 1649 until he was deposed in what year?", "answer": "1651", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what part of the Absheron Peninsula did Eldar Gasimov host a 2012 song contest?", "answer": "Baku", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Epcot ride closed in 1995 to be refurbished and closed permanently in 1996?", "answer": "World of Motion", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who founded Maverick Aviation Group headquartered in Las Vegas, Nevada?", "answer": "Greg and Brenda Rochna", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When does the American comic actor born who became a star Legends of Oz: Dorothy's Return?", "answer": "June 15, 1954", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where were the early settlers of La Boca from?", "answer": "Italian city of Genoa", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the informal name of the British soap opera created by Granada Television that Jon Rollason has appeared in episodes of?", "answer": "Corrie", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "High Noon, Part II: The Return of Will Kane is a 1980 made-for television film sequel to the classic 1952 Western film \"High Noon\", it starred Lee Majors in the title role, as well as David Carradine and Pernell Elven Roberts, Jr., Roberts passed away on which date?", "answer": "January 24, 2010", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Aboke was the site of the abductions by what heterodox Christian cult?", "answer": "Lord's Resistance Army", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Sethe is the protagonist of what 1987 novel written by Nobel Award winning author Toni Morrison?", "answer": "Beloved is a 1987 novel by the American writer Toni Morrison.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the 2017 comedy loosely based on the real-life relationship between Kumail Nanjiani and Emily Gordon, played by Zoe Kazan?", "answer": "Michael Showalter", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How did the American lobbyist, lawyer, and United States Senator, Christopher John Dodd, say in his introductory remarks in regard to legislation for Newborn Screening Saves Lives Act of 2007?", "answer": "the legislation \u201cprotect[s] the most vulnerable members of our society: newborn infants.\u201d", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is featured on the album cover of the best-selling 12\" signle of all time?", "answer": "5.25-inch disk", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Simpsons Sing the Blues is the first album released as an offshoot of \"The Simpsons\", the album contains originally recorded music, the first verse of the track \"Moaning Lisa Blues\" which was first featured in which episode, the sixth episode of \"The Simpsons\"' first season, and originally aired on the Fox network in the United States on February 11, 1990?", "answer": "Moaning Lisa", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What university did the footballing legend whose career was launched by Bank Tejarat F.C. attend?", "answer": "Sharif University of Technology", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the stage name of the American rapper from Michigan, who was a member of Funky Cowboys, Good Sqwad, and most notably for a group in which half the members made a guest appearance on the debut solo album 'The People vs' by Trick-Trick?", "answer": "Proof", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "12th & Midtown is in Midtown Atlanta along what street", "answer": "Peachtree Street", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which one has been bred as a GMO creeping bent grass,  Weigela or Agrostis?", "answer": "Agrostis", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What business founded in 1998 and have sports holdings include: the National Football League's New England Patriots, major League Soccer's New England Revolution and the stadium in which both tems play, Gillette Stadium?", "answer": "Kraft Group", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the American child beauty pageant queen born who was killed in her family's home in Boulder and who'smother was Patricia Ann?", "answer": "August 6, 1990", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "James Northcote appeared in a 2013 European two-part art film written and directed by who?", "answer": "Lars von Trier", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "After how many days did the manager born