ather of modern physics?", "answer": "Galileo Galilei", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Vuaqava is an outlier in a country whose closest neighbors to the west are which country ?", "answer": "Vanuatu", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What English electronic music producer based in Croydon handled production on the title track of Miles Kane's EP First of My Kind?", "answer": "Skream", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In between University of Michigan and Universidade Positivo which one was moved to Ann Arbor in 1837?", "answer": "The University of Michigan", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are Yixing and Dezhou the same level of city?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Eldorado Mountain is a summit in a mountain range that stretches how many miles?", "answer": "more than 3000", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are the Garajonay National Park and Caldera de Taburiente National Park located on the same island?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In what city did the seial killer, upon whom Dennis Cooper's \"Jerk\" is based, commit his murders?", "answer": "Houston, Texas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Can both Doug Fieger and David Johansen be described as singer songwriters ?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who created the television series which was a scripted comedy based on Nicole Byers life?", "answer": "Christian Lander and Christine Zander", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year did The Watercolor and The Princess and the Frog come out?", "answer": "2009", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Richard Djerf is often compared with the man who killed his family members in what city and state?", "answer": "Westfield, New Jersey", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the professional association football club formed for which Fulham's Craven Cottage was named?", "answer": "1879", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which award did the Jaleel Ahmad White who starred in Muriel Resnik's 1966  homonymous film collected ", "answer": "Tony Award", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Bernardo Sandals was founded in 1946 by architect Bernard Rudofsky and Berta Rudofsky, the core ideas of the designs were those Bertha taught at which school founded in 1933 in Black Mountain, North Carolina (near Asheville, North Carolina), emphasized the study of art as central to a liberal arts education?", "answer": "Black Mountain College", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Australian talent show was hosted by a man born 2 September 1938?", "answer": "Pot Luck", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "KroniK was an American professional wrestling tag team in World Championship Wrestling (WCW) and the World Wrestling Federation (WWF), composed of Brian Adams, and who?", "answer": "Bryan Clark", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who served in 1942 as the Republican member of the Kentucky House of Representatives who's district is on the border of Green River Lake?", "answer": "Lloyd Fuller Harding", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "On what topic did James Watson and Alex Stokes have papers published in \"Nature\" on 25 April 1953?", "answer": "the structure of DNA", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What American talk show host interviews celebrities on the podcast \"Girl on a Guy?\"", "answer": "Aisha Tyler", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Attix dramatist Euripides made a play similar to which Greek tragedian?", "answer": "Sophocles", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which group developed the first-person psychological horror video game that the upcoming first-person survival horror video game Allison Road is supposedly a spiritual successor to?", "answer": "Kojima Productions", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American content delivery network has Naomi O. Seligman on the Board of Directors and is headquartered in Cambridge, Massachusetts?", "answer": "Akamai Technologies", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jeff Ma graduated from which co-ed independent school?", "answer": "Phillips Exeter Academy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Gran Fiesta Tour is in a pavilion next to which pavilion at Epcot?", "answer": "Norwegian pavilion", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Mantis has a son named Sequoia.  What organization is Mantis a former member of?", "answer": "the Avengers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were the IBM PCjr and CCE MC-1000 both ome computers?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In what movement was the women who made her famous in the Montgomery Bus Boycott an activist?", "answer": "the Civil Rights Movement", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Mike Casey was a part of what some consider to be the best recruiting class in UK history which included a player who named an All American how many times?", "answer": "twice", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was an Australian rock band formed in Adelaide in late 1994 that has worked with Anton Hagop?", "answer": "The Superjesus", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "SkyPoint Observation Deck is most known for what theme park in Queensland, Australia?", "answer": "Dreamworld", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Shakespeare's character Macbeth is based on a historical figure that became King in what year?", "answer": "1040", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Tori Kelly voiced the character Meena in a 2016 animated film written by who?", "answer": "Garth Jennings", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which was released first, Point of Order or The Celluloid Closet?", "answer": "Point of Order", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What type of category does Pine and Bunchosia have in common?", "answer": "genus", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What district did the 13th president of the University of Oklahoma represent in Congress?", "answer": "Oklahoma's 2nd district", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who formed the UK-based global retailer for which David Bernstein was the former chairman?", "answer": "Stephen Marks", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which 