hn Watson lost to hold the WBA lightweight title?", "answer": "2015 to 2016", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which director is also a screenwriter, Keisuke Kinoshita or Daniel McNicoll?", "answer": "Daniel McNicoll", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In what year did this Argentine dancing competition begin airing, in which Bailando 2012 was its eighth Argentinean season?", "answer": "2006", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What TV show featured the salesperson known for promoting Fix-It, OxiClean and Orange Glo?", "answer": "PitchMen", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Scaphosepalum (from Greek \"boatlike sepals\") is a genus of plants belonging to the family Orchidaceae, many species in this genus produce unusual and distinctive flowers; some possessing cushion-like characteristics reminiscent of which large African bovine?", "answer": "African buffalo", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which company produced the 2017 film in which Chanon Santinatornkul starred ?", "answer": "Jor Kwang Films", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Adolph Sutro made a fortune at a silver ore located under the eastern slope of what mountain?", "answer": "Mount Davidson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which producer of Zeitgeist was also the lead singer?", "answer": "Billy Corgan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the actress that portrayed a barmaid at the Rovers Return Inn on the program \"Coronation Street\" born?", "answer": "1942", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Cinema were a short-lived progressive rock band started by former members of an English rock band formed in London in and notabley regarded as what?", "answer": "progressive rock pioneers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who hosted the Radio City Music Hall based event for American daytime TV held in May 2003?", "answer": "Wayne Brady", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the film with LaVita Raynor  played Kionna?", "answer": "Hype Williams", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What type of film are both A Film Unfinished and Round Eyes in the Middle Kingdom?", "answer": "documentary", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who did George Sanders play in Alfred Hitchcock's first American project?", "answer": "Jack Favell", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What castle sits on a cliff overlooking the River Ness and was part of the Scottish Civil War?", "answer": "Inverness Castle", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which joint program with a public research university in Clear Water Bay Peninsula does Menachem Brenner teach for?", "answer": "MSGF", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "This singer became the first Afro Pop artist to feature in \"Guinness World Records\" for his contribution on a song by which Canadian rapper?", "answer": "Drake", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Silverback Gorilla 2 is the sixth studio album by which American rapper, the album features guest appearances from Ghostface Killah?", "answer": "Sheek Louch", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Dutch-based computer manufacturer was founded by Beny Alagem?", "answer": "Packard Bell", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How long was the concert career of the woman that is speculated to be the frustrated love inspiration of Brahms' Liebeslieder Walzer, Op. 52?", "answer": "61-year", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "what else has Bridgette Wilson done", "answer": "\"Santa Barbara\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Albert Odyssey: Legend of Eldean is a role-playing video game produced for a fifth-generation home video game console that was released in North America on what date?", "answer": "May 11, 1995", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which genus has more species, Acanthus or Clematis?", "answer": "Clematis", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are both Jon Anderson and Boots Riley from the same county ?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "When was the company that sponsored Tour 2013 \"Shout to the Walls!\" founded?", "answer": "1906", "type": "bridge"}, {"questi