rave Heights Christian School is located in a low mountain range with its highest mountain rising to how many meters ?", "answer": "633 metres", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the  eyeglass maker buried?", "answer": "29 September 1619", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which country did Gili & Galit perform Darekh Hamelekh for the Eurovision Song Contest?", "answer": "Switzerland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How tall is the Grist mill located in a town apart of Great Neck in Nassau County, New york with a population of 830 per the 2010 census", "answer": "2 \u2044 -story gambrel-roofed structure", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Nilay Konar, is a Turkish volleyball player, born in which capital of the Republic of Turkey?", "answer": "Ankara", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who played Dick in the television adaptation of the series of children's adventure novels written by English author Enid Blyton?", "answer": "Paul Child", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which actor, born in 1926, appeared in the film Sandokan the Great?", "answer": "Steve Reeves", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What American journalist was married to another American journalist who is one of only three Americans buried in the Kremlin Wall Necropolis?  ", "answer": "Louise Bryant", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Whitney Cummings co-created which sitcom featuring two friends owning a cupcake business?", "answer": "2 Broke Girls", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which university,  Universit\u00e9 Laval or Clarkson University is a private research university with its main campus located in Potsdam, New York, and additional graduate program and research facilities in New York State's Capital Region and Beacon, N.Y.?", "answer": "Clarkson University", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the name of the first fully musical episode of the animated television series about a boy who lives in the fictional town of Beach City with the \"Crystal Gems\"?", "answer": "Steve