fy the Vampire Slayer\" who was also portrayed by the actor who played John Hawkes in \"Underground\" introduced?", "answer": "\"The Freshman\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The construction of the Auburn and Syracuse Railroad was delayed because of a panic that lasted until what time period?", "answer": "mid-1840s", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which pizza chain has more locations, Rosati's or Mellow Mushroom?", "answer": "Rosati's", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The 1997\u201398 NBA season was the tenth season for the Charlotte Hornets in the National Basketball Association, early into the season, they traded Muggsy Bogues to which sports organization?", "answer": "Golden State Warriors", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Watford Football Club elevated which assistant manager, now the head coach of Burnley, to the managership in the 2011-12 season?", "answer": "Sean Mark Dyche", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Scieno Sitter is content-control software that, when installed on a computer, blocks certain websites critical of which body of religious beliefs and practices developed in 1954 by American author L. Ron Hubbard, from being viewed?", "answer": "Scientology", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What pitcher, that has won the Cy Young Award for four consecutive years, did Eddie Perez play with?", "answer": "Gregory Alan Maddux", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was portrayed by Waylon Payne in the Original Motion Picture Walk the Line and was often known by his nickname, The Killer?", "answer": "Jerry Lee Lewis", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The drivers title of The 2009 Portuguese GP2 round was claimed by which German professional racing driver currently racing for the Renault Sport F1 Team?", "answer": "Nico H\u00fclkenberg", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Kourtney Kardashian and David Hedison in the same industry?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Under which administration is this American banker, film producer, and former hedge fund manager who is currently married to Louise Linton U. S. Secretary of the Treasury?", "answer": "Trump administration", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Pixie Geldof is the daughter of the writer who was known for work on which two television series?", "answer": "\"The Tube\" and \"The Big Breakfast\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The city of Gavle received its charter during which era?", "answer": "era of the Kalmar Union", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Enerpac business is a division of which organization, NYSE: [ ATU], a $1.5 billion diversified global manufacturing company, and is headquartered in Menomonee Falls, Wisconsin, The New York Stock Exchange (abbreviated as NYSE), is an American stock exchange, it is by far the world's largest?", "answer": "Actuant", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the sugar-free soft drink which was a later entrant to the diet cola market unveiled ", "answer": "July 8, 1982", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which has more species, Nicandra or Halesia?", "answer": "Halesia", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "For which team did this football player whose description of being a kicker inspired the book \"A Few Seconds of Panic\" play most of his career?", "answer": "the Denver Broncos", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the present executive chairman of the corporation which owns KPIX-TV ? ", "answer": "Leslie Moonves", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Between University of Waterloo and University of Texas at Dallas, which institution offers broader programs involving applicable work experiences?", "answer": "University of Waterloo", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What type of vegetation does Orbeopsis and Hesperaloe have in common?", "answer": "plants", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who was the husband of the Australian model, businesswoman, television host and actress born in 1964?", "answer": "Billy Joel", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who carried out the mission that Operation Thunderbolt is based off of?", "answer": "commandos of the Israel Defense Forces", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the character played by the son of veteran comedians and actors Jerry Stiller and Anne Meara in the film Tower Heist?", "answer": "Josh Kovaks", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which magazine, Seventeen or Gallery,  began as a publication geared towards inspiring teen girls to become model workers and citizens?", "answer": "Seventeen", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Larry King was the former husband of a tennis star that won how many Grand Slam titles?", "answer": "39", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What movie combined the work of English film editor Jake Roberts and director John Crowley?", "answer": "Brooklyn", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which Championship did Krzysztof Soszynski, the mixed martial artist who starred in the 2014 action drama 'Tapped Out', compete?", "answer": "Ultimate Fighting Championship", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The star of Beach Road who did not also direct was born in what year?", "answer": "1931", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What former fighter pilot wrote a series of 16 short stories that were released as a collection in 1979?", "answer": "Roald Dahl", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "All the Year Round was a periodical, a British weekly literary magazine founded and owned by Charles Dickens, of which era is this, in which, the novel was the most important literature?", "answer": "Victorian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which university has more colleges within the school, University of Alabama in Huntsville or University of North Texas?", "answer": "University of North Texas", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "When conference is the team that played the Texas Tech Red Raiders in the 1993 John Hancock Bowl in?", "answer": "Big 12 Conference", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were Margaret Storm Jameson and Joseph Conrad both known for their reviews?