rote the 2011 television drama that Gong Yoo played a role in?", "answer": "Gong Ji-young", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the documentary for which a response documentary 'Fahrenhype 9/11' was created featuring an American lawyer, politician, and reality television arbitrator Ed Koch?", "answer": "Michael Moore", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "St. Cuthbert's Co-operative Society followed the set of ideals first set out in what year?", "answer": "1844", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of American politician and osteopathic physician who was replaced by Sue Donahue's appointment in 2016 to serve in the Arizona State Senate?", "answer": "Kelli Ward", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Rory Elizabeth Katherine Kennedy, is an American documentary filmmaker and youngest child of which U.S. Senator, and Ethel Kennedy, an American human-rights campaigner and widow? ", "answer": "Robert Kennedy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are The La's and Spin Doctors from the same country?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Web of Love starred the actor known for being on comedies on what television network?", "answer": "TVB", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Cleveland Show was co-written by this man, who also was married to Mona Simpson?", "answer": "Richard Appel", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The field hockey player who said \"May Campbell is one of the finest players I have seen, man or woman.\" won how many Olympic gold medals ?", "answer": "three Olympic gold", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Johnny Depp played in a 2005 musical fantasy film which was based on a 1964 children's novel that had a sequel called what?", "answer": "Charlie and the Great Glass Elevator", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of the following is native to Japan and Taiwan: Lopezia or Fatsia?", "answer": "Fatsia", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which catastrophic event in 1876, in Brooklyn, resulted in the death of 278 individuals an