orn in 1975 stars in Stranger Things?", "answer": "David Harbour", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What actor stared in both \"Secondhand Lions\" and a movie based on a book by Brian Cruver?", "answer": "Christian Kane", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How far from the Baltic Sea is Koporye located?", "answer": "Koporye (Russian: \u041a\u043e\u043f\u043e\u0440\u044c\u0435 ; Finnish: \"Kaprio\"; Swedish: \"Koporje\" ) is a historic village (\"selo\") in Leningrad Oblast, Russia, located about 100 km to the west of St. Petersburg and 12 km south of the Koporye Bay of the Baltic Sea", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year did the movie come out that is currently the theme for Disneyland's Submarine Voyage?", "answer": "2003", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which battle did Johan Wijnand van Goor die during the War of the Grand Alliance?", "answer": "Battle of Schellenberg", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which English actor, raconteur, and diarist was featured on the regular cast of Carry On Screaming?", "answer": "Kenneth Williams", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which winner of the European Cup Winner's Cup became a Dutch football manager", "answer": "Marcel \"Marco\" van Basten", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Wen was the mother of Archduchess Caroline Ludovika of Austria died?", "answer": "13 April 1807", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the nationality of the author of the short science fiction novel Rogue Moon?", "answer": "Lithuanian-American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the trail which inspired the Tasmanian Trail originally known as?", "answer": "the National Horse Trail", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which gambling tycoon of South China, that died in 1997, gave funds for the Buddhist Yip Kei Nam Memorial College?", "answer": "Yip Hon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "MedStar Georgetown University Hospital and Providence Hospital, are both what kind of medical organization?", "answer": "Hospital", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which son of Neville Neville retired from football in 2011?", "answer": "Gary Neville", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What formerly known as the American International Building, 60 Wall Tower and originally as the Cities Service Building, 70 Pine Street or 40 Wall Street?", "answer": "70 Pine Street", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What Westlife member didn't participate in the Turnaround Tour?", "answer": "Brian McFadden", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the English actor who was one of the trio with John Gielgud and Ralph Richardson born? ", "answer": "22 May 1907", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What American actor received an Academy Award for his role in \"The Usual Suspects\" and starred in the short film \"Envelope\"?", "answer": "Kevin Spacey", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Fantastic Miss Piggy Show stars what character also performed by Bob Zmuda?", "answer": "Tony Clifton", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"This Could Be Heaven\" by Seal featured in the soundtrack for which film starring Nicolas Cage?", "answer": "The Family Man", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the Barrister of the highest-paid American pianist and singer?", "answer": "Gilbert Hugh Beyfus", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of the following dog breeds was originally bred for hunting deer: Bloodhound or Catahoula Cur?", "answer": "Bloodhound", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who was the university, that Steve Cole taught at, named after? ", "answer": "Thomas Aquinas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which character in the Harry Potter Series was the role of the actor who portrayed Andrew Lehman in the miniseries Ashenden ?", "answer": "Lucius Malfoy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "True Grit is an 2010 American Revisionist Western film, in this version, it stars which American actor, film producer, philanthropist and screenwriter?", "answer": "Matthew Paige Damon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which football club hoste