 of the 2003 American action slasher film written by Damian Shannon and Mark Swift in which the fictional character Alice Johnson appears?", "answer": "Ronny Yu", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the Indian air charter venture which launched non-scheduled commercial flights between Rourkela, Jharsuguda and Bhubaneswar on 2 November 2012?", "answer": "Air Odisha", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year was the current star of Belarusian football born?", "answer": "1981", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Fremontodendron and Mitella both native to the southwestern United States and northwest Mexico?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In which city was the theater Judi Dench got her start with located?", "answer": "London, England", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who replaced the singer in S Club 8 and The Saturdays as a host of The Xtra Factor?", "answer": "Matt Edmondson and Rylan Clark-Neal", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Book of Life filmed in Reel FX Creative Studios released in what year?", "answer": "2014", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jack Savage attended a high school located on which road ?", "answer": "Poplar Level Road", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What city near Space Coast has a population of 11,231 in the 2010 United States Census?", "answer": "Cocoa Beach", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which member of the cast of The Jungle Captive was born in Maryland?", "answer": "Rondo Hatton", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which movie starred more actors, Scandalous John or The Light in the Forest? ", "answer": "The Light in the Forest", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which American author wrote both The Idylls of the Queen, and the \"Frostflower and Thorn\" series?", "answer": "Phyllis Ann Karr", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who formed the band that released the debut album \"The Tide Will Swallow Us Whole\"?", "answer": "Jimmy Ryan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the highest US court that heard both the Marsh v. Chambers and Clinton v. City of New York cases? ", "answer": "Supreme Court of the United States", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Term Life stars an American actress and singer who first became known for her portrayal of what role in True Grit?", "answer": "Mattie Ross", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Korean actress Shin Min-a starred in Oh My Venus and what other television dramas?", "answer": "A Love to Kill", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which noted film director and producer was involved in the production of the medical drama House?", "answer": "Bryan Singer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the American football coach that has coached the Cincinnati Bengals for 11 seasons?", "answer": "Marvin Lewis", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Styal Cottage Homes had foundations laid in 1896 by the politician who was from what party?", "answer": "Conservative", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Dieselpunk is a genre similar to that of its more well-known cousin \"steampunk\" that combines the aesthetics of the diesel-based technology of the interwar period through to the 1950s with retro-futuristic technology and postmodern sensibilities, coined in 2001 by game designer Lewis Pollak to describe which of his role-playing game, created by the now defunct Misguided Games, Inc. in 2002?", "answer": "Children of the Sun", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who has performed more stunts, Rex Ingram or J.A. Steel?", "answer": "J.A. Steel", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What occupant of The Sundrome was based in Indianapolis, Indiana? ", "answer": "ATA Airlines", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which park is located in The Canary Islands, Teide National Park or Ordesa y Monte Perdido National Park?", "answer": "Teide National Park", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "At which theater did the artist described as \"one of the most innovative and stylistically diverse rock musicians of his generation\" play at in Sunrise Florida?", "answer": "Sunrise Musical Theater", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "what does Istv\u00e1n Szab\u00f3 and Metodi Andonov have in common?", "answer": "film", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are Drosanthemum and Gentiana both succulent plants?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Edward Morgan Forster's novel A Room with a View was set in which two countries?", "answer": "Italy and England", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Of which boy band was the headliner for Triangle an original member?", "answer": "TVXQ", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What actor born in 1965 starred in A Glimpse Inside the Mind of Charles Swan III?", "answer": "Charlie Sheen", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which artist did Anthony Toby \"Tony\" Hiller appear with that liked showering himself (and others) with confetti?", "answer": "Charles Elmer \"Rip\" Taylor, Jr.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The director of Lara Croft Tomb Raider: The Cradle of Life also directed what 1994 film starring Keanu Reeves?", "answer": "\"Speed\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Veryan was described as one of Cornwall's loveliest inland villages and as \u2032a mild tropic garden\u2032  by a poet who passed away in what year ?", "answer": "1984", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which director worked in more countries, Robert Butler or Bob Clark? ", "answer": "Benjamin \"Bob\" Clark", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who was the father of the leader of the army that fought the Romans at the Battle of Numistro ? ", "answer": "Hamilcar Barca", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What country is the female equivalent of the only player in history to win five FIFA Ballon d'Or awards from?", "answer": "Argentina", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Liu Yichang, in Cantonese Lau Yee Cheung, a notable writer and novelist in Hong Kong, one of his most notable stream of consciousness novellas \"T\u00eate-b\u00eache\" (\u300a\u5c0d\u5012\u300b) inspires Hong Kong filmmaker W