ork was the novel Tropenwee, which was similar to a novella by Joseph Conrad, about a voyage up what river?", "answer": "Congo River", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What team do Andre Russell and Carlos Brathwaite both play for?", "answer": "West Indies", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which public research university in North Dakota has worked in close connection with Williston State College for most of its history?", "answer": "University of North Dakota", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Margaret Bryan was the Lady Governess to which King of England?", "answer": "Edward VI", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were both \u00c9mile Durkheim and Oliver La Farge French?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What nationality is the cricketer who won the eight team competition in Bangladesh in 2017?", "answer": "Sri Lankan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the role of a German stage and film actress who received a letter of thanks from a German politician and Reich Minister of Propaganda of Nazi Germany from 1933 to 1945?", "answer": "Gerda", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Nuri Bilge Ceylan and Gary T. Smith both directors?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In what year was the drama film in which Dorothy Duffy played Rose / Patricia released?", "answer": "2002", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What style of running also known as 'natural running', practiced in parts of Africa and Latin America was championed by South African and Great British athlete Zola Budd?", "answer": "Barefoot running", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Tekno Team 2000 member was also known for his \"Cowboy\" gimmick in his wrestling career? ", "answer": "Bill Watts", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Greg Tremble won in Super Bowl XXX, beating the Steelers by what score?", "answer": "27\u201317", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The \"Diggers' Song\" was recorded by what British rock band?", "answer": "Chumbawamba", "type": "bridge"