: "24", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Vasyl Slipak won an award for the song from what opera?", "answer": "Carmen", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who resides inside the haunted manor that has the theme song \"Grim Grinning Ghosts\"?", "answer": "\"999 happy haunts\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Animal Music was featured in an American music magazine founded by whom?", "answer": "Mike Shea", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "which city has the highest population Qionghai or Jiangmen", "answer": "Jiangmen", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Cearl is the first Mercian king mentioned by which English monk at the monastery of St. Peter and its companion monastery of St. Paul in the Kingdom of Northumbria of the Angles?", "answer": "Bede", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How far away is Modzrew from Poland\u2019s capital?", "answer": "106 km", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which network owned by the American company Access Media Group is also affiliated with Venture Technologies Group?", "answer": "AMGTV", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who had a role in Survival of Dana and played a character who had a younger sister named Laura?", "answer": "Melissa Sue Anderson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both American Scientist and The Caribbean Pioneer Science magazines?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who created the FX/FXX series that Desmin Borges starred on?", "answer": "Stephen Falk", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Irving Cohen was a character that Martin Short used on \"SCTV\", and brought with him to which TV show?", "answer": "SNL", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The writer of the lyrics for the musical \"Rex\" collaborated with what composer on \"Fiddler on the Roof\"?", "answer": "Jerry Bock", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both Louis Jouvet and Mick Jackson a filmmaker?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Hamskifte used to be in which danish band whose compositions featured in Twilight, Mia