es Representative?", "answer": "Steven Joseph Chabot", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American commander of the Asiatic-Pacific Theater had the nickname \"Tooey\"?", "answer": "Carl Andrew \"Tooey\" Spaatz", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which year was the older football player born out of Mehdi Mahdavikia and Ali Daei? ", "answer": "1969", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Of these two U.S airports, Muskegon County Airport and Fresno Yosemite International Airport, which restored service to Chicago through the Essential Air Service?", "answer": "Muskegon County Airport", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What song that Trey Fanjoy directed a music video for was co-written by Taylor Swift and Liz Rose?", "answer": "\"Picture to Burn\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed  Norwegian action thriller film which s based on Nesb\u00f8's novel \"Hodejegerne (The Headhunters)\".", "answer": "Morten Tyldum", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What company does Avengers: Age of Ultron and Hayley Atwell have in common?", "answer": "Marvel", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American former child actor, television director and film producer who appeared in numerous Disney projects between 1957 and 1963 contributed to the 1960 American short animated comedy film \"Goliath II?\"", "answer": "Kevin Corcoran", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the nationality of the actor who played the voice for a black panther from the Jungle Book", "answer": "Swedish", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of this American professional wrestler, who is well known for his time with the World Wrestling Federation, under the name Crush and with the Group The Disciples of Apocalypse? ", "answer": "Brian Adams", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What type of organisms are the South American Echinopsis and the European and Asian Pulmonaria?", "answer": "plants", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is an incorporated community in the hamlet of Copiague located south of an east\u2013west road extending for 95 mi across the southern shore of Long Island in Suffolk County, New York, sometimes referred to as?", "answer": "Great Neck Landing", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the film inspired by the remake of Sang-ok Shin's Godzilla held in North Korea? Pulgasari", "answer": "Pulgasari", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the Asian American who has coached LeBron James in his professional career in the National Basketball Association?", "answer": "Erik Spoelstra", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Punta Gorda Airport offers numerous flights from the company that has headquarters in what city?", "answer": "Summerlin, Nevada", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What church is in a hamlet that is overlooked by another hamlet near a castle that is 4 mi south-southwest of Montrose?", "answer": "Lunan church", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What 2014 film is the actor who played the lead role of James in 2007 South Korean film \"My Father\" known for starring in?", "answer": "Big Hero 6", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What car functionally serves as the replacement to the longest and heaviest SUV to ever enter mass production?", "answer": "Ford Expedition", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what Florida city did the 2015 Clemson Tigers beat the Oklahoma Sooners 37-17?", "answer": "Miami Gardens", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Fourmile Creek is a tributary of which  fourth-largest lake of the five Great Lakes in North America?", "answer": "Lake Erie", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the international airport in Atlanta into which Shuttle America Corporation, a regional airline based in Indianapolis, fed flights for Delta Airlines?", "answer": "Hartsfield\u2013Jackson Atlanta International Airport", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the winner of the 1972 Daytona 500 born ?", "answer": "January 16, 1935", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who narrated the film a