ch makes use of what symbol which is associated with the concept of empire?", "answer": "Double-headed eagle", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which son of Arnold Schwarzenegger and Maria Shriver stars in coming-of-age thriller \"Go North\"?", "answer": "Patrick Schwarzenegger", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What four-engine turboprop military transport is operated by No. 84 Wing?", "answer": "Lockheed Martin C-130J Super Hercules", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the director of the film where voicing characters was done by James Franco?", "answer": "Mark Osborne", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "George Nassar was the client of which attorney who served as the lawyer in the Sam Sheppard trial?", "answer": "Francis Lee Bailey, Jr.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the grandfather of one of the panelist on \"Pawnography\", as well as the co-owner of a Las-Vegas store?", "answer": "Richard Benjamin Harrison", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Mike Hallett was whitewashed by a professional snooker player who won the World Championship how many times?", "answer": "six", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which musician rose to fame earlier, Micky Dolenz or Jeff Lynne?", "answer": "George Michael Dolenz, Jr.", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which organization is this American professional wrestler and former professional mixed martial artist, professional American football player and amateur wrestler born in 1977, who defended his Ultimate Fighting Championship twice, signed with?", "answer": "WWE", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Vanessa Bayer plays a support role in what Christmas comedy film?", "answer": "Office Christmas Party", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American film actress, director, producer, and writer appeared in \"Lady in the Water\", \"The Villiage\", and Clint Eastwood's film \"Hereafter\"?", "answer": "Bryce Dallas Howard", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which facility was founded at an earlier date, University of Pittsburgh or University of California, San Francisco?", "answer": "University of Pittsburgh", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Among film directors, who was more well-known for horror films, Eric Red or Howard Hughes?", "answer": "Eric Red", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "KerPlunk and Ludo, are both which type of items?", "answer": "games", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Mongolia at the 2002 Asian Games clinched the 26th spot in this multi sport event held where?", "answer": "Busan, South Korea", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "James F. Bowman served on a newpaper in a city with a census estimated population of what in 2016?", "answer": "870,887", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What kinds of citizenship does star of Kill Switch have?", "answer": "American, Russian, and Serbian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the Republican challenger when former Secretary of State Hillary Clinton was elected to the senate in 2006?", "answer": "John Spencer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what city and country are the Sinan Erdem Dome and Molla \u00c7elebi Mosque located?", "answer": "Istanbul, Turkey.", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": " \"Bye Bye I Love You\" was the Luxembourgish entry in the Eurovision Song Contest, in which year, the song is notable in the history of the Contest; it was the very first entry composed by Eurovision veteran Ralph Siegel, who would go on write 19 ESC entries throughout the 1970s, 1980s, 1990s and 2000s, 1 for Switzerland, that participated in the Eurovision Song Contest 58 times?", "answer": "1974", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Dave Dennis was one of the organizers of the events that were launched in what month?", "answer": "June 1964", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the population in 2010 of the area where Terry-Ketcham Inn is located ?", "answer": "7,580", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The company that owns and operates Sands Macao also has an art and science museum in what city?"