rector", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Daran Norris provided voices in which television series created by Butch Hartman?", "answer": "The Fairly OddParents", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born first, Shagrath or Seohyun?", "answer": "Stian Thoresen", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are both Kenai Municipal Airport and North Central West Virginia Airport joint-use public and military airports?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "how is Keep It Natural and Lou Pearlman connected?", "answer": "band", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Swedes' Landing is the warehouse road found along the Minquas Kill in Wilmington, Delaware, where the New Sweden colony in 1638, was founded by whom?", "answer": "Peter Minuit", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the upcoming Marvel film in which Divian Ladwa appears ?", "answer": "Peyton Reed", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Rainer Widmayer came after which player born in 1972 as manager of Hertha BSC?", "answer": "Markus Babbel", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Saying Grace by Normal Rockwell was painted for the cover of a magainze that was published weekly during what time period?", "answer": "1897 until 1963", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which year was this Austrian business magnate, engineer and executive whom Hans Dieter P\u00f6tsch succeeded as chairman of the supervisory board of Volkswagen born?", "answer": "1937", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the final movie released by Universal Studios in their series of sex comedy films?", "answer": "American Reunion", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Diego Raymond De Girolamo, is a professional footballer who plays as a forward for League Two club Chesterfield, on loan from which organization, that's the highest division of the English Football League and second-highest overall in which football league system, after the Premier League?", "answer": "English", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Bertha von Suttner, the second woman to win the Nobel Peace, was awarded after which other female scientist who won in 1903?", "answer": "Marie Curie", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which film, 16 Days in Afghanistan or A Year and a Half in the Life of Metallica was produced by Juliana Roberts and directed by Adam Dubin?", "answer": "A Year and a Half in the Life of Metallica", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Brendan Hunt had voicing duties for two characters in what 2015 Bethesda Game Studios game?", "answer": "Fallout 4", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What band which means 'good winter' played at the Eaux Claires?", "answer": "Bon Iver", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both  Knut Hamsun and Harry Crosby Norwegian?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "When was the American actress born who is a star in both Mad Men and Flowers in the Attic?", "answer": "November 10, 1999", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which team did Tyson Gay and Rodney Martin both run for?", "answer": "Olympic Team", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A tour puzzle is a puzzle in which the player travels around a board, using a token which represents a character, which type of puzzles are often which term used for a path or collection of paths, typically from an entrance to a goal?", "answer": "Maze", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Chanur novels is a series of five science fiction novels, forming three separate stories, written by American author C. J. Cherryh, an American writer of speculative fiction, and published by which organization? ", "answer": "DAW Books", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Godzilla starred the American voice actor who was known for starring in what television sitcom?", "answer": "The Simpsons", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "SlamNation and Super Size Me are both what type of film?", "answer": "documentary film", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "\"Amusement Today\" won the Impact Award in the services category for \"Best New Product\" from the Internati