anager of what team?", "answer": "the New York Rangers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Dr. Giggles is a 1992 horror film starring a comedian known as Benny Stulwicz in what?", "answer": "L.A. Law", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What kind of music is the song \"Nothing Is Keeping You Here\"?", "answer": "pop", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born first, Adam Darski or Robb Flynn?", "answer": "Robert Conrad \"Robb\" Flynn", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the name of the place in the Town of Huntington which has the Harry E Donnell House, a 33 room Tudor mansion?", "answer": "Eatons Neck", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Fernando Francisco Gonz\u00e1lez Ciuffardi played his only major final in 2007 losing to a Swiss professional tennis player who has won 19 what?", "answer": "Grand Slam singles titles", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Monastic Living is an EP by the American indie rock band Parquet Courts, an American rock band formed in what year", "answer": "2010", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the occupation of the Baron Archer of Weston-super-Mare's son?", "answer": "stock market trader", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Philadelphia Stars were part of a United States professional baseball league that was comprised of teams predominantly made up of African Americans, but that also included who?", "answer": "Latin Americans", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which film stars Drew Barrymore and Jimmy Fallon and is written by brothers that are 2 years apart in age?", "answer": "Fever Pitch", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed Park Gun-hyung in a 2005 South Korean film?", "answer": "Park Young-hoon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who organized the beauty pageant at which Hoyan Mok was the winner in 1993 ? ", "answer": "TVB", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Supreme Commander of the Irish Defence Forces' father was executed by the nascent Irish Free State?", "answer": "Erskine Hamilton Childers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What two states does the mountain range directly to the east of Krell Hill border?", "answer": "Montana and Idaho", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What technical director of FC St. Pauli was seriously injured in a foul in 1981?", "answer": "Ewald Lienen", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Is Baylor University or Istanbul Technical University closer to the capital of the United States?", "answer": "Baylor University", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What country does Pio La Torre and Palermo have in common?", "answer": "Italy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Elia Suleiman and Wilson Yip from the same country?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What Lexington university did Luke P. Blackburn earn a medical degree at?", "answer": "Transylvania University", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which tennis star is from Zimbabwe, Wayne Black or Andr\u00e9s G\u00f3mez?", "answer": "Wayne Hamilton Black", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which game, Rummoli or CirKis, is a piece placing board game, for two to four players, invented by Phil E. Orbanes and developed by Winning Moves Games USA in 2009?", "answer": "CirKis", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which former Governor of Georgia Sonny Purdue replaced Mike Young in which cabinet office in April 2017?", "answer": "United States Secretary of Agriculture", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which director is from a country closer to New Zealand, Gillian Armstrong or Pierre Morel?", "answer": "Gillian May Armstrong", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Water passes east via Nubanusit Brook to this River and flows in a northward direction?", "answer": "Contoocook River", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is an Italian politician and has the European Union Special Representatives report to her?", "answer": "Federica Mogherini", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both Jinghong and Qiongshan District of the same administrative level?", "answer": "no", "type": 