s of Carthage or The Carthage Eagles)\"? ", "answer": "Rachid Turki", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of this Australian generation, electricity and gas retailing private company that is owned by Hong Kong-based Chow Tai Fook Enterprises and operated and maintained the Northern Power Station in Port Augusta? ", "answer": "Alinta Energy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Harold Young and Jerry Belson both directors?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which plant grows in a specific region, Dendromecon or Aulax? ", "answer": "Dendromecon", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What do Tim Kaine and Aneesh Chopra have in common?", "answer": "American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Leandro Firmino played the role of Thiago in \"Trash\" alongside the actress who had a breakout role in which 2009 film?", "answer": "Tanner Hall", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born first, Byambasuren Davaa or Richard Attenborough?", "answer": "Richard Samuel Attenborough", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What name of a Canadian rock band formed in 1995 in Hanna, Alberta, Canada for which Robert John \"Mutt\" produced albums for? ", "answer": "Nickelback", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which contains rum, Sea Breeze or The Goldeneye?", "answer": "The Goldeneye", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The actress that voices the character Bart Simpson starred in what 1982 film directed by Robert Day?", "answer": "Marian Rose White", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What county town of 26,000 does the A414 road run through?", "answer": "Hertford", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who won a Gemini Award in 2008 and was star of the Canadian comedy The Indian Detective?", "answer": "Russell Peters", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the top three pick of the 1992 draft that played most of his career for the Miami Heat?", "answer": "Alonzo Mourning", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What single for \"Home\", a 2015 animation film based on the 2007 children book \"The True Meaning of Smekday\",  was recorded by Barbadian singer Rihanna?", "answer": "Towards the Sun", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Dave Rayner shares the record for most NFL teams played for with the placekicker who played for what college?", "answer": "Drake University", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In May 2010 the Portland Farmers Market was named one of the ten best farmers markets in the US by a magainze that has how many readers?", "answer": "4.8 million", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which county in Florida is the third-most populous and is north of Deerfield Beach?", "answer": "Palm Beach County", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In between Best Friend Forgotten and I.O.U.S.A. and which ones director was Patrick Creadon?", "answer": "I.O.U.S.A.", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Neptunes are a two-member producing group consisting of Pharrell Williams, and who?", "answer": "Chad Hugo", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the famous last line in the speech about the war guilt of the Germans published by G\u00fcnther Ruprecht?", "answer": "Then they came for me-and there was no one left to speak for me", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The castle that was the Seat of the Culdares line was owned by what person from the 1920s until the 1950s? ", "answer": "Sir Ernest Wills", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"The One Hundredth\" (also known as \"The One With The Triplets\") is the third episode of \"Friends\"' fifth season, Rachel was played by which American actress, producer, and businesswoman, and the daughter of Greek-born actor John Aniston and American actress Nancy Dow?", "answer": "Jennifer Joanna Aniston", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which route crosses the town of Bethany besides the one that is a part of the U.S. Highway System that runs from Newport, Oregon, to Boston, Massachusetts?", "answer": "NYS Route 63", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "This compilation album contains 28 songs spanning from a debut album that was released on October 11, 1994, through what label?", "answer": "Immortal/Epic Records", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Amber Gray was in what 2016 Off-Broadway musical written by Anais Mitchell?", "answer": "Hadestown", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Cantopop group is the lead actress in the movie Calling For Love in?", "answer": "Twins", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 1990 Detroit Tigers season saw the record broken of \"The Hebrew Hammer\" by whom?", "answer": "Cecil Fielder", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Daniel Th\u00fcrer is a member of a humanitarian institution based in what country?", "answer": "Switzerland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which cinder cone volcano located in the Mexican state of Michoac\u00e1n is part of the scenes of Captain from Castile ", "answer": "Par\u00edcutin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What type of university did Julius C. Holmes attend?", "answer": "a public research university", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which epic poem was \"Ave Maria\" loosely based on, which is used by Wilfred Jackson in Walt Disney's \"Fantasia\"?", "answer": "The Lady of the Lake", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Michelle Gomez is known for her comedy role in a British sitcom produced by Tiger Aspect Productions for who?", "answer": "BBC Three", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which actor lived longer, Edward F. Cline or Tom Forman?", "answer": "Edward Francis Cline", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Viken Babikian and John Najarian, both work as which mutual location?", "answer": "University", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Robert Nardelli was succeeded as CEO by Frank Blake in 2007 after being named as one of the \"Worst American CEOs of All Time,\" at which retailer?", "answer": "Home Depot", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What episode was broadcast on BBC One on 12 April 2008 and starred an actress who would later play Nellie Bertram in the U.S. version of \"The Office?\"", "answer": "The Fires of Pompeii", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where are the majority of members of the conference that the Hilltoppers are in from?", "answer": "Texas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the ice resurfacer that Sobotka is mostly known for driving?", "answer": "Zamboni", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Patty Jenkins is known for directing \"Wonder Woman\" and this film, based in the life of serial killer and former prostitute Aileen Wuornos?", "answer": "\"Monster\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The meters in which  Zhang Yingying qualified forAt only 18 years  is one of the track event for which game", "answer": "Olympic Games", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the population of the North Woodmere's hamlet section?", "answer": "5,962", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which band is based in Los Angeles, Anberlin or That Dog?", "answer": "That Dog", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Last Dragon, is a 1985 martial arts film produced by Rupert Hitzig for Berry Gordy, an American record producer and songwriter, and is best known as the founder of which record label?", "answer": "Motown", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What female representative of Minnesota's 6th Congressional District has New Yorker columnist Ryan Lizza written a profile of?", "answer": "Michele Bachmann,", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In 1964, The Statler Brothers began singing backup for a singer born in what year?", "answer": "1932", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What film was written by Katherine Fugate, Abby Kohn and Marc Silverstein and was directed by Garry Marshall?", "answer": "Valentine's Day", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Hocking Canal and Shinnecock Canal were both used in what century?", "answer": "19th century", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Were Anadoluhisar\u0131 and G\u00fcl Mosque in Istanbul both constructed by the Ottomans?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the french name for a river that crosses a territory in maine with a population of 10?", "answer": "Grande Rivi\u00e8re Noire", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the third stadium used by the football team for the Portuguese sports club in Porto demolished?", "answer": "2004", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "C. S. Lewis and Arthur Koestler, share with nationality?", "answer": "British", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "When was the company that sponsors the Tuborg Stage Image Awards founded?", "answer": "1873", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the middle name of the man who starred alongside Jane Alexander in \"Welcome Home, Johnny Bristol\"?", "answer": "James", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who produced the album \"Loud\" by Rihanna?", "answer": "Rihanna was the executive producer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was the defending Drivers' Champion in 2015\u201316 Formula E season born?", "answer": "Heidelberg, West Germany", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Tim Tadlock, born 21 December 1968 in which city in Texas, is a collegiate baseball coach and former player, He served as head coach of the Texas Tech Red Raiders, representing Texas Tech University, from 2013 \u2013 present, The Texas Tech Red Raiders baseball team represents Texas Tech University in NCAA Division I college baseball?", "answer": "Denton", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which fifth studio album by American singer Lady Gaga was newer material part ", "answer": "Joanne", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of a Raggedy Ann doll that has been compared to Robert the Doll which is alleged to be cursed?", "answer": "Annabelle", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What team did the Bristol Rovers play against in the game which promoted them from the Conference Premier?", "answer": "Grimsby Town", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Uncharted 3: Drake's Deception is an action-adventure video game developed by Naughty Dog, the plot draws from the archaeology days of