ure", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What producer and political activist co-founded a production company with Bud Yorkin?", "answer": "Norman Lear", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the middle name of the fictional character, who used characters called spock and McCoy as his logical and emotional springboard, and who was captain of the starship USS Enterprise in an American Science fiction franchise which included an episode called Space Seed where the crew discover a sleeper ship holding superpeople from Earth's past? ", "answer": "Tiberius", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which city was the film actress, who held German and French citizenship, and starred in the comedy film 'Kitty and the Great Big World', born? ", "answer": "Vienna", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Meredith Gentry is the protagonist of a fantasy series by an American fantasy writer who was born in 1963, and is also what type of writer?", "answer": "romance", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year did Ocean Park Hong Kong,a marine mammal park, oceanarium, animal theme park and amusement park situated in Wong Chuk Hang and Nam Long Shan in the Southern District of Hong Kong, change its Ocean Park Halloween Bash to  All-Day-and-Night Halloween Celebration?", "answer": "2013", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The actor who founded a production company and best known for his roles in \"Places in the Heart\" and \"In the Line of Fire\" received what?", "answer": "Academy Award nominations", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Lamborghini model is the most expensive model that is a two-door, two-seater with a V10 high-performance engine?", "answer": "Lamborghini Sesto Elemento", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where did the proposed Maryland team that was meant to be owned by the same person owning Manchester United and the Tampa Bay Buccanneers get its proposed name?", "answer": "B-26 Marauder", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the console, for which the game Tench: Fatal Shadows was made, released in Japan?", "answer": "March 4, 2000", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Jacob Hoggard and Lee Sung-min singers?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who won the championship the same year that Sevilla F\u00fatbol Club failed to qualify for European competition?", "answer": "Valencia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which movie had Kris Marshall in it and was directed by Richard Curtis?", "answer": "Love Actually", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Leura railway station is located on the Main Western line in New South Wales, it serves the Blue Mountains town of Leura, opening on which date?", "answer": "6 December 1890", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "John Will completed his blackbelt under one of these men, a brother renowned for his BJJ skills?", "answer": "Jean Jacques Machado", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Albert S. Rogell and Michael Lembeck related?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Olaf Stapledon and Maurice Maeterlinck, are British?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The architect of Albany's United Traction Company Building was born in what city?", "answer": "Great Barrington, Massachusetts", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who has more albums, Gerard Way or The Calling?", "answer": "The Calling", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What year was the song that was the lead single in the Paramore album that is compared to the likes of Kelly Clarkson and Avril Lavigne released?", "answer": "2007", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which film, When I Came Home or The Queens of Comedy, won the \"New York Loves Film Best Documentary\" award in 2006?", "answer": "When I Came Home", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "How many rooms has the hotel which hosted EVO2014 ?", "answer": "2,956", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the birthdate of this American writer and political activist who became an early leader of the Black Panther Party and for whom Max