rican film maker is an Iraq War veteran, Chris Mandia or Bryan Singer?", "answer": "Chris Mandia", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which star of Pitch Perfect was born on July 31, 1989 ?", "answer": "Alexis Knapp", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which film is older, \"The Seafarers\" or \"Go Further\"?", "answer": "The Seafarers", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "An American voice actress and actress who had a distinctive speaking style starred what title character in Cartoon Network's comic science fiction animated television series created by Genndy Tartakovsky ?", "answer": "Chuckie Finster", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What do Joyce Cary and James M. Cain have in common?", "answer": "author", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is a science fiction role-playing game produced by TSR beginning in 1982, that was worked on by Tom Moldvay ?", "answer": "Star Frontiers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Moorish Barracks are located in the peninsula named after whom?", "answer": "Lawrence of Rome", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Mutants in Orbit is a role-playing game authored by which British designer/publisher? ", "answer": "James Wallis", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which producer also wrote scripts, Frank Lloyd of Doug Liman?", "answer": "Frank William George Lloyd", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In the film \"The Godfather\", Salvatore Tessio was portrayed by an actor born in which year ?", "answer": "1921", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Chief Executive of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region served between 2012 and 2017?", "answer": "Leung Chun-ying", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which university has a mascot that is a horned frog: Texas Christian University or Emory University?", "answer": "Texas Christian University", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "\"Should've Said No\" was a song release by what record company?", "answer": "Big Machine Records", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The actor that played Andy Dufresne in \"The Shawshank Redemption\" stars with Sean Penn in a 2003 drama film directed by who?", "answer": "Clint Eastwood", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were Summer Wars and Eleanor's Secret released in the same year?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which singer was born earlier, Warrel Dane or Grace Slick?", "answer": "Grace Barnett Slick", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Lower Swineshaw Reservoir is operated by which largest listed water company in the UK?", "answer": "United Utilities", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What animation division was tasked for production feature length animated film worked with Tor Seidler's books?", "answer": "Twentieth Century Fox Animation", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Do Vector and Cage9 both feature Panamanian members?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Earth, Wind & Fire were kept off of the Number One spot on the Billboard Hot 100 by \"My Sharona\", by which band?", "answer": "The Knack", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Paulino Uzcudun and  Max Schmeling both fought which boxer?", "answer": "Joe Louis", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the 1989 song which reached No. 13 on the UK Singles Chart, and written by the English singer-songwriter, guitarist, keyboardist, producer, remixer, and DJ also known for writing hits such as \"Enjoy the Silence\", \"Stripped\", \"It's No Good\", \"In Your Room\", \"Strangelove\", \"I Feel You\", \"People Are People\", \"Precious\", \"A Question of Time\", \"Policy of Truth\", \"Everything Counts\", \"Behind the Wheel\", \"Shake the Disease\", \"Never Let Me Down Again\", and many more? ", "answer": "Personal Jesus", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the top scoring striker for the Watfor 2007-08 season sold?", "answer": "January 2008", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where were the band formed who recorded the song, In the Street, for their 1972 album ?", "answer": "Memphis, Tennessee,", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What TV show did Stephen Glover write that was renewed for a second season?", "answer": "Atlanta", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year did the cosmonaut that manned Vostok 4 die?", "answer": "2009", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What publication does Atlantic Media produce whose audience consists of high-ranking civilian and military officials?", "answer": "Government Executive", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which university has more than one campus, University of Southern Denmark or Purbanchal University?", "answer": "University of Southern Denmark", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What actor stared in a film directed by Mark L. Lester?", "answer": "Drew Snyder", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\u02bbIolani Palace was the royal residence of Hawaii beginning with which king who ruled from 1825 to 1854?", "answer": "Kamehameha III", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What type of forest can be found only eastern/central China in this area of of the United States once represented by Ohio General Assembly member Oakley C. Collins?", "answer": "mixed-mesophytic forest", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The birth city of  Ad Moolhuijzen is home to what zoo?", "answer": "Royal Burgers' Zoo", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the signing policy for Athletic Club Femenino players?", "answer": "only sign players who were born in the Basque Country, or who learned their football skills at a Basque club.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the population of the small town and civil parish where Bernie Calvert was born?", "answer": "8,200", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both Matty Mullins and Wayne Coyne from the same band?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who allied with the Pecheneg prince who appears as a villain in a 2006 Russian traditionally-animated feature film loosely based on the story of prince Vladimir the Fair Sun?", "answer": "Svyatoslav I of Kiev", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What nationality is the musician who produced the song Have You Ever by Brandy Norwood ?", "answer": "Canadian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who developed the series on which Zabryna Guevara played Sarah Essen?", "answer": "Bruno Heller", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Georges Bataille and David Lodge from the same country?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Wickedly Welsh Chocolate is sold at what Pembrokeshire attraction?", "answer": "Oakwood Theme Park", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "U.S. Route 4 (US 4) is a part of the U.S. Highway System that runs from East Greenbush, is a town in Rensselaer County, New York, in which country?", "answer": "United States", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Let My Burden Be\", featured the talents of harpist, pianist, vocalist, and lyricist Joanna Newsom, is the first album by the group Golden Shoulders, which was formed in what city?", "answer": "Nevada City, California", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What general type of band are Ra Ra Riot and Mother Goose?", "answer": "rock band", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The third-largest city in Mongolia is 60 km to the southwest of what monastery?", "answer": "Amarbayasgalant Monastery", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ernie Watkins made appearances for which football club based out of Bermondsey?", "answer": "Millwall Football Club", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which documentary was released first, Olympia or The Punk Singer?", "answer": "Olympia", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Philippe de Chauveron directed what French comedy film released in 2014?", "answer": "Serial (Bad) Weddings", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When I pray for You was recorded for the soundtrack of what 1917 American Christian drama film that was directed by Stuart Hazeldine?", "answer": "The Shack", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Narakasuravadham is an Aattakatha authored by a maharajah that was born in what year?", "answer": "1724", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Atticus is named after the characted from the book published in what year?", "answer": "1960", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Roger Claessen played 17 times with a national team that plays most of their home games at what stadium?", "answer": "King Baudouin Stadium", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the film in which the soundtrack was the first solo album by a member of the Beatles?", "answer": "Joe Massot", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What ethnicity are both Steve Keiner and the National Baseball Hall of Fame and Museum?", "answer": "American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The largest gift of private land ever given to a government in South America was donated by the a family closely connected to which outdoor gear company?", "answer": "Patagonia, Inc.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the  American actress of stage, screen, and television who starred in The Tiger Makes Out born? ", "answer": "September 3, 1925", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "On the  American reality competition Under the Gunn, singer Zendaya appear as a guest judge with what other single name singer?", "answer": "Macklemore", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "American actress, model and singer, Angelica Bridges, was trained by Robert Chapin, who is also known for creating what for the film \"American Beauty\"?", "answer": "visual effects", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which album did Scott Hendricks produce that was also featured on \"The Angry Birds Movie: Original Motion Picture Soundtrack\"?", "answer": "If I'm Honest", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Oslo based Norwegian singer-songwriter was featured in the fourth studio album by American rapper Tyler, the creator?", "answer": "Anna of the North", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which German professional racing driver won the 2015 24 Hours of Le Mans along with Earl Bamber and Nick Tandy?", "answer": "Nico H\u00fclkenberg", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the 2017 film David Scarpa wrote the screenplay for?", "answer": "Ridley Scott", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What actor starred in The Man in the Iron Mask and  \"Romeo + Juliet\"?", "answer": "Leonardo DiCaprio", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which director was born first, Lothar Mendes or Baz Luhrmann?", "answer": "Lothar Mendes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What prefecture-level city has its administrative center located at Hailar District, Qingyang or Hulunbuir?", "answer": "Hulunbuir", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What episode of South Park, aired on April 21, 2010, started the \"Draw Mohammed Day\" event? ", "answer": "201", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What corporation was founded by an American inventor and businessman who sponsored a program through the end of June 1946 when it failed to find a larger audience?", "answer": "Lear Jet Corporation", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the town, formerly known as Webster, that currently has the Regional School Unit 4 as the district headquarters?", "answer": "Sabattus", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What type of media does Lion and Rooney Mara have in common?", "answer": "film", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In 2001, Six Flags bought the theme park that was adjacent to Six Flags Ohio. What year did this originally open?", "answer": "1970", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was an Italian-American composer and librettist, Anton\u00edn Dvo\u0159\u00e1k or Gian Carlo Menotti ?", "answer": "Gian Carlo Menotti", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What style of karate was featured in the movie where Ralph Macchio portrayed Daniel LaRusso?", "answer": "G\u014dj\u016b-ry\u016b", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"These Are the Times\" is the second single released from the second album of Dru Hill, an American singing group, most popular when?", "answer": "late 1990s", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the origin of the conductor of Where are You, my Brothers?", "answer": "Armenian and Russian descent.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The producer of the single by American rappers Dr. Dre and Eminem is from where? ", "answer": "Wood Green, London", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What type of media does John Boorman and Janez Lapajne have in common?", "answer": "film", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Max Neukirchner currently competes on a sports bike that has been manufactured since what year?", "answer": "1998", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the Republican Senator of Mississippi that has been in office since 2007, who in 2013 was a letter addressed to that contained ricin?", "answer": "Roger Wicker", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Orlando Maturana made several appearances for the senior Colombia national football team, his success in the national team was hampered by the availability of several more successful strikers such as which Colombian retired footballer who played as a striker?", "answer": "Adolfo Jos\u00e9 Valencia Mosquera", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where does the Crown Princess of Norway who was born in 1973 officially reside?", "answer": "Skaugum", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "We're both Myles Kennedy and Buffalo Tom American?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Im Si-wan starred in the 8th best-selling Korean film of all time in 2013 and which cable series in 2014?", "answer": "Misaeng", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which magazine is published more times each year, Soccer America or Reader's Digest?", "answer": "Reader's Digest", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who was dubbed the father of the type of rock music that emerged from post-punk in the late 1970s?", "answer": "Brian Healy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which college located in Northfield, Minnesota, United States provides employment to Professor Anantanand Rambachan as a Professor of Religion?", "answer": "St. Olaf College", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The-Dream's co-writing credits include a song from Beyonce that explores men's unwillingness to propose or commit, and was on what album?", "answer": "I Am... Sasha Fierce", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "ZeniMax Media Inc. is an American media company, The company is known for owning Arkane Studios, developer of Prey is a first-person shooter video game, published by which organization?", "answer": "Bethesda Softworks", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "when was the Austro-Daimler Sascha designer born?", "answer": "3 September 1875", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "John Weaver created three busts of which US fleet admiral?", "answer": "Chester William Nimitz, Sr.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which is formed by more people, Relient K or Gotye?", "answer": "Relient K", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "How long did a series of 6 erotic feature films run after being ushered in by the 1965 Danish coming-of-age sex comedy;Sytten?", "answer": "from 1973\u201378", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which actor is American, G\u00e9za von Bolv\u00e1ry or Michael Gordon?", "answer": "Michael Gordon", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Black Earth is a book by a historian and a member of what council?", "answer": "Council on Foreign Relations", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Vafa\u2013Witten theorem is named after Cumrun Vafa and another person who is a professor at what school?", "answer": "Institute for Advanced Study", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Treklanta (formerly \"TrekTrax Atlanta\") is an annual convention for what American science fiction media franchise?", "answer": "Star Trek", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the Give Us a Clue host from 1984 to 1992 born?", "answer": "1935", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American Negro league baseball player called Chino Smith one of the two most dangerous hitters in Negro league history?", "answer": "Satchel Paige", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Melina Matsoukas won a Grammy for her work on a music 