icks was hosted by the Privy Councillor of which party?", "answer": "Conservative Party", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "At what school did the \"Poker Face\" singer and Noritaka Tatehana shoe owner study in New York?", "answer": "Tisch School of the Arts", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where does the Canadian-American actor and comedian born in 1950 own cottages?", "answer": "Lake Rosseau", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Mason Moon Moorhouse has been a model for a global fashion brand founded in what year?", "answer": "1965", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Islamabad United is a franchise owned by what sports affiliate that is focused on promoting sports through out Asia?", "answer": "Leonine Global Sports", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Sigma Films co-produced which Danish film that stars Nikolaj Lie Kaas, Connie Nielsen and Ulrich Thomsen?", "answer": "Brothers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is the castle located that Daniel S. Pena Sr currently resides in?", "answer": "Angus, Scotland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is from farther north, Heather Nova or The Delgados?", "answer": "The Delgados", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which author is from Israel, Yehuda Amichai or Iris Rainer Dart?", "answer": "Yehuda Amichai", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who was the producer of the series of political theatrical adventure mystery films in which the father of actress Angelina Jolie starred? ", "answer": "Jerry Bruckheimer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "the town of Kstovo is 22 km southeast of a city that is the capital of which federal district ?", "answer": "Volga Federal District", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Toyota GZ engine is used as the powerplant for what  large four-door limousine produced mainly for the Japanese market?", "answer": "Toyota Century", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What artist was born in 1948 that was featured on the record label Bigger Picture Music Group?", "answer": "Alice Cooper", "typ