The 2015\u201316 Xavier Musketeers women's basketball team represented Xavier University during the 2015\u201316 NCAA Division I women's basketball season, they were third year members of the newly reorganized Big East Conference, a collegiate athletic conference that competes in NCAA Division I in all sports except football, and has been officially recognized as a Division I multi-sport conference, effective on which date?", "answer": "August 1, 2013", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What occupation do American Stephen Sommers and Italian Duccio Tessari share?", "answer": "screenwriter", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What direct-to-films series features Batman: The Killing Joke?", "answer": "DC Universe Animated Original Movies", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year did the New Brunswick band that Mike Crossey has produced records for form?", "answer": "2006", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Australian opera and musical theatre performer classically trained lyric baritone was featured in the video \"The Main Event?\"", "answer": "Anthony Warlow", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the large village situated bewteen Scunthorpe and Gainsborough that is near to the village of Scotton?", "answer": "Scotter", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where in Iowa's second largest city was an Ultimate Fighting Championship held?", "answer": "Five Seasons Events Center", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the mother of Karigaila born?", "answer": "1325", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "how is Fukang and Xuanwei related?", "answer": "China", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "One of the first African Americans to host a national television variety show also performed what best-known composition from Peter van Steeden?", "answer": "Home (When Shadows Fall)", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year did 21st Century Fox begin selling beer originally created by the producer of \"The Simpsons\"? ", "answer": "2015", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "King Lear is a tragedy written by William Shakespeare, which term designation is given to most tragedies, written by playwright William Shakespeare?", "answer": "Shakespearean tragedy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which \"Saturday Night Live\" actress, who won an award for her work in \"Other People\", played the character Mary Katherine Gallagher?", "answer": "Molly Helen Shannon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Marshallian demand function was named after an economist known as one of the founders of what?", "answer": "neoclassical economics", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which is a flowering plant, Syagrus or Ecballium?", "answer": "Ecballium", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the collaborational pen name of the Russian poet on whose novel \"The Night of Devils\" is loosely based on?", "answer": "Kozma Prutkov", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Pepe\" was attempting to replicate Cantiflas' success from a movie produced by whom?", "answer": "Michael Todd Company", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which company, headed by Thomas Tull, produced the 2013 film that was the first installment in the DC Extended Universe?", "answer": "Legendary Entertainment", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "American pop rock band Fun Was formed by this Former lead singer of the The Format who also started performing as a solo musician in this year?", "answer": "2015", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of the following received two Academy Awards: Jerome Robbins or Michael Curtiz?", "answer": "Jerome Robbins", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who is the sister of Jenn productions Jennifer Graziano and is also a television personality from the shows, \"Mob Wives\" and \"Celebrity Big Brother\"?", "answer": "Renee Graziano", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Name the American football quarterback for the Dallas Cowboys who played college football for the Mississippi State Bulldogs and who was one of the ten finalists in the N