hotography", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "John Cabot had a first landing site of the province that blocks the mouth of what river?", "answer": "Saint Lawrence", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What company created the Bushmaster IV?", "answer": "Alliant Techsystems", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What are two of the trade names of the medication designed, synthesized, and patented by Indian-born American organic chemist and pharmacologist Nariman Bomanshaw Mehta?", "answer": "Wellbutrin and Zyban", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Glen of Imaal Terrier and Appenzeller Sennenhund, are a breed of what?", "answer": "dog", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who was born first, Rowan Atkinson, or Maxim Baldry?", "answer": "Rowan Sebastian Atkinson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the dark wizard in the fantasy series by Joanne Rowling?", "answer": "Lord Voldemort", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Phillies were early contenders for the Wild Card but were unable to overcome injuries to players such as the eight time winner of what?", "answer": "Gold Glove", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Abdellah Bidane, also known as Abdellah Bidar, is a Moroccan football defender who played for Morocco in which tournament, held in Mexico from 31 May to 29 June 1986?", "answer": "1986 FIFA World Cup", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was one of the creators of Teletubbies born?", "answer": "1937", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What occupation do both Michael Jones and Maher Sabry share?", "answer": "film director", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Army Man (tagline: \"America's Only Magazine\") was a short-lived comedy what published in the late 1980s by George A. Meyer, an acclaimed writer for \"The Simpsons\", and American producer?", "answer": "magazine", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Man Who Cried is a film that starred the actor who was in what 1998 film?", "answer": "The Big Lebowski", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": 