y cars produced by what company?", "answer": "Mattel", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Name the date of birth of one of the stars of Foolproof.", "answer": "2 May 1946", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What album was produced by Don Gehman and contains one of R.E.M.'s earliest environmentally conscious songs?", "answer": "Lifes Rich Pageant", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 1979 book by French philosopher Catherine Cl\u00e9ment, Opera: The Undoing of Women, explores this opera in five acts that premiered at the Op\u00e9ra-Comique in the early 1900 and was conducted by which conductor?", "answer": "Andr\u00e9 Messager", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "B\u00fcck dich and Du hast are both songs from what Neue Deutsche H\u00e4rte band Rammstein album?", "answer": "\"Sehnsucht\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both a Whisky Mac and a Black Russian made with vodka?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Toynbee Convector is a short story collection by American writer Ray Bradbury, some of the stories that originally appeared in which men's magazine published by Magna Publishing Group?", "answer": "Gallery", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The statue of Tlaloc resides in a museum located in the area between what streets in Mexico City?", "answer": "Paseo de la Reforma and Mahatma Gandhi Street", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Both Arthur C. Clarke and Jean Rhys are known for what profession?", "answer": "novelist", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the population of a city where Rockhampton Airport has direct flights to ", "answer": "2.4 million", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who won the qualifying event for the competition that will be held in 2018 in Barranquilla, Colombia?", "answer": "United States", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which director is American, Jorge Olgu\u00edn or Philip Kaufman?", "answer": "Philip Kaufman", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which airport is closer to its central business district, Mercedita Airport or MidAmerica St. Louis Airport?", "answer": "Mercedita Airport", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What team, part of the Big 12 Conference of NCAA Division I, was Gary Hudson the coach of?", "answer": "Oklahoma Sooners women's basketball", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where did the band that created the song \"Extra Ordinary\" get formed?", "answer": "Baton Rouge, Louisiana", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Cooper MacNeil is a racing driver who operates a car under the high performance division of what company?", "answer": "Mercedes-Benz", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which company operate the railway station which was near Wrawby Junction that was part of Trent, Ancholme and Grimsby Railway?", "answer": "TransPennine Express", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " What was the Team that Robert Wilson played for that was based in Rotherham, South Yorkshire?", "answer": "Rotherham United Football Club", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Guy Carawan served as what at the school secondarily known as Highlander Folk School?", "answer": "music director and song leader", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is that actor that hosted Last Hero 4:End Game?", "answer": "Aleksandr Domogarov", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which is longer, the Black River Canal or Gowanus Canal?", "answer": "Black River Canal", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the hub of the airline that was a main sponsor of the 2007 Lexus Cup?", "answer": "Singapore Changi Airport", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " \"Here's a Drink\" is a single by The Beatnuts, a group in  regional subgenre of hip hop music that originated in the area of what city?", "answer": "New York City", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who coached the team that stunned the Longhorns 39-33 on a last second touchdown pass in the 2008 Texas vs. Texas Tech football game?", "answer": "Mike Leach", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "51824 Mikeanderson is an asteroid named for the recipient of what United States award?", "answer": "Congressional Space Medal of Honor", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Adriano Zumbo is a chef from a country with what capital?", "answer": "Canberra", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which province was the 1995 winner of the Dutch National Time Trial Championships born in?", "answer": "South Holland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Taylor Swift song, \"Tim McGraw,\" which charted within the top forty in the United States was written about all the different things that would remind Swift's whom of Swift and their time spent together, once he departed?", "answer": "her senior boyfriend", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American actor starred in Detention", "answer": "Joshua Ryan \"Josh\" Hutcherson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What American Western filmmaker's film did Norman Lumsden appear in?", "answer": "Clint Eastwood", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Between Jason Bateman and Jan Troell, which filmmaker has had a more diverse career?", "answer": "Jan Gustaf Troell", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Since 2006 Jeremy Norcliffe Haslehurst has been Professor of Spanish Golden Age Studies at a  public research university that was granted a Royal Charter in what year?", "answer": "1948", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which sport included Sir Walter Winterbottom as the first manager of the England team and Roy Hodgson as a former player and manager?", "answer": "Football", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what city is the DeVry Advantage Academy and CLC at H.P. Carter, that works with the university formerly known as DeForest Training School?", "answer": "Houston, Texas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born first Douglas Sirk or Melville Shavelson?", "answer": "Douglas Sirk", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The territory of the modern state of Iraq was defined in 1920 as Mandatory Iraq, its history includes much of the world's earliest writing, literature, etc, which type of literature is the literature written in the Sumerian language during the Middle Bronze Age?", "answer": "Sumerian literature", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Daniel Amos and The Ramones both started in New York City?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What team did Danny Mills play for that has home matches at Select Security Stadium ", "answer": "Widnes Vikings", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Adventures of Elmo in Grouchland was a 1999 film which involved the use of puppets from a puppeteer who was also the voice of what character from \"Star Wars\"?", "answer": "Yoda", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Saving Private Ryan  is a movie set in which country?", "answer": "France", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Chariton Review is based at what kind of university?", "answer": "a public liberal arts and sciences university", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Villa Senar is located near Lake Lucerne, which literally translates to what?", "answer": "Lake of the Four Forested Settlements", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Charles Louis Critchfield earned his PhD in Physics from George Washington University under the direction of which theoretical physicist who was known as \"the father of the hydrogen bomb.\"", "answer": "Edward Teller", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which actor that had a cameo in \"Se\u00f1or Macho Solo\" was born on October 13, 1971?", "answer": "Billy Bush", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the former Hong Kong singer and model who starred in The G\u00e2teau Affairs? ", "answer": "Bobo Chan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is younger Shy Carter or Charlie Puth ?", "answer": "Charlie Puth", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the American actor and comedian who featured in 'Who's Got the Action'  American comedy and is also best known for his role as Oscar Madison in ''The Odd Couple''?", "answer": "Walter Matthau", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many shots did the last person prosecuted under The Treason Act 1842 fire at Queen Elizabeth II?", "answer": "six", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What name was given to the son of the man who defeated the usurper Allectus ?", "answer": "Constantine the Great", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which building is taller, 1166 Avenue of the Americas or 712 Fifth Avenue?", "answer": "712 5th Avenue", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What actor born in 1980 starred in Shaolin?", "answer": "Nicholas Tse", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is a television director, Mark Rosman or Aaron Kozak?", "answer": "Mark Rosman", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Frank S. Giles, Jr., was a politician who was a Member of the Massachusetts Public Safety Commissioner, and a Member of which lower house of the Massachusetts General Court, the state legislature of the Commonwealth of Massachusetts, is called what? ", "answer": "Massachusetts House of Representatives", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "One of the Republican representatives proposing Bill S.978 also served in which role for the 115 Congress?", "answer": "Senate Majority Whip", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Nariman Bomanshaw Mehta, was an Indian-born American organic chemist and pharmacologist who designed, synthesized, and patented which organic compound, medication primarily used as an antidepressant and smoking cessation aid?", "answer": "Bupropion", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which rock group has more members: Unsane or Pupil?", "answer": "Pupil", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What famous cartoonist became famous for animated holiday specials like \"A Charlie Brown Thanksgiving\"?", "answer": "Charles M. Schulz", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who opted out due to injury The 1997 NBA All-Star Game, who currently serves as a color commentator for Houston Rockets home games?", "answer": "Clyde Austin \"The Glide\" Drexler", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What television station did WCCO-TV worked for?  ", "answer": "CBS Corporation", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where are the headquarters of the business that includes Houghton Wines as a subsidiary?", "answer": "South Australia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "On which island of Japan did Cathy Branta win gold in the 1985 Summer Universiade?", "answer": "Honsh\u016b", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which British neurologist, naturalist, historian of science and author delivered the Foundation Lecture on \"Creativity and the Mind\" at the Centre for the Mind's gala public opening on 5 August 1997?", "answer": "Oliver Sacks", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Thurmond is a town in Fayette County, West Virginia, on the New River, the town was the filming location for which 1987 American drama film written and directed by John Sayles?", "answer": "Matewan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Habenaria and Cymbopogon both found in tropical climates?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What was the name of the iconic speech given by Martin Luther King, Jr. to over 250,000 civil rights supporters from the Lincoln Memorial in August of 1963?", "answer": "I Have a Dream", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Does Darren Bravo's half brother bat left-handed or right-handed?", "answer": "right-handed", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which actor starred in both Cheers and the Village Barbershop", "answer": "John Ratzenberger", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Rod Laver and Mary-Ann Eisel both nationals of the same country ?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which of the creator of Legit was born on 14 February 1977?", "answer": "Jim Jefferies", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the former CEO of Enron Corporation.who had a case in theUnited States Supreme Court born ", "answer": "November 25, 1953", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "From what country is the movie that Rocky Handsome is based on from?", "answer": "South Korea", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What historic castle, located on the north bank of the River Thames is famous for imprisoning people such as Clement Walker?", "answer": "Tower of London", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How long is the footpath devised by the author of the book which devotes an entire chapter to the Maiden Moor?", "answer": "192-mile", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year did the writer of \"Mind of My Mind\" die?", "answer": "2006", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Lloyd Center is a shopping mall includes the Lloyd Center Ice Rink where a former American firgure skater first learned to skate and was later she was banned for life from what?", "answer": "U.S. Figure Skating Association", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Is Lehigh University or the Technological Institute of the Philippines established in 1865 by Asa Packer?", "answer": "Lehigh University", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "At a tournament where Wisoon Wichaya was coaching Thai football in 206, at least 38 teams were playing. How many of those teams were women's teams? ", "answer": "8 teams", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Apex and Islander 23 are both gangs from which country?", "answer": "Australia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which professional footballer plays as a striker for Italian club Juventus?", "answer": "Gonzalo Higua\u00edn", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year did the founder of The Peabody Museum of Natural History die?", "answer": "1869", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Woodside Presbyterian Church was built on land owned by a businessman born in what year?", "answer": "1794", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where are the singers of \"Tear in My Heart\" from?", "answer": "Columbus, Ohio", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Hazel Mae Barker, is a Canadian sportscaster, she was the former lead anchor for which's organization, SportsDesk news program, which is an American regional sports cable and satellite television network that is owned by a joint venture of Fenway Sports Group?", "answer": "NESN (New England Sports Network)", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Olof Sk\u00f6tkonung's mother appeared in what line of sagas?", "answer": "Icelandic", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the German heavy metal singer-songwriter born who  first two solo albums are contained in Earth Shaker Rock?", "answer": "3 June 1964", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the band formed that sang \"I'm One\"?", "answer": "1964", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What actor played Lucas McCain and also played in both Major League Baseball and in the National Basketball Association?", "answer": "Chuck Connors", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Together We Are Beautiful\" is a popular single by which American R&B and disco singer, who is best remembered for her releases, \"Groove Me\" and \"Together We Are Beautiful\"?", "answer": "Fern Kinney", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Columbus Crew SC has a head coach who is of what heritage?", "answer": "American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which hospital was establish almost a century before the other, Howard University Hospital or the Psychiatric Institute of Washington?", "answer": "Howard University Hospital", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Were Ken Annakin and Michael Crichton both involved in the film industry?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are University of Wisconsin\u2013Madison and Florida International University in the same state?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which movie came out first Chernobyl Heart or Lake of Fire ?", "answer": "Chernobyl Heart", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Legends of the Wild West is a walkthrough attraction located in Disneyland Paris, in which one of the \"themed lands\", at the many Disneyland-style parks run by Disney around the world?", "answer": "Frontierland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "how is Smith Magazine and Six-Word Memoirs connected?", "answer": "storytelling", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What type of building was built between 1752 and 1756 in the capital city of Mauritius?", "answer": "It is a religious building", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Amigos para la aventura was Directed by this Argentine singer and Actor who was born on what date?", "answer": "March 8, 1942", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Games like Tales of Xillia 2 first made their appearance during what decade?", "answer": "1980s", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Kunichika Tomiyama was an actor from a puppet state that was seized by Japan in what year?", "answer": "1931", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was the band that Tom William HIngley is the frontman for formed?", "answer": "Oldham, Greater Manchester", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were Pavel Alexandrov and Yuri Matiyasevich both working in the same area of mathematics?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which band was formed first Fugazi or Anarbor?", "answer": "Fugazi", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What electro-pop musician was born on September 11th 1971?", "answer": "Alessandra Rosaldo", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jaz Beer is a pilsner-type rice beer limited to non-Muslims at outdoor areas in which beer and local food are served, typically at what?", "answer": "shared tables", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which founder of the Romantic Novelists' Association was born in  Berkshire, England?", "answer": "Vivian Stuart", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Between Leucadendron and Anchusa, which genus has more species?", "answer": "Leucadendron", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Texas Private Investigator worked on a case involving a New York millionaire primarily known for what?", "answer": "being suspected of foul play against three individuals in different states", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What former broadcast centre was acquired by the partnered university of the women's Twenty20 cricket team captained by Georgia Elwiss?", "answer": "the former broadcast centre at the Queen Elizabeth Olympic Park", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "To which taxonomic category do both Swainsona and Olsynium belong?", "answer": "genus", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Portland Winterhawks have produced alumni which include the Swiss hockey player for the Minnesota Wild nicknamed what?", "answer": "El Ni\u00f1o", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who first recorded the childre's ryme that All the King's Men's bame came from?", "answer": "James William Elliott", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which star of Heaven Help Us was also is \"Toy Story\"?", "answer": "Wallace Michael Shawn", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Mary Ochsenhirt Amdur studied the effects of smog on what town? ", "answer": "Donora, Pennsylvania", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Archduchess Sophie of Austria's mother was, in addition to being Empress of Austria, Queen of which country?", "answer": "Hungary", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which song on Lil Wayne's Dedication 4 mixtape is a remix of the original, featuring Young Jeezy?", "answer": "My Homies Still", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Hot Shots! featuring Charlie Sheen includes scenes spoofing a film about a boxer named Rocky Balboa, who is portrayed by whom in the original 1976 film?", "answer": "Sylvester Stallone", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What sovereign country located in the Maghreb region of North Africa is Wiam Dislam from?", "answer": "Morocco", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What television series ran for two seasons from September 1997 to March 1998, and was based on Walt Disney's adaptation of Dodie Smith's 1956 novel \"The Hundred and One Dalmatians\"?", "answer": "101 Dalmatians: The Series", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Jack Finney and Tim O'Brien both considered writers?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Mozart composed the Serenade No. 5 for ceremonies at a university established in what year?", "answer": "1622", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 1993 Mobil Cotton Bowl