": "bridge"}, {"question": "Sebastian Janikowski shares the record for the longest field goal with which kicker for the Atlanta Falcons?", "answer": "David Roy Akers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 2016 Boise State Broncos football team represented Boise State University during the 2016 NCAA Division I FBS football season, They were invited to the Cactus Bowl where they lost to Baylor, the 2016 Baylor Bears football team represented Baylor University in the 2016 NCAA Division I FBS football season, were coached by which interim head coach, in their 118th football season?", "answer": "Jim Grobe", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who has directed a movie featuring the music of Omar Fadel?", "answer": "Larry Charles", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Lewis Hastings Sarett was a research scientist at one of the largest what, in the world?", "answer": "pharmaceutical companies", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The official remix of Up! features a rapper who was shot how many times in 2000?", "answer": "nine", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which former social conservative and member of the Conservative Christian Fellowship was a politician before Helen Grant in the British Conservative Party?", "answer": "Ann Widdecombe", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where does the ferry one would take at the east end of New York State Route 25 lead to?", "answer": "New London, Connecticut", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Until what year did the political party of which Benjamin Tallmadge was elected to the United States House of Representatives as a member control the federal government?", "answer": "1801", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which thriller novel by the widow of the 2005 Nobel Laureate in Literature, Harold Pinter, features sleuthing heroine Jemima Shore?", "answer": "Quiet as a Nun", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The AXIS is a mid-sized auditorium located at a hotel and casino operated by who?", "answer": "Caesars Entertainment Corporation", "type": "br