amily?", "answer": "DeCavalcante crime family", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the middle name of the man whom Johny Srouji reports to at Apple?", "answer": "Donald", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Time magazine's best novel of 2005 had it's screenplay written by what person?", "answer": "Alex Garland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Russian physician originally proposed the death drive in her paper \"Destruction as the Cause of Coming into Being\"?", "answer": "Sabina Nikolayevna Spielrein", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Laurence Boswell directed the Canadian actor who earned a Golden Globe award nomination for what 2001 film?", "answer": "Life as a House", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Insect Dreams: The Half Life of Gregor Samsa\" is a sequel to a Franz Kafka story first published in which year?", "answer": "1915", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is presented every four years to the most \"outstanding boxer\" at the Olympic Games and won by a retired Scottish amateur boxer in 1995?", "answer": "Val Barker Trophy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Strange Changes\" is a song that was co-written by the former wife of an American actor known for his role in what 1970's musical-sitcom?", "answer": "The Partridge Family", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Lisbeth Hummen stared in which 1975 French erotic fantasy horror film?", "answer": "La B\u00eate", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which actor on the show Nathan Barley was the director of the film Submarine?", "answer": "Richard Ayoade", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What 1995 Iron Maiden album  graphically depicts the band's mascot, Eddie, being vivisected by machine?", "answer": "\"The X Factor\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many World Series has the team Frank Bushey played for won?", "answer": "eight", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Spy Who Loved Me is the ninth novel in the James Bond series authored by Ian Fleming, who was educated at Eton, Sandhurst, Muni