ocated in southwestern Montana?", "answer": "Philipsburg", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the actress that starred both in the TV series Pretty Little Liars and in the thriller horror film Evidence born?", "answer": "June 8, 1984", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which band was formed first, Travis or Birthmark?", "answer": "Travis", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are Paul Hindemith and Maurice Ravel both violinists?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The first ever player drafted by the Indianapolis Colts attended what university?", "answer": "University of Oklahoma", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Between the British film directors, Gil Kenan, and B. E. Doxat-Pratt, which was also a screenwriter?", "answer": "Gil Kenan", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Cape Codder and Cosmopolitan are both what?", "answer": "cocktail", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who was born first, Sunye or Mike Ness?", "answer": "Michael James Ness", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which restaurant focuses more on just pizza, Valentino's and Imo's Pizza?", "answer": "Imo's Pizza", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What American country music artist recorded the song \"Heaven Help Me\" and was born Christina Claire Ciminella?", "answer": "Wynonna Judd", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Kim Han-sol (Korean: \uae40\ud55c\uc194 , born 16 June 1995) is the eldest son of Kim Jong-nam, Kim Jong-nam (Chos\u014fn'g\u016dl: \uae40\uc815\ub0a8 ; Hancha: \u91d1\u6b63\u7537), was the eldest son of the North Korean leader Kim Jong-il, date of death ?", "answer": "13 February 2017", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "United States v. Cecil Price, et al., also known as the Mississippi Burning trial, was a criminal trial where the United States charged a group of 18 men with conspiring in a Ku Klux Klan plot to murder three young civil rights workers (Michael Schwerner, James Chaney, and Andrew Goodman) in Philadelphia, Mississippi on which date, the mu