amed after the youngest person to receive six Academy Award nominations", "answer": "Agra katewinsletae", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Talk to La Bomb utilizes a multi-genre style involving electro which can be represented by what prominent characteristics made popular by such artists as Skrillex, Steve Aoki, Dimitri Vegas and Like Mike?", "answer": "prominent bassline or kick drum and a tempo between 125 and 135 beats per minute", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What role is the actress, who also stars in a 2006 film directed and co-written by Matt Williams, is known for on the ABC drama \"Private Practice?\"", "answer": "Charlotte King", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The head coach of the 2016 Temple Owls football team is currently the head football coach at what university?", "answer": "Baylor University", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Eileen Murray is co-CEO at which firm founded by Ray Dalio?", "answer": "Bridgewater Associates", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many local government districts are there where the London Hockey League is based?", "answer": "33", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When did Disney's Contemporary Resort and Disney's Polynesian Village Resort open?", "answer": "October 1, 1971", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What lake aka Twin Lakes is the fifth largest lake entirely in New Hampshire?", "answer": "Lake Sunapee", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed a 1996 American science fiction Western film starring an actress best known for her role on Cheers as Kelly Gaines?", "answer": "Sam Irvin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What landmark, built by J. W. Eddy is at the Bunker Hill district in California?", "answer": "Angels Flight", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What number was the president whose policies were taken from Heritage's policy study \"Mandate for Leadership\"?", "answer": "40th", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Kenneth Hugh de Courcy, editor of the British subscription newsletter 'Intelligence Digest' was confidant of which British King who also held the title Emperor of India until his abdication in 1936?", "answer": "Edward VIII", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Silent Hill HD Collection is a compilation of remastered ports of \"Silent Hill 3\", and \"Silent Hill 2\", a survival horror video game published by which company?", "answer": "Konami", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What American bluegrass singer guest performs on an album by American country music singer Daryle Singletary?", "answer": "Rhonda Vincent", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In 2006, Keith Slettedahl appeared in an episode of \"How I Met Your Mother\" that originally aired on which date ?", "answer": "May 1, 2006", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which group of Native American tribes have roots in the Oneota?", "answer": "Sioux", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "He's the DJ, I'm the Rapper, by DJ Jazzy Jeff and the Fresh Prince, was an early project by which famous rapper and film star?", "answer": "Will Smith", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the achievement Jeffrey Sachs book \"The End of Poverty\" earned?", "answer": "It was a \"New York Times\" bestseller", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who made the popular 2006 manhwa that film Director Cho Geun-hyun his 2012 film on?", "answer": "Kang Full", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What country are both Daresbury and AppSense located in?", "answer": "England", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What type of publications are both The American Interest, focusing on politics and economics and OK!, specialising in reality TV news?", "answer": "magazine", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are both filmmakers Don Siegel and Allan Moyle from the same country?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What Manhattan college was Theodore Shapiro a professor emeritus at?", "answer": "Weill Cornell Medicine", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 1993-94 Portland Trail Blazers season included Harvey Grant, who also has