 1884?", "answer": "Edward Severin Clark", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Lucky is an American comedy series based around ludomania, which is also known as what? ", "answer": "Problem gambling", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Do film makers James Cameron and Claude Sautet share the same nationality?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Gottlieb Heileman took a track for business that was unlike which St. Louis, Missouri-based competitor?", "answer": "Anheuser-Busch", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Uncluded was formed by which American singer-songwriter, best known as a solo performer and as one half of The Moldy Peaches?", "answer": "Kimya Dawson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Raphael \"Raphi\" Rom is an Israeli computer scientist working at Technion \u2013 Israel Institute of Technology, a public research university in which city, in Israel?", "answer": "Haifa", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "from 2003 to 2009, Charlie Sadler was the defensive ends coach for a football team that plays its home games at which stadium ?", "answer": "Jones AT&T Stadium", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Does Mellow Mushroom or East of Chicago Pizza have more locations?", "answer": "Mellow Mushroom Pizza Bakers", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which film director is still living, Ian Schneider or Michael Anderson?", "answer": "Ian Schneider", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In what film did the founder of the American Symphony Orchestra appear?", "answer": "Fantasia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In regards to the album released on October 22, 2012, where did the Tour that was launched in support of it end?", "answer": "Singapore", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the name of the eighth episode of the American animated television series created by Pendleton Ward and produced by Cartoon Network Studios?", "answer": "Furniture & Meat", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American hip hop duo from Port Arthur, Texas did Mean Green feature?", "answer": "UGK", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who owns Scopus, a bibliographic database, which abstracted and indexed the International Journal of Private Law?", "answer": "Elsevier", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Heather Barnett gave a talk about slime mould on a program from what media organization which posts talks online for free distribution, under the slogan \"ideas worth spreading\"?", "answer": "TED", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which novelist was American, Michael Shaara or Guillermo Cabrera Infante?", "answer": "Michael Shaara", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Peckforton Hills  form a significant part of the longer Mid Cheshire Ridge which extends southwards from Frodsham towards Malpas,  large village that used to be what type of town?", "answer": "a market town", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Brian Tinsley is a physicist whose wife made fundamental contributions to the astronomical understanding of how galaxies what?", "answer": "evolve, grow and die", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "This Godless Endeavor, is the sixth album by which American progressive metal band from Seattle, Washington, United States?", "answer": "Nevermore", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the Democratic candicate that won the Unithed States Senate election in New York, 2012?", "answer": "Kirsten Gillibrand", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who stared in \"The Vampire Diaries\" and Blue Like Jazz?", "answer": "Claire Holt", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ruth Carter Stapleton is the sister of a politican that served as President of the United States during what years?", "answer": "1977 to 1981", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Reg Mountford played football that for a team that competes in which league?", "answer": "the Premier League", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Alfred Charles Kinsey, was an American biologist, professor of entomology and zoology, and sexologist who in 1947 founded the Institute for Sex Research at Indiana Uni