hat Mesoamerican people founded the Yucuita site?", "answer": "Mixtec", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Applied Physics Reviews is an annual peer-reviewed scientific journal publishing reviews of topics of experimental or theoretical research in applied physics and applications of physics to other branches of science and engineering, it was originally a part of  \"Journal of Applied Physics\", published since which year, by the American Institute of Physics?", "answer": "1931", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is a type of German sausage made from veal, beef, or pork and cooked in vinegar? ", "answer": "Bratwurst", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "On what date was the NHL Entry Draft held that resulted in the Avalanche selecting the first draft choice overall in 2013?", "answer": "June 30, 2013", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which year was this mall located across the street from the historic home Belmont opened?", "answer": "1968", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Linfen and Weihui are both found in what country?", "answer": "Republic of China", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which was released first, The Computer Wore Tennis Shoes or The Watcher in the Woods?", "answer": "The Computer Wore Tennis Shoes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which intergovernmental military alliance signed in 1949 are Denmark and the Netherlands both members of? ", "answer": "NATO", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the best known brand name of the material other than dacron often used to replace the aneurysmal portion of the aorta in OAS?", "answer": "Teflon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which band did Craig Northey formerly play with before releasing his solo album Giddy Up?", "answer": "Odds", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What are country are both John Wayne Airport and Brainerd Lakes Regional Airport located in?", "answer": "United States", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who is the male presenter on Sky News Tonight, who has also presented for Sky News?", "answer": "Dermot Murnaghan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which landmark, between Lake Baikal and Rara Lake, can be found further north in Asia?", "answer": "Lake Baikal", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What city do Biagio Black and Kate Moss both have in common?", "answer": "New York City", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Besides writing the lyrics to Koduka Kodula, what was Acharya Aatreya known for?", "answer": "known for his works in Telugu cinema, and Telugu theatre", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What nationality was the Lax pair's namesake?", "answer": "Hungarian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the debut album that featured the number 1 song of the decade of 2000's on the Adult Pop Charts by \"Billboard\" magazine released?", "answer": "July 10, 2001", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Daniel Biveson's first World Cup win in 2001 occured in a city located in what Australian state?", "answer": "Tyrol", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The first production vehicles of Modec were destined for a retailer with how many stores across Asia and Europe?", "answer": "12", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the UFC Middleweight ranking of one of Matt Hume's students?", "answer": "#13", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What country does Artichoke River and West Newbury, Massachusettshave in common?", "answer": "United States", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What nationality is the inventor of Integer BASIC?", "answer": "American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born November 27 1967?", "answer": "Kapoor (born 27 November 1967)", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Canal in England is part of the British canal system and has a village with a remarkable series of 21 locks on the canal?", "answer": "Grand Union Canal", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What are Hypoestes and Cycad ?", "answer": "plants", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Ole Thyssen is a professor at a school established in what year?", "ans