 born first out of Menno Oosting and Anna-Lena Gr\u00f6nefeld?", "answer": "Menno Oosting", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Laura Loomer previously worked for Project Vertias with a political activist of what ideology?", "answer": "conservative", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Scaffold's musical performer attended what institute?", "answer": "Liverpool Institute", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 1913 New York Giants were led by the manager nicknamed what?", "answer": "\"Little Napoleon\" and \"Mugsy\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Lemlair House was originally built as a fortified seat for the chief of this, which also held the Foulis Castle from the twelfth century?", "answer": "Clan Munro", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of the following, Olive or Ceraria, is known by the botanical name Olea europaea?", "answer": "olive", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which band has had more names in it's history, The Cult or Simple Kid?", "answer": "The Cult", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Domhnall Dubh was imprisoned at the castle on the island near what Scottish city?", "answer": "Dalavich", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Dan Swan\u00f6 and Simone Simons are both what? ", "answer": "vocalist", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who has received more academy award nominations, John Boorman or Rick Rosenthal?", "answer": "John Boorman", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What was the middle name of the man whose first TV show was \"Hey, Landlord\"?", "answer": "Kent", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which documentary was released first, The Plow That Broke the Plains or Seal Island?", "answer": "The Plow That Broke the Plains", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Where did the actor playing Melody in The Little Mermaid II: Return to the Sea win an award from?", "answer": "the Academy of Interactive Arts & Sciences", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who ordered the execution of Fadilla's sister?", "answer": "Roman Emperor Commo