ts?", "answer": "Advance Auto Parts", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Does the satirical Disney Comedy Moon Pilot mirror the mysticism, adventure, morality and camaraderie of the novel The Wind in the Willows?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Was Edward Avedisian or Edward Keonjian born first?", "answer": "Dr. Edward Keonjian", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "At the 1988 Prize of Moscow News, who was the Soviet who lost against an American figure skater later banned from the U.S. Figure Skating Association?", "answer": "Natalia Lebedeva", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year was this battle fought, in which Matthew Caldwell was caused the Paul Revere of Texas because of his recruitment ride ahead of it?", "answer": "1835", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which steam locomotive built for Pere Marquette Railway (PM) by Lima Locomotive Works in Lima, Ohio looks very similar to the 2-8-4 \"Berkshire\" type steam locomotive built for the Nickel Plate Road?", "answer": "Pere Marquette 1225", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year did Larry McMurtry's screenplay adaptation about the complex emotional and homosexual relationship between Ennis Del Mar and Jack Twist in the American West from 1963 to 1983 win him an oscar?", "answer": "2005", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ermenegildo Pistelli is a practitioner of what study of historical language?", "answer": "Philology", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What award did the composer of the music for the film Pankajavalli win?", "answer": "Madras Music Academy's Sangeetha Kalanidhi", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How long is the main river that is located in Oxford County, Maine?", "answer": "8.6 mi", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which star of The Last Rites of Joe May was born on June 20, 1942 ?", "answer": "Chelcie Ross", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What company manufactured a \"Crazy Mouse\" roller coaster at a theme park located in Woodmore CDP, Prince George's Count