ka", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Patricia Morison was the lead in what musical written by Samuel and Bella Spewack?", "answer": "Kiss Me, Kate", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Andrew Ross Sorkin, is an American journalist and author, and the co-creator for which channel series \"Billions\"?", "answer": "Showtime", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which University was founded earlier, Mahidol University or University of the East?", "answer": "Mahidol University (MU), an autonomous research institution in Thailand, had its origin in the establishment of Siriraj Hospital in 1888.", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Elizabeth Cecil, 16th Baroness de Ros Was the granddaughter of who?", "answer": "Henry Manners", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 2016 Africa Eco Race replaced a rally raid organised by who?", "answer": "Amaury Sport Organisation", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What mine is farther north of Yellowknife, Northwest Territories, Ruth Mine or Camlaren Mine?", "answer": "Camlaren Mine", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are both Battle Sheep and Clans board games?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What team prior to joining the Big Ten, the team was a member of the American Athletic Conference, had a head coach who moved on to become the head football coach at Columbia University?", "answer": "Rutgers Scarlet Knights", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the writer of the  American action horror-thriller film which was directed by Adam Wingard?", "answer": "Simon Barrett", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Michael O. Steinitz is the editor of a journal established in what year?", "answer": "1951", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "One of the supporters of the Edinburgh Seven released a joint publication detailing natural selection with which man?", "answer": "Alfred Russel Wallace", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Renee Props played Lois in an episode titled \"The Race\" from the 6th season of a tv sitcom that ended in what year?", "answer": "1998", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the early Indie role-playing game written by S.John Ross was first published?", "answer": "in 1993", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What magazine is designed as a members\u2019 publication with a focus on health articles, competitions, and arranging discounts for members on a range of services, Woman's Journal or Candis Magazine ?", "answer": "Candis", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The company that now owns Imagekind was founded in where?", "answer": "San Mateo, California", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Four-Inch Course name was derived from regulations adopoted by a British private club which formerly owned what kind of company?", "answer": "automotive services company", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American horror film franchise created by Sam Raimi, which inspired Evil Aliens, a British slapstick horror-comedy film?", "answer": "Evil Dead", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The main international airport of Holland also serves as one of the main bases for which airline?", "answer": "CHC Airways", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which exhibition of 1964 Joseph James Paparella was an umpire?", "answer": "35th midseason exhibition", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Princess Maria Clotilde of Savoy's mother died in what year?", "answer": "1855", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The tv series \"My Only Love Song\" stars Gong Seung-yeon and the lead guitarist of what band?", "answer": "CNBLUE", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What television drama did Lee Bo-young star in that aired on SBS?", "answer": "I Can Hear Your Voice", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Joseph Mazilier wrote what ballet, with music by \u00c9douard Deldevez and Ludwig Minkus?", "answer": "Paquita", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which director is from India, Hall Bartlett or Kamal Haasan?", "answer": "Kamal Haasan", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In what year was the man who founded the Podesta Group with Tony Podesta born?", "answer": "1949", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Do Mollie King and David Sylvian share the same nationality?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What type of colleges are the University of Wisconsin\u2013Madison and the University of Texas at Austin?", "answer": "public research university", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "\"Earned It\", is a song by Canadian singer The Weeknd, the song was released as the lead single from the soundtrack to the film \"Fifty Shades of Grey\", released in which year?", "answer": "2015", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Charles Deering Library, on the campus of Northwestern University in Evanston, Illinois, the library is named for Charles Deering, a Northwestern benefactor and chairman of which company, that was a United States manufacturer of agricultural machinery, construction equipment, trucks, and household and commercial products?", "answer": "International Harvester Company", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the 1993-1994 USAC National Champion born?", "answer": "1962", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "To the south of Irvington is a village whose ZIP code is what?", "answer": "10522", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What county in Maine is the George W. Smith Homestead located in?", "answer": "Penobscot County", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Walter Thane Baker was born in a city with a population of what as of the 2010 census?", "answer": "2,205", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Romanogobio elimeius is a species of ray-finned fish in the Cyprinidae family found in Greece and the Republic of Macedonia, became a member of the United Nations in what year?", "answer": "1993", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Legislative Council of the Territory of Florida governed Florida after a treaty was made between Spain and what other country?", "answer": "the United States", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Was Ghosts of the Abyss or Land of Silence and Darkness directed by James Cameron?", "answer": "Ghosts of the Abyss", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Lane Boy was written by the musical duo hailing from which Ohio city?", "answer": "Columbus", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of the actors is more likely to have performed on a stage, James Bridges or Michael Dolan?", "answer": "Michael Dolan", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What position was held between 2013 and 2015 by a man placed under investigation by ruling political party of the People's Republic of China on June 26, 2015?", "answer": "Vice-Chairman of the Tibet People's Congress", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Chetna includes a song by the playback singer of what nationality?", "answer": "Indian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "are Zo\u00e9 and Elbow both from Mexico?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Was Peter Collier the founder of both ToyFare and Collier's?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What airport is in the same community as the Indie Rock Record Label founded by Ken Katkin?", "answer": "Lebanon Municipal Airport", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many American causalities were there in the battle that earned Clinton LaVor Romesha the Medal of Honor?", "answer": "8", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " A fairy tale is a type of short story that features  human-shaped supernatural beings in Germanic what?", "answer": "mythology and folklore", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is the football club that Dominik Stroh-Engel currently plays for based?", "answer": "Karlsruhe, Baden-W\u00fcrttemberg", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Bod\u00f8 Air Station, is a military airbase of the Royal Norwegian Air Force (RNoAF) located at Bod\u00f8, in which country, the 330 Squadron. [3] Air defense is provided using NASAMS?", "answer": "Norway", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Mick Jones and Frank Iero, have which occupation in common?", "answer": "musician", "type": "comparison"},