ia?", "answer": "the Fredericksburg Line from Fredericksburg, Virginia, and the Manassas Line", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the companion series of the 10-episode documentary television series presented by science historian James Burke.", "answer": "The Day the Universe Changed", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Pau Gasol S\u00e1ez, is a Spanish professional basketball player for the San Antonio Spurs of the National Basketball Association (NBA), and the older brother of fellow NBA player Marc Gasol, of which sports team?", "answer": "Memphis Grizzlies", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who owns the news television channel who Andrew Ehinger is a reporter for?", "answer": "Altice USA", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What nationality was Theodor Seuss Geisel, better known as Dr. Seuss, children's author and creator of the Grinch?", "answer": "American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What award did the young actress who starred in the 1993 spy thriller film based on the novel by Tom Clancy win for her film debut?", "answer": "Young Artist Award for Best Young Actress Under Nine Years of Age", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Annie Golden plays Norma Romano is a tv series based on a memoir by who?", "answer": "Piper Kerman", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What day of the week does a South Korean television series starring a German-South Korean actress aired on?", "answer": "Thursdays", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The  folklore  which Daniel C. Taylor gavea definitive explanation for the century-old is for which people ", "answer": "Nepal,", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Eric Lynn Wright, better known by his stage name Eazy-E, was an American rapper who performed solo and in the hip hop group N.W.A. and is known for portraying Eazy-E on what album?", "answer": "\"Straight Outta Compton\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What character in All You Need Is Kill inspired Tom Cruise's character in Edge of Tomorrow?", "answer": "Keiji Kiriya", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What country are both the Brechin Castle and the Dalhousie Castle located in?", "answer": "Scotland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is older, Roger Daltrey or Brian Fair?", "answer": "Roger Harry Daltrey", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In what county of Maine is the town in which the West Lebanon Historic District is located?", "answer": "York County", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American guitarist, songwriter and author related his second studio album on April 16, 2002?", "answer": "Chris P\u00e9rez", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The King of the Gospel Singers is a studio album from a musician that was born in this year?", "answer": "1932", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Tropicana Country Club is located across from a hotel and casino that is owned and operated by Penn National Gaming, and is a franchise of what chain?", "answer": "Hilton's DoubleTree", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Open House is a 2004 real estate musical film that stars an actor and singer who is best known for originating the role of Mark Cohen in what Broadway production?", "answer": "Rent", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Chunkey, is a game of which nationality origin, gambling was frequently connected with the game, the wagering of money or something of value (referred to as \"the stakes\") on an event with an uncertain outcome with the primary intent of winning money or material goods?", "answer": "Native American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the brother of the actress who made her screen debut as a child alongside her father, Jon Voight, in \"Lookin' to Get Out\"?", "answer": "James Haven", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Harry 'The Hunchback' Riccobene became a major figure in the gang war that followed the death of a mobster who had a preference for conciliation over what?", "answer": "violence", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What place Dayton metropolitan area centered on Dayton, Ohio takes after Cincinnati metropolitan area also known as Greater Cincinnati which is the largest metropolitan area in Ohio and has population of 2,11,580 people?", "answer": "It is the fourth largest", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Suraj Sharma is an Indian actor, who made his debut with 2012 film adopted from a Canadian fantasy adventure novel by who?", "answer": "Yann Martel", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "E. Ann McGee received her doctorate from a university that consists of how many colleges ?", "answer": "18 colleges", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What number album was Organik for the man known for his composition \"Children\"?", "answer": "third", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Dominick V. \"Quiet Dom\" Cirillo briefly served as acting boss for a mobster who started out as a what?", "answer": "professional boxer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The ship that was originally called La Gallega helped Christopher Columbus establish colonies on which island?", "answer": "La Santa Mar\u00eda,", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which writer has his novels take place in a fictional Ozark Mountain town: Brian O'Nolan or Donald Harington?", "answer": "Donald Douglas Harington", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who was born first, Philip Terzian or John Berberian?", "answer": "John Berberian", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What do both Hundred Reasons and Pale Saints have in common?", "answer": "alternative rock band", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What work of Rommel N. Angara was printed in the liwayway?", "answer": "His poems saw print", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Festival Foods was founded as what brand of US grocery stores?", "answer": "IGA", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Cirque de Gavarnie is compared to what oval amphitheatre built of concrete and sand is the largest amphitheatre ever built?", "answer": "Colosseum", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Peter Watkins and Albert de Courville, are of which nationality?", "answer": "English", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which Roman Catholic monarch of England, Scotland, and Ireland appointed Sir Brian O'Neill as judge? ", "answer": "James II of England", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What do John Huston and James Bridges have in common?", "answer": "American screenwriter", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who wrote and performed a song in a 2000 comedy-drama film directed by Curtis Hanson?", "answer": "Bob Dylan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which magazine does the author of \"The Diana Chronicles\" work for?", "answer": "The New Yorker", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What MASH cast member who was known for his work on the Doris Day Show helped write the Army-Navy Game episode of MASH's first season?", "answer": "McLean Stevenson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "To which taxonomic category do both Lysiloma and Backhousia belong?", "answer": "genus", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The leader of the Anglo-Portuguese Army that defeated French forces during the Battle of Bu\u00e7acoalso  defeated Napoleon during what battle?", "answer": "Battle of Waterloo", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what region of the United States is the expression Uff da popular among Scandinavian Americans?", "answer": "Upper Midwest and Pacific Northwest", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who wrote The Annual Register and also served for many years in the House of Commons with the Whig Party?", "answer": "Edmund Burke", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Yannick Noah and Julian Knowle both tennis players?", "answer": "professional tennis player", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Dad's Week Off was a film that starred which stand-up comedian and actor?", "answer": "Richard John Colangelo", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "who made a fully autonomous unmanned mini watercraft capable of independent operation underwater that differs from a submersible, which has more limited underwater capability?", "answer": "BAE Systems", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who worked on a geometry used in the design and construction of religious structures?", "answer": "Henry Pelham Holmes Bromwell", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Esther Norma Arrostito (January 17, 1940 \u2013 January 15, 1978) was an Argentine political activist and leftist militant, initially close to communist ideology, In 1970, she became one of the founders of the peronist revolutionary movement of which organization, along with Fernando Abal Medina, what was an Argentine leftist terrorist and urban guerrilla group, active during the 1960s and 1970s?", "answer": "Montoneros", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What country are both Dalhousie University and the  Dalhousie Corporate Residency MBA located in?", "answer": "Canada", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What rank on the Billboard's album chart did Broken Blossom, which was created by the American singer born in 1945, reach?", "answer": "#51", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Wong Shun Leung, was a Chinese martial artist from where, who studied Wing Chun kung fu under Ip Man, also known as Yip Man, was a Chinese martial artist, and a master teacher of Wing Chun?", "answer": "Hong Kong", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Steven Sydness was a CEO of what company founded in 1997 in Burlington, Massachusetts?", "answer": "Endurance International Group", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of the movie where Johnny Pacar starred is a 2005 Disney Channel Original Movie?", "answer": "Now You See It...", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "George Howard, 4th Earl of Suffolk, was the son of which English nobleman and politician?", "answer": "Theophilus Howard, 2nd Earl of Suffolk", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the American politician from Illinois died who defeated Charles Harting Percy in 1985?", "answer": "December 9, 2003", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which country is the home stadium of the Wigan Warriors?", "answer": "England", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Lawyer M