s Wild", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Cap Stubbs and Tippie was a syndicated newspaper comic strip created by the cartoonist Frances Edwina Dumm, was a writer-artist who drew the comic strip \"Cap Stubbs and Tippie\" for how long?", "answer": "six decades", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What town did Nate Leaman coach the Union Dutchmen?", "answer": "Schenectady", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who has appeared with The Black Eyed Peas and is an artist with Uprise Music?", "answer": "Kryoman", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Die Hochzeit des Camacho (\"Comacho's Wedding\") is a Singspiel in two acts by Felix Mendelssohn,was a German composer, pianist, organist and conductor of the early Romantic period, and died on which date?", "answer": "4 November 1847", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What movie was created with the skills of Don L. Harper and produced by Walt Disney Pictures?", "answer": "National Treasure", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the Macau, China based resort named after the finance chair of the Republican Nation Committee (RNC)?", "answer": "Wynn Palace", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What 1997 computer game had a sequel published by Activision in 1999 for Microsoft Windows?", "answer": "Heavy Gear", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which English actor starred along with Chris Hemsworth and Natalie Portman in Thor: The Dark World?", "answer": "Adewale Akinnuoye-Agbaje", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which British, American, Indian, German, Romantic, Sports and Indian-Themed, Comedy, Drama, Family film had a song from Malkit Singh in it?", "answer": "Bend It Like Beckham", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"I Believe I Can Fly\" is a song from the soundtrack of a film directed by who ?", "answer": "Joe Pytka", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which major Egyptian deity had a priest whose daughter's mummified remains are in the Ulster Museum in Belfast?", "answer": "Amun", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "what does Jim Ryan and Rod Blagojevich have in common?", "answer": "American politician", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which is a film magazine, Kilobaud Microcomputing or Premiere?", "answer": "Premiere", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What boy band from Los Angeles, California appears on the Mulan soundtrack?", "answer": "98 Degrees", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The author of 1957 novel Atlas Shrugged, had a documentary film written, produced and directed by Michael Paxton, in what year?", "answer": "1996", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what county in New Hampshire had significant development in the second half of the 19th century and first decades of the 20th?", "answer": "Merrimack County", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "For how many years did the animal who had a role in 2010 FIFA world cup as Sonny Wool in 2011 Rugby world cup live ?", "answer": "(26 January 2008 \u2013 26 October 2010)", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Lupita Jones was an actress, director, and beauty queen who competed in a competition in 1991 that was held in what theatre located in Las Vegas, Nevada?", "answer": "the Aladdin Theatre", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Based on the 2010 census, what was the population of the town that owns Sugarloaf Regional Airport?", "answer": "761", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What type of music does the radio station WWJD owned by Alice Lloyd College play?", "answer": "Contemporary Christian music", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which national park is in more provinces, Caba\u00f1eros National Park or Atlantic Islands of Galicia National Park", "answer": "Caba\u00f1eros National Park", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In what country is Closeburn railway station located?", "answer": "Scotland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which policy implemented by President Brarack Obama did Cindy Lee Miller Sheenhan object to, regarding his cooperation with Allies, ending of the Iraq war, and killing Osama bin Laden, to name a few details.  ", "answer": "The foreign policy of Barack Obama", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 1972 Baylor Bears defeated Texas A&M by a score of 15-13 in the rivalry that debuted in what year?", "answer": "1899", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the film in which Jenifer Tilly featured in 1996 ?", "answer": "The Wachowskis", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What American adventure film directed by Barry Levinson portrays Brian Oulton as a pompous character?", "answer": "Young Sherlock Holmes", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the second eldest of the owners of Fanjul Corp. born?", "answer": "1944", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which DIY and DIWO magazine featured Tekla Labs in their publications?", "answer": "MAKE", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which writer served as president of the Eugenics society, Havelock Ellis or Italo Calvino?", "answer": "Havelock Ellis", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What Native American Tribe indigenous of the Great Plains had two chiefs named Satanta and Big Tree?", "answer": "Kiowa", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American television series stars Eddie Jemison and is loosely based on a DC Comics series?", "answer": "IZombie", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Cenotaph is the ninth studio album released by an English musician who became known as the founder of what band?", "answer": "Porcupine Tree", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Tracy Reiner appeared in a movie that tells a fictionalized account of the real-life what?", "answer": "All-American Girls Professional Baseball League", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which English comedian, screenwriter, and actress who has won three BAFTAs, an International Emmy Award, a British Comedy Award, a Rose d'Or Light Entertainment Festival Award, two Writers' Guild of Great Britain Awards, and a People's Choice Award provides a voice in the 2004 American computer-animated fantasy film Shrek 2?", "answer": "Jennifer Saunders", "type": "bridge"}, {"questi