ed in ten languages and released her last album in the 1950s?", "answer": "Dalida", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What station does the show that the actress born on August 31, 1989 air on?", "answer": "KBS2", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the nickname of the basketball team from 1982 to 1984 that included Hakeem Olajuwon? ", "answer": "\"Texas' Tallest Fraternity\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Two Saints Way is a recreated pilgrimage route of 92 miles between the cathedral cities of Chester in Cheshire and Lichfield in Staffordshire, one of the saints referenced are St Werburgh, was an Anglo-Saxon princess who became the patron saint of the city of Chester in Cheshire, her feast day, is which calendar day?", "answer": "3 February.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are The Jesus and Mary Chain and New Politics both from Scotland?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Of Thee I Sing: A Letter to My Daughters is a children's book by former United States President Barack Obama, the stories of thirteen Americans are told in the book, including Jackie Robinson, who was an American professional baseball second baseman who became the first African American, to play in which organization?", "answer": "Major League Baseball (MLB)", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Holmskioldia and Echinocereus both types of plants?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which director has directed 10 feature films including Hadewijch: Wong Jing or Bruno Dumont?", "answer": "Bruno Dumont", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which movie was released first, My Favorite Martian or The Shaggy Dog?", "answer": "My Favorite Martian", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "How many detective novels did the author of the play Black Coffee write ?", "answer": "66", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "During what conflict was Albert Verbrugghe's wife killed?", "answer": "the Katanga conflict", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What type of media does The Ugly Dachshund and The Three Lives of Thomasina have in common?", "answer": "film", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is name of live album performed with the San Francisco Symphony from the band who performed the song \"Fuel\"?", "answer": "S&M", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Milk Duds are manufactured by a company headquartered in what state?", "answer": "Pennsylvania", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which type of horse has been used by both the British Household Cavalry and Anheuser-Busch Brewing Company for commercials?", "answer": "Clydesdales", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which film Babes in Toyland and One of Our Dinosaurs Is Missing was produced first ?", "answer": "Babes in Toyland", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Leslie Pearce and John Ince, have which mutual occupation?", "answer": "film director", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "To satisfy what dynasty, did the Duchy of Pomerania get partitioned several times who was later granted as a whole and the Principality of R\u00fcgen as a fief to the dukes of both Pomerania-Stettin and Pomerania-Wolgast, by a King of Bohemia and the first King of Bohemia to also become Holy Roman Emperor?", "answer": "House of Pomerania dynasty", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What does the German citizen who is one of the two main protagonists is the film The Promise deny?", "answer": "having committed the crime", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " \"Lovertits\" is a song by a musician and performance artist of what nationality?", "answer": "Canadian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was Charles Robert Rattray in a Football League with that was located in Accrington, Lancashire?", "answer": "Accrington Stanley", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Did both bands Short Stack and Poster Children release more than 10 studio albums?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What former 1985 Scottish League Cup Final player managed Machester United from 1986 to 2013?", "answer": "Alex Ferguson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the 2002 science fiction drama film that Natascha McElhone acted in?", "answer": "Steven Soderbergh", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the Russian dramatist who wrote The libretto born?", "answer": "13 May [O.S. 1 May]", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Little Bear Movie is an animated film based on the television series \"Little Bear\", Little Bear is an educational Canadian children's animated series based on the \"Little Bear\" series of books written by who?", "answer": "Else Holmelund Minarik", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who has written more novels, James Der Derian or Chris Bohjalian?", "answer": "Chris Bohjalian", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which South Korean actress born in 1979 appeared in the South Korean television series, \"Whisper\"?", "answer": "Lee Bo-young", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Khadija Sharife is an African journalist and author whose writings have appeared in a Biritish journal of literary essays that is published how often?", "answer": "fortnightly", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Moonraker is the soundtrack to a James Bond film released in what year?", "answer": "1979", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the nationality of the person co-starring with Bharathiraja in Padai Veeran?  ", "answer": "Indian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "General Qadam Shah Shahim resigned after the attack on whose headquarters?", "answer": "the 209 Corps of the Afghan National Army", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Deadly Tower, also known as Sniper, is a 1975 television film, it stars which American actor?", "answer": "Kurt Vogel Russell", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which building, nicknamed the \"Catheral of Art in Mexico\", is located near the Barrio Chino neighborhood?", "answer": "The Palacio de Bellas Artes", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which  German professional racing driver won  2007 Masters of Formula 3 ", "answer": "Nicolas H\