 in World War I? ", "answer": "Frances Mary Gore Micklethwait", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Lauren Pierce Bush, is the CEO and Co-Founder of FEED Projects, she is a daughter of Neil Bush and who?", "answer": "Sharon Bush", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Taylor Swift's song inspired by Drew Hardwich was directed by whom?", "answer": "Trey Fanjoy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Vera Lynn 100 is a compilation album that features collaborations with a an English tenor and actor, notably performing in what?", "answer": "musical theatre", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Treaty of Vienna, concluded on 27 May 1657, was an Austro\u2013Polish alliance during the Second Northern War, the House of Habsburg, also called House of Austria, was one of the most influential and outstanding royal houses of where?", "answer": "Europe", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Scout movement was first introduced in Ethiopia around 1919 and opened a school in 1934 in a city that had how many inhabitants in 2007 ?", "answer": "3,384,569", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The battle Bucephalus died after took place in what modern province of Pakistan?", "answer": "Punjab", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which actress was nominated for three Tony Awards and played the character of Mollie in Take Her, She's Mine?", "answer": "Elizabeth Ashley", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Aside from the British-American computer scientist, physicist, and businessman who wrote the book \"A New Kind of Science\", who designed the Symbolic Manipulation Program?", "answer": "Chris A. Cole", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Tom Noonan and Jonathan Glazer, are in the film industry?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What Polish and naturalized French physicist had a small rocky island near the eastern end of the G\u00e9ologie Archipelago named after her?", "answer": "Marie Sk\u0142odowska Curie", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which American film directed by John McTiern