rton Senna and Roland Ratzenberger, an Austrian racing driver who raced in sports prototype, at which location, two weeks previously?", "answer": "San Marino Grand Prix", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Irish television and radio presenter regularly visits the Dunbrody Country House Hotel?", "answer": "Graham Norton", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Harvest Christian Academy is located along a road that runs parallel to what motorway?", "answer": "Tema Motorway", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Fulk FitzWarin rebelled against what King, who lost the Ducy of Normandy to King Phillip II of France?", "answer": "John", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The second season of the American legal comedy-drama Suits was ordered on August 11, 2011, the season had six series regulars playing employees at the fictional Pearson Hardman law firm in Manhattan, including Rachel Meghan Markle, an American actress, model and humanitarian from which California location?", "answer": "Los Angeles", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Robert Dornhelm and Serguei Kouchnerov both Romanian?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What monument did Sassoon David finance that was commemorating the landing of King George V and Queen Mary on their 1911 visit to India?", "answer": "Gateway of India", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " \"Groovejet \" is a song by Cristiano Spiller that featured an English singer born in which year ?", "answer": "1979", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the  2016 American Christmas comedy that casts include an  American comedian and actress who also starred as Dr. Jillian Holtzmann in the 2016 \"Ghostbusters\" reboot?", "answer": "Josh Gordon and Will Speck", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the co-founder of a brokerage and investment firm on institutional brokerage in Asia-Pacific stock markets? ", "answer": "Gary Coull", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The loch where the Dorback Burn river originates is home to the ruins of what castle?", "answer": "Lochindorb Castle", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What treaty was signed by the United Kingdom and President James Polk?", "answer": "Oregon Treaty", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The male star of the Nativity Story was born in which year ?", "answer": "1979", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which stadium replaced the RCA Dome and hosted the Super Bowl in which the New York Giants defeated the New England Patriots?", "answer": "Lucas Oil Stadium", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who died first, Krzysztof Kie\u015blowski or Thorold Dickinson?", "answer": "Thorold Barron Dickinson", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What role playing game set in Japan was designed by the co-author of Shadowrun?", "answer": "Bushido", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which console was J.B. Harold Murder Club released for that was developed by Hudson Soft?", "answer": "TurboDuo", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the film that Shuna Harwood was nominated for an Academy Award for adapted from?", "answer": "William Shakespeare's play", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Larry Wolgast served in the Cabinet of the 30th Governor of Kansas, from what year to what year?", "answer": "1979 to 1987", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What organization in the film starring English actress and comedian referred to as Miranda center around?", "answer": "CIA", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The USS Florid was laid down at a navy yard with what nickname?", "answer": "\"The Can-Do Shipyard.\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 78th Army Band is an organization of the Army that served during what conflict?", "answer": "World War II", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What movie, starring Ren\u00e9e Zellweger, was based on a book by the director's close friend? ", "answer": "Bridget Jones's Diary", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Giorgio Mazzon, was born in Waltham Cross, located within the metropolitan area of London, the Greater London Urban Area, and the Borough of Broxbourne in where?", "answer": "Hertfordshire", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The I See You Tour was the third concert tour by English indie band The xx, in support of their third studio album which was released through what label?", "answer": "Young Turks", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Johnny M. Hunt is currently the senior pastor at a Baptist church is which city in the Atlanta, Georgia, metropolitan area?", "answer": "Woodstock", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which game was releaed sooner, Downfall or Camelot?", "answer": "Camelot", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The War at Home and Project Grizzly, are films of which genre?", "answer": "documentary", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which magazine Decibel or Skeptic is published more frequently ?", "answer": "Decibel", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What nationality is the concertmaster of the principal opera company in Australia?", "answer": "Irish", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What government operated lottery headquartered in Austin originated the concept for All or Nothing?", "answer": "Texas Lottery", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Dethalbum is the debut album of Dethklok, from what show that aired on Adult Swim from September 23, 2007 - September 7, 2008?", "answer": "Metalocalypse", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Judith Roberts had a role in the 2007 film by the director of what dual nationality?", "answer": "Malaysian-Australian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What hit single was sung by a band created by Jacques Morali and Henri Belolo and was also the title of its eponymous album?", "answer": "Macho Man", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which publication covers a broader range of topics, Cigar Aficionado or Our State?", "answer": "Our State", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who was born earlier, Daniil Kharms or Andr\u00e9 Schwarz-Bart?", "answer": "Daniil Kharms", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "how is Piers Dutton and Norton Priory connected?", "answer": "Monasteries", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Fred G. Meyer's chain of one-stop Fred Meyer superstores spread across the western states, but which state did it originate from?", "answer": "Oregon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the Dutch artist who was part of Art Concret born? ", "answer": "30 August 1883", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "which American professional poker player purchased  LeggoPoker ", "answer": "Phillip Dennis Ivey Jr.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Since 1923 where was the Spengler Cup been held?", "answer": "Eisstadion Davos", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are the Tahltan Bear Dog and Siberian Husky both dogs originating from the same country ?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What year did the Indian film actor who came on It Happens Only in India after the former host was touring Mumbai make his screen debut?", "answer": "2000", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Hangman stars what actress who began her acting career in \"Campfire Tales\"?", "answer": "Amy Smart", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who created the characters which appear in the film series where Hugh Jackman  plays Wolverine ?", "answer": "Stan Lee and Jack Kirby", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Bryce Dejean-Jones played for which basketball team with the fourth highest winning percentage?", "answer": "NCAA Division I", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year did Susan McFadden join the Celtic studio group also featuring Mairead Carlin and Tara McNeill?", "answer": "2012", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Styphelia and Taro are both examples of what?", "answer": "plants", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Were the bands Stone Sour and Thirty Seconds to Mars formed in the same state?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "When was the american rock band hosted at Kongre\u00dfhalle active? ", "answer": "late 1960s and early 1970s", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is the headquarte