o is the father of the current United States ambassador to Russia?", "answer": "Jon Meade Huntsman", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "To Play the King is a 1993 television serial broadcast by  the world's oldest national broadcasting organisation and the largest broadcaster in the world by what?", "answer": "number of employees", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Oxleys Wood is located in a settlement of what origin?", "answer": "Saxon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which star of Lovely But Deadly was born in 1915 ?", "answer": "John Randolph", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Hertford East branch line, and Lea Valley lines, are both in which country? ", "answer": "United Kingdom", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What nationality was the male star of Scarlet Angel? ", "answer": "American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What 1949 movie did the actress born as Maureen FitzSimmons appear in?", "answer": "Father Was a Fullback", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which documentary film was produced first, A Diary for Timothy or The Age of Stupid?", "answer": "A Diary for Timothy", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which magazine was funded in part by a loan from the owner's mother, Airliners or Playboy?", "answer": "Playboy", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Steve Johnson is the current head football coach at a University which also has a second campus in which California city?", "answer": "San Diego", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Alice Normington has worked on the British biographical musical drama about which singer?", "answer": "John Lennon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what country was the Kraftwerk studio album which had the song \"Metal on Metal\" recorded?", "answer": "Germany", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The MGA Sessions is a solo album by Siobhan Fahey, more famous for Shakespear's Sister and which girl group?", "answer": "Bananarama", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What role did the star of Love Rules play in the TV series \