ow was the actress from Scream 3 who is also an anti-vaccine activist on?", "answer": "\"The View\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which album released on September 22, 2017, by the Killers, features the song 'Some Kind of Love'?", "answer": "Wonderful Wonderful", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what building is the sponsor of the 2017\u201318 EuroLeague headquartered?", "answer": "Turkish Airlines General Management Building", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ranulf I, was the count of Caiazzo in the Principality of Capua from about 1078, he also brought the formerly Lombard counties of Alife, Telese and Sant'Agata dei Goti and the castles of Airola and Tocco Caudio under his control, dominating the region between Capua and which city and \"comune\" of Campania, Italy, capital of the province of Benevento, 50 km northeast of Naples?", "answer": "Benevento", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Nobel Prize in Physics was awarded to Carl Edwin Wieman and which German physicist born on October 21, 1957?", "answer": "Wolfgang Ketterle", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Challenger 1 was superseded by a battle tank designed and built by which company ?", "answer": "Vickers Defence Systems", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What character did the actress who played Samantha Carter in the \"Stargate\" television series play in the show \"Sanctuary\"?", "answer": "Helen Magnus", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Murphy's Law featured former members of what band known for \"Victim in Pain\"?", "answer": "Agnostic Front", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Kai is a Japanese actor , what country does the other Kai come from?", "answer": "South Korean", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which magazine was published in London and was influential in the 1840s and 1850s?", "answer": "Punch", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Visitors was directed by a man that died in what year?", "answer": "2003", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Hans Christian Anderson story has been used as a source for multiple television serial episodes?", "answer": "The Emperor's New Clothes", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both RocketMan and The Apple Dumpling Gang Rides Again science fiction films?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Edward F. Cline and Alexander Butler, share which occupation?", "answer": "director", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are Nagisa Oshima and David Hewlett of the same nationality?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Simpsons episode \"The Old Man and the Key\" features which Simpsons family member?", "answer": "Grampa Simpson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was a marathon runner who came first at the Boston Marathon in 1946, Stylianos Kyriakides or 20,000 Leagues Under the Sea?", "answer": "Stylianos \"Stelios\" Kyriakides", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Type 31e frigate, also known as the Type 31 frigate or General Purpose Frigate (GPFF), is a planned class of frigate for the United Kingdom's Royal Navy intended to enter service in the 2020s alongside the more advanced Type 26 frigate, a class of frigate being built for which organization of the United Kingdom?", "answer": "Royal Navy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Alabama Crimson Tide football team's first Heisman Trophy winner plays for what NFL team?", "answer": "New Orleans Saints", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The York River is a 13 mile stream in southeast Maine that flows southeast to the Atlantic Ocean at what town, which is home to three 18-hole golf clubs, four sandy beaches, and Mount Agamenticus?", "answer": "York", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What nationality is the female mixed martial artist that Chris Luttrell is credited with training?", "answer": "Brazilian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Woodstock Opera House is a historical venue for performing arts and receptions located in Woodstock, Illinois, perhaps the most notable performer to grace the stage was Orson Welles, 