r, screenwriter and actor", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Hard Choices is a memoir of former United States Secretary of State Hillary Rodham Clinton, published by Simon & Schuster in 2014, giving her account of which event, where she served as the 67th United States Secretary of State, under President Barack Obama, from 2009 to 2013, overseeing the department that conducted the Foreign policy of Barack Obama?", "answer": "Hillary Rodham Clinton", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Argentine town was the home of the legendary racing driver Juan Manuel Fangio, and has a circuit named after him hosting touring-car and other events?", "answer": "Balcarce", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the movie to which Yolanda Be Cool have a reference scene? ", "answer": "Quentin Tarantino", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were Andrei Bitov and Wilhelm Reich were both prominent authors?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Sadqay Tumhare is produced by a Pakistani born in what year?", "answer": "1971", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which actress born in 1951 starred next to Hart Bochner and Robert Carradine in the 1984 film \"The Sun Also Rises\"?", "answer": "Jane Seymour", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What do the Crash Test Dummies and The Nymphs have in common with each other?", "answer": "rock band", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which broadcasting company owned the website that premiered \"Penelope Princess of Pets\" in 2007?", "answer": "Turner Broadcasting", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which movie has more actors starred in it, The Great Locomotive Chase or Herbie Goes Bananas?", "answer": "Herbie Goes Bananas", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Innocent Man, is a 2012 South Korean television series, stars include which South Korean actress, that first attracted attention in 2008 in her supporting role as a gisaeng in \"Painter of the Wind\"?", "answer": "Moon Chae-won", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "how is Pomegranates and Nicolas Jaar related?", "answer": "album", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were both Inside Out and Hercules made by Walt Disney Pictures?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which world's largest rotating and revolving globe did Globe of Peace  succeeded ", "answer": "Eartha", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Fox and the Hound and The Apple Dumpling Gang, are produced by which organization?", "answer": "Walt Disney Productions", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which Formula One car besides the Tyrrell P34 was one of the most radical entries ever to succeed in F1 competition, that used flat panel heat exchangers? ", "answer": "The Brabham BT46", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What politician served in an electoral division in the state of New South Wales?", "answer": "Michael John Randal MacKellar", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Have Tim Wheeler and Joe Strummer both been members of a band?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "This grandmaster chess player at age 13 surpassed the highest rating in what year?", "answer": "2013", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Northern Ireland international footballer who played with Cliftonville from 1949 won the inaugural winner of Ulster Footballer of the Year for the 1950/51 season?", "answer": "Kevin McGarry", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Agust\u00edn de Iturbide y Green was the adopted son of which Belgian princess?", "answer": "Carlota of Mexico", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Sleeper Agent and Pupil both rock bands?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Near where in Australia did the battle that Mullah Abdullah helped perpetrate take place?", "answer": "Broken Hill, New South Wales", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Borio is a brand of biscuits local to Egypt that is similar to a cookie that has become the best-selling cookie in the United States since its introduction in what year?", "answer": "1912", "type": "bri