am All-NB elections in history.", "answer": "Kobe Bryant", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What actress and produced from Northern Ireland, born 6 May 1960, starred in TV producer Vanessa Greene's 1998 made for television film?", "answer": "Roma Downey", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Manuel Rosas was the youngest goal scorer in World Cup history until the player who scored how many goals in his career broke his record?", "answer": "1281", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what city is the bi-weekly newspaper published whose current owner and editor is Steven Fowle?", "answer": "Portsmouth, New Hampshire", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Animal is a song by which heavy metal band, written by the American songwriter and musician, Blackie Lawless, the song was released as the band's first single?", "answer": "W.A.S.P.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is linfield football club based?", "answer": "Northern Ireland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The American sportscaster Pat Hughes spent 12 years calling games with this broadcaster who played in the American Major League Baseball and now works as a comedian and actor?", "answer": "Bob Uecker", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Fatima Mansions and Dead Sara, have which genre in common?", "answer": "rock", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What did the actor who had his first appearance in \"Chief Surgeon Who?\" play?", "answer": "a cross-dressing corporal", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the nickname of the Western Australian cricket team currently captained by Mitchell Marsh?", "answer": "Western Warriors", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "what is the highest federal court of the United States. who decided the case of United States v. Payner,", "answer": "The Supreme Court", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What style of architecture superseded that of Agecroft Hall?", "answer": "Elizabethan architecture", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Jumeirah Carlton Tower is located near what luxury British department store that was founded in 1831?", "answer": "Harvey Nichols", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Comedy of intrigue is a genre that includes what comedy by William Shakespeare that is thought to have been written in 1598?", "answer": "Much Ado About Nothing", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "what does Exidy Sorcerer and Heathkit H11 have in common?", "answer": "computer", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "When did the Indian-language comedy television series starring Anup Upadhyay first premier?", "answer": "March 02, 2015", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Delegates were a novelty song group who scored a hit in the United States in 1972, Bob and the two record men made a record, with reporters asking questions of current politicians, involved in that year's presidential election, such as Thomas Francis \"Tom\" Eagleton, was a United States Senator from Missouri, serving from 1968 to what year?", "answer": "1987", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Church Age is the fourth album by Mr. Del, as a play on which traditional logo that adorns many hip hop albums, the cover of this album features which warning label first introduced by the Recording Industry Association of America (RIAA) in 1986  logo that says \"Spiritual Advisory Gospel Content\", ", "answer": "Parental Advisory", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which housewife, who had three of her war-time diaries published between 1981-2010, was Housewife, 49 based on?", "answer": "Nella Last", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which flowering plant genus, Pelargonium or Sutherlandia, includes about 200 species of perennials, succulents, and shrubs, commonly known as geraniums?", "answer": "Pelargonium", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "\"Heima\" and \"The Living Planet\" are both what kind of film?", "answer": "documentary", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": " III - Odyssey of the Mind is the sixth album by a German band formed in what city?", "answer": "D\u00fcsseldorf", "type": "b