ring which American actor, director, screenwriter, and produce, his accolades include two Academy Awards, three Golden Globe Awards, two BAFTA Awards and two Screen Actors Guild Awards?", "answer": "Ben Affleck", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Buddy Baker scored which 1977 American animated film from the Walt Disney Company?", "answer": "The Many Adventures of Winnie the Pooh", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born first, Rebecca Miller or Inge Morath?", "answer": "\"Inge\" Morath", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Frank Melville Memorial Park was dedicated to the memory of the son of the businessman active in what location in western Suffolk County, New York?", "answer": "Three Villages", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Azul Linhas A\u00e9reas Brasileiras S/A, is a Brazilian carrier based in Barueri, a suburb of S\u00e3o Paulo, and it was established on May 5, 2008 by which Brazilian-born ntrepreneur who has founded four commercial airlines, Morris Air, Westjet, and JetBlue Airways?", "answer": "David Neeleman", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Roland (Frankish: \"*Hr\u014d\u00feiland\") was a Frankish military leader under Charlemagne, also known as who?", "answer": "Charles the Great", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Savings Bank of South Australia is a division of the bank that has headquarters in what city?", "answer": "Sydney", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What city in Minnesota has an eleven day festival that was impacted adversely by the collapse of a bridge over the Mississippi River in 2007?", "answer": "Minneapolis", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Born in captivity, what lion was introduced into the wild by conservationist George Adamson?", "answer": "Christian the lion", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Svein Mathisen, or \"Matta\" is most associated with the yellow and black of IK Start football club, but which Scottish team did he also play for?", "answer": "Hibernian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who hosted the annual Kids' Choi