r and producer appeared in \"Life as a House\" (2001) and \"American Heist\" (2014)?", "answer": "Hayden Christensen", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What type of industry does Burton L. King and Frank Coraci have in common?", "answer": "film", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which film was released first, Never a Dull Moment or National Treasure?", "answer": "Never a Dull Moment", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "When was the second season of  the American-Canadian television show premiered in which Jennifer Spence has recurring roles and which  is promoted as TV's \"first polyromantic comedy\"?", "answer": "February 14, 2017", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What neoconservative religious journal was written by the film and music critic Armond White?", "answer": "First Things", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "David Feldshuh's play \"Miss Evers' Boys\" is based on an experiment conducted by who?", "answer": "U.S. Public Health Service", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "According to the 2010 census, what was the population of the county which headquarters the DeKalb County School District?", "answer": "691,893", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What American actor received a posthumous credit for a Walt Disney film that was released on January 29, 1959?", "answer": "Robert Wayne Amsberry", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which animal named after Chattanooga's former football coach is a permanent resident in North America?", "answer": "\"Mimus polyglottos\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Sheriff of Lorn was responsible for enforcing law and order in Scotland and would be seated in which castle?", "answer": "Dunollie Castle", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was one of the tallest structure built which is taller than The Milwaukee City Hall and is the seat of government for the city of Philadelphia?", "answer": "1901", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What league is the team that Harry Britter  played on currently in?", "answer": "Australian