k Mall?", "answer": "Interstate 81", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Transparent and Gates of Heaven, have which mutual genre?", "answer": "documentary", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which came first for Buzz Aldrin, the walk on the moon, or being portrayed in a movie?", "answer": "July 21, 1969", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Cedar County was a policital subdivision of a nation that maintains a special relationship with who?", "answer": "both the United States and Oklahoma", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "She's a Woman was credited to the songwriting partnership that published approximately how many songs between 1962 and 1969?", "answer": "180", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which one is a private college, Rose-Hulman Institute of Technology or Boise State University?", "answer": "Rose\u2013Hulman Institute of Technology", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Acaena exigua was endemic to the state that received statehood on what date?", "answer": "August 21, 1959", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year was the play written in which the Third Murderer appears?", "answer": "1606", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "which  amusement ride system was  Adventure Thru Inner Space the first attraction to utilize", "answer": "The Omnimover", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Cerberus's parents are Echidna and who?", "answer": "Typhon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was TV film Jeremiah, starring Patrick Dempsey released?", "answer": "1998", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the eleventh album produced by Iron Maiden that featured Blaze Bayley as vocalist on the hit Futureal? ", "answer": "Virtual XI", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are John Lanchester and David Guterson both writers?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Manning M. Kimmel was a military officer who served on both sides of the American Civil War, as well as the father of what admiral in the United States Navy was the Commander in Chief of the Uni