ots or Chvrches, was founded in Glasgow?", "answer": "Chvrches", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Did Twist or The Pastel Journal come out first?", "answer": "Twist", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who wrote a Latin narrative poem of history from the cosmogonic myth to Caesar?", "answer": "Ovid", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "B\u00e9al na Bl\u00e1th was the site of the assassination of which leading figure in the Irish independence movement?", "answer": "Michael Collins", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "John Edward Sununu (born September 10, 1964) is a former Republican United States Senator from New Hampshire, on November 4, 2008, Sununu lost his re-election bid to which former governor, the senior United States Senator from New Hampshire, since 2009?", "answer": "Cynthia Jeanne Shaheen", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Edward Otto Laumann (born August 31, 1938) is an American sociologist, Laumann earned his Ph.D. in the Harvard Department of Social Relations in 1964, where he studied under Talcott Parsons, an American sociologist of the classical tradition, best known for his what, and structural functionalism?", "answer": "social action theory", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the  Soviet, Russian and American theoretical physicist died who describe the magnetic phase diagram of type-II superconductors of Onsager?", "answer": "29 March 2017", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "English cow's-milk cheese from the county of Lancashire includes Bowland cheese, which is a cheese that is mixed with what?", "answer": "apple, sultana and cinnamon prior to setting", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Doomquest establishes which Marvel Comics supervillain, the archenemy of the Fantastic Four?", "answer": "Doctor Doom", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "WPZE (\"\"Praise 102.5\"\") is a radio station located in Atlanta, Georgia, it is assigned Mableton as its city of license, Mableton is a census-designated place in Georgia , United States, in which county?", "answer": "Cobb County", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "For which team does this American football quarterback play who was taken first in the 2010 National Football League Draft?", "answer": "Minnesota Vikings", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What road in the West End of London features the John Lewis department store?", "answer": "Oxford Street", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the chief of this tribal group from whom John Copp purchased the present-day Ridgefield, Connecticut from?", "answer": "Dwaine Perry", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both genus, Goldenseal and Breynia, endemic to the same continent ?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In which year were the Back to the Future rides at both Universal Studios theme parks replaced?", "answer": "2008", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were both Javier Frana and Anders J\u00e4rryd professional tennis players?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What Graham King produced and GK Films financed film went on to gross $278 million at the worldwide box office?", "answer": "The Tourist", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Jeep Cherokee was originally sold as a variant of the first what?", "answer": "luxury 4x4", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who build the transportation commonly used on Melbourne's traditional main street?", "answer": "Melbourne & Metropolitan Tramways Board", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which school located at Korle Bu Teaching Hospital employed Charles Odamtten Easmon?", "answer": "University of Ghana Medical School", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Did the Second Battle of the Marne occur prior to the Battle of Pusan Perimeter?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are Santorini and Cosmic Encounter both board games?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which Italian European Space Agency astronaut holds the record for the longest uninterrupted spaceflight of a European astronaut (199 days,