dger, or Don Siegel?", "answer": "Clarence G. Badger", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "St Boniface's Church stands prominently in the village of Bunbury, Cheshire, England, Bunbury is a village and civil parish in the unitary authority of Cheshire East and the ceremonial county of Cheshire, England, south of Tarporley, north west of where , and on the Shropshire Union Canal?", "answer": "Nantwich", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed a film starring Bae Doo-Na with The Wachowskis?", "answer": "Tom Tykwer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Range Regional Airport and Buffalo Niagara International Airport both located in the US?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who was a nomination announcer at the 68th Golden Globe Awards and also played Joey Potter on Dawson's Creek?", "answer": "Katie Holmes", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which noblewoman who inherited her title after the death of her father in the late 1400s signed an instrument that gave the provinces and towns such as Flanders local rights?", "answer": "Mary of Burgundy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who did the performer on Breakthrough co-star with on \"Terra Nova\"?", "answer": "Maddy Shannon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Kelly Sheehan wrote songs for which rapper and former backing singer?", "answer": "Mary Jane Blige", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which rock band was founded by two brothers, Pedro the Lion or Half Japanese?", "answer": "Half Japanese", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What Tata Group joint venture featured Xerxes Desai as it's first managing director?", "answer": "Titan Company", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What type of inquiry does University of Dayton and University of Alaska Fairbanks have in common?", "answer": "research", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What village forms part of the Milton Ulladulla urban area in the southern Shoalhaven in to the narrow coastal belt from Sydney in the north to the border with Victoria in the south in the south-eastern part of the State of New South Wales, Australia?", "answer": "Kings Point", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who wrote one of Jaume Collet-Serra's action-thrillers?", "answer": "Byron Willinger and Philip", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The composer that scored the film \"The Accidental Tourist\" was the Boston Pops' principal conductor during what years?", "answer": "1980 to 1993", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What country music singer born randy bruce trawick topped the charts with ray scotts pray for the fish?", "answer": "Randy Travis", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "English folklore is the folk tradition which has developed in England over a number of centuries, from such obvious manifestations as the traditional Robin Hood tales, the Brythonic-inspired Arthurian legend, to contemporary urban legends and facets of cryptozoology such as the Beast of Bodmin Moor, a phantom wild cat purported to live in Cornwall, in which country?", "answer": "England", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Baldwin City Signal was published by The World Company in a city that is the sixth largest city in Kansas, and is the county seat of what county?", "answer": "Douglas County", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Waterboro Grange, No. 432 is a building located in which Maine county?", "answer": "York", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "the episode aired on May 3, 2006", "answer": "on May 3, 2006", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What film first attracted attention for this actress who also starred in Over the Rainbow?", "answer": "Voice", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Migliorino Ubaldini designed fortifications for the castle in what Scottish county?", "answer": "East Lothian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Li Dawei is also a columnist for a magazine whose name means what in English?", "answer": "\"Finance and Economics Magazine\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Soviet mathmatician won a Nobel Prize, Alexander Gelfond or Nikolay Bogolyubov?", "answer": "Alexander Osipovich Gelfond", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which Ukrainian-born American ballet dancer is remembered for his long association with a musical based on Lynn Riggs' 1931 play, \"Green Grow the Lilacs\"?", "answer": "Vladimir Kostenko", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the middle name of the husband of Sylvia Fine?", "answer": "Daniel", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The actor that plays the title role in the 2011 film \"Conan the Barbarian\" played what role on \"Game of Thrones\"? ", "answer": "Khal Drogo", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What movie starred both Alicia Vikander and Colin Morgan?", "answer": "\"Testament of Youth\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Carbon Copy stars what American actor and musician whose most acclaimed roles include Ship of Fools and King Rat?", "answer": "George Segal Jr.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which genus can be found on the most continents, Hechtia or Zantedeschia?", "answer": "Zantedeschia", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Femina Miss India 2017 was the 54th edition of the Femina Miss India beauty pageant, which Indian model was crowned?", "answer": "Manushi Chhillar", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the first online casino, also known as virtual casinos, started allowing for online gambling?", "answer": "1994", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Protectworth Tavern is located in what county?", "answer": "Sullivan County", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the person born whose work inspired Also sprach Zarathustra?", "answer": "15 October 1844", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who played for Real Madrid as a forward and has a yearly, friendly tournament named after him?", "answer": "Santiago Bernab\u00e9u de Yeste", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What act of denying the genocide of Jews has the Nation of Islam been considered doing?", "answer": "Holocaust denial", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Is Levon Mkrtchyan of the