um which also contains the Niobid Krater?", "answer": "Approximately 38,000", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Bruce C. McKenna was a researcher on the miniseries that premiered in the US on what date?", "answer": "March 14, 2010", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Film-Makers' Cooperative a.k.a. he New American Cinema Group is an artist-run, non-profit organization founded in which year, in New York City by Jonas Mekas?", "answer": "1962", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Kim S\u014fng-ae is the wife of which leader of North Korea who died in 1994? ", "answer": "Kim Il-sung", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the Chancellor of Germany that Alfred Delp was falsely accused of attempting to overthrow?", "answer": "Adolf Hitler", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The D.C. Lottery (official name District of Columbia Lottery & Charitable Games Control Board) is run by the government of Washington, DC, the capital of the US, games offered include which multi-state lottery game administered by the Iowa-based Multi-State Lottery Association (MUSL), which is best known for operating the Mega Millions and Powerball games?", "answer": "Hot Lotto", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Serianna is a band of what genre that combines elements of heavy metal and hardcore punk?", "answer": "Metalcore", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which President of the Ultimate Fighting Championship has grown it into a globally popular enterprise and recruited famous fighters such as Devin Clark?", "answer": "Dana White", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What town is 5 miles south west of the town where the Winterton and Thealby railway station is built?", "answer": "Scunthorpe", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of these belongs in the Cyperaceae family, Uncinia or Woodsia?", "answer": "Uncinia", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Name the American theoretical physicist, mathematician, and string theorist who has been professor at Columbia University since 1996 and who wrote the b