r": "Alma, Kansas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What American actor, playwright, director and producer, best known for playing Morpheus in \"The Matrix Trilogy\" also starred as Dr. Joshua Larabee in the 2006 film Akeelah and the Bee?", "answer": "Laurence Fishburne", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "what is also called net's tongue and used in the garnish \u00c0 la zingara?", "answer": "Beef tongue", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Domingo Jes\u00fas Ram\u00f3n Menargues, a retired long-distance runner from Spain, was born in Crevillente, in which city and port in Spain on the Costa Blanca, the capital of the province of the same name, and of the comarca of Alacant\u00ed, in the south of the Valencian Community, both the Spanish and Valencian being official names?", "answer": "Alicante", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What band that Jens Bogren worked with was originally called \"Inferior Breed\"?", "answer": "Soilwork", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 2007 Rose Bowl included a player of the game who now plays as inside linebacker for what NFL team?", "answer": "Houston Texans", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What album by the Kronos quartet featured a composition from an Austrian composer who lived from 3 December 1883 to 15 September 1945?", "answer": "Winter Was Hard", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The actress born in 1871 who starred in the 1927 film Land of Hope and Glory married whom in 1893?", "answer": "Seymour Hicks", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the most populous county in New Jersey and has Barnstable Academy as one of its institutions?", "answer": "Bergen County", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Kidz Crewe made a national appearance on the television show hosted by which star of \"Keeping Up with the Kardashians\"?", "answer": "Kristen Mary Jenner", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "what does Sinbad and Sergeant Stubby have in common?", "answer": "dog", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What river in south Central America saw a battle fought on its right bank on 19 December 1810", "answer": "Paran\u00e1 River", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who drafted the Act which lead to the imprisonment and deaths of Joseph and Michael Hofer?", "answer": "Hugh S. Johnson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Both Nalini by Day, Nancy by Night and Capturing the Friedmans are what type of films?", "answer": "documentary film", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In what year was the author of the book subtitled \"Growth Without Compromising Your Message & Mission\" born?", "answer": "1954", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the name of first husband of the character that Judy Catherine Claire Parfitt played in Tony Richardson's 1969 film adaption of \"Hamlet\".", "answer": "King Hamlet", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Huh Jung's second feature film starred which two actors?", "answer": "Yum Jung-ah and Park Hyuk-kwon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the director of the Canadian comedy horror monster movie, in which the actress who played the role of Dinah Lance on the television series \"Birds of Prey\", played a role?", "answer": "Jon Knautz", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ernst John von Freyend served during World War II as the adjutant to a Field Marshal born in which year ?", "answer": "1882", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Geoff Boss won a race in which city, 22 miles from Lake Tahoe?", "answer": "Reno", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Fever Pitch was the final film for the director who shot the film based on the non-fiction novel by whom?", "answer": "Truman Capote", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What group was tasked with making nuclear weapons in April of 1939, and was sabotaged by the Allied Nations in World War II?", "answer": "The German nuclear weapon project", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When did the Football League that Stuart Myall began his career in debut?", "answer": "the 2017\u201318 season", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Carver Glacier is on t