ng Council in September 2003, served in the government of the fifth President of where?", "answer": "Iraq", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Matilde Camus and Sara Teasdale, have which occupation in common?", "answer": "poet", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What fictional Supervillain that is one of the world's first mutants caused damaged that North America needed to recover from in Age of Apocalypse", "answer": "Apocalypse", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Since when he Francis Wallace Grenfell's rank in the British Army been the highest rank?", "answer": "1736", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which magazine closed in 2014 was rival to Zip?", "answer": "Nuts", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year was the American death metal band who recently ended their career-long record deal with Roadrunner Records formed?", "answer": "1987", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are  Hanzhong and Pingliang in the same province?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Salmita Mine and Tundra Mine, produced what?", "answer": "gold", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": " \"With a Little Help from My Friends\" is a song by the Beatles, written by which English singer-songwriter, multi-instrumentalist, and composer, from the album \"Sgt. Pepper's Lonely Hearts Club Band\" issued worldwide in June 1967?", "answer": "James Paul McCartney", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the creator of Paddy's TV Guide born? ", "answer": "14 August 1973", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "X-15 is a film that fictionalized the research rocket that set speed records in what decade?", "answer": "1960s", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Army of Anyone and the Goo Goo Dolls played what genre of Music?", "answer": "rock", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "When the park founded by George Millay announced addition of the Aquatica water park to its adventure park family", "answer": "March 5, 2007", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the paternal grandfath