rk?", "answer": "The Snowman", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Papal conclave was convened to elect a pope following a resignation was first announced on the morning of what date?", "answer": "11 February 2013", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are B\u00e9la Ga\u00e1l and Quentin Tarantino both American directors?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "After what year did the Canadarm become paired with the Orbiter Boom Sensor System?", "answer": "February 1, 2003", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What profession does Alex Borstein do?", "answer": "comedian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Demetress Carte Bell, is the alleged son of a former basketball star that played for the Utah Jazz and went by what nickname?", "answer": "The Mailman", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jon Hunter Spence's 2003 biography was adapted into a British-Irish biographical romantic drama directed by who?", "answer": "Julian Jarrold", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the wife of the prince who was the victor of the battle that is celebrated in part by a series of parades known as \"Orange walks\"?", "answer": "Mary II", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the director of the 2013 South Korean disaster film in which Park Min-ha plays a role?", "answer": "Kim Sung-su", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American Football wide receiver who formerly played for Florida State University, East Mississippi Community College and Auburn University did Buddy Stephens coach?", "answer": "John Franklin III", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Mexican Kickapoo also have a tribe in this state, home to one of three Federally recognized tribes of Kickapoo people?", "answer": "Kansas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the official name of the country where the Manzini Wanderers are based?", "answer": "the Kingdom of Eswatini", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of the following is named after a Swedish medical doctor and botanist: Bromelia or Prunella?