ilms such as \"Sex Drive\", a sex comedy film about a high school graduate who goes on a road trip to have sex with a girl he met online released in what year?", "answer": "2008", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which magazine was published for a longer time, Godey's Lady's Book or Lear's?", "answer": "Godey's Lady's Book", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who wrote The Beauty Queen of Leenane and has dual citizenships in Britian and Ireland?", "answer": "Martin McDonagh", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both Idlewild and 7 Year Bitch rock bands?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which group was first formed between Dinosaur Pile-Up and Enanitos Verdes?", "answer": "Enanitos Verdes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What musical stars Sean Ryan Fox from \"Henry Danger\" and is based on the famous book that tells the story of a mischievous yet innocent little boy who can fly, and has many adventures on the island of Neverland?", "answer": "Jake and the Never Land Pirates", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What album is considered one of the greatest of hip-hop history and who's title originates from a 1978 martial arts film?", "answer": "Enter the Wu-Tang", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Dyro has released an official remix of a Rihanna song from what album?", "answer": "\"Unapologetic\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of this high-performance version of the 6 series coupe/ convertible, which appeared on the Moscow BMW billboard?", "answer": "BMW M6", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What employee owned supermarket chain anchors the Gateway Town Center in Jacksonville, Florida?", "answer": "Publix", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Great Limber is situated 8 miles east from a town with how many households according to the 2001 UK census ?", "answer": "2,213", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the first album by the American alternative Southern rap quartet, who are best known for their singles 'Po' Folks' and 'Good Day' and who had a second album by the name Wooden Leather?", "answer": "Watermelon, Chicken & Gritz", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "This American artist made the Billboard top 25 and was a well known YouTuber and also for her participation in which NBC singing competition? ", "answer": "The Voice", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A football team known as the Ducks represented which University in 2000, and included Joey Harrington the Detroit Lions professional?", "answer": "University of Oregon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 2017-2018 Phoenix Suns selected the player who played for what college team with the #4 selection in the Draft?", "answer": "Kansas Jayhawks", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ann-Margaret, a Swedish-American actress, singer, and dancer starred in what movie with Walter Matthau?", "answer": "\"I Ought to Be in Pictures\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Question:What station did Pierre Perifel's Annie award winning short broadcast on?", "answer": "NBC", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "George Newhouse was the Labor candidate for the seat that was first proclaimed in what year?", "answer": "1900", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Rapha\u00ebl Colantonio is co-creator of a stealth action-adventure video game set in what fictional city?", "answer": "Dunwall", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born in 1824 and served in a regiment of the United States Army currently stationed at Fort Hood, Texas?", "answer": "Robert Murray Morris", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the broadcasting location of the program on which the music video for the song \"Out of the Woods\" premiered?", "answer": "New York City's Times Square", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Between Yam and Pueraria, which flower is used in traditional Chinese medicine?", "answer": "Pueraria", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What profession does Action at a distance and Albert Einstein have in common?", "answer": "physicist", "type":