ned by what company?", "answer": "Simon Property Group", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was a British Black and White film released that starred a famous English actor, filmmaker, entrepeneur and politician that died in 2014?", "answer": "1946", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Y.A.L.A.\" is a song by recording artist M.I.A. from her fourth album \"Matangi\", released in which year?", "answer": "2013", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "why is fiberglass and carbon composite material in the Saqr models stealthy?", "answer": "reduce reflection/emission of radar, infrared, visible light, radio-frequency (RF) spectrum, and audio, collectively known as stealth technology.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "in 2013, The Longhorns were led by a coach born in which year?", "answer": "1951", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which was built first, Central Park Tower or Paramount Plaza?", "answer": "Paramount Plaza", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What singer, best known for his recording of the song \"Raindrops Keep Fallin' on My Head\", had his single \"Most of All\" reach #2 on the \"Billboard\" Adult Contemporary singles chart in 1970?", "answer": "B. J. Thomas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "George Vjestica performed with a band on the album \"Push the Sky Away\" that was formed in Australia in what year?", "answer": "1983", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Brighton railway station is located on what kind of line?", "answer": "a suburban commuter line", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the character played by Chloe Bennet that was auditioned for my Parisa Fakhri?", "answer": "Daisy Johnson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which actor, whose real name is Emanuel Hirsch Cohen, starred in the 1981 action film Lovely But Deadly?", "answer": "John Randolph", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born first, Pepper Keenan or Lou Reed?", "answer": "Lewis Allan Reed", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The actor who appeared in every episode of \"House\", season 6 is of what descent?", "answer": "English", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Name the 2005 romantic comedy written by the writer of \"What Happens In Vegas\" and based on a novel by Elizabeth Young titled \"Asking For Trouble\".", "answer": "The Wedding Date", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which famous American band was formed in the Upper Midwest, The Verve Pipe or Candlelight Red?", "answer": "The Verve Pipe", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In what location in Lincolnshire can you find the historic Jew's House?", "answer": "Steep Hill is a popular tourist street in the historic city of Lincoln", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the most recent publication date for the games Masterpiece and Mutant Meeples?", "answer": "2012", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "A diced radish kimchi that is a popular side dish, does not contain a traditional type of Chinese cabbage that originates near the Beijing region of China, but is replaced with what?", "answer": "Korean radish", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which concept that was similar to  Type 2 Ho-I was developed in the late  1930s?", "answer": "Panzer IV", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American production duo consisting of Pharrell Williams and Chad Hugo also produced the LL Cool J's unsuccessful tenth album \"10\"?", "answer": "The Neptunes", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "For what two teams did both Billy Truax and Lance Rentzel both play?", "answer": "Los Angeles Rams and the Dallas Cowboys", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who's net worth is US$950 million, Marcel Duchamp or Stephen Chow?", "answer": "Stephen Chow Sing-chi", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "\"Winnie the Pooh\" is the title song for the franchise of the same name, a music video was released for this version and it was included in The Many Adventures of Winnie the Pooh,  an American animated film produced by Walt Disney Productions and distributed by Buena Vista Distribution, released in