r that was first introduced in 1973, is manufactured where? ", "answer": "Hermosillo Stamping & Assembly plant", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What type of art, best known for its visual artworks and writings, did Australian abstract artist Aelita Andre, engage in?", "answer": "Surrealism", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Do Harold Young and David Hayman have the same nationality?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Justin Hurwitz is best known for scoring an American musical romantic comedy-drama film that stars who as a jazz pianist?", "answer": "Ryan Gosling", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many seasons did, the Guard with a FG% around .420, play in the NBA ?", "answer": "14 seasons", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which project of the Future and Emerging technologies projects aims to create a digital reconstruction of the brain by reverse-engineering mammalian brain circuitry?", "answer": "Blue Brain Project", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which author was also a soldier, James M. Cain or Alain-Fournier?", "answer": "Alain-Fournier", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In multiplicibus curis and the 1948 Arab\u2013Israeli War speaks to what other war in regards to conflict?", "answer": "1948 Palestine war", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year did the father of Marietta Robusti die?", "answer": "1594", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the occupation of both  Nelson DeMille and Imre Kert\u00e9sz?", "answer": "author", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Liam Aiken played Klaus Baudelaire in the movie that was an adaptation of which three novels?", "answer": "\"The Bad Beginning\", \"The Reptile Room\", and \"The Wide Window\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Geneva Carr, who starred in the 2012 American superhero comedy film Alter Egos, was born in what year?", "answer": "1971", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are the Schapendoes and the Border Collie both sporting dogs?", "answer": "no", "type": "compariso