hat collection of whimsical poems by T. S. Eliot featured the poem Gus: The Theatre Cat?", "answer": "Old Possum's Book of Practical Cats", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Joseph Dalry \"Swede\" Alexander was the head coach at a private four-year co-educational liberal arts college on a campus of how many acres?", "answer": "1000", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what city is Beautiful Indonesia Miniature Park located?", "answer": "Jakarta", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 161st New York Volunteer Infantry Regiment participated in a war that began shortly after which presidents inaguration?", "answer": "Abraham Lincoln", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jonathan Martinez Florencio, is a multiple-award winning composer, audio engineer and record producer, he attended which public high school located on a 21 acre campus in Bellmore, New York, United States?", "answer": "Wellington C. Mepham High School", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "R\u00f3mulo M\u00e9ndez refereed in what 24 team format soccer tournament?", "answer": "1986 FIFA World Cup", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Marcin Kromer, was Prince-Bishop of Warmia (Ermland), a Polish cartographer, diplomat and historian in the Kingdom of Poland and later in the Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth, he was a personal secretary to two Kings of Poland, Sigismund II Augustus and Sigismund I of Poland, of the Jagiellon dynasty, reigned as King of Poland and also as the Grand Duke of Lithuania, during which time span?", "answer": "1506 until 1548", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "XII is an album by a country music singer that has released how many studio albums?", "answer": "10", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Sandra Dallas and Dee Brown, are of which nationality?", "answer": "American", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Video game, Summer Games, was released in 1984 for what home video game console, released on September 11, 1977?", "answer": "Atari 2600", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the title o