ier National Park", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What English indie rock band formed in 2002 had their song called \"Light the Night\" featured in the 2012 animated short film, The Snowman and the Snowdog?", "answer": "Razorlight", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was the base of the professional baseball team in which the American manager in Major League Baseball for the Cleveland Indians played?", "answer": "Homestead, Pennsylvania", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who were originally members of the 10th Cavalry Regiment of the United States Army, and included William H. Thompkins, a recipient of the Medal of Honor, for his actions in the Spanish-American War?", "answer": "Buffalo Soldier", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The actress who starred in the episode \"Clear\" of the series \"The Walking Dead\" was also the writer of what Tony Award-winning play?", "answer": "Eclipsed", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the upper chamber of the United States Congress?", "answer": "The United States Senate", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which star from Too Good to Be True passed away on March 17, 2016 ?", "answer": "Larry Drake", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The actor that plays Captain Jack Sparrow in \"Pirates of the Caribbean: On Stranger Tides\" has won a Screen Actors Guild Award in what category?", "answer": "Best Actor", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which gender is the main focus of both Woman's Journal and Avantages?", "answer": "women", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Frans Hoek is a Dutch football coach and former player the worked with \u0141ukasz Fabia\u0144ski, who plays what position?", "answer": "goalkeeper", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is Agostino Vallini in relation to the place commonly known as Lateran Basilica?", "answer": "Archpriest emeritus", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Richard Reeve Baxter, was a widely published American jurist and from what year, until his death the preeminent figure on the law o