ublic Enemies?", "answer": "Superman/Batman: Public Enemies", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "what is the nationality of the 2012 Lenox Industrial Tools 301 third finisher ?", "answer": "American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the birthdate of the founder of MAD Symposium?", "answer": "16 December 1977", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Nadsat plays a fictional character is in both Anthony Burgess's novel and the movie adaption directed by Stanley Kubrick?", "answer": "A Clockwork Orange", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ernest Augustus Anderson  was installed in Hay, New South Wales as the second Anglican Bishop of the Diocese of Riverina, Hay is a town in the western Riverina region of south western New South Wales, in which country?", "answer": "Australia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jonah Anthony Bolden, is an Australian professional basketball player for Maccabi Tel Aviv, is a professional basketball club based in Tel Aviv, in which country?", "answer": "Israel", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What city was Tomas Swartwout born in that was previously known as Beverwijck?", "answer": "Albany, New York", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What car is based on the full-size Blazer?", "answer": "Hummer H2", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Billy Bragg and the group Arcane Roots were both from what country?", "answer": "England", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Masjid al-Hisn was built by a caliph who ruled between what years ?", "answer": "from 717 to 720", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The host of the 8th AVN Awards attended what university?", "answer": "University of Houston", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What show did Ta-Ronce Allen, Raymond Allen and Norman Lear work together on?", "answer": "Good Times", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the stadium owned by the State of Georgia where LSU defeated Tennessee to keep them from their second straight BCS National Championship Game appearance?", "answer": "Georgia Dome", "