 "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What race was won by a driver born on September 20, 1975?", "answer": "The 2015 Firestone Grand Prix of St. Petersburg", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Knife Edge Two Piece 1962\u201365 is an abstract bronze sculpture by Henry Moore, three casts are on public display, one at which garden at the area, also known also as the John D. Rockefeller Estate, is a 40-room National Trust house in Westchester County, New York?", "answer": "Kykuit", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Robert Zickert plays for the football club that is near what major city?", "answer": "Leipzig", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Daniel Trevor \"Danny\" Kedwell, is an English footballer who plays as a forward for which club, currently named the Vanarama National League for sponsorship reasons, is the top division of the National League in English football?", "answer": "Ebbsfleet United", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which station airs The Shareef Show Mubarak Ho hosted by Umer Shareef?", "answer": "Geo TV", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What show a host of My Bare Lady was famous for has aired on the US network Ovation since 28 September 2014?", "answer": "Pineapple Dance Studios\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Between the two writers Ferenc Moln\u00e1r and Karen Joy Fowler, who was born earlier?", "answer": "Ferenc Moln\u00e1r", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which film was created first out of Unidentified Flying Oddball and The BFG?", "answer": "Unidentified Flying Oddball", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who is the lead singer of a rock band that created an album called \"Oracular Spectacular?\"", "answer": "Andrew VanWyngarden", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What two rivers converge near the city where the Eugene Public Library is located? ", "answer": "the McKenzie and Willamette Rivers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What song included in Megamix was originally written and recorded by The Melodians?", "answer": "Rivers of Babylon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the act which changed the collective noun of the group Byron Chief-Moon identifies with?", "answer": "Constitution Act 1982", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the 2007 American adventure comedy-drama film in which the Indian film actor who Marked his screen debut in 1988 with the Academy Award nominated Salaam Bombay played a cameo role?", "answer": "Wes Anderson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What profession does Chris Buck and Mack V. Wright have in common?", "answer": "film director", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "German Hound and Samoyed are both what?", "answer": "dog", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Israel Theo Hicks and August Wilson were involved with plays depicting what ethnicity?", "answer": "African-American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The type of the novel the 2012 American coming-of-age drama film The Perks of Being a Wallflower is based on is a novel written in what form?", "answer": "a series of documents", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which party did the Prime Minister of Norway belong to when the Tresfjord Bridge was opened to traffic?", "answer": "Conservative Party", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What film, starring the eight year old Matin Rey Tangu, was set in the 1962 Sino-Indian War?", "answer": "Tubelight", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the 2015 population of the largest settlement and administrative centre of Svalbard, Norway, which is also located around Isfjorden, the second longest fjord in the Norwegian archipelago?", "answer": "2,144", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year did the band that features Jesse Hasek on lead vocals release their fourth studio album, Division?", "answer": "2008", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Kerry Condon is the youngest Royal Shakespeare Company actress ever to play a character who is whose daughter?", "answer": "Polonius", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who has captained both Toronto F