nt both writers?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What was Richard Dean Anderson famous from before Stargate?", "answer": "the television series \"MacGyver\" (1985\u20131992)", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which referee for the 135th FA Cup Final is based in Gosforth, Newcastle now?", "answer": "Mark Clattenburg", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Mike DuBose came to the University of Memphis after being the head coach at which college, located in Jackson, Mississippi?", "answer": "Millsaps College", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the part of the Republic of the Marshall Islands inwhich Roi-Namur is an island in its north part ", "answer": "Kwajalein Atoll", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which came first, the movel by Philippa Gregory or the TV drama series of The White Queen?", "answer": "novel", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "On what campus did the chemist that won the 1951 Nobel Prize in Chemistry make his discovery?", "answer": "University of California, Berkeley", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "what does How Does a Moment Last Forever and Beauty and the Beast have in common?", "answer": "soundtrack", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What nationality was the actor who starred with Trevor Howard, Sally Gray and Rosamund John in the film Green for Danger ? ", "answer": "Scottish", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "From where was the Swedish heavy metal band which was compared to Methods to End It All?", "answer": "Stockholm", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which late 1980s live-action film from Walt Disney Pictures did Bruce Rowland appear?", "answer": "Cheetah", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Does Albert Camus or Stella Gibbons have a Nobel Prize rather than 22 novels to their name?", "answer": "Albert Camus", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which 1998 Canadian-American indepent film starred Adam Beach as Victor?", "answer": "Smoke Signals", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the album on which the Beatles covered a song from the album The Fabulous Miracles by The Miracles?", "answer": "With the Beatles", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Louis Leaky encouraged who to work in Rwanda and eventually found Karisoke Research Center?", "answer": "Dian Fossey", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which German \"Schutzstaffel\" (SS) officer and physician in Auschwitz concentration camp worked with Hans Wilhelm Konig?", "answer": "Josef Mengele", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "NU'EST, acronym for New Establish Style Tempo, is a South Korean boy group formed by which organization, in 2012, the group includes Hwang Min-hyun, a South Korean singer-songwriter and actor?", "answer": "Pledis Entertainment", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "William Frederick Varney (October 1, 1884 \u2013 December 13, 1960 Rockville Centre, New York) was an American politician, Rockville Centre is an incorporated village located in which County in New York, in the United States?", "answer": "Nassau", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was the Director of Officials, in the wake of a scandal by a referee born in 1967, born?", "answer": "Brooklyn, New York", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who committed the deadliest school massacre in United States history in 1927?", "answer": "Andrew Kehoe", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the name of the WWE fighter that is brothers with Ranjin Singh and is played by Dalip Singh Rana? ", "answer": "The Great Khali", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Now Baroness Lane-Fox of Soho, CBE, which travel company did this British businesswoman start?", "answer": "lastminute.com", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is the company that won a contract to build an automated monorail for the King Abdullah Financial District based?", "answer": "Montreal, Quebec, Canada", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what film did the lead star of Thor: The Dark World also star in 2013?", "answer": "Rush", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Winter Olympics did Leslie Thomas compete at, where the host city was chosen over Falun and Cortina d'Ampezzo?", "answer": "1988 Winter Olympics", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What 2017 American animated film produced by Warner Bros. is part of the DC Animated Universe?", "answer": "Batman and Harley Quinn", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Canadian band, formed in 1999 in London, Ontario, released their third EP called Imaginary Monsters on August 9, 2011?", "answer": "The Birthday Massacre", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which magazine is twice monthly, Reason or CCM Magazine?", "answer": "CCM Magazine", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Maria s played by Elizabeth De Razzo in which HBO baseball themed comedy series?", "answer": "Eastbound & Down", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Elaine Farrell Wynn, is an American businesswoman, philanthropist and art collector, she co-founded Mirage Resorts and which publicly traded corporation based on the Las Vegas Strip, Nevada that is a developer and operator of high end hotels and casinos?", "answer": "Wynn Resorts", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Actor is known for his role in Love Machine and Tony Rome? ", "answer": "Shecky Greene", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what province was the XXI International AIDS Conference of 2016 held in?", "answer": "KwaZulu-Natal", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the former Brithish soldier who was  first leader of the Ulster Volunteer Force which initiated the 2011 Northern Ireland riots?", "answer": "Gusty Spence", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 1932 German football championship Final was held at the stadium that opened in what year?", "answer": "1928", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Sanford H. Calhoun High School is part of what district that covers the Long Island hamlets of Bellmore, North Bellmore, Merrick, and North Merrick, New York?", "answer": "Bellmore\u2013Merrick Central High School District", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What movie did Bill Stinchcomb star in that featured a large, heavily armored warship?", "answer": "Battleship", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The ninth installment of the game featuring character Heihachi Mishima was published by what company?", "answer": "Bandai Namco Entertainment", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year was the AFC football team founded that Charles Louis Bivins played for?", "answer": "1933", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the nationality of the comedian who made the album Making Lite of Myself?", "answer": "American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Is \"Tommy heavenly6\" a handle or pseudonym for Japanese singer Tomoko Kawase, or Tom Chaplin, the singer from Keane?", "answer": "Tomoko Kawase", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "A Midsummer Night's Dream is a two-act ballet choreographed by George Balanchine to Felix Mendelssohn's composed music of which famous writers play?", "answer": "William Shakespeare", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Minimalists are authors who moved from their hometown to a cabin in the county seat of what Montana county?", "answer": "Granite", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Juan Jos\u00e9 Campanella achieved worldwide fame with the release of this 2009 Argentine-Spanish crime drama  based on what novel", "answer": "\"La pregunta de sus ojos\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the code, defined by International Civil Aviation Organization, for Ridali Airfield?", "answer": "EERI", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the first Master of Emmanuel College, Cambridge which was founded in 1584 by Sir Walter Mildmay, Chancellor of the Exchequer to Elizabeth I?", "answer": "Laurence Chaderton", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Peter Rabbit is an upcoming 2018 3D live-action/CGI animated adventure comedy film written, directed and produced by Will Gluck, the film features voice roles played by Margot Robbie, an Australian actress and producer, who earned her how many Logie Award nominations?", "answer": "two", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What famous composer is related to American professional boxer Barney Ross?", "answer": "Baruch Leib Rosowsky", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What digital audio software came bundled with Linux's Puredyne?", "answer": "Ardour", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is Gilgit called in Wakhi, an Indo-European language in the Eastern Iranian branch of the language family spoken today in Wakhan District, Afghanistan and also in Northern Pakistan, China, and Tajikistan?", "answer": "Gilt", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where did this polar explorer and commander in the Imperial Russian Navy establish an anti-communist government under whom Robert Bitker served during the Russian Revolution of 1917?", "answer": "Siberia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is the college that Stephen Williams is currently coach of located?", "answer": "Adelaide, South Australia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which region did the settlers have conflict with the Mexican government where it escalated to a rebellion led by John Dunn Hunter?", "answer": "Texas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Dennis Anderson is a professional driver known for driving which monster truck considered to be one of the most influential and iconic monster trucks of all time?", "answer": "Grave Digger", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What nationality was the composer of the symphonic poem Prince Rostislav ? ", "answer": "Russian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The actor who won the awards for Best Danish Film and Best Actor in a Supporting Role for \"King's Game\" was born in what city?", "answer": "Copenhagen", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were both Petar B. Vasilev and Ren\u00e9 Laloux involved in the film industry?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Norbert Siegmann seriously injured the current technical director of what?", "answer": "FC St. Pauli", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who assembled the phonograph records that were included aboard both Voyager spacecraft launched in 1977?", "answer": "Carl Edward Sagan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Eden Studios, Inc. is best known for the RPG based on what game system?", "answer": "Unisystem", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year was the director of the 56th episode TV series \"The Vampire Diaries\" born?", "answer": "1956", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the award rewarded by the Saints?", "answer": "Trevor Barker Award", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born first, Celedonio Calatayud or Wilhelm Conrad R\u00f6ntgen?", "answer": "Wilhelm Conrad R\u00f6ntgen", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Hospital serves as a teaching hospital for Georgetown University School of Medicine,  MedStar Washington Hospital Center or Walter Reed Army Medical Center?", "answer": "MedStar Washington Hospital Center", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are both Laizhou and Suixi County, Anhui located in China?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What company is a 1931-born rival promoter to Don King in the 1980's the CEO of?", "answer": "Top Rank", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is in the cast of the 2017 prequel The Prelude that also was the winner of the Mr. Hong Kong pageant?", "answer": "Benjamin Yuen", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who wrote the screenplay for American film director and screenwriter Brian De Palma's \"The Bonfire of the Vanities\"?", "answer": "Michael Cristofer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year was the author of \"The Last Arrow\" born?", "answer": "1950", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What team did the football club that had a goalkeeper born in December of 1953 merge with in 2010?", "answer": "KV Red Star Waasland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Zhongzheng District is a district in Taipei, Republic of China, the late President of the Republic of China was Chiang Kai-shek, who died on which date? ", "answer": "April 5, 1975", "type": "bridge"}, {"ques