uth?", "answer": "Shaw Brothers Studio", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Root Beer Rag is a song from the 1974 albuim by what American pianist?", "answer": "William Martin Joel", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the director of an Astronomy Institute located on an island with an area of 4028 sqmi?", "answer": "G\u00fcnther Hasinger", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the director of the 2016 American biographical black comedy-drama film in which the actor, who earned an Academy Award for his role in \"The Wolf of Wall Street\", played a role?", "answer": "Todd Phillips", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Spanish classical guitarist and composer is acclaimed for the popular opera \"Telemachus on Calypso's Island.\"", "answer": "Fernando Sor", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The novel which had a line from which the title of the album \"Boats Against the Current\" is taken is from what year?", "answer": "1925", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What census designated place features a shopping mall located at corner of Montgomery and Kenwood Roads?", "answer": "Kenwood", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the nationality of the author of \"Not Without Laughter\"?", "answer": "American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What film producer co-created Mickey Mouse along with Ub Iwerks?", "answer": "Walt Disney", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which was founded first, McCall's or Christianity Today?", "answer": "McCall's", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Governance of the Gaza Strip is carried out by the administration whose name translates to what?", "answer": "Islamic Resistance Movement", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is Chadderton located?", "answer": "North West England", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Nominated for an award for \"Who's Afraid of Virginia Woolf,\" what actress starred in a supernatural romantic horror film directed by Karen Mocrieff? ", "answer": "Carrie Alexandra Coon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Her