m was directed by Josh Boone and featured the Ed Sheeran song \"All of the Stars\" over the credits?", "answer": "The Fault in Our Stars", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "This actress and former fashion model is best known for her rols in such movies as \"The Craft\", \"Half Bakes\" and an American black comedy drama film written and directed by who?", "answer": "Gregg Araki", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which show did Lana Golja appear on that was created by the producers of \"Packed to the Rafters\"?", "answer": "Winners & Losers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Irish costume designer is known for her work for the 2008 film \"Brideshead Revisited\"?", "answer": "Eimer N\u00ed Mhaoldomhnaigh", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who, also known as \"The Killer,\" released A Taste of Country in 1970? ", "answer": "Jerry Lee Lewis", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born first, Philip Labonte or Don Dokken?", "answer": "Donald Maynard Dokken", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Adele Romanski is an independent film producer, she is best known for producing the critically acclaimed film, \"Moonlight\" received eight Oscar nominations at the 89th Academy Awards, and took place on which date?", "answer": "February 26, 2017", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Which professional ice hockey team based in Denver, Colorado did Rick E. Berry play with?", "answer": "The Colorado Avalanche", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "what does Rivelin Rocks and A57 road have in common?", "answer": "England", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the nationality of the director of Kickboxer 4: The Aggressor ?", "answer": "American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the Mexican business magnate, investor, and philanthropist that owns the historic building located in downtown Detroit, Michigan built in 1905?", "answer": "Carlos Slim", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Body of Song is the sixth solo album from an American musician principally known for his work with what 1980's band?", "answer": "H\u00fcsker D\u00fc", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what city and state was the American aircraft manufacturer, that specializes in the design and manufacture of ultralight aircraft in the form of plans and kits for amateur construction and ready-to-fly aircraft, based in?", "answer": "Detroit Lakes, Minnesota", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "EuroMillions is a transnational lottery, launched on which date, by the Camelot Group, are the operators of the UK National Lottery?", "answer": "7 February 2004", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Mstislav Rostropovich, Daniil Shafran and Sviatoslav Knushevitsky were leading examples of what kind of musician among 20th century Russians?", "answer": "cellist", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the full name of the top scorer of the 2012-13 Blackpool F.C. season?", "answer": "Thomas Christopher Ince", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Simpsons episode \"The Debarted\" is a parody of a film directed by who?", "answer": "Martin Scorsese", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Soy egg can also be made with a substitute cultivated by coagulating soy milk also known as what ", "answer": "bean curd", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What unique place have Franco Malerba and Bertalan Farkas both traveled to?", "answer": "space", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Operation Falcon Summit was led in a battle fought when?", "answer": "mid-2006", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the Japanese manga series written by Eiichrio Oda and voice-acted by Travis Willingham?", "answer": "One Piece", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Peter Berg, is an American director, actor, producer, and writer of film, television, and music videos, his directorial film works include which 1998 American black comedy film directed by Peter Berg?", "answer": "Very Bad Things", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Brazilian politician was also FIFA World Player of the year, bypassing Dada Maravilha