ve co-ordinator is now their head coach?", "answer": "Paul Chryst", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the physician of Tycho Brahe a Danish nobleman known for his accurate and comprehensive astronomical and planetary observations?", "answer": "John Craig M.D.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the French name for the 1964 French-German romantic musical film directed by the same man who directed Une chambre en ville?", "answer": "French: Les Parapluies de Cherbourg", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which school is located in Kentucky, University of Rochester or Berea College?", "answer": "Berea College", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What ensign, used by Parliment during the Fifties, Sixties, and Seventies in Northern Ireland, was also used to represent Northern Ireland at the 2010 Commonwealth Games?", "answer": "the Ulster Banner", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are  Erica Jong and Nancy Mitford both novelists?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the family of loa that has the Goddess of Love called?", "answer": "Erzulie", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "I Let The Music Speak, is a compilation album by which Swedish mezzo-soprano?", "answer": "Anne Sofie von Otter", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A Bellanca CH-300 Pacemaker airplane had funds raised by the Chicago newspaper that was known in English as?", "answer": "The Lithuanian Daily News", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Lee Gae-byok, is a South Korean film director and screenwriter, Lee debuted with which 2005 South Korean romantic comedy film?", "answer": "The Beast and the Beauty", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the historic prison which has Mansfield Correctional Institution in the adjacent built? ", "answer": "between 1886 and 1910", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where did the company expand that produced 40 million varieties of watches?", "answer": "Marin-Epagnier/Neuch\u00e2tel, Switzerland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Min Yoon-