ie goreng, also known as what, is a flavourful and spicy fried noodle dish, made with thin yellow noodles fried in cooking oil with garlic,and includes Chinese cabbage, a Chinese leaf vegetables often used in Chinese cuisine?", "answer": "bakmi goreng", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Swiss film actress starred in the movie Fun in Acapulco with Elvis Presley? ", "answer": "Ursula Andress", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Liga de Elite and Sporting Clube de Macau compete for which country?", "answer": "Hong Kong", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "About how much oceanfront is included in the coastal region along which the New Jersey Coastal Heritage Trail Route extends? ", "answer": "141 mi", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The English Separatist (born in 1590) originally from the West Riding of Yorkshire wrote about accounts of whom in his renowned journal?", "answer": "Pilgrims", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Inverallochy Castle lies .5 miles south of what z-plan castle that was described as one of the nine castles of the Knuckle?", "answer": "Cairnbulg Castle", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which city is this American rock band that released the song \"Emperor's New Clothes\" from?", "answer": "Las Vegas, Nevada", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Scottish singer and part of The Tourists has The Scumfrog remixed?", "answer": "Ann \"Annie\" Lennox, (born 25 December 1954) is a Scottish singer,", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What academic journal is published by U.S. Army educational institution which grants its graduates a master's degree in Strategic Studies?", "answer": "Parameters", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ur-Nungal of Uruk was the sixth Sumerian ruler in the First Dynasty of Uruk, he was the father of which person that became the seventh Sumerian ruler in the First Dynasty of Uruk?", "answer": "Udul-kalama of Uruk", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How large in area is the studios that were once part of the cemetery where George Ha