e film The Magic Carpet?", "answer": "Raymond Burr", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " No\u00eblle Boisson has won the C\u00e9sar Award for Best Editing for a family drama film directed by who?", "answer": "Jean-Jacques Annaud", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " The Jabberwocky Engine is a Java program whose purpose is to create neologisms of the type used in the poem \"Jabberwocky\"by Lewis Carroll, whose real name is what?", "answer": "Charles Lutwidge Dodgson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the best known name of the voice in an American animated superhero film produced by Warner Bros in 2017?", "answer": "Edward Kenway", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Museum, located in the Bloomsbury area of London was Richard B. Parkinson a curator in the Department of Ancient Egypt and Sudan", "answer": "British Museum", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which U.S. President, the 40, 41, 42nd, was this passage speaking about?", "answer": "40th", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Duke basketball player was All-ACC and plays for the Atlanta Hawks?", "answer": "Quinn Cook", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In 2013, Cami Bradley appeared on a television show that began in what year?", "answer": "2006", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What people principally inhabit the Sahara desert and also live in the Gao Region?", "answer": "The Tuareg people", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What city is an urban contemporary broadcast radio station located in that, as of 2016, had an estimated population of 389,902?", "answer": "Wichita, Kansas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which company contains more household name brands, Newell Brands or Ecolab?", "answer": "Newell Brands", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": " The Sociedad de Beneficencia de Buenos Aires was created by the president of a nation once called what?", "answer": "United Provinces of Rio de la Plata", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the English singer, songwriter and guitarist, best known as the leader of Buzzcocks born who hadcontributions in The Invisible Girls?", "answer": "17 April 1955", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The best selling single of John Lennon's solo career was used as a teference by who to erect a memorial?", "answer": "Yoko Ono", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which genus covers a wider rage of habitation, Basselinia or Crescentia?", "answer": "Crescentia", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who was the 25th Presidente del Consiglio?", "answer": "Ivanoe Bonomi", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What has the man who voiced George in the 2006 version of \"Curious George\" been for most of his career?", "answer": "voice actor", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What country did the 1998 Ariana Afghan Airlines crash happen in?", "answer": "Afghanistan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What airline flies to the Sultan Ismail Petra Airport and is headquartered in Petaling Jaya, Selangor, Malaysia?", "answer": "Malindo Air", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many rounds are in the tournament where Sherron Collins earned three championships?", "answer": "four", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 1932 Nevada Wolf Pack football team represented the University of Nevada located in what city?", "answer": "Reno, Nevada", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who first portrayed the Commander shown in Star Trek Beyond in the original Star Trek media franchise?", "answer": "Leonard Nimoy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "J.D. Fortune and Wes Scantlin, have which occupations in common?", "answer": "singer and songwriter", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Naazim Richardson trained the boxer known for winning gold medal at what 2007 event?", "answer": "Pan Am Games", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Windermere Preparatory school is located in windermere a small town in which county of florida?", "answer": "Orange County", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Jaguar C-XF, was a concept car that was designed to showcase the preliminary 