: "Fish", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who was a German candle maker and was a part of the Anheuser family?", "answer": "Eberhard Anheuser", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Along with the author of the video game Eureka who co-founded the gamebooks \"Fighting Fantasy\"?", "answer": "Steve Jackson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What fundamental law of the Republic of Ireland allowed athletes who participated with Great Britain in the 1976 Winter Paralympics to later elect to hold Irish citizenship?", "answer": "Constitution of Ireland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the aircraft that The Silver Falcons fly introduced?", "answer": "1978", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the University established at which Warren Smith played college football ?", "answer": "1903", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Young Messiah is a 2016 American biblical drama film, directed by Cyrus Nowrasteh, the film stars which English actor, best known for playing Argus Filch, in the \"Harry Potter\" film series?  ", "answer": "David John Bradley", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who founded the company that Saturday Primetime presented by DirecTV appears on?", "answer": "Bill Rasmussen along with his brother Scott and Ed Egan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year was the university the Nevada Wolf Pack men's basketball team represents founded?", "answer": "1874", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "John William Maule Ramsay served as Secretary for Scotland in the administration of a British Liberal statesman and Britian's oldest what?", "answer": "Prime Minister", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Rosario Castellanos and Jodi Picoult, shared which occupation in literature?", "answer": "writer", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What's the former name of the regional airline providing regularly scheduled passenger service at Churchill Falls Airport?", "answer": "Provincial Airlines", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which position in the us military must you be in to be eligible for the achievement medal?", "answer": "junior officers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Name the American actress and singer who starred in the 1997 comedy film Sprung and who is best known for her role as Regina Waters in the FOX series?", "answer": "Tisha Campbell\u2013Martin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which film director lived longer, Andrzej Munk or Tengiz Abuladze?", "answer": "Tengiz Abuladze", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Michael Arbuthnot Ashcroft,  was a code breaker at Bletchley Park during World War II, working in Hut 8 under which English computer scientist, mathematician, logician, cryptanalyst, philosopher and theoretical biologist?", "answer": "Alan Turing", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which late 1950s rock and roll guitarist is Howard Wyeth remembered for working with?", "answer": "Link Wray", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is considered one of the central founders of the science of thermodynamics and is one of the people that the Clausius\u2013Mossotti relation was named after?", "answer": "Rudolf Julius Emanuel Clausius", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What type of media does Death on the Nile and Mia Farrow have in common?", "answer": "film", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Donald Sawyer and Valeria Sarmiento, have which mutual occupations?", "answer": "film director", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "\"Love Put a Song in My Heart\" is a 1975 single by a singer born in what year?", "answer": "1951", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Swedish Livonia, which constituted the southern part of modern Estonia, was fully ceded in what peace treaty between Sweden, the Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth, the Habsburgs and Brandenburg-Prussia?", "answer": "Treaty of Oliva", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of the following was the name of a Brooklyn-based women's magazine, ROCKRGRL or Missbehave?", "answer": "Missbehave", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who is the lead vocalist of the Bow