ny participants did the person who shot Adrian Pracon kill at a summer camp?", "answer": "69", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Bad Biology is a dark horror comedy film directed and produced by Frank Henenlotter and a rapper who signed to what major label at the age of 18?", "answer": "Jive Records", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which county is the oyster river high school located?", "answer": "Strafford County", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which game was released first, Take It Easy or Diplomacy?", "answer": "Diplomacy", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who directed the film Rogue Male staring popular Scottish character actor and West End performer Alastair Sim?", "answer": "Clive Donner", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What 10 year old provided the voice of title character Junior Healy in the USA Network's animated series \"Problem Child\", and was replaced by  Blake Ewing during its 5th season?", "answer": "Benjamin Diskin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Marco Antonio \u00c1vila Garc\u00eda was murdered prior to the Mexican general election, 2012, which is where voters went to do what?", "answer": "to elect, on the federal level", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which is native to Mexico, Sanvitalia or Buckinghamia?", "answer": "Sanvitalia", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "When was the name of the debut single by the group that finished fourth in The X factor and was signed by the company founded as American Record Corporation in 1929?", "answer": "Carry You", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Two Lanes of Freedom included a cameo by which other male country singer on guitar?", "answer": "Keith Urban", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American-born British socialite was Montagu Porch's stepdaughter, and Randolph Churchill's wife?", "answer": "Lady Randolph Churchill", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 2007\u201308 Premier League was sponsored by which British multinational bank?", "answer": "Barclays", "type": "bridge"}, {"question