rd Day and Institute both American Christian rock bands?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In which state is the Aero-propulsion Systems Test Facility located where aircraft propulsion systems are tested in true mission environments without leaving the ground?", "answer": "Tennessee", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was opened just before the First Houses located in Atlanta, Georgia, that replaced a shantytown just south of Georgia Tech along Techwood Drive as America's first what?", "answer": "housing project", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When did the issuers of The Macau Pass begin service?", "answer": "1988", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What 2006 tale of Inspector Clousseau was produced by the same director as the popularly-loved, critically-hated 2003 romantic comedy \u201cJust Married\u201d?", "answer": "The Pink Panther", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Royal Academy of Dramatic Art student stars in Cristiada a 2012 historical war drama film?", "answer": "Peter O'Toole", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which actress born in 1968 appeared on a Danish television show with Peter Mygind?", "answer": "Sofie Gr\u00e5b\u00f8l", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Ocean County seat is home to Artisan's Brewery?", "answer": "Toms River", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What body of water bounds, to the north and west, the region of Australia where the Muccan Station resides?", "answer": "the Indian Ocean", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The romantic comedy film Hairshirt, starring Katie Wright, was released in what year?", "answer": "1998", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The mall, in which General Growth Properties sold one third ownership in 2011, plays concerts during which summer months?", "answer": "May to August", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the former American football coach and a former college baseball player who made Air raid offense popular born? ", "answer": "November 9, 1969", "type": "bridge