 the 2001 film \"Dead Awake\" also starred in \"Threesome\"?", "answer": "Stephen Baldwin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "David Charles Abell is recognised as an authoritative interpreter of the musicals of a composer that has won how many Tony Awards?", "answer": "eight", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which movie and entertainment conglomerate was behind Million Dollar Arm and Herbie Rides Again?", "answer": "Walt Disney", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which shopping and entertainment district in Atlanta, that was first opened in 1969, has the Atlanta Zero Mile Post stone merker in its basement?", "answer": "Underground Atlanta", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Australian politician with a degree in law from the University of Melbourne led the incumbent Liberal Party of Australia to election in 1966? ", "answer": "Harold Holt", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which South Korean television series will be remade into a Philippine movie starring Jennylyn Mercado?", "answer": "\"My Love from the Star\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many seasons did Doug Gilmour play as after being named captain in during the 1994\u201395 Toronto Maple Leafs season?", "answer": "20 seasons", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Whose biography was the basis of the film for which John W. Corso was nominated for an Academy Award in Best Art Direction?", "answer": "Loretta Lynn", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 1998\u201399 NBA season was the Wizards' 38th season in the National Basketball Association, the Wizards continued to under achieve as which American basketball.head coach was fired after a 13\u201319 start?", "answer": "Bernard Tyrone Bickerstaff", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "did both cases United States v. Morrison and McCollum v. Board of Education happen in the same year ?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Hannah Baker played by Katherine Langford in ?", "answer": "Thirteen Reasons Why", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Lonesome Suzie, written and sung by piano player Richard Manuel, was part of the debut album of which group?", "answer": "The Band", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which animated musical fantasy film originally released by RKO Radio Pictures was the second animated feature film by Disney?", "answer": "Snow White", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which genus has more species, Terminalia or Aucuba?", "answer": "Terminalia", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Name the actress who wrote the autobiography \"My Life as a 10-Year-Old Boy\" who was also the voice of Bart Simpson and characters for the shows Todd Flanders and Database?", "answer": "Nancy Jean Cartwright", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "New Scientist and World are both what?", "answer": "magazine", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Maggie Simpson in \"The Longest Daycare\", or simply The Longest Daycare, is an American traditionally animated 3D comedy short film, released in which year, the short originated with \"Simpsons\" producer James L. Brooks, who enlisted long-time veteran of the series, David Silverman, to direct the film, an American animator best known for directing numerous episodes of the animated TV series \"The Simpsons\"?", "answer": "2012", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are  Riverside Church and Trump Tower both skyscrapers?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which major prize did the honorary president of the International Thorium Energy Committee share ?", "answer": "the Nobel Prize in Physics", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was central park in Moscow named after, in 1932, when it opened the world's first children's railway?", "answer": "Gorky Park", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What French film magazine was Pascal Bonitzer a critic for?", "answer": "Cahiers du Cin\u00e9ma", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What city situated at the northern extremity of Brisbane Water, is also where the Central Coast Mariners FC is based?", "answer": "Gosford", "ty