i-Slavery Society included speakers such as the abolitionist lecturer who was born into slavery in what Kentucky county?", "answer": "Montgomery", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What American comedian, actor, poker commentator and professional poker player, starred in the American sitcom Lewis & Clark?", "answer": "Gabe Kaplan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The second Hancock was one of the first 13 frigates of the Continental Navy, and was named for John Hancock, an American merchant, statesman, and prominent Patriot of which event?", "answer": "American Revolution", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What did the American actress and singer that starred in There Goes My Heart play?", "answer": "a wealthy heiress", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Bestgore.com received media attention in 2012 for hosting a video of the murder of an international student of what nationality?", "answer": "Chinese", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The bus line, the Metro Red Line, runs from the shopping mall located in Bloomington, Minnesota, southeast of what junction?", "answer": "Interstate 494 and Minnesota State Highway 77", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which plant grows in East Asia, Aquilegia or Semiarundinaria?", "answer": "Semiarundinaria", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Weinstein Company, a mini-major film studio, founded in New York City by Bob and Harvey Weinstein, retained ownership of Dimension Films after leaving what film distributor?", "answer": "Miramax Films", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who does the player who won the Best Footballer in Asia 2016 play for? ", "answer": "Leicester City", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What kind of compound is Oxalic acid?", "answer": "organic compound", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jean Negulesco and Colin Campbell are both film directors and screenwriters but which is also an actor?", "answer": "Colin Campbell", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the spanish name for the organization that Rafael E. Martinez was a candidate for in 2003?", "answer": "Organizaci\u00f3n de los Estados Americanos", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many series does have the adventure novels who's first novel is The Maze of Bones?", "answer": "five series", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Commenwealth Games athlete also starred in Mary Poppins?", "answer": "Gavin Lee", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " The 1915 Carlisle Indians football team represented what school?", "answer": "Carlisle Indian Industrial School", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who has more scope of profession, Harun Farocki or Boaz Yakin?", "answer": "Harun Farocki", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the seat of the county where Sugarloaf Regional Airport is located?", "answer": "Farmington", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Terttu Nevalainen works on the history of the language that evolved from which dialects brought to Britain in the 5th-7th centuries?", "answer": "Anglo-Frisian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the man who won Irish Presidency and also led the introduction of the Constitution of Ireland?", "answer": "\u00c9amon de Valera", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What animated sitcom did the writer of \"New Leads\"  work on?", "answer": "The Simpsons", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Swiss football club based in Basel did Thomas H\u00e4berli join in July 2000?", "answer": "FC Basel", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A World War II vehicle with the German word for kitten in its name, was a smaller version of the German tank known by American soldiers as what?", "answer": "King Tiger", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Bill Fagerbakke is an American actor and voice actor best known for his role as what fictional character in the American animated television series \"SpongeBob SquarePants\"?", "answer": "Patrick Star", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is an A&R man for the band that Adam Duritz is in?", "answer": "Jack Joseph Puig", "type": "bridge"}, {"ques