y metal band since 2011?", "answer": "Adrenaline Mob", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was Janet Rogers' tribe historically based?", "answer": "the Mohawk Valley", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jimmy Ibbotson former member of American country rock band founded in Long Beach, California in 1966, released his first solo album in what year?", "answer": "1977", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "International Organization for Standardization (ISO)", "answer": "International Organization for Standardization (ISO)", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is the Go-Op's main partner located?", "answer": "Balloon Street, Manchester", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which band The Neighbourhood or Orgy was formed first ?", "answer": "Orgy", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": " Which university, classified as a Research University with very high research activity (RU/VH) by the Carnegie Foundation for the Advancement of Teaching, is The Gilmour B. and Edith Craig MacDonald House is a historic building located?", "answer": "Iowa State University", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which plant genus includes more species, Hedychium or Malephora?", "answer": "Hedychium", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What brother of Sharon Nazarian  is the founder of an entertainment group?", "answer": "Sam Nazarian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed a 2003 film starring Moon So-ri?", "answer": "Im Sang-soo", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "which ITV comedy series starring Nicholas Lyndhurst and Janet Dibley as Ashley and Elaine?", "answer": "The Two of Us", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who replaced Linda Wells at the fashion magazine where Victoria Bartlett was Fashion Editor?", "answer": "Michelle Lee", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Egyptian boxer, Saleh Khoulef, defeated the Ukrainian professional boxer who held the WBA welterweight title from when to when?", "answer": "2009 to 2012", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 1977 Green Bay Packers season included the quarterback who previously played for what other team?", "answer": "Houston Oilers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Zhang Xiaoming as director of theHong Kong and Macau Affairs Office helps connect mainland China to what? ", "answer": "Hong Kong and Macau", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the nickname of the creator of the comic strip character \"Pig-Pen\"?", "answer": "Sparky", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Courtney Kennedy, is an American ice hockey player, she won a bronze medal at the 2006 Winter Olympics, commonly known as Turin 2006 or Torino 2006, was a winter multi-sport event which was held in Turin, Piedmont, Italy during which time span?", "answer": "February 10 to 26, 2006", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of Kanye West's albums features a song touching on his breakup with an American model and actress born in October, 1983?", "answer": "\"Cruel Summer\" (2012)", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Between Saraca indica and Saraca asoca, the sorrow-less\" plant, which is know for its non-clasping bracteoles, lower number of ovules, smaller pods, and more eastern geographic distrubution?", "answer": "Saraca indica", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What edition of the Eurovision Song Contest featured a Lithuanian entry sang by Sasha Son and performed in English with the final verse in Russian?", "answer": "54th", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What park contains the Wild Beast and a 20 acre water park?", "answer": "Canada's Wonderland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Milton Elting Hebald is an artist whose has 23 of his works displayed in public in New York City and at the Port Authority of New York and New Jersey, which is headquartered at what building?", "answer": "World Trade Center", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the common name for members of the Irish Brotherhood led by Charles Guilfoyle Doran in the 19th century?", "answer": "Fenians", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Out of Williamson County Regional Airport and Dothan Regional Airport, which airport is more north on the map?", "answer": "Williamson County Regional Airport", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In which date did the TV show on which Stephen Tobolowsky had the role of Action Jack Barker premier ?", "answer": "April 6, 2014", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the proposed 18-kilometre tollway in Melbourne which will connect the Eastern Freeway with the Western Ring Road and for which the Bendigo street housing campaign, a series of occupations of empty state owned properties began in March 2016?", "answer": "East West Link", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many years old is the stone circle near Penrith in Cumbria?", "answer": "3,500-year-old", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the nationality of the novelist whose eighteenth novel was published in 1976? ", "answer": "Anglo-Irish", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "T3 is located in what theme park formerly owned by Six Flags?", "answer": "Kentucky Kingdom", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year did the National Basketball Association team who was located in Baltimore and had a player named George McLeod fold?", "answer": "1954", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jennifer Spence had a recurring role on which American-Canadian television show about a suburban married couple in a three-way relationship?", "answer": "You Me Her", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which mountain is taller, Saltoro Kangri or Makalu?", "answer": "Makalu", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which of the American professional basketball player for the Dallas Mavericks of the National Basketball Association (NBA) spoke well about  \"The 21 Irrefutable Laws of Leadership\"?", "answer": "Harrison Barnes", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Art Smith was personal chef to a talk show host that was awarded the Presidential Medal of Freedom in what year?", "answer": "2013", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Piquet Sports was created by a brazilian born on which day ?", "answer": "August 17, 1952", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What owner of Avior Regional is based in Barcelona?", "answer": "Avior Airlines", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the wife of the German poet who wrote \"Die L\u00f6sung \"?", "answer": "Helene Weigel", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Los Lobos made a cover of this song which appeared in the 2008 release of \"Velvet Touch\"", "answer": "La Bamba", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Chaconne in F minor was created by the composer of what nationality?", "answer": "German", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which genus of monocots native to the hot and arid regions of Mexico, features the genus plant Polianthes?", "answer": "Agave", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Offspring and Let's Active, are of which music genre?", "answer": "rock", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What member of the Canadian alternative rock band, Sandbox, is best known for his portrayal of \"Bubbles\" and for being the co-writer of the ongoing cult classic \"Trailer Park Boys?\"", "answer": "Mike Smith", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The soundtrack Marie Antoinette is attached to a film based on a ruler who reigned during the time leading up to what revolution?", "answer": "the French Revolution", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was the father of the author of the novel on which The Man with the Golden Gun is based a Member of Parliament for?", "answer": "Henley", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jim Sweeney was in a tribute video to mark the anniversary of which 1992 American crime thriller?", "answer": "Reservoir Dogs", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American Singer recorded a song in 2016 that was co-produced by the Brit Award for Best British Male Solo Artist recipient of 2008?", "answer": "Lady Gaga", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which musician is from Canada, Raine Maida or Kevin Parker?", "answer": "Raine Maida", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The 1966 Oakland Raide