d the Gaddafi government?", "answer": "protests in Benghazi", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Cranberries song, written by their lead singer singer Dolores O'Riordan and included on their 1994 album No Need To Argue, is considered their most successful single?", "answer": "Zombie", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the Pakistani pop group who's first album contained a rendition of a song originally written, performed, and record by Neil Diamond called?", "answer": "Vital Signs", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which song covered by Tori Amos ends with Eminem killing his wife?", "answer": "Kim", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Dwayne Johnson and Naomie Harris appear in the film Rampage directed by which film director?", "answer": "Brad Peyton", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ferncroft country Club is owned by Affinity Management and located in Essex County Massachusetts. What is the total population of Essex County?", "answer": "743,159", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Leonora Mary Grosvenor's father was the richest man in Britain in what decade?", "answer": "1970s", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which genus is in the verbena family, Citharexylum or Laelia?", "answer": "Citharexylum", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which snooker competitor in the 1988 Masters Tournament was also a television sports commentator?", "answer": "Mike Hallett", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what province were Guitar and Drums for Just Visiting recorded?", "answer": "New South Wales", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Nike Hypervenom is endorsed by an English footballer who plays for the English national team and what Premier League club?", "answer": "Tottenham Hotspur", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year was the artist that released the album \"At 89\" born?", "answer": "1919", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What are the nationalities of Leonid Khachiyan and Sofia Kovalevskaya?", "answer": "Russian", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Nangpai Go