", "answer": "road", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which movie features a song from Beaucoup Fish's fifth album and stars Arnold Schwarzenegger?", "answer": "Batman & Robin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Anfal genocide was the Kurdish genocide that killed between 50,000 and 182,000 Kurds committed during the Al-Anfal campaign, a campaign against Kurdistan in northern Iraq, led by which Ba'athist Iraqi Defense Minister, Interior Minister, military commander and chief of the Iraqi Intelligence Service, in the final stages of the Iran\u2013Iraq War?", "answer": "Ali Hassan Abd al-Majid al-Tikriti", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Avnet, Inc. is one of the world's largest distributors of electronic components and embedded solutions and is headquartered in Phoenix, Arizona, the company became incorporated in 1955 and began trading in 1961, on which organization, an American stock exchange located at 11 Wall Street, Lower Manhattan, New York City, New York? ", "answer": "New York Stock Exchange", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Hurricane Keith weakened to a tropical storm, before another landfall occurred near a city with a population of what?", "answer": "57,169", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What river is the weapons manufacturer that developed the M15 pistol located on?", "answer": "Mississippi River", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Yu Darvish was named MVP of the 2006 Asia baseball series. Which MLB team does he pitch for?", "answer": "Los Angeles Dodgers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which magazine did Richard Taylor jointly edit that is also one of the oldest scientific journals published in English?", "answer": "Philosophical Magazine", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Civil Rights Heritage Center (CRHC) was established on the campus of Indiana University South Bend as a result of student interest and faculty support as a center for the study and documentation of civil rights history, it's housed in which former public swimming pool tha