estion": "What is the occupation of Mark Rankin and Mark Mothersbaugh?", "answer": "singer", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What United States television channel aired the film about a man who died on September 11, 2001 and led hundreds out of the South Tower before dying in its collapse?", "answer": "The History Channel", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the band that released \"Time to Pretend\" formed?", "answer": "2002", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what month was the chef who loaned money to Jimmy Doherty for his farm born?", "answer": "May", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was the draft that Chad Johnson was drafted held at?", "answer": "Madison Square Garden", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Latrell Fontaine Sprewell, is an American former professional basketball player; despite his accomplishments, his career was overshadowed by a 1997 incident in which he choked coach P. J. Carlesimo during a practice, which ultimately resulted in a 68-game suspension, Peter John \"P. J.\" Carlesimo, is an American basketball coach, who coached in both which organization, and college basketball for nearly 40 years?", "answer": "NBA", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many former members from the band where Zack De La Rocha was a rapper/vocalist took part in the Audioslave discography? ", "answer": "three", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Red, White and Brown was by the comedian who was introduced to the stage by the lead rapper for which group?", "answer": "Grandmaster Flash and the Furious Five", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " No issue was a Pakistani television advertisement campaign started by a mobile network created by the merger of which two companies ?", "answer": "Mobilink and Warid", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which book does Ken Ham interpret in his organization?", "answer": "Book of Genesis", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Baylor University and Duke University, are both what type of universities?", "answer": "private",