rn Cosm\u00e9 McMunn; February 22, 1901 \u2013 August 22, 1980) was a Mexican-American pianist and composer, best known as the accompanist to notably tone-deaf soprano Florence Foster Jenkins, (born July 19, 1868 \u2013 November 26, 1944) was an American socialite and amateur soprano who was known and mocked for her flamboyant performance costumes and notably poor singing ability, Jenkins's full given name?", "answer": "Narcissa Florence Foster", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is Helios located near that would qualify as the 33rd most visited tourist attraction in the world?", "answer": "Pike Place Market", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Bo\u0159e\u0148 is a structure similar to the butte in what mountains in Wyoming?", "answer": "Bear Lodge Mountains", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Heinz Linge served as a valet for a German politician who initiated what?", "answer": "World War II", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Harper Valley PTA was the first female-created song to top the Hot 100 and U.S. Hot Country Singles charts until the 1980 song by whom?", "answer": "Dolly Parton", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was an old ship sunk in the Indian Ocean on 23 January 1977 by a bomb planted by Austrian businessman Udo Proksch, whos owner of the cargo was aslo the owner of a famous pastry shop and chocolaterie established in 1786 in Vienna, Austria ?", "answer": "Lucona", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who direction the live action sequel to the Disney film based on Dodie Smith's 1956 novel \"The Hundred and One Dalmatians\"?", "answer": "Kevin Lima", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Otis Sistrunk played his entire NFL career with a team from what state?", "answer": "California", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Willi Willi Caves Nature Reserve is located on what continent?", "answer": "Australia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American sitcom, broadcast on NBC, earned Harris Yulin a Primetime Emmy Award Nomination in 1996?", "answer": "Frasier"