": "Legion", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Do the Bronx cocktail and the Bramble cocktail both have juice in them?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The author of the short story collection \"Jesus' Son\" also wrote a book which won the National Book Award for Fiction featuring a protagonist by which name?", "answer": "Skip Sands", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was the theme park directed by Nicholas William Robert Thompson that won best theme park in the United Kingdom and the ninth best park in Europe by the Travelers' choice awards located?", "answer": "Fylde coast in Blackpool, Lancashire, England.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "who was formed first Fatboy Slim or Our Last Night?", "answer": "Fatboy Slim", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The music video of the song Hey Porsche features a car produced by which company ?", "answer": "Porsche Konstruktionen GesmbH", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What musical with music by Noel Gay did Susan Goforth perform in?", "answer": "Me and My Girl", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the province that Formosa and Villa Dos Trece are located?", "answer": "Formosa Province", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is the main campus of the private Tusculum College?", "answer": "Tusculum, Tennessee", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which magazine is published more frequently, Sojourners or Science News?", "answer": "Science News", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Ruth Wilson has film credits that include the 2015 World War II drama directed by whom?", "answer": "Saul Dibb", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What B-29 Superfortress bomber was stationed on Tinian Island?", "answer": "Enola Gay", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "what is the name of the Munsee sachem who led the most populous and widespread North American native language groups?", "answer": "Katonah", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What album was released on March 3, 2017 and features Location as the debut single?", "answer": "American Teen", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of the following is best known for his love poems such as Funeral Blues: W. H. Auden or Maurice Blanchot?", "answer": "Wystan Hugh Auden", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In what year was the city in which Dan Academic Center was established founded?", "answer": "1878", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which american novelist won the pulitzer prize for fiction, Cynthia Ozick or Jane Smiley?", "answer": "Jane Smiley", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which 2016 Irish independent horror film did Catherine Walker star in?", "answer": "A Dark Song", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Mike Barnett negotiated many contracts including which player that went on to become general manager of CSKA Moscow of the Kontinental Hockey League?", "answer": "Sergei Fedorov", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Pygmoelian\" is the sixteenth episode of the eleventh season of the American animated sitcom \"The Simpsons\", in the episode, after getting his face censored out on which brand of beer, on a calendar, that originally started as a fictional beverage?", "answer": "Duff Beer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both documentaries The Big One and the Ring of Fire documentaries about natural disasters?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who is this retired Chinese professional basketball player from the Houston Rockets of the National Basketball Association that is one of the tallest players in China along with Mu Tiezhu and Sun Mingming?", "answer": "Yao Ming", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which author wrote four plays, John Crowley or E. E. Cummings?", "answer": "Edward Estlin \"E. E.\" Cummings", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which goalkeeper that Frans Hoek played with plays for Swansea City and the Poland national team?", "answer": "\u0141ukasz Fabia\u0144ski", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which 1975 Hindi thriller movie is centers on the life of a king pin of gambling ring based on betting on the New York Cotton Exchange?", "answer": "Dharmatama", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Edmund Sanford was a professor of Psychology at the private university located in what Massachusetts city?", "answer": "Worcester", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What team's name comes from a band of armed guards and is the opposite to Kansas Jayhawks in the Border War?", "answer": "Missouri Tigers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Thousands (perhaps even millions) of performances of William Shakespeare's plays have been staged since the end of the 16th century, among the actors of these original performances were Richard Burbage, who played the title role in the first performances of The Tragedy of Hamlet, Prince of Denmark, often shortened to Hamlet, a tragedy written by William Shakespeare at an uncertain date between, 1599 and what year?", "answer": "1602", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Brian Schmidt won the 2011 Nobel Prize in Physics with which  physics at the University of California, Berkeley?", "answer": "Saul Perlmutter", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which former American football linebacker on the  the Baltimore Ravens of the National Football League (NFL) did Roosevelt Barnes negotiate contracts for?", "answer": "Ray Lewis", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born first, Marcus Lovingood or Jane Lynch?", "answer": "Jane Marie Lynch", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What album was released by Top Dawg Entertainment and contains lyrical themes delivered by rasism and medication tolerence.", "answer": "Kendrick Lamar", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Platonia Dilemma was introduced in the book \"Metamagical Themas\" which was written by an author born in what year?", "answer": "1945", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the middle name of a star of April 9th movie?", "answer": "Dittmann", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is best known for his work in alternate history, John Irving or Harry Turtledove?", "an