 both Lindsay Davenport and Wayne Black nationals of the same country ?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Steven Fowle is the current owner, editor, and publisher of America's oldest newspaper, which non-profit, alternative, bi-weekly newspaper published in Portsmouth, New Hampshire?", "answer": "New Hampshire Gazette", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of these Disney productions was released earlier--The Three Caballeros or The Monkey's Uncle?  ", "answer": "The Three Caballeros", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In what year was the cathedral, that Arnao de Vergara produced several windows for, registered as a World Heritage Site?", "answer": "1987", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Riverport Railroad operates a former army depot track that was opened in what year?", "answer": "1917", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Helen Francis Hood, was an American pianist, composer and teacher, she was born in which city and state, in the United States?", "answer": "Chelsea, Massachusetts", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which British Conservative Party politician who serves as editor of the \"London Evening Standard\" contributed to the setting up of The Atlantic Bridge?", "answer": "George Osborne", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Lawrence \"Larry\" Guterman is a Canadian film director known for his work in companies like DreamWorks, Warner Bros. and New Line Cinema, he directed feature films including which 2001 American-Australian family action comedy film, directed by Lawrence Guterman with screenplay by John Requa and Glenn Ficarra?", "answer": "Cats & Dogs", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In 2012 Michael Malitowski and partner Joanna Leunis won first place at a festival held at what ballroom?", "answer": "Empress Ballroom", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which cast in 2012 American comedy film written and directed by Coley Sohn, was born, April 10, 1988?", "answer": "Haley Joel Osment", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many