e Recilia dispar is endemic to?", "answer": "4,503,000", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Yegoshikha Cemetery is located in a city that is located on the banks ofr what river?", "answer": "Kama River", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many staff members were taken hostage during the prision riot that David Rothenberg was a civilian observer of?", "answer": "42", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Revenge with Music had music by the composer and film producer of what nationality?", "answer": "American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the name of the team that rugby league footballer Brian Gregory played for in Greater Manchester?", "answer": "Wigan Warriors", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the man who directed the 1986 American romantic comedy-drama film starring Rob Lowe and Demi Moore born?", "answer": "1952", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The State Fair Classic occurs before what game commonly called the Red River Rivalry?", "answer": "Red River Showdown", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Mitchell Mohawks are an amateur ice hockey team based in what Canadian province?", "answer": "Manitoba", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When did the coach of the 1967 Penn State Nittany Lions football team die?", "answer": "January 22, 2012", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Dave O'Brien is a sportscaster for which regional sports cable and satellite network?", "answer": "New England Sports Network", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which state is Sisters State Park located in, which is bisected by U.S. Route 20, the longest road in the United States, spanning 3365 miles?", "answer": "Oregon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Irish boxer is the president of the Malta Boxing Commission?", "answer": "Steve Collins", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Sukhothai Kingdom is in the north central area of this country formerly known as what", "answer": "Siam", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which singer is from South Korea, Hyomin or Peter S