idge"}, {"question": "Who is the Malasian-Austrailan film, born in 1977 that was discovered at the Melbourne Underground Film Festival?", "answer": "James Wan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "the Klaip\u0117da Revolt of the Directorate of the Klaip\u0117da Region took place at the north of which river?", "answer": "Neman River", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Compared to the Key West International Airport, who owns the University of Illinois Willard Airport?", "answer": "University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "\"Happy Birthday to You\", more commonly known as simply \"Happy Birthday\", is a song that is traditionally sung to celebrate the anniversary of a person's birth, the melody has traditionally been attributed to American sisters Patty and Mildred Jane Hill, an American songwriter and musicologist, in what year?", "answer": "1893", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Fiery Trial: Abraham Lincoln and American Slavery is a historical non-fiction book written by which American historian born on February 7, 1943?", "answer": "Eric Foner", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Kansai International Airport, is an international airport located on an artificial island in the middle of Osaka Bay, 38 km southwest of \u014csaka Station, the airport serves as an international hub for Nippon Cargo Airlines Company, Limited, or NCA, a cargo airline with its head office on the property of Narita International Airport in Narita, Chiba Prefecture, outside Tokyo, its main base is where?", "answer": "Narita Airport", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which free agent picked up by the Denver Nuggets in the 1996-97 season is an All-American at the University of North Carolina, and a two-time NBA Champion with the Houston Rockets?", "answer": "Kenny Smith", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the Dutch singer who, along with Guus Meeuwis, replaced Marco Borsator and Anouk as coaches on \"The Voice Holland\" born?", "answer": "1980", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Of the persons who Dezider Hoffmann photographed, who was the idol of the \"bobby soxers\" ?", "answer": "Frank Sinatra", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Ghazi Attack stars an Indian actor who is known for his owrks in Telugu cinema, and who, in 2006, received the National Film Award for co-producing what?", "answer": "Bommalata \u2013 A Bellyful of Dreams", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Does both The Classic Crime and Black Light Burns feature a current lineup with Matt MacDonald?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Victoria Arches are located in the North West area of what country?", "answer": "England", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Orgone is a pseudo-scientific and spiritual concept described as an esoteric energy with no scientific what?", "answer": "evidence for the existence of such energy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In the 90's movies Heavyweights and That Darn Cat dot ehy have any of the same actors?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "S. R. D. Vaidyanathan was an Indian musician who played which double reed wind instrument?", "answer": "The nadaswaram,", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Civil rights advocate  Carolyn Goodman's murdered son was born in what year?", "answer": "1943", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Charles Henry Gaylord learned what hybrid martial art from Hawaii?", "answer": "Kajukenbo", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which filmmaker's family emigrated permanently to the United States when he was fourteen, Masaki Kobayashi or Josef von Sternberg?", "answer": "Josef von Sternberg", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which actress in Galveston also played a character named \"Betty Cooper\" in another production?", "answer": "Lili Pauline Reinhart", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Cypress Point Creamery is a cheese producer that sells a Dutch yellow cheese accounting for for 50 to 60% of the world's what?", "answer": "cheese consumption", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Isaac Bashevis Singer and Ernesto Sabato both writers ?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the name of the South Korean-Chinese boy group whose hits include \"Growl\", and members include Byun Baek-hyun?", "answer": "EXO", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which film was released first, Max Keeble's Big Move or Pinocchio?", "answer": "Pinocchio", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Where was the comedian and actor, who stars in the British comedy Taskmaster, born?", "answer": "St Asaph, Denbighshire", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the middle name of the actress who starred with Hailee Steinfeld, Muna Otaru, Sam Worthington, Amy Nuttall, and Ned Dennehy in the film The Keeping Room ?", "answer": "Heyworth", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Capt. Denver Vernon Truelove took part in what raid on the Japanese capital Tokyo on Saturday, April 18, 1942.", "answer": "Doolittle Raid", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Elton John album included a song that was later covered in 2002 by Tim McGraw?", "answer": "Madman Across the Water", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What a World Series of Poker Ladies' Event bracelet winner starred with  Donald Sutherland in Shadow of the Wolf?", "answer": "Jennifer Tilly", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who owns the Flobal Rallycross that Scott Speed competes in?", "answer": "Red Bull", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Run, Cougar, Run and The Bears and I both drama films?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The 2003 Cincinnati Bengals season was the team's 36th year in professional football and its 34th with the National Football League, the Bengals are now under first year Head Coach Marvin Lewis, who replaced which American football coach and former cornerback, that was fired following the 2002 season?", "answer": "Charles Richard LeBeau", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Shaura and Sharleen Spiteri recorded singers ?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which American football linebacker, who was honorably inducted into the The Chiefs hall of fame following his death from severe injuries sustained in a car accident in 2000?", "answer": "Derrick Thomas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the capital of the district that includes the community council Ratau?", "answer": "Maseru", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which actress portrays Jenna Hamilton on the MTV teen comedy series \"Awkward\"?", "answer": "Ashley Nicole Rickards", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which documentary was released first, Wrath of Gods or Punk's Not Dead?", "answer": "Wrath of Gods", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What are both Dichondra and Peperomia?", "answer": "plants", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Han Jae-rim directed the 2013 film starring which actor?", "answer": "Song Kang-ho", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the birthday of the producer of the album \"A Different Ship\"?", "answer": "28 February 1971", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What ethnicity was the New York Times Best Selling Author of \"Start With Why\"?", "answer": "British/American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Flowered Up were a five-man British band, formed in Camden Town, London, they were influential in the Baggy movement alongside which music and cultural scene, that developed in the Manchester area of the United Kingdom, titled?", "answer": "Madchester", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Three Artists One Song is part of an annual series of a shoe company that is a subsidiary of this corporation since 2003.", "answer": "Nike", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which type of large intestine worm was primarily studied by Ivan Mackerie?", "answer": "He was most notable for his search of the Mongolian death worm,", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A 125 tonne stone statue of Tlaloc discovered in Texcoco now resides at a museum that contains significant artifacts from what?", "answer": "Mexico's pre-Columbian heritage", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Cinefantastique and Marie Claire both the names of magazines?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Plaxton Centro is a low floor single-decker bus body designed by Bluebird Vehicles and manufactured by Plaxton, in 2010, Blackpool Transport took delivery of Volvo examples, Blackpool Transport Services Ltd. (BTS) is a bus and tram operator running within the boroughs of Blackpool and Fylde and into the surrounding area, including Fleetwood, Lytham St Annes, Poulton-le-Fylde and Cleveleys, and is owned by which organization?", "answer": "Blackpool Borough Council", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which band, He Is We or Bright Eyes, was founded by singer-songwriter and guitarist Conor Oberst?", "answer": "Bright Eyes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Ridemakerz and Build-A-Bear Workshop are both what kind of companies?", "answer": "American retailer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Habibia High School educated the pop singer who was likened to what American pop star of the time?", "answer": "Elvis Presley", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which battle did the man whose name was used for Bowie County, Texas, die at?", "answer": "Battle of the Alamo", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The wooden rollercoaster that supercedes the Millennium Force in duratation is located in which amusement park?", "answer": "Kings Island", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Pride, based on the International Military Tribunal for the Far East of 1946\u201348, depicts the Japanese prime minister responsible for ordering which infamous attack?", "answer": "Pearl Harbor", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 28th AVN Awards ceremony was co-hosted by which American pornographic actress born as Michelle Chapman?", "answer": "Tori Black", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the hometown of actress who plays Madeline in \"Night Owls\"?", "answer": "Greenbelt, Maryland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who has represented the congressional district for Wilkins Township, Allegheny County, Pennsylvania since 2003", "answer": "Tim Murphy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Battle of the Ch'ongch'on River and Battle of Aachen, both occurred after which year?", "answer": "1944", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Texas Wrestling Academy has produced well-known wrestlers one of which is the on-screen general manager of what?", "answer": "SmackDown", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the former linebacker for the Seattle Seahawks that starred in the movie Phase IV?", "answer": "Brian Bosworth", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What man stars in the British sitcom  that started in 1990 in which he, with Richard Curtis, created?", "answer": "Rowan Atkinson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was the service academy at which Jack Owsley served as a head football coach located? ", "answer": "Annapolis, Maryland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Nipponanthemum and Dionysia, are types of which shared entity?", "answer": "plants", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "One of the cities in which Auckland Park Theological Seminary has a campus is part of what municipality?", "answer": "eThekwini Metropolitan Municipality", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "On what date was the Bye Bye Birdie and Wicked actress born?", "answer": "September 1, 1977", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Birchfield is an area of Perry Barr, Birmingham, it gave its name to the Birchfield Harriers athletics club, now based at which nearby international athletics stadium located within Perry Park in Perry Barr, Birmingham, England, at grid reference [ SP065925]?", "answer": "Alexander Stadium", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Aero Engine Controls produces any of several types of control systems for what kind of engines?", "answer": "gas turbine", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which guitarist played in the rock band Kansas?", "answer": "Mike Slamer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "