y", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A Bellini includes what type of Italian white wine?", "answer": "Prosecco", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Denkova-Staviski Cup is an annual international figure skating competition named after two-time World champion ice dancers Albena Denkova, and Maxim Staviski, a Russian-born naturalized Bulgarian ice dancer, Denkova is related to her, in which two ways?", "answer": "partner and fianc\u00e9e", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which director is American, Lino Brocka  or Arthur Penn?", "answer": "Arthur Hiller Penn (September 27, 1922 \u2013 September 28, 2010) was an American director and producer of film, television and theater.", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "\"Social Text\" was probably an attempt to criticize people who believe that scientific theories are what?", "answer": "social constructs", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Both the movie Pippi on the Run and the character Pippi Longstocking , are based on books by what author?", "answer": "Astrid Lindgren", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of director who made a movie with an actress who debuted on that movie in 1959?", "answer": "Ren\u00e9 Cardona", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Stylo was a single by which virtual band created in 1998?", "answer": "Gorillaz", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the 1989 film on which \"Batman: The Ride\" is thematically based?", "answer": "Tim Burton", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "John Harrison Surratt, Jr. (April 13, 1844 \u2013 April 21, 1916) was accused of plotting with John Wilkes Booth to kidnap US President Abraham Lincoln, his mother, Mary Elizabeth Jenkins Surratt, was an American boarding house owner who was convicted of conspiracy and hanged by the US government, she was hanged and became the first woman executed by who?", "answer": "US federal government", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The person who published New System of Chemical Philosophy\" (1803) was born on what date?", "answer": "6 September 1766", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "John Powell was nominated for an Academy Award in the 2014 3D film produced by what company?", "answer": "DreamWorks Animation", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What town in Penobscot County, Maine was Daniel Coombs born in?", "answer": "Lincoln, Maine", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who wrote Elephant Stone with the song writer John Squire?", "answer": "singer Ian Brown", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who set up the company which produces the BBC children's show based on the American-Canadian books of the same name?", "answer": "Waheed Alli", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Ilha  is a civil parish in the municipality of Santana in a Portoguese archipelago that had how many inhabitants in 2011 ?", "answer": "267,785", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What author was named one of the \"50 greatest British writers since 1945\" and wrote the novel The Tin Princess?", "answer": "Philip Pullman", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the psychoanalyst after which psychoanalyst author and trainer John Steiner has been called \"a prolific London post-Kleinian\"?", "answer": "Melanie Reizes Klein", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Joshua Dugdale and Larisa Shepitko the same nationality?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which Eighties band was more successful in the British charts, The Darling Buds or The Housemartins?", "answer": "The Housemartins", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Lawrence Jacobs is the Executive Vice President of what resort operating company?", "answer": "Las Vegas Sands", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Mar\u00eda de Jes\u00fas Patricio Mart\u00ednez was chosen as a representative indigenous spokeswoman for an election held on what date?", "answer": "1 July 2018", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The town that Anneliese Seubert moved to at age 9 is how far from the capital Canberra?", "answer": "114 km", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Battle of San Roque was part of the Argentine Civil War, the Federalist forces of C\u00f3rdoba Province governor Juan Bautista Bustos were defeated by which forces of General Jos\u00e9 Mar\u00eda Paz, who were the proponents of the concept of a unitary state (centralized government) in Buenos Aires during the civil wars? ", "answer": "Unitarian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Bones is an American crime procedural drama television series focusing on forensic anthropology and archaeology, on which actor Eric Millegan plays which character?", "answer": "Dr. Zack Addy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "On what day is the holiday that commemorates the day also known as V-P day celebrated in North and South Korea?", "answer": "August 15", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Napoleon and Samantha and Sky High both comedy films?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which magazine Me Naiset or Marie Claire is published more frequently ?", "answer": "Me Naiset", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What district is the Warner Bros. Studios located in?", "answer": "the Three Rivers district.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which mall that has a Bobby's Burger Palace opened October 1, 1962?", "answer": "Dadeland Mall", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What band position does the member of Guns N' Roses that a member of Buffalo Springfield and Crosby, Stills & Nash worked with have?", "answer": "drummer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The \"black spider\" memos are letters and memos, to British government ministers and politicians over the years, written by Charles, Prince of Wales, the eldest child and heir apparent of who?", "answer": "Queen Elizabeth II", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Walkley Heights, South Australia is located on land that formerly was a prison originally known as what?", "answer": "The Stockade", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the nickname of the 2005 Toyota Grand Prix of Long Beach Polesitter ?", "answer": "the thrill from West Hill", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which movie starring John Travolta was directed by the same person who directed \"The Sender\"?", "answer": "Battlefield Earth", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What country are Belgravia, and Knightsbridge are located in?", "answer": "London", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Lieutenant General Winston Mensa-Wood's position from 1987 to 1990 is currently held by what Major General?", "answer": "William Ayamdo", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Christopher Markus and Stephen McFeely are screenwriters for a series of fantasy films by C.S. Lewis, what was the film series?", "answer": "The Chronicles of Narnia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What English author, best known for his books about the teddy bear Winnie-the-Pooh and for various poems as well as Wurzel-Flummery is a play performed for the first time in 1917, in London.", "answer": "A. A. Milne", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What film did Sarah Snook star in that was a revenge comedy-drama film written and directed by Jocelyn Moorhouse?", "answer": "The Dressmaker", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the director of the movie that featured \"Be Like That\" on its soundtrack? ", "answer": "James B. Rogers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many bills were passed by the United States Congress on September 18, 1850, as part of the Compromise of 1850 between Southern slave-holding interests and Northern Free-Soilers?", "answer": "five", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the American rapper born who's album is Stoney?", "answer": "July 4, 1995", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which movie, The Super Snail Adventure and Cloudy with a Chance of Meatballs, was based on a children's book?", "answer": "Cloudy with a Chance of Meatballs", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Isaac McCoy was an advocate of what policy where Native Americans were forcibly removed from their ancestral homelands in the eastern United States to lands west of the Mississippi River?", "answer": "Indian removal", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Thoovalsparsham is a 1990 Malayalam film that was inspired by an American comedy film that stars Tom Selleck, Steve Guttenberg, and Ted Danson, and was directed by who?", "answer": "Leonard Nimoy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which battle lasted longer, the Battle of Tarawa or the Battle of Leyte?", "answer": "The Battle of Leyte", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who directed the film that Iron Virgin's early stage garb was compared to?", "answer": "Stanley Kubrick", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Liberian politician was the granddaugher of a market woman?", "answer": "Ellen Johnson Sirleaf", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Tune is a group of investment companies similar in many ways to Virgin, owned by Tony Fernandes and based in which Asian country?", "answer": "Malaysia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the comedian who was starred in \"Lionel Nimrod's Inexplicable World\" with Stewart Lee born?", "answer": "1967", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Between Boaz Yakin and Murray Grigor, which one served as director of the Edinburgh International Film Festival?", "answer": "Murray Grigor", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which is from farther west, U2 or Queens of the Stone Age?", "answer": "Queens of the Stone Age", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The music of the \"Harry Potter\" film series was recorded and released in conjunction with the post-production and releases of each of how many corresponding films, Jeremy Soule helped write for the \"Harry Potter\" video games, he's an American composer of soundtracks for film, television and video games?", "answer": "eight", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which company works with petroleum, Apache Corporation or Alexion Pharmaceuticals?", "answer": "Apache Corporation", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What Virginia county is the Marshall-Rucker-Smith House located in?", "answer": "Albemarle 