: "Darden Restaurants, Inc.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Troy McClure first appeared in what 13th episode of The Simpsons second season?", "answer": "Homer vs. Lisa and the 8th Commandment", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Taking Back Sunday and CKY, which genre are these ?", "answer": "rock", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which Film, Pete's Dragon or Frozen, is a 3D computer animated musical?", "answer": "Frozen", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The 494th Fighter Squadron is part of what Royal Air Force station near the town on Lakenheath?", "answer": "RAF Lakenheath", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Runaways\" is a song from an album released by which record label in the UK ?", "answer": "Vertigo Records", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the 2010 population of the county that includes Pinesdale, Montana?", "answer": "40,212", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Kellyn Tate, is an American softball coach, and former player, she previously held coaching positions at which are the athletic teams that represent Texas Tech University?", "answer": "Texas Tech Red Raiders and Lady Raiders", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was the company that manufactures Tic Tac founded? ", "answer": "Alba, Piedmont, Italy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Kim Chung-sim is a North Korean football midfielder who competed at the world championship for women's national association football teams held on what dates?", "answer": "26 June to 17 July 2011", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the bass player for the band that sang \"All We Ever Knew\"?", "answer": "Chris Zasche", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What MLB team did Scott Cooper play for, besides the Red Sox and Royals?", "answer": "St. Louis Cardinals", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was a career United States Army officer and civil engineer involved in the coastal construction of several lighthouses, one being located in Jupiter, Florida, on the north side of the Jupiter Inlet that had a costof more than $60,000? ", "answer": "George Gordon Meade", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Mundra Port is the largest private port of India located on the north shores of the Gulf of Kutch near Mundra, Kutch district, Gujarat, it's owned by Adani Group, a multinational conglomerate company headquartered in Ahmedabad, Gujarat, India, which later expanded it into  which organization, managing several ports?", "answer": "Adani Ports & SEZ Limited", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Wisconsin Athletic Hall of Fame has honored the MLB right fielder who is now the senior VP of what team?", "answer": "Atlanta Braves", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In 2002, Jump5 released covers of \"Strange Way To Save The World\" and another Christmas carol written by whom?", "answer": "Isaac Watts", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is older, Angelique Kerber or Micha\u00ebl Llodra?", "answer": "Micha\u00ebl Llodra", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What Matt Dillon movie came out a year following his starring in an American romantic comedy-drama directed by Ted Demme?", "answer": "In & Out", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Earl of Carnarvon coined the term \"Voluntaryism\"?", "answer": "Auberon Herbert", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who operates in the most countries around the globe, Dollar Tree or PPG Industries?", "answer": "PPG Industries", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What job do both Milan Kundera and Alan Furst have in common?", "answer": "writer", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What was the title of the 1962 Italian anthology film co-directed by the director best known for his films \"Ossessione\" (1943), \"Senso\" (1954), \"Rocco and His Brothers\" (1960), \"The Leopard\" (1963) and \"Death in Venice\" (1971)", "answer": "Boccaccio '70", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Congressional Pro-Trade Caucus is a party who identify as what?", "answer": "conservative Democrats.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are the geniuses Olsynium and Eriobotrya native to the same parts of the world ?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who is the current head coach for the NCAA Division I basketball team that was previously coached by Dana Altman?", "answer": "Bruce Weber", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Mark Angel played non-league football for what football club based in Bourne, Lincolnshire, England", "answer": "Bourne Town Football Club", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the political party of the congressman Earl Krugel plotted to blow up the office of?", "answer": "Republican", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which periodical is based further to the east, Reptiles or The General?", "answer": "The General", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which Turkish President was the target of a failed assassination attempt?", "answer": "Mustafa Kemal Atat\u00fcrk", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Frederick Hockley participated in what means of divination or fortune-telling?", "answer": "Scrying", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which opera has more acts, Partenope or La sonnambula?", "answer": "La sonnambula", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which director is of French background, Oscar Hammerstein II or Jean Cocteau?", "answer": "Jean Maurice Eug\u00e8ne Cl\u00e9ment Cocteau", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In what League does the club Sheik Mohamed Fankaty Dabo is on loan from play?", "answer": "Premier League", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The H\u00f6rnli Hut is located a few kilometers south-west of Zermatt, in the German-speaking section of what canton of Switzerland?", "answer": "Valais", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which musical duo has an album that has sample as diverse as a the first presenter of the BBC television science programme \"Tomorrow's World\"?", "answer": "The Books", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Croissant and Bella, are both which type of media?", "answer": "magazine", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Toshi Ichiyanagi, who wrote Music for Electric Metronomes, was what nationality?", "answer": "Japanese", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "which ethnic group derived from Turkic-speaking adherents of Karaite Judaism in Central and Eastern Europe was  Eupatorian Kenassas its temple complex ", "answer": "The Crimean Karaites", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of the following is known for his consistently energetic performances such as in Taxi!: Ian Schneider or James Cagney?", "answer": "James Francis \"Jimmy\" Cagney Jr.", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "During the late 1520s and early 1530s Simone Mosca worked with a sculptor described as one of the what?", "answer": "greatest artists of all time", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What song , that Rolling Stone magazine named the second best song of 2012, did \"Started with a Song\" surpass as the most added song at Canadian country radio?", "answer": "We Are Never Ever Getting Back Together", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The empire that Ayurbarwada Buyantu Khan was the eighth Great Khan originated where?", "answer": "Central Asia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Right On! and The Family Handyman both teen magazines?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Talking Propellerheads released songs about the decline of which computer company founded in 1951 and once based in Cambridge, MA?", "answer": "Wang Laboratories", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jean-Jacques Beineix and Angela Murray Gibson are both what?", "answer": "director", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What country of origin does Vasey Houghton and HM Prison Pentridge have in common?", "answer": "Australian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which plant is native to Europe and Morroco, Phyteuma or Goodyera?", "answer": "Phyteuma", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Lego Ninjago Movie starred the voice of which Pakistani-American comedian?", "answer": "Kumail Nanjiani", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was the band formed that released \"Tear Up This Town?\"", "answer": "Battle, East Sussex", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What day was South Korean professional footballer Son Heung-min awarded the Best Footballer in Asia 2014?", "answer": "28th", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Both Carnegie Mellon University and Vanderbilt University are private or public research universities?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "what does The Dig and Industrial Light & Magic have in common?", "answer": "Lucas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was George Philipp Telemann's career?", "answer": "music", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is the company that Barry Allen Greenfield served as the director of research for based?", "answer": "Boston, Massachusetts", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what band was the Canadian featured on vocals in Unweaving the Rainbow the lead singer?", "answer": "Dream Theater", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Johan Martial, is a French football player who currently plays for Maccabi Petah Tikva, and is also the older brother of Manchester United F.C. forward Anthony Martial, a French professional footballer who plays as a forward for which country's national team?", "answer": "France", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which author was born first, James Redfield or James Hanley?", "answer": "James (Joseph) Hanley", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What theory of Biblical literalist chronology places the universes created as only a few millennia ago?", "answer": "Ussher chronology", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American film and theater actress who appeared in over 30 films, as well as on Broadway starred in The Night Club Lady?", "answer": "Mayo Methot", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What self titled album was released by an Indianapolis American Christian music band on January 24th of 2012?", "answer": "Pioneer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who illustrated the American espionage comic book which is well known for i