 yards in three consecutive seasons?", "answer": "the University of Oregon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Whose wife was housed by Ruth Hyde Paine until November 23,1963?", "answer": "Lee Harvey Oswald", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the birth year of the Dodgers General Manager that replaced Dan Evans?", "answer": "1972", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Larry Elin hired which person, that later founded a company that animated the movie Ice Age?", "answer": "Chris Wedge", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which tennis player was born first, Michael Chang or Sara Errani?", "answer": "Michael Te-Pei Chang", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Sir Baboon McGoon was one of 13 bombers which was introduced in what year?", "answer": "1938", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who wrote \"The Office\" episode, \"The Valentine\", guest starring the actor professionally known as Chip Esten?", "answer": "Michael Schur", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Kim So-hyn is a South Korean musical theatre actress who has starred in the South Korean stage production of what musical horror-drama based on the novella by Robert Louis Stevenson?", "answer": "Jekyll & Hyde", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What gang were Buck Barrow and Blanche Barrow apart of?", "answer": "Barrow Gang", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What name did the corporation, who bought the Lavington Square Shopping Centre, previously go by?", "answer": "Federation Centres", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Hero and the Terror is an action film written by a man born in what year?", "answer": "1939", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year did the actor that was in the film The Short Life of Anne Frank and who received classical training at the Bristol Old Vic Theatre School,  made his Broadway debut in Tom Stoppard's \"The Real Thing\" and received a Tony Award for Best Actor?", "answer": "1984", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "what is the population of the place where Pond Monkeys were based ", "answer": "8,087", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the German-themed pavilion in which Biergarten Restaurant is one resturant it", "answer": "Germany Pavilion at Epcot", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What profession does J.T. Ellison and Catherine Coulter have in common?", "answer": "author", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ard Crags and Newlands Valley are both located where?", "answer": "Cumbria, England", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Christopher Ralph played the role of Tobias in a 1998 series based on a book series by what author?", "answer": "K. A. Applegate", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The first book of the Mortal Instruments series is set where?", "answer": "modern day New York City", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Chris Larceny directed the music video Gon Jock, featuring a Haitian rapper who first achieved fame as a member of what New Jersey hip hop group?", "answer": "the Fugees", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which airport has changed its name more often: Newark Liberty International Airport or East Texas Regional Airport?", "answer": "Newark Liberty International Airport", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": " Yakutat Airport in Alaska and Muskegon County Airport in Michigan are located in what general direction relative to their city's central business district?", "answer": "south", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Caritea, regina di Spagna premiered at what opera house that in the 19th century, became the site of many famous operatic premieres at which the works of several of the four major bel canto era composers were performed?", "answer": "Teatro La Fenice", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who owns the ABC affiliate for which Susan Peters worked?", "answer": "Lockwood Broadcast Group", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 6th Canadian Infantry Division was originally scheduled to participate in this proposed Allied plan for the invasion of Japan near the end of World War II but the plan was abandoned after t