ny have in common?", "answer": "cartoon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Have both Diana Gabaldon and Karen Joy Fowler written science fiction and fantasy novels? ", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which Italian song written by Francesco Sartori and Lucio Quarantotto was covered by Donna Summer in 1999?", "answer": "Con te partir\u00f2", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born first, Ry\u016bnosuke Akutagawa or Jeff Noon?", "answer": "Ry\u016bnosuke Akutagawa", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What city contains the base of the aviation company that Mobolaji Bank Anthony was a minority investor in?", "answer": "Ikeja, Lagos State, Nigeria", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Airdrome Dream Classic uses what visual arts style?", "answer": "minimalism", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which classic island-set novel gave its hero the authors credit, leading to the belief that the story was true, and that a cave in Tobago was his real-life home.", "answer": "Robinson Crusoe", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Guanghan and Huiyang District both in the Guangdong province?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What was the name of the America's got Talent judge that was born into a musical family in McComb, Mississippi?", "answer": "Brandy Norwood", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which State, did the politician who established the American Action Network with Fred Malek, serve as a Senator ?", "answer": "Minnesota", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Dred Scott v. Sandford and Barron v. Baltimore, have which organization in common?", "answer": "United States Supreme Court", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In addition to the work that would later be translated into English and titled 'Philosophicall rudiments concerning government and society', what other work mentions Bellum omnium contra omnes?", "answer": "Leviathan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "During which time was Callixeinus alive for during 400 BCE?"