 common?", "answer": "Kentucky", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the climate of the country in which the city of Nianing is located?", "answer": "Sahelian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the second leader of La Familia Michoacana born?", "answer": "8 March 1970", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which legendary danish King had a clan called Skj\u00f6ldungs?", "answer": "Hr\u00f3lfr Kraki", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which band features Mark Gibson on the drums, LostAlone or Kaiser Chiefs?", "answer": "LostAlone", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who were the co-creators of the adult-oriented nighttime programming block of Cartoon Network?", "answer": "Brendon Small and Loren Bouchard", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Sir Henry Lynch, 3rd Baronet, died in which year, was an Irish landowner, barrister and judge, hewas one of the Roman Catholic judges appointed by James II of England?", "answer": "1691", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Valeriana and Maranta are both a genus of what types of plants?", "answer": "flowering", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Europop included the lead single, released on what date?", "answer": "15 January 1999", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the scientific journal established by the Indian Physicist who earned the 1930 Nobel Prize for Physics", "answer": "The Indian Journal of Physics", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Columba Bush is the wife of the politician who was governor of what state?", "answer": "Florida", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What three occupations are shared by Bob Clark and Andr\u00e9s Wood?", "answer": "director, producer and writer", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Lindsey Graham sponsored what?", "answer": "common name for Senate Amendment", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Donald E Steward wrote or co-wrote the screenplay for a 1992 American spy thriller that was directed by Phillip Noyce and was based on a novel of the same name that was written by who?", "answer": "Tom Clancy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the band whose second studio album is \"Sound & Color\" formed?", "answer": "2009", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who New Zealand singer-songwriter has performed at the Echoplex?", "answer": "Lorde", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which case, Dolan v. City of Tigard or Glossip v. Gross had a greater impact on property owners?", "answer": "Dolan v. City of Tigard", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Beachouse replaced the old acrade/entertainment venue which closed on what date?", "answer": "18 July 2004", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which film/sitcom aired last starring Molly Ephraim, \"Gravy\" or \"The Last Man Standing\"?", "answer": "\"Last Man Standing\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What 2016 episode of the series Black Mirror was directed by the director of Be Right Back?", "answer": "San Junipero", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the birth name of the rapper who wrote \"Role Model\"?", "answer": "Marshall Bruce Mathers III", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Norwegian black metal band unleashed an album called Masterpiss Of Pain, in 2001 on Satyr's Moonfog label", "answer": "Khold", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Joshua Wanume Kibedi served as Foreign Minister during the regime of the President of Uganda who served during what years?", "answer": "1971 to 1979", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the official name of the bunker where Joseph Goebbels's wife and children died in 1945?", "answer": "Reich Chancellery Air-Raid Shelter", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Why was the lead character in Harriet Beecher Stowe's a derogatory epithet?", "answer": "excessively subservient person", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Derivatives of Phthalane, a bicyclic aromatic organic compound, are found in the drug Citalopram, which is what type of drug?", "answer": "an antidepressant", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jeff A. Schwartz, is President 