": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which band is from Lawrence, Coheed and Cambria or Godsmack?", "answer": "Godsmack", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Do the films Fight for the Planet and Anvil! The Story of Anvil have the same director?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who starts in Mood of the Day?", "answer": "Ahn Yeon-seok", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Neon Alley was an American digital anime service run by which organization, and later evolved into a Hulu-based streaming site, an American subscription video on demand service owned by Hulu LLC?", "answer": "Viz Media.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year did the television programme that announced the discovery of ASW0009io9 first air?", "answer": "2011", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Mr. Pickles is an American animated television series created by Will Carsola and Dave Stewart for Adult Swim, the series revolves around the Goodman family, especially their 6-year-old son named Tommy and the family's border collie, the demonic Mr. Pickles, the Border Collie is a working and herding dog breed developed in which location border region, for herding livestock, especially sheep?", "answer": "Anglo-Scottish", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which community, Ferncroft, New Hampshire or Sandwich, New Hampshire, is more populous?", "answer": "Sandwich", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is Z-40's brother?", "answer": "Omar Trevi\u00f1o Morales", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "John Ball is recorded as one of the 3000 African Americans who escaped to the British lines during the American Revolution in a document about slaves who were evacuated to point in which Canadian Province ?", "answer": "Nova Scotia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which man received the Henri Poincar\u00e9 Prize in 1997, the Fields Medal in 1998, Vladimir Levenshtein or Maxim Kontsevich?", "answer": "Maxim Lvovich Kontsevich", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Besides Europe, what other continent has traditions similar to the solo and mock-battle tradition observed in Nova Scotia?", "answer": "Asia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which film inspired Zahra Laari, A Tiger Walks or Ice Princess?", "answer": "Ice Princess", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The 1953 Belgian Grand Prix was won by a Ferrari driver who was born when?", "answer": "13 July 1918", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the car that Ferdinand Alexander Porsch developed the Porsche 695 from first produced?", "answer": "1948\u20131949", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which city was the band which was formed in 1981 in Los Angeles when vocalist/guitarist James Hetfield responded to an advertisement posted by drummer Lars Ulrich in a local newspaper hosted by L'Amour?", "answer": "New York", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Richard J. Bremer is a sports broadcaster that partners up for road games with an American former professional baseball starting pitcher mainly for what team?", "answer": "Detroit Tigers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the birth year of this English film director and producer best known for directing blockbuster action films, including When a Stranger Calls?", "answer": "1961", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is an alternative name for the tribe that Abdul Ahad Karzai belongs to?", "answer": "Popalzay", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What state was the namesake of Boston Beer Company's first brand of beer from?", "answer": "Massachusetts", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What procreation sonnet within the 126 sonnets of the Fair Youth sequence was published in smaller volumes roughly half the size of Folios?", "answer": "Sonnet 11", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year was the singer born who is featured in Still Growing Up:Live & Unwrapped?", "answer": "1950", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were Arturo Uslar Pietri and Brian O'Nolan both writers?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the founding year of this general circulation newspaper based in Maryland that included publications of works by Reggie Harris?", "answer": "1837", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What 1975 award was a song, that topped the \"Billboard\" Hot 100 in December 1974, by an American singer best known for his folk rock songs like \"Taxi\" and \"W*O*L*D\", nominated for?", "answer": "Grammy Award for Best Male Pop Vocal Performance", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Believe me\" was written before or after Linkin Park was created?", "answer": "\"Believe Me\" is a song by American hip hop artist Fort Minor, the side project of rock band Linkin Park's co-lead vocalist Mike Shinoda", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "what American Industrialist known as the Father of the maerican Industrial Revolution has a state park named after him in Rhode Island?", "answer": "Samuel Slater", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the 2011 American comedy film starring Kali Hawk?", "answer": "Paul Feig", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Nick Cassavetes and Donald Cammell, are actors?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which film is directed by Gary Nelson, Secretariat or Freaky Friday>", "answer": "Freaky Friday", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Was Life in Cold Blood broadcast in the same country that Black Tar Heroin was filmed in? ", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who won the US Open men's singles in 1975, Francesca Schiavone or Manuel Orantes ?", "answer": "Manuel Orantes Corral", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are both Waratah and Trachymene native to Fiji?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the area of the park where  Maui \u2018alauahio could be found? ", "answer": "33,265 acre", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Sophia B. Jones was the founder of the nursing program at a college located in which US state ?", "answer": "Georgia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who founded Eurasia Group in 1998?", "answer": "