on was constructed south of a city whose population was what in the census of 2010?", "answer": "139,966", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Both Mississippi State University and Florida International University in the United States?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "This thought experiment about an apparent perpetual motion machine was popularized by an American physicist who put out a lecture series concerning the nature of the laws of physics that was later recorded and published into a book by which organization?", "answer": "BBC", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed \"The Lake House\" with Hollywood actors Sandra Bullock and Keanu Reeves in 2006, Alejandro Agresti or Charles Barton?", "answer": "Alejandro Agresti", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Were both Stephen Spender and Charles Palliser Poet Laureates in 1965?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "When was the fort at which Lester W. Grau is the Research Coordinator for the Foreign Military Studies Office built ?", "answer": "1827", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What position does Emma Andersson's husband play?", "answer": "forward", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "More danico was a type of marriage that took place during what approximate timeframe?", "answer": "between c. 800AD and c. 1300AD", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Mexican state is Enrique Abaroa Castellanos from?", "answer": "Nuevo Le\u00f3n", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "WBAE (1490 kHz) is a commercial AM radio station licensed to Portland, Maine, WBAE's weekday schedule is made up of nationally syndicated shows from Westwood One and Premiere Networks, including America Now with which American columnist, author, former Fox News host and contributor, and blogger?", "answer": "Meghan McCain", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What hydraulic accumulator tower and a maritime landmark did James William Wild design?", "answer": "Grimsby Dock Tower", "type": "bridge"}, {"question"