ucky Wildcats football team represented the University of Kentucky, in the Southeastern Conference during the 1962 college football season, the winning margin was provided by a field goal by Clarkie Mayfield, one of the heroes of the game, who later died in which event that occurred on the night of May 28, 1977, during the Memorial Day holiday weekend, at which location event, in Southgate, Kentucky, is the third deadliest nightclub fire in U.S. history?", "answer": "Beverly Hills Supper Club fire", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Pascali's Island is a 1988 British drama film starring an English actor who began her acting career with what company in 1967?", "answer": "Royal Shakespeare Company", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Did Edwin Greenwood and Curtis Hanson create movies during the same time span?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Alan Mills composed the classic folk song that tells the story of what? ", "answer": "woman who swallowed increasingly large animals", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How is the climate where Paljor Stadium lies?", "answer": "a year-round mild temperate climate", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the classification of the novel that won the \"Los Angeles Times\" Book Prize, the 2001 Dilys Award written by an author best known for a series of suspense novels featuring Dr. Tony Hill?", "answer": "crime novel", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Fred Manville Taylor's book, \"Principles of Economics\", follows the lineage of which 19th century economist?", "answer": "Alfred Marshall", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Did both Burwell v. Hobby Lobby Stores, Inc. and Missouri v. Holland take place in the U.S.?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The 326th Airlift Squadron is part of the 512th Airlift Wing at a United States Air Force base located how far from the city of Dover, Delaware?", "answer": "2 mi", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Charles Wigram Long was a Conservative Party politician in what lower house from 1895 to 1910?", "answer": "The House of Commons", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The father of Monika Hertwig was the commandant of what concentration camp?", "answer": "Krak\u00f3w-P\u0142asz\u00f3w", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 2008 Asia Cup was broadcast on a Pakistani channel owned by what corporation?", "answer": "Independent Media Corporation", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Megan Kathleen Hilty, is an American actress and singer, she rose to prominence for her roles in Broadway musicals, including her performance as Glinda the Good Witch in which play?", "answer": "Wicked", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Y\u016bki Tokiwa (\u5e38\u76e4 \u7950\u8cb4 , Tokiwa Y\u016bki , born on August 16, 1991 in Hy\u014dgo-ken) is a Japanese voice actor, he  is the official Japanese voice dub-over artist for actor: \"Rupert Grint\" as which fictional character in J. K. Rowling's \"Harry Potter\" series?", "answer": "Ronald Bilius \"Ron\" Weasley", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Walter Iooss is a photographer who has taken images of the boxer who was of what nationality?", "answer": "American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Cliffhanger starred which actor who played Rocky Balboa?", "answer": "Michael Sylvester \"Sly\" Gardenzio Stallone", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Robertryan Cory, is an American animator known for his work in character design for series such as \"Secret Mountain Fort Awesome\", an American animated television series created by Peter Browngardt that debuted in which year, on Cartoon Network?", "answer": "2011", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were George Pearson and Sidney Lanfield both film directors?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who designed the plant near the Ford World Headquarters?", "answer": "Albert Kahn", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the dean of an international business school located in Paris, France that is widely considered to be one of the most prestigious and selective graduate schools in the world, between 1996 and 2015?", "answer": "Bernard Ramanantsoa", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Green Square railway station is located on the Airport line, serving which city suburb of Alexandria, a suburb in the inner-east of Sydney, New South Wales, Australia?", "answer": "Sydney", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who, Daniel Dennet or Alastair hannay, uses a more scientific approach to their research?", "answer": "Daniel Dennett", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which country is Casciana Terme found?", "answer": "Italy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A luxury train ran by what company travels a landlocked country in Southern Africa, neighbouring the Democratic Republic of the Congo to the north? ", "answer": "Rovos Rail", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When did was the cease fire of the event that started when the Kwantung Army of the Empire of Japan invaded Manchuria?", "answer": "May 31, 1933", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Swiss vocalist born in 1975 founded the Swiss folk metal band which released 7 studio albums?", "answer": "Christian \"Chrigel\" Glanzmann", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The owner of the production company 40 Acres and a Mule Filmworks worked with Marvin Worth to create what film?", "answer": "Malcolm X", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Terryfold\" is a song created for an animated tv series that appears on what network?", "answer": "Cartoon Network", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the father of the man born Rudolph Valentino Clay?", "answer": "Cassius Marcellus Clay, Sr.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Zvuki Mu and Birdland both rock bands?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which university hosts the Plattsburgh State Television station in Plattsburgh, NY?", "answer": "SUNY", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "General Abdul Hamid Khan, (what is the official, and \"lingua franca\" of Pakistan: \u0639\u0628\u062f \u0627\u0644\u062d\u064