estion": "Who owns the channel that Business Nation aires on monthly?", "answer": "Comcast", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are GCA Savvian and Houlihan Lokey both global investment banks?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Khadijah Farrakhan is the wife of the Supreme Leader of a movement founded in what city?", "answer": "Detroit", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Major League Baseball 2K12 or, in short, MLB 2K12, is a Major League Baseball licensed baseball simulation video game published by 2K Sports, Justin Verlander of the Detroit Tigers is the game's cover athlete, Verlander  is an American professional baseball pitcher for the Houston Astros, of which sports organization?", "answer": "Major League Baseball (MLB)", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\u00c6thelwulf of Berkshire (before 825 \u2013 4 January, 871) was a Saxon ealdorman, he received a land grant in 843/44 from Brihtwulf, king of Mercia; and lost his life at which battle event?", "answer": "Battle of Reading", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The lead vocalist of what band presented awards with Bryan Ferry and Ian \"Molly\" Meldrum?", "answer": "The Undertones", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the film in which Jack Albertson played Grandpa Joe ?", "answer": "Mel Stuart", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Anton Karlsson was drafted by which Glendale, Arizona based hockey team in 2014?", "answer": "Arizona Coyotes", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "This American poet and lecturer has her poems appear in which American online magazine that publishes poetry, short stories and creative nonfiction?", "answer": "Word Riot", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "WFGC is a CTN owned-and-operated television station serving a city incorporated in what year?", "answer": "1894", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American actor, who is best known for playing Dan Conner, stars in the 2016 American science fiction psychological thriller film 10 Cloverfield Lane?", "answer": "John Goodman", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How are Exeter Cathedral and Plymouth Cathedral similar?", "answer": "Anglican cathedral", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are both World and Cricket published in Ashenville?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What indigenous people in Western Canada named Lake of the Little Fishes?", "answer": "Nakoda", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "S\u00fcleymaniye Mosque and R\u00fcstem Pasha Mosque share what style?", "answer": "Ottoman", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Did Brandenburg v. Ohio occur prior to Miranda v. Arizona?  ", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Alec Baldwin guest starred in which 2004 \"The Fairly Oddparents\" television film? ", "answer": "Channel Chasers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What's the name of a perennial flowering plant who's female root name Valeria, meaning \"to be strong\"?", "answer": "Valerian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "During which period Dame Mary Ethel Hughes GBE's husband hold the responsibility of administering the Department of the Prime Minister and Cabinet?", "answer": "1915 to 1923", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Andrzej Zebrzydowski served as chaplain for which powerful member of the house that ruled the Duchy of Milan?", "answer": "Bona Sforza", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which location hosts both the Throne of Jahangir and the UNESCO World Heritage site?", "answer": "Agra Fort", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What county was Emily Lesueur born in?", "answer": "Los Angeles County", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which English musician wrote a song to pay tribute to the founder and front man of the Motown vocal group the Miracles?", "answer": "George Harrison", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Black Windmill is a film produced by a man best known for coproducing what? ", "answer": "Jaws", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Alvin Ailey and Virgil Thomson both worked in what American metropolis?", "answer": "New York City", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When did the process occur that occurred after the futhorc runes are thought to have been developed, resulting in the Anglo-Saxon runes to also being called the Anglo-Frisian runes?", "answer": "mid-fifth to early seventh centuries", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which businessman contributed to the construction of the theme park where Intimidator is found?", "answer": "Earl Patterson Hall", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Hamilton JournalNews was a daily broadsheet newspaper based in Hamilton, Ohio owned by Cox Media Group, in September 2013, Cox Media Group Ohio announced that, effective November 1, the \"Hamilton JournalNews\" would be merged with \"The Middletown Journal\" into which new paper, which daily newspaper published by Cox Media Group in Liberty Township, Butler County, Ohio, United States?", "answer": "Journal-News", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What do the song \"What Would I Do If I Could Feel\" and Nipsey Russell have in common?", "answer": "The Wiz", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which show is is directed by the same people who were presenters for the Holy Trinity?", "answer": "W. Chump and Sons", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What British-Italian film premiered in 1968 which included the song \"A Time for Us\" written by Larry Kusic?", "answer": "Romeo and Juliet", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is a writer of a musical that has been performed at a school in British Columbia?", "answer": "Lynn Ahrens", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What county is DerpyCon held in?", "answer": "Morris County", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Sugarloaf Regional Airport is owned by a town with a population of what, as of the 2010 census?", "answer": "761", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Montenegrin Mountain Hound and Mudhol Hound are both used for what common purpose?", "answer": "hunting", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What role did the actor, who starred in the 1980 Italian crime-d