ns of Shakespearean plays, has its home in a 1,800 seat open air theater located in Central Park?", "answer": "Shakespeare in the Park", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which park in Manhattan can be seen from the San Remo, the 27-floor apartment building opened in 1930?", "answer": "Central Park", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which animated film did John Powell compose the score to that became the highest-grossing stop motion animated film ever?", "answer": "Chicken Run", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Royal Republic and The Lemonheads are both what?", "answer": "rock band", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What companies does the creator of Heroes for Hire work for?", "answer": "Marvel Comics and DC Comics", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who did Paul Ziert coach who went on to compete in the 1984 Summer Olympic Games?", "answer": "Bart Conner", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "what are T.I. and Sam Martins ethinic background?", "answer": "American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which ancient civilzation of ancient Northeastern Africa did the official Djehuty under the ruling queen Hatshepsut live? ", "answer": "Ancient Egypt", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " are Orychophragmus and Chrysobalanus a genus of the same family", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "World's Greatest Dad is a 2009 American satirical black comedy film, its stars include Daryl Sabara, an American actor, perhaps best known for playing who in the \"Spy Kids\" film series?", "answer": "Juni Cortez", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " The Siege of Fort Pitt was part of a war named after which leader ?", "answer": "the Odawa leader Pontiac", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the magazine aimed at that Judson Jerome wrote the poetry column for over thirty years?", "answer": "beginning and established writers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How long was the reign of the king whose court Paon de Roet became attached to?", "answer": "50 years", "type": 