01 by a benefaction, from which former CEO of Tyco International?", "answer": "Leo Dennis Kozlowski", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many cultural/linguistic divisions are there in the tribe of which Sacajawea was a member?", "answer": "four", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What SBS television series aired in 2009 staring lead vocalist in the band CNBLUE?", "answer": "You're Beautiful", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Delamere railway station serves which large wood near Frodsham?", "answer": "Delamere Forest", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "David M. Ewalt worked at a digital magazine which is headquartered in San Francisco, and was first published in 1985 by who?", "answer": "CMP Media", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "My First Night Without You was a single released from which LGBT rights activist?", "answer": "Cynthia Ann Stephanie \"Cyndi\" Lauper", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Agnee is a remake of the 2011 film produced by whom?", "answer": "Luc Besson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What state did Qiudong Wang recieve his Ph.D in?", "answer": "Ohio", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What executive agency of the U.S. state of New Hampshire charged with overseeing the state correctional facilities is in charge of New Hampshire State Prison for Women?", "answer": "New Hampshire Department of Corrections", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Blue Lacy, official breed of Texas, and Chesapeake Bay Retriever, are both dog breeds developed during which century?", "answer": "19th century", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Ballester\u2013Molina is a pistol designed and built by a company that manufactures what ?", "answer": "vehicles, aircraft, machinery, weaponry and parts for public works", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the 2010 census of the town at which Pillsbury State Park was located? ", "answer": "1,123", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What  American young earth creationist and geophysicist was on  a research project conducted by the Creation Research Society and the Institute for Creation Research between 1997 and 2005?", "answer": "John R. Baumgardner", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where do the team that Dick Dickey played for in the NBA play their home games ?", "answer": "the TD Garden,", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How old was Amon G\u00f6th's daughter (Monika Hertwig) on his hanging for war crimes in this 2006 documentary \"Inheritance\"?", "answer": "10 months old", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Australian rules footballer dubbed Mick Nolan as  \"The Galloping Gasomete", "answer": "Lewis Thomas Charles", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Kempinski Residences, Jakarta is a residential skyscraper at Jalan M.H. Thamrin, Central Jakarta, Indonesia, the building is connected to Grand Indonesia Shopping Town, an integrated multipurpose complex at Jalan M.H. Thamrin, Central Jakarta, Indonesia, and is located near what?", "answer": "Selamat Datang Monument", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Housatonic Congregational Church is located in what county?", "answer": "Berkshire", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which major metropolitan area do the Senior Pastors of International Church of Las Vegas reside?", "answer": "Las Vegas Valley", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Anthony Levandowski's project, Waymo, is from what company?", "answer": "autonomous car development company spun out of Google's parent company, Alphabet Inc., in December 2016.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Both Ben Foster and The Grey have this country in comman?", "answer": "British", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Catherine Opali\u0144ska and  Marie Leszczy\u0144ska both consorted with which Polish King?", "answer": "Stanis\u0142aw I", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the American head football coach for the Arizona Cardinals that has also been a college level coach?", "answer": "Bruce Charles Arians", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which musician formed the band The Genuine Fakes?", "answer": "Johan Bergqvist", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Bridge Day is an annual one-day festival in Fayetteville, Fayette County, West Virginia, United States The event is coordinated by the New River Gorge Bridge Day Commission, the event, held on the third Saturday every October, commemorates the 1977 completion of which steel arch bridge 3030 ft long over the New River Gorge near Fayetteville, West Virginia, in the Appalachian Mountains?", "answer": "New River Gorge Bridge", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "AnnoZero is an Italian television talk show hosted by the Italian journalist Michele Santoro and has been broadcast on Rai 2 since 2006, which member of the ancient aristocratic House of Borromeo, and she is well known in the Italian news media as a television personality, was a collaborator on this show from 2006\u20132008?", "answer": "Beatrice Borromeo", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the area of the country of origin of Emil Szolomajer?", "answer": "238397 km2", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Resurrection of Gavin Stone starred the actress who was a cast member of what show during its 13th season?", "answer": "MADtv", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Name the aria from \"The Barber of Seville\" sung at the first entrance of the title character and which also features in the seven-minute long Technicolor animated short film, One Foggy Evening, often referred to as Figaro's aria?", "answer": "Largo al factotum", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The English actress Raine Davison and which actress, who rose to fame after winning a talent contest, appeared in the same English Soap Operas (different years)?", "answer": "Suzanne Shaw", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name character in Magnum P.I. that was played by the star of The Closer?", "answer": "Thomas Magnum", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is older, Khlo\u00e9 Kardashian or George Aghajanian?", "answer": "George Aghajanian", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "W