ist that worked alongside physicists Eugene Wigner and John Archibald Wheeler as part of the Princeton Three?", "answer": "Oskar Morgenstern", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Let Love Lead the Way\" is a song by an English girl group formed in what year?", "answer": "1994", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Mbangoi-Koni-Mizidjou is a village on the island of Grande Comore in an archipelago island nation located in what ocean?", "answer": "Indian Ocean", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Lee Edwards is a distinguished fellow in conservative thought at the B. Kenneth Simon Center for American Studies at The Heritage Foundation, he has published more than 15 books, including the biography of which American attorney, law professor, author and member of the Republican Party?", "answer": "Edwin Meese III", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Roberta Latow gave Andy Warhol the idea to paint an artwork that was produced in what year ?", "answer": "1962", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which film did David Newman compose music for, based on a 1955 play by Marcelle Maurette?", "answer": "Anastasia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What fungus, which is widely distributed across the Northern Hemisphere is related to the fungus Bloetus austroedulis?", "answer": "Boletus edulis", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The clothing company founded by Arthur Ryan is an anchor tenant of what shopping center in Redditch, England?", "answer": "Kingfisher Shopping Centre", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which English actor and musician, born 16 May 1990, was in which 2014 American dystopian science fiction action thriller film?", "answer": "Thomas Brodie-Sangster", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Michael Dobson is an author who has helped with the RPG that was published by what company in 1984?", "answer": "TSR, Inc.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Liam O'Connor is a multi-instrumentalist musician, described as \"the Jimi Hendrix of the accordion\", Hendrix was an American rock guita