cksburg?", "answer": "Battle of Fredericksburg", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Mark Lawrence ran in the US Senate election that was held on what date?", "answer": "November 7, 2000", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the prequel in the Guardians of Ga'Hoole series, written by Kathryn Lasky, that was published in 2013?", "answer": "The Rise of a Legend", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was a monk, Thomas Merton or Frank Norris?", "answer": "Thomas Merton", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Benjamin Wallfisch composed the original score for which movie based on the 1986 Stephen King novel?", "answer": "It", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who started earlier, Sidney Franklin or John McKay?", "answer": "Sidney Arnold Franklin", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "A Concert: Behind Prison Walls is the fifty-fourth overall album and a live album recorded by Johnny Cash in the Tennessee Prison 1974, Cash's conceptual series of live albums recorded before an audience of prison inmates, At San Quentin is which ordinal numeral, overall album by Johnny Cash, recorded live at San Quentin State Prison on February 24, 1969?", "answer": "31st", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Do Stanley Tucci and Michael Anderson have the same nationality?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Willis 'Shorty' Hogue was a boxer in California during the 1940s, along with which American professional boxer and the longest reigning World Light Heavyweight Champion of all time?", "answer": "Archie Moore", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Der Vampyr and Pomone both operas?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Hassan Saleh is from which state capital of New South Wales?", "answer": "Sydney", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What English group's seventh studio album was featured on Lauren Laverne's BBC Radio 6 show?", "answer": "Goldfrapp", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the cover which \"Prog\" features released originally ", "answer": "22 March 1985", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Batura Sar and Siguang Ri both located in Tibet?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Man with Rain in His Shoes starred which English voice actress and producer?", "answer": "Lena Headey", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Queens Place Mall includes a footwear retailer located in what Ohio city as one of its flagship stores?", "answer": "Columbus", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Grutter v. Bollinger and Korematsu v. United States, are concerning which mutual organization?", "answer": "United States Supreme Court", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What mountain range includes the gully that borders Eagle On The Hill?", "answer": "Mount Lofty Ranges", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Red Badge of Courage is a war novel by American author Stephen Crane, Stephen Crane died June 5, 1900, was an American poet, novelist, and short story writer, born when?", "answer": "November 1, 1871", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the rain goddess praised in a Tamil folk dance during Isha Gramotsavam?", "answer": "Mariamman", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born first, Maurice Ravel or Mikhail Glinka?", "answer": "Mikhail Ivanovich Glinka", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What was the name of the daughter of the only sitting house member elected president that married the private secretary Joseph Stanley Brown?", "answer": "Mary \"Mollie\" Garfield", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which genus has more species, the Catharanthus or the Bosea?", "answer": "Catharanthus", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Blind Alfred Reed, was an American folk, country, and old-time musician and singer-songwriter, he was one of the artists who recorded at the Bristol Sessions in which year, alongside more famous names such as The Carter Family, a traditional American folk music group that recorded between 1927 and 1956?", "answer": "1927", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Lee Pelty was best known for his performances in numerous productions of a musical adapted from what Dale Wasserman non-musical 1959 teleplay?", "answer": "I, Don Quixote", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Do the genuses Hyacinthoides and Mikania belong to the same family?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which company published both SpongeBob SquarePants: SuperSponge and Tak and the Power of Juju?", "answer": "THQ", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Shootout at Wadala, is a 2013 Indian biographical-crime film, in which a Mumbai gangster plays a lead role?", "answer": "Manya Surve", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where does English footballer Jack King play home games?", "answer": "Broadhall Way", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which writer is older, Alessandro Baricco or Patrick White?", "answer": "Patrick Victor Martindale White", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What country singer who released the album \"Hero\", helped write the song \"Craving You\" by Thomas Rhett?", "answer": "Maren Morris", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Navier\u2013Stokes equations were partially named after which French engineer?", "answer": "Claude-Louis Navier", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which conference did this football team compete in 1997 for which Chris Floyd played as a senior?", "answer": "Big Ten Conference", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the occupation that both Giulio Caccini and Peter Philips have?", "answer": "composer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the voice for all major male Warner Bros, cartoon characters, except Elmer Fudd, and provided voice for Racketeer Rabbit?", "answer": "Mel Blanc", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Heat Miser\" is a character from which Christmas special based on Phyllis McGinley's 1974 book?", "answer": "The Year Without a Santa Claus", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Whose performing act had more members, Marie Fredriksson or Dee Snider?", "answer": "Daniel \"Dee\" Snider"