ervation Society of Newport County", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the Ulster-Scots name for the island where Thomas de Thelwall held office as Master of the Rolls and clerk to the Privy Council?", "answer": "Airlann", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Eh, Eh (Nothing Else I Can Say)\" is a song by a singer who rose to fame with the release of her debut album titled what ?", "answer": "The Fame", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Henry Davis, was an American Broadway actor and singer, he created the role of Robbins in George Gershwin's opera, titled what?", "answer": "Porgy and Bess", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "how long did Alan McCarthy play for Watfor F.C.?", "answer": "he spent loan spells", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Big Sir is a band that includes which bass guitarist, a Mexican-American musician, best known as the longtime bassist of Racer X and The Mars Volta?", "answer": "Juan Alderete", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In the pilot episode of The Golden Girls, who had the last name given as Hollingsworth, but was somewhat \"corrected\" in later episodes, by making this her maiden name?", "answer": "Blanche Devereaux", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Samantha Sainte-Claire Ponder, is an American sportscaster from Phoenix, Arizona who is currently the host of Sunday NFL Countdown on ESPN, Ponder replaced Erin Andrews, on which TV show?", "answer": "College GameDay", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Search for the Super Battery and Crazy English both American documentaries?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which English town is 11 miles south of Manchester and along with Prestbury and Alderley Edge makes up the Cheshire Golden Triangle?", "answer": "Wilmslow", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Pigeon Key, Florida is located off an old bridge in which county ?", "answer": "Monroe County", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both the Small M\u00fcnsterl\u00e4nder and Grand Anglo-Fran\u00e7ais Tricolore dog breeds?"