ecting films earlier, Edmund Goulding or Marc Webb?", "answer": "Edmund Goulding", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The smallest denomination of the Hong Kong dollar is the one mil coin which has which identifying feature?", "answer": "hole in the middle", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Army of Darkness: Shop till You Drop Dead continues the comic book saga of a film directed by which director ?", "answer": "Sam Raimi", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Indian film actress born in 1994 has starred in Naiyaandi as well as other Tamil and Malayaam films?", "answer": "Nazriya Nazim", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What nationality is the basketball player who holds the most points scored during the Nike Hoops Summit game?", "answer": "Turkish", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is  best known for their 1995 radio hit \"Stars\", The Virgins or Hum ?", "answer": "Hum", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Of what origin is the name of the Russian game that inspired Puyo Puyo?", "answer": "Russian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jonathan Burton founded the parent company of Traveller's Tales in what year?", "answer": "2005", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both Redbook and Bust targeted towards women?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Nick Saglimbeni has photographed commercials for the performance footwear brand headquartered where?", "answer": "Manhattan Beach, California", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Hungarian composer wrote a piece for solo piano which contained Romanian, Arabic, and North African rhythmic influences?", "answer": "B\u00e9la Bart\u00f3k", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was Francis Crick's co-discoverer of the structure of the DNA molecule which was based partly on fundamental studies done by English chemis and X-ray crystallographer Rosalind Franklin?", "answer": "James Watson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Both Arctotis and Cyphomandra are what classification level of plants?", "answer": "genus", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which state in the midwestern region of the United States, houses the Cremastobombycia ignota moth?", "answer": "Illinois", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who has more tennis titles, Svetlana Kuznetsova or Andr\u00e9s G\u00f3mez?", "answer": "Svetlana Aleksandrovna Kuznetsova", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who wrote the music for the video games, which are based on the movies which Alexandre Desplat wrote the musical scores for?", "answer": "Jeremy Soule and James Hannigan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Canadian communications and media company that owns broadband internet service provider Rogers Hi-Speed Internet in headquartered where?", "answer": "Toronto, Ontario", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year was Midwives star, Allison Pill, born in?", "answer": "1985", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "District B was a housing district located near what textile manufacturer which founded Manchester, New Hampshire?", "answer": "Amoskeag Manufacturing Company", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Manning Kimmel is the son of which US Navy Admiral?", "answer": "Husband Edward Kimmel", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the Chinese physician, writer and philosopher died for who's birth places Cuiheng village was famous for?", "answer": "12 March 1925", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What ammunition plat was built 6km north of a city that was incorporated in 1889?", "answer": "The Alabama Army Ammunition Plant", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "On February 12, 2015, the Islamic State of Iraq and the Levant (ISIL) released a report in which online magazine used by the Islamic State of Iraq and the Levant (ISIL) for islam and recruitment, showing photos of 21 Egyptian Coptic Christian construction workers who that they had kidnapped in the city of Sirte, Libya, and whom they threatened to kill?", "answer": "Dabiq", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many episodes were included in the sixth season of the series that included Fairly OddBaby?", "answer": "20", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year did the The Teddy Bear Song, sung by a popular American country and gospel singer, reach No. 32 on the \"Billboard\" Hot 100?", "answer": "1973", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What position did both Andy Bell and Judith Durham hold in their music groups?", "answer": "lead singer", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The central ring of the Hammerstein Ballroom holds several thousand people for events which can take place in a raised platform square with 4 parallel ropes attached with turnbuckle called what?", "answer": "A boxing ring", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the Muslim name of the man who put out the album \"Soul Finger\"?", "answer": "Abdullah Ibn Buhaina", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which French Emperor annulled The Le Chapelier Law in 1864?", "answer": "Louis-Napol\u00e9on Bonaparte", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which documentary came out first, \"The Climb\" or \"It Might Get Loud\"?", "answer": "The Climb", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which French football celebrity did Welsh manager Chris Coleman replace at Fulham FC in 2003?", "answer": "Jean Tigana", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What team did the man who turned down the first head coach job of the New York Islanders play for for 25 seasons?  ", "answer": "Detroit Red Wings", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the film that opened the 2017 Cannes Film Festival?", "answer": "Arnaud Desplechin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was American actress, best known for her film roles in Where the Boys Are and 1981 horror comedy film, Saturday the 14th, born?", "answer": "March 4, 1938", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Mick Jackson (born 4 October 1943 in Grays, England, United Kingdom) is a British film director and television producer, relocating to Hollywood, he directed feature films, including \"The Bodyguard\" starring Kevin Costner and which 