icts working-class life where in one episode the family visits Itchy & Scratchy Land for a perfect vacation?", "answer": "The Simpsons", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Kim Tae-woo and Shaun Ryder both singers ?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What the man who received a medal of honor during the American Civil War capture that represented the Confederacy?", "answer": "Confederacy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "This band was founded in 2002 by a male vocalist who was born where?", "answer": "Basel, Switzerland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were both Reno v. American Civil Liberties Union and Curtis Publishing Co. v. Butts related to the First Amendment?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What award, established by philantropist Peter Thiel, was Dale Stephens an original recipient of?", "answer": "the Thiel Fellowship", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Directed by an English-born American puppeteer, Bowfinger, a 1999 American satirical comedy film, grossed how much money during its showing?", "answer": "$98 million", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which band was formed first The Exies or Circus Diablo ?", "answer": "The Exies", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In what year was the actor who starred with Tom Payne, Dominique Tipper, Melia Kreiling, Antonia Campbell-Hughes, and Oliver Stark in the film \"MindGamers\" born?", "answer": "1947", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was the company that owned the St. Louis Cardinals headquartered?", "answer": "Leuven, Belgium", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which music group was active earlier, Massive Attack or Violent Femmes?", "answer": "Violent Femmes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "what is the name of the poison isolated from Duscle garden nightshade?", "answer": "Solanine", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the pen name of the author of Junkie: Confessions of an Unredeemed Drug Addict?", "answer": "William Lee", "type": "bridge"}, {"