l known for popularising what in England?", "answer": "tobacco", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What historic site in Macon County was supplied by Lucius B. Northrop?", "answer": "Andersonville", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which building was constructed first - 1095 Avenue of the Americas or One Vanderbilt Place?", "answer": "1095 Avenue of the Americas", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which magazine, Airliners or Y'all, had its editorial headquarters in Castro Valley, California?", "answer": "Airliners", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who is the current president of the organization in which Naoki Inoue is signed and competes in the flyweight division?", "answer": "Dana White", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the nationality of the creator of Hello Ladies?", "answer": "English", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "William O. Studeman served under which Director of Central Intelligence born on September 21, 1941 ?", "answer": "R. James Woolsey Jr.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is this British West End theatre producer and film producer that appeared on \"When Joseph Met Maria\" as a judge?", "answer": "Bill Kenwright", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The San Francisco Demons were part of a failed professional American football league which played one season in what year?", "answer": "2001", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Lee Valley White Water Centre was officially opened by the only daughter of what Queen?", "answer": "Queen Elizabeth II", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Cattleya and Leucocoryne of the same genus of flowers?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who wrote the music for musical comedy in which Heidi Blickenstaff originated the role of Bea ?", "answer": "Karey and Wayne Kirkpatrick.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Robert Knight co-founded a clothing manufacturing company that is headquartered in what city?", "answer": "Bowling Green", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "which German 88 mm an