her Side of AIDS and Control Room, share which genre?", "answer": "documentary", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which company's brewery is located adjacent to the theme park where the Zierer multi-launching steel roller coaster, Verbolten, is located?", "answer": "Anheuser-Busch", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was the man who Mick Kelly was production assistant to born and raised?", "answer": "Detroit, Michigan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Tuborg Squash is a Danish orange flavoured soft drink, brewed and distributed by a comany founded by who ?", "answer": "Carl Frederik Tietgen", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which candidate did Edward Timpson defeat, Laura Smith or Tamsin Dunwoody? ", "answer": "Laura Smith", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Price of Inequality: How Today's Divided Society Endangers Our Future is a 2012 book by Joseph Eugene Stiglitz that deals with income inequality in the United States, an American economist and a professor at where?", "answer": "Columbia University", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Helter Skelter presented the firsthand account of the murder who was a part of whose \"family\"?", "answer": "Charles Manson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What college football team is a part of KWWN's programming and has home games played at Sam Boyd Stadium?", "answer": "UNLV Rebels football", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Caf\u00e9 Oz Australian Bar features Little Creatures Pale Ale which is named after which band?", "answer": "Talking Heads", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Californian band, formed in Modesto in 1992, once wrote a song about an android who drinks himself to death?", "answer": "Grandaddy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The last living pilot of the X-15 program was inducted into the National Aviation Hall of Fame in what year?", "answer": "2001", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which has more acts, Elektra or From the House of the Dead?", "answer": "From the House of the Dead", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What singer had a song reach number ninety-eight on the UK Singles Chart and was featured in a film starring Jeff Bridges and Ryan Reynolds?", "answer": "Robyn", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which is larger in area, Garajonay National Park or Timanfaya National Park?", "answer": "Timanfaya National Park", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Georges Bizet and Peter Maxwell Davies, were both European, and had which occupation?", "answer": "composer", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "On what Marc Cherry show did the actor who played Jim Ellison on The Sentinel star?", "answer": "Desperate Housewives", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Matt Serra was one of four fighters to win both the Ultimate Fighter and UFC welterweight classifications, along with the police officer from what state?", "answer": "Georgia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Insulin detemir is a long-acting human insulin analogue for maintaining the basal level of insulin, Novo Nordisk markets it under which trade name?", "answer": "Levemir", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is the online shoe and clothing store owned by Tony Hsieh based?", "answer": "Las Vegas, Nevada", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was a renowned French actor and director, Louis Jouvet or Luis Bu\u00f1uel?", "answer": "Louis Jouvet", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Pulp and My Morning Jacket both having their sound rooted in which genre?", "answer": "rock", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Rucellai Sepulchre was built by an Italian humanist author who epitomised what?", "answer": "the Renaissance Man", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the American hamburger restaurant described as a \"breastaurant\", which features skimpily-clad female wait staff, known for serving high-calorie menu items, located in Downtown Las Vegas after it moved from Tempe, Arizona?", "answer": "Heart Attack Grill", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What lake is the farm Peter Gi