d at stadium that accommodates a total of how many spectators?", "answer": "32,912", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which institution is women only: Texas Christian University or Wellesley College?", "answer": "Wellesley College", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Dale Cregan was sentenced to life imprisonment for the murder of two police officers. The officers were responding to a report of a what?", "answer": "burglary", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What city was the group, in which James Iha and Taylor Hanson are members, founded in?", "answer": "New York City", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Between two Americans, Mameve Medwed and Sherman Alexie, who works in a broader range of arts?", "answer": "Sherman Joseph Alexie, Jr.", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Do both the American Pit Bull Terrier and Rhodesian Ridgeback originate from South Africa?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Between Donatos Pizza and Extreme Pizza what is the only country to have one of these restaurants besides the United States?", "answer": "Ireland", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which film was released first, Hero of the Rails, or Laura's Star?", "answer": "Laura's Star", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Both Claude Nicollier and Franco Malerba had what occupation?", "answer": "astronaut", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What movie starred Scott Gordon Patterson and was directed by David Hackl?", "answer": "Saw V", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is older, Tom E. Lewis or Fred Schepisi?", "answer": "Frederic Alan \"Fred\" Schepisi", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Geoffrey Wilder is the father of which Runaways supervillain?", "answer": "Alex Wilder", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "On which college campus in Manchester, New Hampshire is the Southern New Hampshire Fieldhouse located?", "answer": "Southern New Hampshire University", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What continent are the genuses Allocasuarina and Acacia mainly native to? ", "answer": "mainly native to Australia", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "When was the  German political and military leader died who's collections during World War Two were written in the first comprehensive catalog of Nancy H. Yeide?", "answer": "15 October 1946", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were Lytton Strachey and Ir\u00e8ne N\u00e9mirovsky both writers?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The problem that Banca Civica was created to deal with began in what year?", "answer": "2009", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was a famous Persian Sufi who lived in the 11th century in Herat who's works refer to a particularly important group of God's saints?", "answer": "Khajah Abdullah Ansari", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was Brasserie d'Achouffe bought by the brewery known for its \"Duvel\" pale ale?", "answer": "September 2006", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the actor younger brother of the co-writer of Club Paradise?", "answer": "Bill Murray", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What profession do both Tim Conlon and Kehinde Wiley have?", "answer": "artist", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what school district is the high school Jonathan Florencio attended?", "answer": "Bellmore-Merrick Central High School District", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born first, Robert Rossen or Lamont Johnson?", "answer": "Robert Rossen", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "K2 and Khartaphu, are both elevated land masses, what are they called?", "answer": "mountain", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Rehmannia and Cunninghamia are both native to what country?", "answer": "China", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which of these films was produced most recently--Day of the Fight or Woodstock?  ", "answer": "Woodstock", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which canal was in operation longer, Leiper Canal or Carondelet Canal?", "answer": "Carondelet Canal", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are Saludos Ami