ue Act of 1924 was named born? ", "answer": "March 24, 1855", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Wong Ka Kui and Hugh Cornwell are both known for what musical talent?", "answer": "being the vocalist and guitarist", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "On what piece of equipment was the first part of the In Colour album produced?", "answer": "laptop", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What song by a Barbadian singer was covered by Mari\u00e9 Christina Digby?", "answer": "\"Umbrella\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Monster House  is a 2006 American 3D computer-animated family horror comedy film directed by Gil Kenan, produced by ImageMovers and Amblin Entertainment, and distributed by Columbia Pictures about a neighborhood that's being terrorized by a demonic house : and is also, a  Discovery Channel television program that documented the themed remodeling of a what, in a five-day time frame?", "answer": "residence", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which statue of John Henry Foley's full name is Francis Albert Augustus Charles Emmanuel?", "answer": "Prince Albert", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What type of music does the artist who recorded \"God Bless the U.S.A.\" specialize in?", "answer": "country", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the birth date of this American writer of history and folklore of Appalachia, who wrote the Bimbos of the Death Sun?", "answer": "February 26, 1948", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who came to prominence first, Saul Metzstein or Elem Klimov?", "answer": "Klimov", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In what year was the man who commanded the Nachtjagdgeschwader 4 from 20 November 1944 to 8 May 1945 born?", "answer": "1922", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was a widely used high-level programming language for general-purpose programming, created by the \"Benevolent Dictator For Life\", first released?", "answer": "1991", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The sixteeth episode of the 25th season of \"The Simpsons\" has 