ation where the Tumbler and Goblet Factory was located in 2010?", "answer": "2,415", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Toy Trawler Spaniel and Podenco Canario are both breeds of what?", "answer": "dog", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who had a fuller tennis carrer, Am\u00e9lie Mauresmo or Corina Morariu?", "answer": "Am\u00e9lie Simone Mauresmo ] (born 5 July 1979) is a French former professional tennis player, and a former world No. 1. Mauresmo won two Grand Slam singles titles at the Australian Open and at Wimbledon, and also won a Silver Medal at the 2004 Summer Olympics.", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which Queen of England and Ireland who lived from 18 February 1516 - 17 November 1558 did Sir George Howard serve under?", "answer": "Mary I", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "London Buses route 28 begins at a shopping centre located in what part of London?", "answer": "Wandsworth Town, Wandsworth, London, England", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Fake Problems and Kaizers Orchestra from the same country?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who is the co-star of the current co-president of the Actors Studio in the movie Youth?", "answer": "Michael Caine", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Stand-In was released in which year, an American comedy film directed by Tay Garnett, and starring Leslie Howard, born on 3 April 1891 - June 1943, was an English stage and film actor, director and producer?", "answer": "1937", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is Stephen F. Cohen's wife's nationality?", "answer": "American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Myrtus and Chrysanthemum, are which mutual specific types?", "answer": "flowering plants", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "By what nickname was the star of the film Alien 51 referred to? ", "answer": "\"Hollywood Madam\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Stephan Pastis and Endurance both based in the comedy fields?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Atom Egoyan received his commercial success in a film directed by who?", "answer": "Atom Egoyan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 1965 Italian Grand Prix (formally the XXXVI Gran Premio d'Italia), was a Formula One motor race held at Monza, on 12 September 1965, the preceding retirement of which Ferrari driver, an English Grand Prix motorcycle road racer and Formula One driver, helped ensured that Dan Gurney of the Brabham-Climax team picked up the final position on the podium?", "answer": "John Surtees", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the most famous king of the House of Griffins, and King of Sweden, Denmark and Norway in the 14th and 15th centuries?", "answer": "Eric of Pomerania", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the stage name of Carlo Maria Michelangelo Nicola Broschi, Italian castrati, who was portrayed by Stefano Dionisi in a movie.", "answer": "Farinelli", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Lee El was an actress in what neo noir political crime film?", "answer": "Inside Men", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The founder of the band \"Black Veil Brides\" appears in an upcoming American thriller film written by what two people?", "answer": "Ash Avildsen and Matty Beckerman", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is a word that connects the two paragraphs?", "answer": "The", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Connor Freff Cochran interviewed what American musician and composer that was born in Rode Island, and studied physics and music at Brown University?", "answer": "Wendy Carlos", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which movement was lead by the poet who is included among those David S. Reynolds is an expert on?", "answer": "transcendentalist", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the band who released Double Dubliners founded?", "answer": "1962", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How long did Bobby Bowden coach for the team that represented Florida State University in the 1998 NCAA Division 1 season?", "answer": "1976 to 2009", "type": "bridge