hart?", "answer": "number 7", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the author of \"Blow-up and Other Stories\" born? ", "answer": "August 26, 1914", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Adrian the Barbarian (later Olaff the Madlander) was a comic strip in the comic The Beezer, and later the merged Beezer and Topper, first introduced in which year?", "answer": "1989", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Walt Disney Pictures films was released first, \"Honey, I Shrunk the Kids\", or \"Blank Check\"?", "answer": "Honey, I Shrunk the Kids", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "are K\u00f6nigskinder and  Pomone the same type of production?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What company manufactured the plane on which the Doomsday plane was based?", "answer": "Voronezh Aircraft Production Association", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What 1999 movie is the person who palys a young lady in My First Wedding known for?", "answer": "She's All That", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Magic Labyrinth and Near and Far, have which mutual attributes?", "answer": "board game", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The first Alabama football Heisman winner was drafted by what NFL team?", "answer": "New Orleans Saints", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where we these two people from?", "answer": "Hawaii", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the star born who Who has roles in both The Pursuit of Happyness and The Death and Life of John F. Donovan?", "answer": "6 November 1972", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "At which university the beverage was first developed in 1965 and for which Gary Shore directed commercials?", "answer": "University of Florida", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What has been an event at the Asian Games since they were first held in Delhi, India?", "answer": "Handball", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of Kim Yeo-jin's movies had overt sexual dialogue?", "answer": "Girls' Night Out", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What 