roduced by the British studio Aardman Animations?", "answer": "Chicken Run", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Heaven's Gate was an American UFO religious millenarian group, based in San Diego, California, founded in 1974 and led by who, also known as \"Bo\" and \"Do\", among other names, was an American cult leader who founded what became known as the Heaven's Gate religious group, and organized their mass suicide in 1997, claiming the lives of thirty-nine people?", "answer": "Marshall Herff Applewhite, Jr.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What man is credited with helping Dan Emmett write the song which has become a toponym for the Southern United States?", "answer": "Thomas Snowden", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The drum software synthesizer \"Superior Drummer\" is compatible with what modern electronic musical instrument that consists of an electronic or digital sound module and can be struck by sticks or by the hands?", "answer": "electronic drum", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were both Time and Teen designed to be read by teenage girls ages 10 to 15?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are both Spacemen 3 and Said the Whale English bands?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The show Pole Chudes is hosted by a well-known television and internet personality is named based on what story?", "answer": "The Golden Key", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which director is of Danish descent, Mikael Salomon or Lewis Seiler?", "answer": "Mikael Salomon", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In what year was the man whose Argentine government was overthrown in the 1930 Argentine coup d'\u00e9tat born?", "answer": "1852", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "White Farm Equipment is owned by which Duluth, Georgia-based company?", "answer": "AGCO", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Buckinghamia and Smyrnium are both what type of plant catagory?", "answer": "genus", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Liberation is a 2009 docudrama t