at? ", "answer": "Cash collection", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which 2010 Disney fantasy film starred Nicole Ehinger from \"Louie\"?", "answer": "The Sorcerer's Apprentice", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Corey Gibson, known professionally as Corey Chorus, is an American songwriter, record producer, vocal producer, sound engineer and publisher, known for having written songs such as which song recorded by Barbadian recording artist Rihanna, from her fifth studio album, \"Loud\" (2010)?", "answer": "Cheers (Drink to That)", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Andaman Islands are home to which peoples, including the sentinelese?", "answer": "Andamanese peoples", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Phu Quoc Ridgeback and Mudi both dogs?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "We Could Be Kings was used in the sports film directed by whom?", "answer": "Craig Gillespie", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the original name of one of the teams Erik Cole played for?", "answer": "Minnesota North Stars", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What sort of role did American actor, known for his role in the film Step Up, play in the movie 22 Jump Street?", "answer": "American action comedy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "William Hughes Miller was born in a city with how many inhabitants ?", "answer": "7,402 at the 2010 census", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which state was man who's second album was released in 2000 by Uniphone Records born in?", "answer": "North Carolina", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Colin O'Meara voiced a character in which French-Canadian animated television series?", "answer": "The Adventures of Tintin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What campaign was launched by \"Bomber\" Harris?", "answer": "Battle of Berlin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Martin McDonagh and Steve James both examples of British playwrights?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "who is better known for horror genres  Gary 