n?", "answer": "Xu Chao Ping", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American spy film did Claude Rains star in?", "answer": "Notorious", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What medal did the new namesake of the campus of the Patchogue-Medford High School receive", "answer": "the Medal of Honor", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Die Macher and S\u00e1hkku are what type of entertainment?", "answer": "board game", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Robert Ellis Orrall wrote singles for Reba McEntire, Taylor Swift, and an American actress and singer who made her motion picture debut in Disney's 1998 remake of what?", "answer": "The Parent Trap", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What sport do both Horia Tec\u0103u and Je\u013cena Ostapenko play?", "answer": "tennis", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Fiorello Giraud created a roll in an opera that had how many acts?", "answer": "two acts", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Between Morina and Malva, which genus is spread more widely?", "answer": "Malva", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Herbert John Hodgson published the literature by this British archaeologist, military officer, diplomat, and writer renowned for his involvement in the Arab Revolt against the Ottoman Empire and whose wartime activities were depicted in which film?", "answer": "Lawrence of Arabia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Evolvulus and Acalypha, have which mutual characteristics?", "answer": "flowering plant", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Winnisquam is an unincorporated community in the Lakes Region of New Hampshire, the village is centered on the U.S. Route 3 bridge over the narrows of Winnisquam Lake and covers portions of three towns, including Belmont, a town in Belknap County, New Hampshire in which country?", "answer": "United States", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The eastern terminus of Grand Junction Road is in the suburb of Hope Valley, at the intersection of Hancock Road and Lower North East Road, just before the latter proceeds into the Adelaide Hills, past a park managed by a what volunteer group? ", "answer": "The Friends of Anstey Hill", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the author of Lord of Scoundrels born?", "answer": "1949", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How old was director Jeff Tremaine when Jackass Presents: Bad Grandpa debuted?", "answer": "(born September 4, 1966", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In 2017 Jo Platt replaced Andy Burnham as Labour MP for Leigh after he left to take which office?", "answer": "Mayor of Greater Manchester", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the Irish guitarist who was a member of the band Spooky Tooth and was also involved with the recording of the song \"Give Ireland Back to the Irish\"?", "answer": "Henry McCullough", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which observatory/satellite was launched into space first, Hakucho or Chandra X-ray Observatory?", "answer": "Hakucho", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the 5th studio album released by the singer of \"A Girl's Gotta Do (What a Girl's Gotta Do)\"?", "answer": "\"I'm Still Here\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who coaches the University team for which Morenike Atunrase played", "answer": "Gary Blair", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many clubs were featured in  a preseason soccer tournament held at Walt Disney World's 220 acre athletic complex located in the Walt Disney World Resort?", "answer": "four Major League Soccer clubs", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The father of the current general manager of the San Francisco 49ers is CEo of what company?", "answer": "Broadcast Company of the Americas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Isabel Paterson, was a Canadian-American journalist, novelist, political philosopher, and a leading literary and cultural critic of her day, along with who she was an American journalist, travel writer, novelist, political theorist, and daughter of which American writer?", "answer": "Laura Ingalls Wilder", "type": "bridge"