. 1946) covered Tim Hardin's \"Reason to Believe\"?", "answer": "The Carpenters", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was a Catholic missionary to the group of people who called themselves Neshnab\u00e9?", "answer": "Benjamin Marie Petit", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American actress starred in the 1981 Australian television mini-series?", "answer": "Olivia Brown", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Hopscotch starred which American actor who was born on July 6?", "answer": "Ned Beatty", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which person has had more occupations, Scott Brick or Stephen J. Cannell?", "answer": "Stephen Joseph Cannell", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "On which tv station does the show The Walking Dead appear including its episode \"Something They Need\"?", "answer": "AMC", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Augustus Phillimore created a modern dockyward at which British Overseas Territory?", "answer": "Gibraltar", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The band who made the single \"Hard Charger\" were formed in what California city?", "answer": "Los Angeles", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which was released first, The London Connection or Secrets of Life?", "answer": "Secrets of Life", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "This retired boxer from Thailand is the brother of kickboxer who who lit the torch during the opening ceremoney of the Asain Games in Bangkok in what year?", "answer": "1998", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Pierre Bouvier and Marie Fredriksson are both what?", "answer": "singer-songwriter", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What city south of Cimetta has a population of about 16,000?", "answer": "Locarno", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the British singer, songwriter and record producer born who was involved in both album LP1 and Process?", "answer": "16 November 1988", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Aaron Rhyne is best known for his designs in the Broadway productions of play that is based on a film of the same na