ephone, and founding the American Telephone and Telegraph Company (AT&T), in 1885?", "answer": "Alexander Graham Bell", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of the town which constituted part of the Megunticook Lake was in Waldo County, Maine, United States?", "answer": "Lincolnville", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Zou is one of the twelve departments of an African country formerly known as what?", "answer": "Dahomey", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Clancy Barone worked with which Chargers player as an offensive coach?", "answer": "Antonio Ethan Gates Jr.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Excursions, Op. 20, is the first published solo piano piece by a composer born in what year?", "answer": "1910", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "While Michel Foucault  was a French philosopher, what was Kenneth Grahame?", "answer": "Scottish writer", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who was born first, Rosey or Roman Reigns?", "answer": "Rosey", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What film staring Christian Slater did Christian Wagne collaborate on?", "answer": "True Romance", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Wendie Jo Sperber was an American actress, known for her performances in what film?", "answer": "I Wanna Hold Your Hand", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What tennis player, Simone Bolelli or  Andr\u00e9s Gimeno Tolaguera, is a Grand Slam champion since he won the 2015 Australian Open doubles event with Fabio Fognini?", "answer": "Simone Bolelli", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "what is the name of an American metalcore band from Orange County, California?", "answer": "Of Mice & Men", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who has won more ATP titles, Julien Benneteau or Ryan Harrison?", "answer": "Ryan Harrison", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In what year was the comedian who co-wrote the 2015 drama film \"Entertainment\" with Rick Alverson and Gregg Turkington born?", "answer": "1976", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Australian Electoral Division in So