ied the MCEM-2's combine wrap-around bolt and magazine in pistol grip considered to be?", "answer": "machine pistols", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who published a supplemental sourcebook to the core rules of the second edition of the \"Advanced Dungeons & Dragons\" designed by an American game designer at a company where he was employed for over fifteen years?", "answer": "TSR, Inc.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which actors star in the the movie that inspired Karle Pyaar Karle?", "answer": "Marion Cotillard and Guillaume Canet", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the name of the German team that featured Robert Garrett and the 7ft power forward from the Dallas Mavericks?", "answer": "DJK W\u00fcrzburg", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which country is the professional football club Located With which levi risamasu play until he got transfered to AGOVV apeldoorn?", "answer": "Netherlands", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Araujia and Azorina, are a type of genus of foliage?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What National Library of France holds the Annales ianuenses?", "answer": "Biblioth\u00e8que nationale de France", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the religious organization led by an American musician, writer, and convicted child molester born in 1945?", "answer": "Nuwaubian Nation", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What county is Princeton Stadium located in?", "answer": "Mercer County", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Was the Battle of Belleau Wood fought on the same continent as the Korean War?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which airport is owned by a higher-ranked authority? Saipan International Airport or St. Cloud Regional Airport\uff1f", "answer": "Saipan International Airport", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In the 2015 Pan American Games, Canada is third behind who?", "answer": "United States and Cuba.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are McGill University and American 