dge"}, {"question": "The MKT Nature and Fitness Trail runs nine miles in the right of way of what former Class 1 railroad company that was established in 1865, and had its last headquarters in Dallas?", "answer": "The Missouri\u2013Kansas\u2013Texas Railroad", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Repentance Tower was built in 1565, and served as a watchtower for what tower house that is located by the River Annan?", "answer": "Hoddom Castle", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Red Swoosh was founded by an American businessman born when?", "answer": "August 6, 1976", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which long-serving Australian politician and Attorney-General stepped down from his seat at Berowra in 2016, after endorsing Julian Leeser as his successor?", "answer": "Philip Ruddock", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were the films Escape to Witch Mountain and The Barefoot Executive both produced by Walt Disney Productions?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In what year was the school that is located at St. Agnes Cathedral founded?", "answer": "1917", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ed Grier was previously president of the hotel located at the resort in what California city?", "answer": "Anaheim", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are The Devils of Loudun and Ormindo both opera houses?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who joined their band first, Paul Roberts with The Stranglers or Joey Cape with Lagwagon?", "answer": "Active since 1989, Cape is best known as the frontman of the California punk rock band Lagwagon", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Jonas Bloquet played the role of Vincent in a film based on a novel from what year?", "answer": "2012", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the birthdate of this Argentine author, who wrote a novel that was adapted into a broadway musical in 1993 with music by John Kander and Fred Ebb?", "answer": "December 28, 1932", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where did the celebrity who presented the prizes at the 1971 World Championship Tennis Finals earn his bachelor's degree ?", "answer": "Purdue University", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Shanghai Noon was the directorial debut of a man born in what year?", "answer": "1965", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 2001\u201302 FA Cup was lost Chelsea Football Club, a professional football club based in Fulham, London, England, against what team?", "answer": "Arsenal", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the county in which the Kamm's Corners neighborhood is located?", "answer": "Cuyahoga County", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "James Jones and John Gunther, are of which nationality?", "answer": "American", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Besides Iggy Pop, which other singer who was known for her partnership with Serge Gainsbourg, contributed to the \"We are the Lillies\" project?", "answer": "Jane Mallory Birkin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The nursery rhyme that inspired The Queen Was in the Parlour is listed as what number in the Roud Folk Song Index?", "answer": "13191", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What football club relocated to the stadium at Marshgate Lane in the Lower Lea Valley in 2016?", "answer": "West Ham United Football Club", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the seventh episode of South Park before Ass Burgers?", "answer": "You're Getting Old", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who did Carolina Panther play against that led to the nickname No Fly Zone?", "answer": "Denver Broncos", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What game did the writer of \"Blackmoor\" help co-develop?", "answer": "Dungeons & Dragons", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The inaugural Hall of Game Awards show was hosted by a skateboarder with what nickname?", "answer": "\"The Birdman\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In who's debut Werner Daehn appeared momentarily?", "answer": "Florian Henckel von Donnersmarck", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the 2013 South Korean spy action thriller film which Ha Jung-woo showcased his versatility on", "answer": "Ryoo Seung-wan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 1960 American Eastmancolor Western film Seven Ways from Sundown starred what actor who was also a decorated American combat soldier in World War II?", "answer": "Audie Murphy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Mehmet Celal Bey was an Ottoman statesman and a key witness to the Armenian Genocide, today, he is often called the Turkish who, he was a German industrialist, spy, and member of the Nazi Party, who is credited with saving the lives of 1,200 Jews during the Holocaust?", "answer": "Oskar Schindler", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which band, OneRepublic or Alien Ant Farm, made their first album with producer Greg Wells during the summer and fall of 2005 at his studio, Rocket Carousel, in Culver City, California?", "answer": "OneRepublic", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What member of Miami Sound Machine was married to producer Emilio Esefan?", "answer": "Gloria Estefan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which film did Elizabeth Pe\u00f1a co-star in alongside Tim Robbins and Danny Aiello?", "answer": "Jacob's Ladder", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which project will create more buildings, One Manhattan Square or 80 Flatbush?", "answer": "80 Flatbush", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Harald Edelstam earned the nickname that was in reference to the novel by whom?", "answer": "Baroness Orczy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Henry Chinaski appeared in the comedy drama film directed by whom?", "answer": "Barbet Schroeder", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What country do Nemesis and Nemesis Inferno have in common?", "answer": "England", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the nickname of the football team in which Ridha Rouatbi played for in the 1960 Summer Olympics?", "answer": "Les Aigles de Carthage", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the population of the city where The Ch\u00e2teau du Grand-Blottereau is located ?", "answer": "nearly 300,000", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which commissioner on the Mississippi Public Service Commission was born in 1976?", "answer": "Brandon Presley", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What English actor starred in Where DAnger Lives?", "answer": "Claude Rains", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A Mexican recording artist, dancer, songwriter, and actor, best known for portraying who in an Argentine telenovela filmed in Buenos Aires, Argentina and developed by Disney Channel", "answer": "Le\u00f3n Vargas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the gross income of the movie produced in 1997 by Brent Armitage, starring John Cusack  and Minnie Driver?", "answer": "$28,084,357", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ravenscroft lies on a plateau that goes through which US states ?", "answer": "much of eastern Kentucky and Tennessee, and portions of northern Alabama and northwest Georgia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Pok\u00e9mon and  Pok\u00e9mon Tetris are a series of video games developed by whom?", "answer": "Game Freak and Creatures Inc.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The painting Also sprach Zarathustra was inspired by a novel by a philosopher that held the Chair of Classical Philology at what university in 1869?", "answer": "University of Basel", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Nikolajs \u0160telbaums was forced to move to Siberia because of which mass deportation that took place in March 1949?", "answer": "Operation Priboi", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Phyllis Dalton did work on a 1993 British romantic film based on whose work?", "answer": "William Shakespeare's", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Hun shrew, is a species of mammal in the family Soricidae, and is found in the Democratic Republic of the Congo, also known as Zaire, or simply the Congo, is a country located in the Central location of which country?", "answer": "Africa", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Download Festival is a British rock festival, held annually at Donington Park in Leicestershire, England, since 2003, it's the  most popular British summer rock and heavy metal festival and has hosted some of the genres' biggest names, including which rock band formed in England in 1978 by David Coverdale, after his departure from his previous band Deep Purple?  ", "answer": "Whitesnake", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Zack Snyder directed film was Jay Olicia, director of \"Batman: The Dark Night Returns,\" a storyboard artist for?", "answer": "Man of Steel", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which opened first The Mills at Jersey Gardens or Woodbury Common Premium Outlets?", "answer": "Woodbury Common Premium Outlets", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Buddy Bell is the father of which St. Louis Cardinals bench coach?", "answer": "David Michael Bell", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " What novel was published in seven parts between 1913 and 1927 and was adapted into a musical that ran Off-Broadway in 2003?", "answer": "In Search of Lost Time", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Li Na and Matt Lucena both American tennis players?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which actress starred in \"Perfect High\" and currents stars in the television series \"Famous in Love\"?", "answer": "Bella Thorne", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What airport is the company headquartered that Michael Bimha is a previous chairman of?", "answer": "Harare International Airport", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who played Donna Hayward and directed How I Got Into College?", "answer": "Lara Flynn Boyle", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Portico of the Aetolians and Delphi refer to what culture?", "answer": "Greek", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A Spanish model that has been the face of Jimmy Choo, and an Italian luxury fashion house that was founded in 1983, is known for what facial feature?", "answer": "her eyes", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "For which famous artist did the Luke Ebbin produce the first single for his 11 million selling album?", "answer": "Bon Jovi", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what country are Gaizhou and Zhengzhou located?", "answer": "China", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are Barkley Regional Airport and T. F. Green Airport in the same state?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What nationally is the artist behind Planet Blue?", "answer": "Danish", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "PECOTA was developed by a statistician who is a Special Correspondent of who?", "answer": "ABC News", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Petters Group Worldwide had assents in an airline headquartered in what Minnesota town?", "answer": "Eagan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which city of Pennsylvania can you find Veterans Stadium with a seating capacity of 56,371 for baseball and where the 1996 Major League Baseball All-Star Game, a midsummer classic was played? ", "answer": "Philadelphia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Spinto is a term that describes a voice that is near what type of voice that can sing over an orchestra?", "answer": "dramatic soprano", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 1962 children's novel Mine for Keeps was written by which  Canadian children's author as a different plot twist after Frances Hodgson Burnett's The Secret Garden?", "answer": "Jean Little", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who helped more to define literary journalism, Buckminster Fuller or Gay Talese?", "answer": "Gay Talese", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the real name of the author of \"Treatise on Tolerance\"?", "answer": "Fran\u00e7ois-Marie Arouet", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What magazine was started at an earlier date, Naval History or The Open Road for Boys?", "answer": "The Open Road for Boys", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Name the upcoming insect movie produced by an American motion picture studio based at Walt Disney Studios in Burbank, California and in which Divian Ladwa an English actor known 