ad is a 2015 action film, which Australian film actress and model, featured who?", "answer": "Courtney Eaton", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the actor who founded the Praja Rajyam Party who made their debut in the 1978 film Punadhirallu?", "answer": "Chiranjeevi", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Massachusetts Institute of Technology and Southern Methodist University, are which type of specific universities?", "answer": "private research", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "When was the rapper who made '97 Bonnie & Clyde\" born?", "answer": "October 17, 1972", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Both Jars of Clay and Imagine Dragons are considered what?", "answer": "rock band", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What player who played football for the University of Southern California was featured on the Madden NFL 10 cover?", "answer": "Troy Polamalu", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What subsidiary group owns the television network that televised the 73rd Academy Awards?", "answer": "Disney\u2013ABC Television Group", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "John Brown, was an American abolitionist who believed and advocated that armed insurrection was the only way to overthrow the institution of slavery in which location, during the Kansas campaign, Brown commanded forces at which battle that took place on June 2, 1856, when anti-slavery forces, led by the noted abolitionist John Brown, attacked the encampment of Henry C. Pate near Baldwin City, Kansas?", "answer": "United States", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many albums has the band, for which Sombre Romantic was a studio album, released ?", "answer": "4", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Shchedryk was arranged by a composer and teacher who was born and raised in the Podolia Governorate of the Russian Empire, and educated where as a priest?", "answer": "Kamianets-Podilskyi Theological Seminary", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the founder of the company that markets Jack Daniel's, and Finlandia Vodka?", "answer": "George Garvin Brown", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What television series was the former host of Canada's Next Top Model best known for performing in?", "answer": "\"Battlestar Galactica\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Curse of the Jade Scorpion is a 2001 crime comedy film featuring an American actress who starred in what for seven years?", "answer": "Mad About You", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many instructional faculty members were employed in fall 2015 by the college for which Mel Taube served as head football coach from 1960 to 1969?", "answer": "245", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which drink is considered a highball, a Rickey or a Greyhound?", "answer": "Rickey", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Adina Howard sung a song written by which American singer-songwriter nominated for the Academy Award for Best Supporting Actor in 2004?", "answer": "Jamie Foxx", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jacqueline Gareau was awarded the victory at the 1980 Boston Marathon when which Cuban-American runner was disqualified?", "answer": "Rosie Ruiz", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Abacoa is a community in what county directly north of Broward County?", "answer": "Palm Beach County", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which man,David Hayman or Reginald Barker, has played Hamlet?", "answer": "Hayman", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Russian Roulette is the which number studio album by German heavy metal band Accept, released in 1986, it would be the last Accept album to feature Udo Dirkschneider as lead vocalist, Dirkschneider is a German heavy metal singer? ", "answer": "seventh", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the director of a film where  David Kelly had a role as Michael O'Sullivan?", "answer": "Kirk Jones", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Until its closure Ashton Moss Railway Station served a town that had a population of what at the 2011 census?", "answer": "45,198", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "With which college basketball team had the 2017 76ers newly drafter point guard previously played for one season?", "answer": "Washington Huskies", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Colin Wilson produced the film John Carter, a 2012 American science fiction action film, directed by whom? ", "answer": "Andrew Stanton", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are the dog breeds Mudi and Barbet from the same country?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who is this English professional footballer for Manchester United and the England national team, who won  the Premier League, FA Cup, UEFA Champions League, League Cup, UEFA Europa League and FIFA Club World Cup?", "answer": "Michael Carrick", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What team did the man who most recently tied Tilleman's Olympic three-point record play for?", "answer": "Oklahoma City Thunder", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born first, Victor Amaya or Robin White?", "answer": "Victor Amaya", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What type of movie does The Living Desert and The Saved have in common?", "answer": "documentary", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Whose novels are set in the deep South, Mameve Medwed or Carson McCullers?", "answer": "Carson McCullers", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the name of the underground rap group that former American drug dealer who partnered with Rich Porter and Alpo Martinez founded?", "answer": "MobStyle", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Virginia Coigney is the mother of what singer who was part of a group with Peter Yarrow?", "answer": "Mary Allin Travers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Both Javier Mora and Alexander Povetkin are professional what?", "answer": "boxer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was an American dancer, singer, and actor who hosted the anthology series \"Alcoa Premiere\"?", "answer": "Fred Astaire", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "G\u00fcttingen is in a canton in which part of Switzerland?", "answer": "northeast", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How far is the city that the Texas Legends are in from Dallas/ Fort Worth International Airport?", "answer": "approximately 25 mi", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is a large mountain massif in Antarctica that is 21 km long and 13 km wide and lies within the Sentinel Range of the Ellsworth Mountains, named after  a United States Representative from Georgia ?", "answer": "Vinson Massif", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Hiten tejwani starred in kasautii zindagii kay, which was produced by which company?", "answer": "Balaji Telefilms", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are the movies The Rookie and Toy Story made by Disney?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which of the following is known for directing \"Die Another Day\": Lee Tamahori or Terry Zwigoff?", "answer": "Lee Tamahori", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Thor: God of Thunder is an action hack and slash video game, released in which year, it marks Thor's first standalone appearance in a video game and features the voices of Chris Hemsworth, and Tom Hiddleston, an English actor, producer and musical performer?", "answer": "2011", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which nationality do Dell Henderson and Peter Segal share?", "answer": "American", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which is still operational, the Meadowbank Gold Mine or the Salmita Mine?", "answer": "The Meadowbank Gold Mine", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which Danish heavy metal band from Copenhagen released a compilation album of rare demo tracks?", "answer": "Mercyful Fate", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Mondkopf born Paul R\u00e9gimbeau, in Toulouse, France, in what year, is an electronic music composer, Toulouse is the capital of the French department of Haute-Garonne and of the region of Occitanie?", "answer": "1986", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which came out first ESPN The Magazine or Nickelodeon Magazine ?", "answer": "Nickelodeon Magazine", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "McLemore Avenue is a 1970 album by Booker T. & the M.G.s, consisting entirely of mostly instrumental covers of songs from the Beatles' album Abbey Road, and also is a thoroughfare in the borough of what, and the City of Westminster in London?", "answer": "Camden", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who coached the team other than Michigan in a football game known as \"The Game\" in the 2001 season?", "answer": "Jim Tressel", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is a professional skateboarder, Belinda Carlisle or Duane Peters?", "answer": "Duane Peters", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "There are many styles of street fashion in Japan, created from a mix of both local and foreign labels, the rise and fall of many of these trends has been chronicled by Shoichi Aoki since 1997 in which fashion magazine, a monthly Japanese street fashion magazine founded in 1997, by photographer Shoichi Aoki?", "answer": "Fruits", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Heroes starred which American actress and director who starred in \"Gidget\"?", "answer": "Sally Margaret Field", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the occupation of both Albert de Courville and John Francis Dillon?", "answer": "director", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What band was brian may the lead guitarist of?", "answer": "Queen", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Social Studies studio Album by Loudon Wainwright III, has a satirical song about the comments made by a Republican Senator from which state ?", "answer": "North Carolina", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "At which age did one of the greatest batsmen of all time, nicknamed Master Blaster, take up cricket?", "answer": "eleven", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What school did the author of \"2016: Obama's America\" hold the role of president of from 2010 to 2012?", "answer": "The King's College", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jani H\u00f6lli is a musician who has played keyboard for the band named after a feral dog native to what continent?", "answer": "Australia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which band chose an image from the 1963 horror film directed by Mario Bava for the cover art on their album Luck of the Corpse?", "answer": "Deceased", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Joshua Lucas Easy Dent Maurer (born June 20, 1971), better known as Josh Lucas, is an American actor, he has appeared in many films, including which 2001 American biographical drama film based on the life of John Nash, a Nobel Laureate in Economics?", "answer": "A Beautiful Mind", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Swordbearer was republished in 1985 by which company, that completely relies on outside talent for their designs?", "answer": "Fantasy Games Unlimited", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When Lorraine Dunn finished third in the 200 metres and finished fourth in the 80 metres hurdles what country was she in?", "answer": "Brazil", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Does Ben Okri write non-fiction, similar to Maxine Hong Kingston?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What year what the lead singer of 3 Doors Down born?", "answer": "1978", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Cactus Range is a small mountain range 23 miles east of an unincorporated community with a population of what at the 2010 census?", "answer": "268", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which singer was born first Phil Mogg or Lynn Strait?", "answer": "Phillip John Mogg", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Stanegate, or \"stone road\" (Old Norse), was an important Roman road built in what is now northern England, it linked two forts that guarded important river crossings; Corstopitum (Corbridge) in the east, situated on Dere Street, and Luguvalium (Carlisle) in the west, Luguvalium was a Roman town in which northern location, in antiquity?", "answer": "Britain", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Steve Neil was a business executive at what American packaged food company that specializes in marketing nuts?", "answer": "Diamond Foods", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which rock band released the album \"Megalithic Symphony\", Awolnation or World Party?", "answer": "Awolnation", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Between YINSH and Mikado, which game is older?", "answer": "Mikado", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In which language was this film directed by Kewal Misra starring this Indian film actress who appeared in \"Sawan Bhadon\" remade?", "answer": "Telugu", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "when was the  Irish dancer and actress which Leila Mackinlay novel was  based on born ", "answer": "17 February 1821", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the father of Queen Elizabeth II born? ", "answer": "14 December 1895", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What movie won the most number of Annie Awards the same year that the musical dark fantasy film about Jack Skellington in \"Christmas Town\" won two Annie Awards? ", "answer": "The Lion King", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the third member of the trio that  \"The Professor\" a part of on the Atlanta Braves with John Smoltz?", "answer": "Tom Glavine", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of the 32 Federal Entities of Mexico is Aar\u00f3n Ir\u00edzar L\u00f3pez, a Mexican politician with the PRI, representing?", "answer": "Sinaloa", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is the lab that is connected to artists by the Human Digital Orchestra located?", "answer": "Murray Hill, New Jersey", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What form of play does Merle M. Rasmussen and Top Secret have in common?", "answer": "role-playing game", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which show about a forth grader who lives with his grandparents in an inner-city boarding house did Christopher Castile voice a character?", "answer": "Hey Arnold!", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "CineForm Inc was aquired by an American technology company founded by who?", "answer": "Nick Woodman", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born first, Ryo K