ersity adjacent to Fort New Salem, and founded by Seventh Day Adventists, founded?", "answer": "1888", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Fleance (or Fl\u00e9ance), is a figure in legendary Scottish history, he was depicted by 16th-century historians as the son of Lord Banquo, the Thane of Lochaber, is a character in William Shakespeare's play \"Macbeth\", from what year?", "answer": "1606", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Erin Sander plays the character Quinn Pensky on a tv series that was initially filmed at what college?", "answer": "Pepperdine University", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the Canadian actor and comedian died who was a star in both \"Planes, Trains and Automobiles\" and Delirious?", "answer": "March 4, 1994", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Big Twin Sauce is a condiment featured by the Hardee's and which restaurant chain, Hardee's Food Systems Inc., is an American-based fast-food restaurant chain, operated by CKE Restaurants Holdings, Inc. (\"CKE\") ?", "answer": "Carl's Jr.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Supergirl, an American superhero action-adventure televison series, written by Cindy Lichtman and Rachel Shukert aired on what TV station?", "answer": "CBS", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the French professor that the Robert brothers built the world's first hydrogen balloon for?", "answer": "Jacques Alexandre C\u00e9sar Charles", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Underground was a sketch comedy series produced by a man from what family of entertainers?", "answer": "Wayans family", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "who helped form United Helicopters twenty-two years before his death?", "answer": "Henry John Kaiser", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Marcia Louise Fudge is the U.S. Representatieve for which city in Cuyahoga County?", "answer": "Cleveland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Gulfstream International Airlines later became a regional carrier based out of what airport?", "answer": "Fort Lauderdale-Hollywood Inte