mes that were replaced by the 1928 Winter Olympics which Sven-Olof Lundgren participated in?", "answer": "Nordic Games", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Theresa Randle appeared in a 1996 film that contained what cartoon characters?", "answer": "the \"Looney Tunes\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What nickname is given to the smaller of the home venues of the basketball team for which Robert Stone plays ?", "answer": "The Cage", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which editor in chief of Marvel comics created the fictional deity Hera?", "answer": "Stan Lee", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both Anti-Semitism in the 21st Century: The Resurgence and Spencer Halpin's Moral Kombat documentary films?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": " Alligator wrestler Tahar Douis performed at which Las Vegas hotel, that was later demolished to make way for the Global Business District? ", "answer": "Riviera", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Kaslo and Slocan Railway was a narrow gauge railway between Kaslo, Slocan, and the mining community of Sandon in the Kootenay region of British Columbia, it was operated originally by the Great Northern Railway, was an American Class I railroad, ruunning from Saint Paul, Minnesota, to Seattle, in which state?", "answer": "Washington", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Satte Pe Satta is adapted from the 1954 movie Seven Brides for Seven Brothers, which starred an American singer, dancer, and actress, who was a contract player for who?", "answer": "Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer pictures", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Bella Hadid is signed to a company that has offices in which cities ?", "answer": "New York City, Los Angeles, London, Milan, Paris, and Sydney", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Phelps-A-Thon was a pro-LGBT group that counteracted the message of Fred Phelps, an American Baptist minister. He believed the deaths of homosexuals was the result of God's hatred of America's what?", "answer": "bankrupt values", "t