, "answer": "Pinellas County", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the American writer which James Burr work was compared with born", "answer": "December 16, 1928", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " John Mathieson, BSC is one of a group of film makers who emerged from the music video industry whose peers include the director of  a 2007 British romantic war drama that chronicles a crime and its consequences over the course of how many decades? ", "answer": "six", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What state is HInds County in where one of the oldest houses was built in 1839?", "answer": "Mississippi", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "James Edward Franco, is an American actor, director, screenwriter, and producer, he voiced characters in the animated film Sausage Party, an American adult computer-animated comedy film, released in which year, directed by Greg Tiernan and Conrad Vernon?", "answer": "2016", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Although Martin Stellman wrote Quadrophenia, who performed it?", "answer": "The Who", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is one of the oldest beverages humans have produced with recipes found in Sumerian writings?", "answer": "Beer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Was the event on disc two of The Best Of: 1994-1999 album by Bush, the first or second one after the original one in 1969?", "answer": "second", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What hall of fame was the founder of FAME Studios inducted into?", "answer": "Alabama Music Hall of Fame", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Hospital Food is a song by what English singer-songwriter who released his first studio album in 1993?", "answer": "David Gray", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The book in which the film \"All Quiet on the Western Front\" is based was written by an author who was born in what year?", "answer": "1898", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which British actress known for her appearance in \"Angels\" appeared in a 1976 British musical gangster comedy film directed by Alan Parker?", "answer": "Kathryn Apanowicz", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What major city was included in the congressional district that Brandon Patty ran for in 2016?", "answer": "Daytona Beach", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were Hollywood directors Mike Figgis and Mick Jackson both originally from England?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Iain Armitage's father was born in what year?", "answer": "1977", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who sponsored the 2011 Big 12 Men's Basketball Tournament and is headquartered in Westchase, Houston, Texas?", "answer": "Phillips 66", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "are  Gay Talese and Russell Edson known for working on the same magizines?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What Palmeiras left wing back/midfielder footballer formerly played for Bayer Leverkusen?", "answer": "Z\u00e9 Roberto", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Derek Pearcy designed a role playing game based on another game created by Croc in what language?", "answer": "French", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Age of Youth, is a South Korean television series stars include Ryu Hwa-young, a South Korean singer and actress, and is a former member of which South Korean girl group?", "answer": "T-ara", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 2022 FIFA World Cup will be held in Qatar, what is the next quadrennial international men's football championship called that will take place in 2026?", "answer": "23rd FIFA World Cup", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Lunic's album Future Sex Drama is similar to which English indie pop band formed in 2005?", "answer": "The xx", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the other person who escaped  from Clinton Correctional Facility with the murdrerer who lived from (June 25, 1966 \u2013 June 26, 2015) ? ", "answer": "David Sweat,", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Motherland\" and \"The Life of Birds\" are both examples are which type of film?", "answer": "documentary film", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which writer, Dan Simmons or Madeleine L'Engle, is known for young adult fiction, including \"A Wrinkle in Time\"?", "answer": "Madeleine L'Engle", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What album won the Best British Single award at 2017 BRIT Awards and featured a song remixed by Machine Gun Kelly?", "answer": "Glory Days", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The superbowl that Nate Hobgood-Chittick's team won was played on what date?", "answer": "January 30, 2000", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "An English dub version for \"Animals United\" stars an ensemble cast, including what australian actor and singer born 1 June 1968", "answer": "Jason Donovan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who had more members, Stabbing Westward of State Radio?", "answer": "State Radio", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In what year did a mid-sized auditorium, owned and operated by Caesars Entertainment Corporation first host Justin Timberlake's annual concert to benefit the Shriners Hospitals for Children?", "answer": "2007", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What American senior operations officer for the Central Intelligence Agency (CIA) ran the Eclipse Group?", "answer": "Duane \"Dewy\" Clarridge", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the island named after a medium-sized marine mammal in the order Sirenia?", "answer": "Sea Cow Island", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What novel written by an Irish novelist, playwright and satirist,  who wrote under the pseudonym Flann O'Brien, was published by MacGibbon & Kee in 1967?", "answer": "The Third Policeman", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the maker of the game series featuring the six time FIFA's \"Best Referee of the Year\" on the cover in its fourth installment?", "answer": "Konami", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the 2008 film where Lance E. Nichols played Larry Williams?", "answer": "David Fincher", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Sidney Irving Smit