urrent Vice President of which country?", "answer": "United States", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What language other than English is heard in a Beatles song that was released as the A-side of their eleventh album?", "answer": "French", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American writer and philosopher was a nominated finalist for the Pulitzer Prize for Fiction in 1992 for a semi-autobiographical novel?", "answer": "Robert M. Pirsig", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What university has its home in Gaetano Callani's native city?", "answer": "the University of Parma", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Northwest Passage is a 26-episode half-hour adventure television series, about an American colonial frontiersman, who served in the British army during what?", "answer": "both the French and Indian War and the American Revolution", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What car was launched at the 2012 Paris Auto Show following the model unveiled at the 2008 Paris Auto Show?", "answer": "Volkswagen Golf Mk7", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "K-1 Grand Prix '93 was a martial arts event held by the K-1 organization on April 30, 1993 at the Yoyogi National Gymnasium in Tokyo, Japan, thetournament winner was Branko Cikati\u0107 who defeated Ernesto Hoost in the final, Hoost is a Dutch kickboxer, he announced his retirement on December 2, 2006 after the K-1 World GP Final tournament in Tokyo Dome, in which country?", "answer": "Japan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What company broadcasts an Indian Hindi stand-up comedy and talk show that revolves around a man  first appeared in the Forbes India Celebrity list in 2012, ranked 69th?", "answer": "Sony TV", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "English actor Ben Batt appeared in \"Scott & Bailey\" as DC Kevin Lumb, the show features what fictional police team?", "answer": "Manchester Metropolitan Police", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Sky Witch\" is the twenty-ninth episode of the fifth season of which American animated television series created by Pendleton Ward for Cartoon Network?", "answer": "Adventure Time", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the singer who recorded \"A Texas State of Mind\" with Shelly West born?", "answer": "1941", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Covenant, the Sword, and the Arm of the Lord, founded by James Ellison, was active in what country?", "answer": "that was active in the United States", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "On which island is found the main hub of the airline formerly known as Air Pacific?", "answer": "Viti Levu", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Visioo-writer supports document formats such as KWord, and this, an open-source word processor written in C++?", "answer": "AbiWord", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the nationality of the composer of the opera The Twelve Charis?", "answer": "Russian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who wrote the screen play depicting the man that could have been the sixth person to land of the moon?", "answer": "William Broyles, Jr. and Al Reinert", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "During what was did William W. Morris serve in charge of the place that would go on to become a designated National Park in 1925, and a \"National Monument and Historic Shrine\" in 1939?", "answer": "American Civil War", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What actress and singer and three time Tony nominee has collaborated with Paul Schwarts and sang on Pl\u00e1cido Domingo's recording, \"The Broadway I Love\"?", "answer": "Rebecca Luker", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Schmalturm turret was a tank turret designed for use on the Panzer V Ausf, the Panther was a German medium tank deployed during which time period, on the Eastern and Western Fronts in Europe from mid-1943 to its end in 1945?", "answer": "World War II", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "From which US state is the sonic experimental heavy metal band featuring bassist Ryan Martinie?", "answer": "Illinois", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "