embers than Skunk Anansie?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "John Fletcher Hanson helped establish what Atlanta university?", "answer": "Georgia Institute of Technology", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of the following, The Love for Three Oranges or G\u00f6tterd\u00e4mmerung, is the last in Richard Wagner's cycle of four music dramas titled \"Der Ring des Nibelungen \"?", "answer": "G\u00f6tterd\u00e4mmerung", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Saint Croix Island, long known to locals as Dochet Island, is a small uninhabited island in Maine near the mouth of the Saint Croix River that forms part of the Canada\u2013United States border separating Maine from New Brunswick, the island was the site of an early attempt at French colonization by Pierre Dugua, Sieur de Mons in which year, Pierre Dugua de Mons, was a French merchant, explorer and colonizer?", "answer": "1604", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who created the fictional character named after the Hindi and Urdu word for \"elephant\" in the book where the principal character is the boy or \"man-cub\" Mowgli?", "answer": "Rudyard Kipling", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who developed an action role-playing video game that revolves around Aloy, a hunter and archer living in a world overrun by robots, that had the voice actor best known for portraying Cedric Daniels in \"The Wire\" and Phillip Broyles in \"Fringe\"?", "answer": "Guerrilla Games", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What college did Eric Kumerow's nephew, Joey Bosa, play for?", "answer": "Ohio State", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Writer Bill Coffin made contributions to several of Palldium's game series, including the book Heroes Unlimited, written by who?", "answer": "Kevin Siembieda", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Infinix Hot 4 was a smartphone developed by which Hong Kong-based manufacturer?", "answer": "Infinix Mobile", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the cup series' name of the tournament who foll