"The Uncluded was a folk rap group formed by which half of The Moldy Peaches?", "answer": "Kimya Dawson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What movie did Han Jae-suk star alongside an award-winning Hong Kong actress who is considered a \"Sing girl\"?", "answer": "\"Speed Angels\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Seven Stars is formerly an independent family regional brewery that was founded in Chiswick, West London in what year?", "answer": "1845", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Lady Caroline Faber was the daughter of which Conservative British Prime Minister?", "answer": "Maurice Harold Macmillan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many members are in the boy group Lee Jin-ki is a member of?", "answer": "five", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The musician resposible for the the song \"Please Please Let Me Get What I Want\" also holds a career an English what?", "answer": "actress", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Changsha and Xianyang, are in which country?", "answer": "China", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Geoffrey Oryema was smuggled across the Ugandan border in the trunk of a car during the reign of a political leader who was president of Uganda between which years ?", "answer": "from 1971 to 1979", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the nationality of the actor who plays a Thracian gladiator who, from 73 to 71 BC, led a major slave uprising against the Roman Republic?", "answer": "Australian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Award Theatre was a recurring television showcase of major first-run motion pictures sponsored by a brand of american beer produced by a company that went public in what year?", "answer": "1968", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What role did the star of Gideon's Crossing win an Emmy for?", "answer": "Detective Frank Pembleton", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the airline created that has its headquarters in the Torre Bouchard skyscraper ?", "answer": "1949", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What song was presented by Mirjam Weichselbraun at the biggest charity event in Europe supporting people with HIV? ", "answer": "Dancing Stars", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is older, Yannis Philippakis or Joel Pott?", "answer": "Joel Laslett Pott", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "How many rounds did it take the winner of a driving event in a  is a line of compact executive cars produced since late 1994 by the German car manufacturer ?", "answer": "ten", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What sitcom did Alexandra Erinn Hayes star in that premiered in 2016?", "answer": "Kevin Can Wait", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Masatoshi Ono and Charlie Huhn from the same country?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Lorraine Pilkington, is an Irish actress from Dublin, and appeared onstage in the play, The Iceman Cometh, written by American playwright Eugene O'Neill in which year?", "answer": "1939", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ruth Wilson has a film credit that includes which 2015 World War II drama film?", "answer": "Suite Fran\u00e7aise", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Steve Zahn starred in which movie based on a satirical realistic fiction comedy novel for children and teenagers written and illustrated by Jeff Kinney ?", "answer": "Diary of a Wimpy Kid", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the ace of the Imperial Japanese Navy Air died who served during World War II and who was squadron mate of Toshio \u014cta?", "answer": "October 26, 1944", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the singer who performed \"Ginger Bread\" born?", "answer": "1940", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "WHICH MULTINATIONAL BANKING CORPORATION SPONSORS CROSS COUNTRY RUNNING COMPETITION IN LEXEMBOURG?", "answer": "The ING Group", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Beverly Hills Brats is a 1989 American comedy film, the film starred which Canadian-born American actress, dancer and singer most famous for her on-screen coupling with Dick Powell in a string of successful early musicals at Warner Brothers?", "answer": "Ethel Ruby Keeler", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Martha Mayer Erlebacher, was born in Jersey City, New Jersey, she attended Gettysburg College, from which time span of years?", "answer": "1955-1956", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Railway Express Agency is like the United Parcel Service becuase they both deliver what?", "answer": "parcels", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the middle name of the director of the television drama film Too Big to Fail ?", "answer": "Lee", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The nominations for the 16th Vancouver Film Critics Circle Awards were four moninations went to an American coming-of-age drama film written and directed by who?", "answer": "Barry Jenkins", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Yulia Makhalina's fellow member of 'the basketball team' studied at what academy? ", "answer": "Vaganova Academy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The monarch that Thomas Parry worked for as Comptroller of the Household became queen in what year?", "answer": "1558", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which is the taller mountain, Dhaulagiri I, or Sia Kangri?", "answer": "Dhaulagiri I", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which plant is a genus of plants native to Mexico, Neomarica or Trachelium?", "answer": "Neomarica", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Harold von Braunhut was the creator and marketer of a group of crustaceans that undergo what process?", "answer": "cryptobiosis", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which city is Rait Castle, home of Andrew de Rait, situated?", "answer": "Nairn", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "California Tortilla was voted as having the best burritos in both 2009 and 2010 by a magazine founded in what year?", "answer": "1965", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Yes? No? is the debut extended play by a singer who was born in which year ?", "answer": "1994", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Do both Technological Institute of the Philippines and the Manipal Institute of Technology focus studies on engineering", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What did Rymill Park and Victoria Park, Adelaide have in common? ", "answer": "South Australian capital of Adelaide", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were both Slint and Boy Hits Car bands formed in the 1980s?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which is a band from Texas, Gnarls Barkley or Residual Kid?", "answer": "Residual Kid", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What doctor survived the massacre that took place March 27, 1836, during the Texas Revolution?", "answer": "Jack Shackelford", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who vacated the seat for which a Republican nominee ran who was suspended from his court position in 2016?", "answer": "Jeff Sessions", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Adam Wilcox is cousins with which 112th overall pick in the 2005 NHL Entry Draft?", "answer": "Alexander Dezmund \"Alex\" Stalock", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Jacobo Morales and Dorothy Arzner both directors?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What kind of group does God & Guns and Lynyrd Skynyrd have in common?", "answer": "rock band", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "At what non-profit government hospital in Las Vegas, Nevada was a 48-year-old deputy U.S. Marshal named Richard Gardner hospitalized at ?", "answer": "University Medical Center of Southern Nevada", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which court case was carried out earlier, Dolan v. City of Tigard or Loving v. Virginia?", "answer": "Loving v. Virginia", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Heinrich Holk was a mercenary in the service of the military leader of what heritage?", "answer": "Bohemian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the English nobleman and favourite of Elizabeth I, who was played by Hugh Dancy in the 2005 historical drama television miniseries?", "answer": "Robert Devereux", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were Giovanni Battista Pergolesi and Jules Massenet in the same industry?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Around which famous playwright does this theory, written by American Congregational and Unitarian minister, revolve?", "answer": "William Shakespeare", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What romantic comedy movie released in 2009, starred both Jamie Elizabeth Pressly and Paul Rudd? ", "answer": "\"I Love You, Man\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Andrew Form produced which 2013 dystopian horror film?", "answer": "The Purge", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who recognized the first woman to fly what is now Boeing AV-8B Harrier II in combat's transition from the military to civilian workforce as an example for others to follow?", "answer": "Michelle Obama", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What the Dead Know is a crime thriller by an author born in what year?", "answer": "1959", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The second largest regional airline operator in Eastern Canada provides regularly scheduled passenger service at an airport located near Labrador, Canada operated by who?", "answer": "Churchill Falls Labrador Corporation Limited", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Mark of the Gorilla is 1950 film starring a man that won how many Olympic gol medals?", "answer": "five", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Kanye West's song \"Hell of a Life\" was inspired by his relationship with a model born in what year?", "answer": "1983", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A Taste for Killing marked the debut role for an American actress and producer  named Hasty Pudding's Woman of the Year in what year?", "answer": "2009", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Don\" Carlos, Duke of Madrid was the senior member of the House of Bourbon, a European royal house of French origin, a branch of what?", "answer": "Capetian dynasty", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who died earlier: Terence Fisher or Jerome Storm?", "answer": "Jerome Storm", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What band after disbanding in 1990, the group reformed in August 2014 to play a benefit show in North Carolina, Walt Mink or Let's Active?", "answer": "Let's Active", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the name of a 2006 animation produced by the company that distributed a 2017 animated film written by Jim Krieg?", "answer": "Justice League Unlimited", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who Done It? was one of how many short-subject films starring The Three Stooges?", "answer": "190", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the character played by Peter Sellers in the movie that inspired Mastermind?", "answer": "Inspector Jacques Clouseau", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How is Damon Stoudamire related to Terrence Jones?", "answer": "cousin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which rock band formed in Orem, Utah, in 2001 with a vocalist, a guitarist, a bassist, and a bassist, released their ourth studio album through Reprise?", "answer": "The Used", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is the team based on for which  Paul Stephen Ranheim played in the National Hockey League (NHL) and team is also the third major-professional ice hockey team to represent the city of Calgary?", "answer": "Calgary, Alberta, Canada", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which politically conservative website has a monthly news magazine compansion?", "answer": "WorldNetDaily", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who took the oath of allegiance and was considered to be the Old Pretender?", "answer": "Prince of Wales", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which author wrote the story on which the movie in which Ko Chang-seok played the movie director was based?", "answer": "Kim Ki-duk", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "That's what I like is a song by Bruno Mars from an album tha twas released on November 18, 2018 by who?", "answer": "Atlantic Records", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Maggie was a series that starred the actress who had a minor role in what