e 1970s and '80s?", "answer": "Chitra Singh", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "James Toback and Thornton Freeland, have which mutual occupation?", "answer": "film director", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Brian Carey Goodwin (25 March 1931 \u2013 15 July 2009) was a Canadian mathematician and biologist, a Professor Emeritus at the Open University, a public distance learning and research university, and one of the biggest universities in the UK for undergraduate education, as a founder of which two subjects?", "answer": "theoretical biology and biomathematics", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Does Werther or War and Peace have more acts?", "answer": "War and Peace", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "A former host of The Next List is an assistant professor of neurosurgery at what school of medicine?", "answer": "Emory University School of Medicine", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When does the 2nd  attraction based at Hong Kong Disneyland opened?", "answer": "11 January 2017", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which famous musician also became an actor, Eddie Vedder or Peter Noone?", "answer": "Peter Blair Denis Bernard Noone", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are The Haunted World of El Superbeasto and The Super Snail Adventure both children's films?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the name of the actress who played both the jaded aristocrat in \"The Roman Spring of Mrs. Stone\" and the murderous Colonel Rosa Kleb in \"From Russian with Love\".", "answer": "Lotte Lenya", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The suburb that contains the Dry Creek railway station contains area formerly devoted to salt crystallisation pans that is managed by what company?", "answer": "Ridley Corporation", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Daughters of Divine love was founded during a time when war was fought between what two factions?", "answer": "government of Nigeria and the secessionist state of Biafra", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is another name for the location where BESS is located?", "answer": "\"Home of the Submarine Force\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American actor starred in both \"The North Star\" and \"The Best Years of Our Lives?\"", "answer": "Carver Dana Andrews", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many times longer than an Association football pitch is the stadium in Prague at which the Spartakiads took place?", "answer": "three", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which church is Catholic based, Vasat Atik Ali Pasha Mosque or Cathedral of the Holy Spirit?", "answer": "Cathedral of the Holy Spirit", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Sam Boyd's family operates what hotel located in Paradise, Nevada?", "answer": "The Orleans", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Andy Williams signature song was originally performed by who?", "answer": "Audrey Hepburn", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "James Newton Howard, is an American composer, conductor, music producer and musician, his film scores include  Blood Diamond, released in which year, a German-American political war thriller film co-produced and directed by Edward Zwick?", "answer": "2006", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Galvatrons rock band admit they were influenced by which American singer known for \"Hit Me with Your Best Shot\"?", "answer": "Pat Benatar", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What metro are both the Magenta line and Palam metro line part of? ", "answer": "Delhi Metro", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What category of Shakespearean plays included subjects like the King of England (from 1483-1485)?", "answer": "histories", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Lion King musical is produced by a company also known by what name?", "answer": "Disney on Broadway", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The serial drama Bikhra Mera Naseeb, written by Saima Youmkus, made it's debut on what Pakastani television channel, which is owned by Geo Television Network?", "answer": "Geo Entertainment", "type": "bridge