st woman in the world?", "answer": "Alice Louise Walton", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Shipping News and Versus both American bands who play in their own genre of rock?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "A Place in England is a novel by Melvyn Bragg, first published in which year?", "answer": "1970", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of the Three Tenors crossed over into popular music?", "answer": "Luciano Pavarotti", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Shuanghe and Yushu City, Qinghai both county-level cities?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the name of this 2012 American war film directed by Dan Bradley and starring Isabel Lucas?", "answer": "Red Dawn", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The show that aired in the United Kingdom on the Hallmark Channel, ABC1 (April 2006) and, more recently, 5 USA (May 2009) and Five (August 2009) was created by the same man who directed this 2009 starring Michelle Pfeiffer, Ashton Kutcher and Kathy Bates?", "answer": "Personal Effects", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "About which famous battle did the author of the book Sea Lord write a nonfiction book ? ", "answer": "the battle of Waterloo", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the American singer, songer, and actress born in 1981 who's grandfather was a jazz drummer and mother won Hong Kong's first Amateur Talent Quest?", "answer": "Teresa Victoria \"T.V.\" Carpio", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who wrote the off-kilter cover for which  The Raincoats album is best known? ", "answer": "Ray Davies", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the director of a 1987 film in which an American ballet dancer named the artistic director of The Washington Ballet performed?", "answer": "Herbert Ross", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which writer was older, Grace Paley or Judy Blume?", "answer": "Grace Paley", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Psychohistory is a fictional science in which Isaac Asimov science fiction book series which combines history, sociology and mathematical statistics to make predictions about the future behaviour of very large groups of people and most notably described in his trilogy series which won him the Hugo award and which reference other works by the author including 'Robot' and 'Empire'?", "answer": "The \"Foundation\" series", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Spinster and Her Enemies: Feminism and Sexuality 1880-1930 is a 1985 book about feminist involvement in the Social Purity movement by which lesbian feminist, an  English expatriate in Australia, is best known as a lesbian feminist scholar and political activist, for her analysis of the history and politics of human sexuality in the UK, and for her controversial views on transsexuals?", "answer": "Sheila Jeffreys", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Daniele Emilio Massaro, is an Italian former footballer, who played as a forward, he is mainly remembered for his highly successful career with which sports organization, during the late 1980s and 1990s, under Arrigo Sacchi, an Italian former football coach?", "answer": "A.C. Milan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born first, Arvid E. Gillstrom or Herbert Achternbusch?", "answer": "Arvid E. Gillstrom", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Alonzo Mourning was traded to the Toronto Raptors but ultimately played for what team?", "answer": "Miami Heat", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the Spanish name for the political alliance that supports social equality and egalitarianism?", "answer": "Islamo-izquierdismo", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were the bands \"+44\" and \"The Dead Milkmen\" formed in the same city?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the name of the cofounder of the Avis Budget Group subsidiary who also founded a peer-to-peer car sharing service that was later acquired by Drivy?", "answer": "Robin Chase", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "At which period the studio operated independently