ere Richard Nauyokas is currently living?", "answer": "Billingborough", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which fictional character was first developed in 1959 and was the main character in a 1983 film?", "answer": "Norman Bates", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which year did the revolution, which Joseph Roth depicted in his 1927 novel \"The Wandering Jews,\" begin?", "answer": "1917", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the hip hop group who did \"Cosby Sweater\" formed?", "answer": "1994", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which member of Donkey's Tail had the middle name of \"Sergeevna\"?", "answer": "Natalia Goncharova", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Andrew James Matfin Bell, is an English actor and dancer, he's known for his roles in which 2011 3D motion capture computer-animated mystery adventure comedy film based on \"The Adventures of Tintin\", the comics series by Belgian cartoonist Herg\u00e9?", "answer": "The Adventures of Tintin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Peter Edgerly Firchow was an American literary scholar and educator, he wrote extensively on the relationship between  German literature and which class of  literature in the English language from the United Kingdom, Isle of Man, and Channel Islands?", "answer": "British literature", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The lead singer of Faith No More also founded which band?", "answer": "Mr. Bungle", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is special about 1961 Summer Universiade and Sofia, Bulgaria", "answer": "international sporting event", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who composed the music for this musical that the 1992 American animated film Aladdin gave inspiration for?", "answer": "Alan Menken", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both Ralph Ceder and Norman Foster a film director?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which film, The Lion King and Midnight Madness, is an upcoming American computer-animated epic musical drama film, directed and co-produ