ormed in?", "answer": "San Diego, California", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Spice Girls Live at Wembley Stadium is the DVD of pop band Spice Girls' tour, \"Spiceworld Tour\", in which year, the show was recorded after Geri Halliwell left the band?", "answer": "1998", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Whistler is a 30-minute U.S. television anthology mystery series, based on the radio series of the same name, notable guest stars included which Irish actress, best known for playing Jane in the \"Tarzan\" series of films?", "answer": "Maureen Paula O'Sullivan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Chris Staley is a member of an association of how many independent schools in the United Kingdom?", "answer": "283", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The twelfth studio album from singer Tim McGraw features a guest appearance on guitar by which other famous musician? ", "answer": "Keith Urban", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the British Canterbury scene singer born who worked with David Lloyd Stewart  since 1981? ", "answer": "5 June 1950", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What country do both the Rachias timbo and Iguazu Falls have in common?", "answer": "Argentina", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the Japanese video game composer who formed The Black Mages born ", "answer": "March 21, 1959", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of the first African-American students admitted to the University of Georgia is an American journalist and former foreign correspondent for National Public Radio?", "answer": "Charlayne Hunter-Gault", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "John III of Egmont, was first Count of Egmont, Lord of Baer, Lathum, Hoogwoude, Aarstwoude, Purmerend, Purmerland and Ilpendam, and Stadtholder of Holland, Zeeland and West-Friesland, in the Low Countries, stadtholder, is an office of steward, designated a medieval official, and then a what?", "answer": "national leader", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Howard Webb was the referee in a game