y", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What colleges do the university that Nana Foulland once played for consist of?", "answer": "College of Arts and Sciences, College of Management, and the College of Engineering", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Franco-Siamese War was a conflict that included the system of government adopted in France in what year?", "answer": "1870", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The song \"Masterpiece\" is by this American singer and songwriter who is  widely cited as an influence by other artists and often referred to as what?", "answer": "Queen of Pop", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How tall is the ride that is nearly identical to the Goliath at Six Flags Over Texas?", "answer": "245 feet", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "An unarmed teen was shot in 2015 by a Wisconsin police officer that drew attention from what group that campaigns against violence and systemic racism towards black people?", "answer": "Black Lives Matter", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the star in the film \"The Bear\" died by an accidental self inflicted blank cartridge gunshot to the head?", "answer": "Jon-Erik Hexum", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Name the proposed state and kingdom conceived in the 19th century by a French lawyer and adventurer, whose modern day capital is Perquenco in southern Chile?", "answer": "Kingdom of Araucan\u00eda and Patagonia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "what does Joseph Frank Wehner and Frank Luke have in common?", "answer": "pilot", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the maiden name of the person Jo Platt became Parliamentary Private Secretary to?", "answer": "Bowen", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Sovetskaya Litva found itself free at the same time as the fall of Supreme Soviet of the Lithuanian SSR, what change allowed both of the actions to happen?", "answer": "The political power shifted from CPL to the Soviet", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who wrote the closing night film from the 2013 Deauville American Film Festival?", "answer": "Bong and Kelly Masterson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Yuma is an Amtrak station with passenger rail service provided thrice-weekly by a train that for most of its history has run between what two cities?", "answer": "New Orleans and Los Angeles", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A Cul\u0103 is a type of building originally made to be able to fortify the ruling class against invasions during which wars?", "answer": "Ottoman\u2013Habsburg wars", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Hertha BSC's 2007\u201308 season began on 4 August 2007, with their DFB-Pokal match against Unterhaching, and ended 17 May 2008, with their Bundesliga match against Fu\u00dfball-Club Bayern M\u00fcnchen e.V., commonly known as FC Bayern M\u00fcnchen, is a German sports club based in Munich, Bavaria (Bayern), in which country?", "answer": "Germany", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the location with a population of 331 where Cardigan Mountain State Park is located?", "answer": "Orange, New Hampshire", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where did the team Mike Gundy coaches play their home games in 2005?", "answer": "Boone Pickens Stadium", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"My Mother the Carjacker\" has a direct link from an episode first aired in the United States on what date?", "answer": "November 19, 1995", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which monarchy had this English peeress executed whose adult life is depicted in the 2014 historical novel The King's Curse?", "answer": "Henry VIII", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What nationality was the unit who fought in the war in the 1807 - 1814 war against Napoleon?", "answer": "Swiss", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Miss Universe 1963 included an outgoing titleholder of a beauty queen who won the title in what city?", "answer": "Miami Beach, Florida", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Peacock Throne was located in what historical fort in the city of Delhi in India that was the main residence