ounded?", "answer": "1819", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which is an American rock band, Jimmy Eat World or Morrissey?", "answer": "Jimmy Eat World", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What serial killer was prosecuted by Bobby Grace in 2007?", "answer": "Chester Turner", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Prior to the movie \"Sweet Virginia\", Jared Abrahamson was most noted for his performance in 2016 for what movie? ", "answer": "Hello Destroyer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year did the president under whom John Elliott Ward was United States Minister to China die?", "answer": "1868", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the wife of the head of the company founded by Gulshan Kumar which is also engaged in film production and distribution?", "answer": "Divya Dua", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which jazz-influenced orchestral piece did Walter Johannes Damrosch conduct the world premiere performances of?", "answer": "An American in Paris", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " The Onizuka Prop Wash Award was named in memory of irst Asian American and the first person of Japanese ancestry to what?", "answer": "reach space", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What system designed by N. Robin Crossby features at Fandemonium?", "answer": "H\u00e2rnMaster", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which series worked on by Aaron Springer ran from June 15, 2012 to February 15, 2016?", "answer": "Gravity Falls", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which film began production first, A Wrinkle in Time or The Fighting Prince of Donegal?", "answer": "The Fighting Prince of Donegal", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "XLink Kai is a method developed by Team-XLink for online play of certain System Link compatible video games, it enables players on various consoles, including The PlayStation 2 (PS2), a home video game console that was developed by which company?", "answer": "Sony Computer Entertainment", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What city was Steve Earle's Grammy-nominated album \"Train' a Comin'\" recorded in?", "answer": "Nashville", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What film did Tamara Tunie and Denzel Washington star in together in 2012?", "answer": "Flight", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is a rare survivor on the David and Catherine Driver Farm from American Civil War campaign led by American soldier, businessman, educator, and author William Tecumseh Sherman?", "answer": "1839 barn", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the nick name given to a fighter pilot with the German Air Force during World War I and whose distant relative is Bolko von Richthofen, a German archaeologist?", "answer": "Red Baron", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which 2003 Heisman winner experienced the Heisman curse of post-award failure as a professional football player?", "answer": "Jason White", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Katherine Elaine Hendrix, is an American actress, model, producer, singer, dancer, and activist, and is best known for her role in What the Bleep Do We Know!?, a film that combines documentary-style interviews, computer-animated graphics, and a narrative that posits a spiritual connection between quantum physics and consciousness, released in what year?", "answer": "2004", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Atomic Monster Productions is an American film production company scheduled to relase a movie on what date?", "answer": "July 13, 2018", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What type of group does Thujopsis and Stanhopea have in common?", "answer": "family", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What profession does Adrian Brunel and Richard Oswald have in common?", "answer": "director", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Renaldo James Woolridge placed for what team in the NVA Development League?", "answer": "Grand Rapids Drive", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the political party of the District of Columbia Mayor who approved the Golden Triangle business improvement district in 1997?", "answer":