ue?  ", "answer": "18", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Around what year was the political party of which Barbara Boggs Sigmund was a member founded?", "answer": "1828", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "At which World Cup, specifically in a match against Sweden, was the Cruyff turn first deployed on the international footballing stage, winning Johan Cruyff the Golden Ball award?", "answer": "1974", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Journal does the Shaw Foundation Professor of Media Technology of the Singaporean University that is ranked 11th in the World edit? ", "answer": "Journal of Computer Mediated Communication", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Normal Wilkinson invented a style of camouflage, consisting of what?", "answer": "it consisted of complex patterns of geometric shapes in contrasting colours, interrupting and intersecting each other", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who did Harland Braun represent in the case of the March 3, 1991 beating of Rodney King?", "answer": "one of the officers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What championship series consisted of Miami Heat and Oklahoma City Thunder and had Eddy Curry as a player for the Heat?", "answer": "2012 NBA Finals", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who are an indigenous Australian people whose traditional lands are primarily located in the Adelaide Hills, that warned the settlers that the area was prone to flooding, but this advice was ignored?", "answer": "The Peramangk", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American Major League Basball team did Joe Kennedy play for that plays at the Rogers Centre?", "answer": "The Toronto Blue Jays", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Trial, released in which year, is a film directed by Orson Welles, the film begins with Welles narrating Kafka's parable \"Before the Law\" to pinscreen scenes created by the artist Alexandre Alexeieff, was a Russian Empire-born artist, filmmaker and illustrator who lived and worked mainly in Paris?", "answer": "1962", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Irvin Kershner directed mystery-thriller film does Patty Oja appear in ? ", "answer": "Eyes of Laura Mars", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The language spoken in the industrial town and cargo port in Cheshire, England is also referred to as what? ", "answer": "Liverpool English or Merseyside English", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the  Dutch film director who directed \"Soldier of Orange\", born", "answer": "18 July 1938", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "what year was the county thats home to the Wolf Mountains founded?", "answer": "1913", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which airline was created in September 2005 with the merger of Sterling European and Maersk Air: Sterling Airlines or EasyJet?", "answer": "Sterling Airlines", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which lasted longer, the Battle of Chancellorsville or the Battle of the Wilderness ?", "answer": "Battle of Chancellorsville", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is a cave diving organisation which was formed in September 1973 that administers and supports cave diving activity in other parts of Australia including the Nullarbor Plain and  a town in inland New South Wales, Australia, located at the junction of the Macquarie and Bell Rivers?", "answer": "Cave Divers Association of Australia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What play was mentioned in the man who was portrayed by actor Geoffrey Rush's Diary?", "answer": "The Stepmother's Tragedy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Imperial Ballroom was a 1982 album released by the singer born whom?", "answer": "Declan Patrick MacManus", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are most Callisia and Adenophora native to the same hemisphere?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Austrofascism was led by which Austrian Patriotic Front statesman?", "answer": "Engelbert Dollfuss", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Heath bar is a candy bar made by a company that is one of the largest chocolate manufac