ience fiction action film did Gina L. Gershon known for ", "answer": "Face/Off", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which University did the gymnastics coach, who recruited a two time gold medal winner in the 1984 Summer Olympics, attend?", "answer": "University of Oklahoma", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "a photo messaging application used for impermanent (self-deleting) photos, developed by an american internet entrepreneur named the youngest billionaire in the world in what year?", "answer": "2015", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What American rapper has worked with drummer Travis Barker and fellow rapper Chamillionaire?", "answer": "Paul Wall", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Coast to Vines rail trail open to pedestrians and cyclists, runs for how many km through the southern suburbs of Adelaide from Marino to Willunga, a town south of Adelaide, South Australia in the City of Onkaparinga local government area 47 km from the Adelaide CBD?", "answer": "34", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What does O.A.R stand for?", "answer": "Of a Revolution", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Matt Harrigan created and hosts which American talk show on Adult Swim?", "answer": "FishCenter Live", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who published the game for which Steven Hall is the lead writer?", "answer": "Electronic Arts", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What christian liberal arts college hosts the WEHS-FM 89.9 radio station?", "answer": "Hope College", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ryan Murphy cowrote a movie based on which book of the same name that appeared on \"The New York Times\" Best Seller list for 187 weeks?", "answer": "Eat Pray Love", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "On what state's commemoration of the abolition of slavery in it did Khingz release an album on?", "answer": "Texas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Robert F. Hughes, an American television director, worked on what American animated television series from the creators of \"Phineas and Ferb\"?",