ata and Willard Huyck both originally from the United States?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "LaLee's Kin: The Legacy of Cotton and Loot, are of which shared genre?", "answer": "documentary", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who is the protagonist in Ayn Rand's most notable novel?", "answer": "Howard Roark", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The actress of the ex-wife of St. John in \"No Such Thing as Vampires\" has appeared in what other films?", "answer": "\"A Knight's Tale\" (2001), \"40 Days and 40 Nights\", \"The Rules of Attraction\" (both 2002), \"The Order\" (2003), \"Kiss Kiss Bang Bang\" (2005) and \"The Holiday\" (2006)", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "On 13 June 2008 a new coach was announced who is currently the coach of what club?", "answer": "Al Jazira", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The movie franchise in which Bruce Davidson plays antagonist Senator Robert Kelly is based on a superhero team appearing in what company's comic books?", "answer": "Marvel Comics", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which English actor stars in both Spanisb drama 'Morrowbone' and American tv show 'Stranger Things'?", "answer": "Charlie Heaton", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Anthony Carfano was a New York gangster who became a caporegime under which Italian-American Mafia gangster and crime boss born on January 26, 1891?", "answer": "Frank Costello", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which is located in New Hampshire, Tulsa International Airport and Portsmouth International Airport at Pease?", "answer": "Portsmouth International Airport at Pease", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "David Auburn wrote what screenplay that starred Keanu Reeves, Sandra Bullock and Christopher Plummer?", "answer": "The Lake House", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Between Nikos Nikolaidis and Claude Lanzmann, who filmmaker has had a more diverse career?", "answer": "Nikos Georgiou Nikolaidis", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Robert William McQuarters played college footbal at Oklahoma State. What Stadium do the Oklahoma State cowboys football team play their home games ?", "answer": "Boone Pickens Stadium", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What company is the owner of regional malls in the United States, headquartered in Bloomfield Hills, Michigan and developed Westfarms?", "answer": "Taubman Centers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What American actor born in 1987 stared in a film with Adam Scott, Brittany Snow, and J.K. Simmons?", "answer": "Alexander Richard \"Alex\" Frost", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Antonio Malfante was a trader from what capital of Liguria?", "answer": "Genoa", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Name the multi-use indoor arena on the Las Vegas Strip which occupies The Dunes golf course, part of The Dunes Hotel, the tenth resort to open on the strip?", "answer": "T-Mobile Arena", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the producer of \"The Crazy World of Julius Vrooder\" born? ", "answer": "April 9, 1926", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Between Woman's Journal and Look, which magazine has had more name changes?", "answer": "Woman's Journal", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In what kingdom that is bordered by Epirus to the west, Paeonia to the north, Thrace to the east and Thessaly to the south did the Trocmi tribe reside?", "answer": "Macedonia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Wincenty Gostkowski, was a lawyer and associate of Antoni Patek, and who?", "answer": "Adrien Philippe", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What profession does Muhammad Iqbal and Allen Ginsberg have in common?", "answer": "poet", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What sport are both Anthony Martial and CO Les Ulis known for?", "answer": "football", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What league did the former aggressive player and AFL Premiership 2006 commentator with Dennis Cometti and Christi Malthouse play in?", "answer": "Australian Football League", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Composer, Niels Finn H\u00f8ffding, and musician, Carl August Nielsen are from what country?", "answer": "Denmark", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Greg Eagles voiced an American television series by Maxwell Atoms that aired on what television network?", "answer": "Cartoon Network", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jamie Sharper is the brother of which broadcaster?", "answer": "Darren Mallory Sharper", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ekaterina Pushkash partnered with the dancer who now competes with what other ice dancer?", "answer": "Tiffany Zahorski", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which band is from a country closer to Canada, Talking Heads or Jesus Jones?", "answer": "Talking Heads", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Alfred Thomas \"Freddie\" Highmore starred in an American drama film involving an 11-year-old musical prodigy living in an orphanage who runs away to where?", "answer": "New York City", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which band has more bass players, Mobile or Ned's Atomic Dustbin? ", "answer": "Ned's Atomic Dustbin", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "WHICH WHITE WOLF IMPRINT CREATED THE GAME EVERQUEST RPG AND HAS ALSO ACTED AS PUBLISHER FIR GAME DEVELOPERS SUCH AS MONTE COOK'S COMPANY AND NECROMANCER GAMES?", "answer": "The Sword and Sorcery Studios", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "which actress portrayed Bonnie Winterbottom as well as starred in \"Gilmore girls\"", "answer": "Liza Rebecca Weil", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Kurtwood Larson Smith is known for playing Clarence Boddicker in which cyberpunk science fiction superhero action film?", "answer": "RoboCop", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What country was the magazine \"Encounter\" published in that John Gross was an editor for?", "answer": "the United Kingdom", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"New Arrangement\" the album by Jackie DeShannon contains which song written and composed by Donna Weiss and Jackie DeShannon?", "answer": "Bette Davis Eyes", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What 