dfield (born March 19, 1950)", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which film was released first Sky High or Operation Dumbo Drop?", "answer": "Operation Dumbo Drop", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which English professional footballer born in 1989 was coached by Youth Academy Director Jim Cassell?", "answer": "Daniel Sturridge", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Winter Garden Downtown Historic District is part of a city with what population as of the 2010 census?", "answer": "34,568", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year did William \"Gipsy\" Daniels knock out the future heavyweight champion of the world?", "answer": "1928", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Tony Hadley and Gregg Rolie in the same industry?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What American stock car racing driver has won the NextEra Energy Resources 250 and had the second most wins in the Nationwide Series (as of 2014)?", "answer": "Mark Martin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which drink is made traditionally with tequilla the Margarita or the Redheaded slut?", "answer": "A margarita", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Where is the group, which organised the Mexican referendums, 1989, based?", "answer": "Chiapas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " \u00c9anna Ryan was born in a county situated in which Irish province ?", "answer": "Connacht", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who founded the company that makes Labello?", "answer": "Paul Carl Beiersdorf", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is similar of Shatranj and 18XX? ", "answer": "game", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which director for American television series \"Prison Break\" also produced \"Horrible Bosses\"?", "answer": "Brett Ratner", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Bang Bang\" is a hip-hop song by Kardinal Offishall, the song, which contains a sample of \"Bang, Bang\", (My Baby Shot Me Down), by the American singer-actress Cher, her second single, from the album, \"The Sonny Side