nd the General fall under?", "answer": "documentary film", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who plays the title character of the British crime drama programme written by Neil Cross that is also credited to the English and Canadian filmmaker Stefan Schwartz?", "answer": "Idris Elba", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Eisenstadt v. Baird and Ware v. Hylton, are related to which government entity?", "answer": "United States Supreme Court", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What sport is Malcolm Wolfe and Geoff Marsh both former athletes of?", "answer": "cricket", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which party has dominated the last elections in the state that the municipality of Agua Fria is located?", "answer": "Workers' Party", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Oakland University and Arizona State University, have which mutual designation?", "answer": "public", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Chamizal dispute was caused by a shift in which one of the principal rivers in the southwest United States and northern Mexico?", "answer": "Rio Grande", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Farley Earle Granger was best know for collaborations with which director who's one of the film was based on based on the 1929 play by Patrick Hamilton?", "answer": "Alfred Hitchcock", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Arena for the River East Royal Knights was named after a hockey player who played what position?", "answer": "goaltender", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Alma Ros\u00e9 was named after which Viennese-born composer born Alma Margaretha Maria Schindler?", "answer": "Alma Mahler", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "UC Berkeley School of Law produced Edwin Meese, an American attorney and law professor, the schools is also one of how many schools and colleges at the University of California Berkeley?", "answer": "14", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many people did the subject of Murder in the Heartland murder?", "answer": "eleven", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "