onal character from Peter Jackson's film adaptation of a novel published in what year?", "answer": "1937", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "This American writer's writings were translated  by Rita Rait-Kovelea, a soviet literary translator and writer", "answer": "Kurt Vonnegut", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where are the headquarters of the bread company whose location at The District is being replaced by Bar Louie?", "answer": "Sunset Hills, Missouri", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who reigned after a report about mismanagement at the residence at which the Queen Elizabeth the Queen Mother resided from 1953 to 2002?", "answer": "Michael Fawcett", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are David Vincent and Cerys Matthews both American?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "SkyWorld is the fourth public album by a group based on what city?", "answer": "Los Angeles", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the lead developer for the game set within the Warhammer 40,000 universe born?", "answer": "May 22, 1975", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Immigrant farm workers during the Dirty Thirties used a route that connected what states?", "answer": "Calexico, California, on the US\u2013Mexico border to Blaine, Washington, on the U.S.-Canada border", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was Taneleer Tivan introduced as and Elder?", "answer": "August 1978", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was the 2009 film shot that starred an actress who also starred in \"Boogie Nights\" and was directed by Rockmond Dunbar?", "answer": "Atlanta, Georgia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What 143 line poem features the Wulfings?", "answer": "Widsith", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both Kuytun and Dongchuan District in China?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Writer Matt Selman's involvement in \"The Simpsons\" led viewers to understand how the show began in the episode titled \"Behind the Laughter,\" which is a play on words of what 