: "1999", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Wellow, Isle of Wight was named by a Germanic people and recently rejected a proposal to erect what?", "answer": "a wind farm", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which pizza chain is located in the San Francisco Bay Area, Dion's or Patxi's Chicago Pizza?", "answer": "Patxi's", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What two stars shared the screen with Andrew Keegan in the 2001 adaptation of William Shakespeare's \"Othello\"?", "answer": "Mekhi Phifer and Josh Hartnett", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which documentary was released first, The City or V-Day: Until the Violence Stops?", "answer": "The City", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What year did British based gambling company take over running the Killiney Novice Chase?", "answer": "Since 2016", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who owns the radio station licensed to the county seat of Lumpkin County, Georgia?", "answer": "Georgia Public Broadcasting", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Romanian basketball player was released from the Washington Wizards during the 1997-98 season?", "answer": "Gheorghe Mure\u0219an", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the retired American basketball player born in 1969, who had sold to him by Michael Heisley a 70% controlling stake in the Grizzlies?", "answer": "Christian Donald Laettner", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the 1976 British-American supernatural horror film for which Jerry Goldsmith composed the theme song \"Ave Satani?\"", "answer": "Richard Donner", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who has been a member of more bands, Ian Ball or Kevin DuBrow?", "answer": "Ian Thomas Ball", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In what ITV crime thriller did Samantha Kate \"Sammy\" Winward star in 2014?", "answer": "Prey is a television crime thriller first broadcast on ITV, 28 April 2014 at 9pm.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which manager that played Urby Emanuelson was born on 16 January 1956?", "answer": "Martin Jol", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which building in Manhattan is featured in the Doctor Who TV series/", "answer": "The Empire State Building", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who did the most work for Dutch Public TV, Willy Lindwer or Gil Kenan?", "answer": "Wolf (Willy) Lindwer", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "An election for the leadership of the Ulster Unionist Party (UUP) was held on 8 April 2017 at the party's Annual General Meeting, the 2017 contested election was triggered after incumbent Leader Mike Nesbitt, elected in 2012, announced following the 2017 assembly election his intention to step down as party leader, the 2017 election to the Northern Ireland Assembly was held on which date?", "answer": "2 March 2017", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Hut 8 was a section in the Government Code and Cypher School (GC&CS) at Bletchley Park (the British World War II codebreaking station) tasked with solving German naval (Kriegsmarine) Enigma messages, the section was led initially by who, which was an English computer scientist, mathematician, logician, cryptanalyst, philosopher and theoretical biologist?", "answer": "Alan Turing", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the club founded that Daniel Follonier currently plays as a winger for?", "answer": "1909", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Cruella de Vil was a character from the live action comedy film released in what year?", "answer": "1996", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is the Albanian singer who appeared with Genc Salihu on the fourth season of The Voice of Albania from?", "answer": "Tirana, Albania", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the American rapper, actor, and television host born who's debut studio album is To the Extreme?", "answer": "October 31, 1967", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who has been in more bands, Mike Muir or Ronald Isley?", "answer": "Michael Allen \"Mike\" Muir", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Revolting Cocks 