bes die?", "answer": "27 March 1625", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the organization whose founding members include the Serbian-American physicist that lends his name to the asteroid 57868 Pupin?", "answer": "National Advisory Committee for Aeronautics", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who created the main character in which the Raiders appear?", "answer": "Stan Lee", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which was exhibited first, Gunnin' for That No. 1 Spot or Ota Benga?", "answer": "Ota Benga", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What do the roots that the alternative name of a Haugtusse derive from mean?", "answer": "\"covered\" or \"secret\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the first mid-size pickup truck from Chrysler's Ram division introduced which is the basis of Dodge Durango?", "answer": "1986", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who stars as Arthur in the film that Rospo Pallenberg helped?", "answer": "Nigel Terry", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What type of Guinness World Record performance does the Cheung Kong Center take part in?", "answer": "the world's largest permanent light and sound show", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Megalithic Symphony and Back from Earth are EP's and albums by what rock band?", "answer": "Awolnation", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Democratic politician born in 1948 did Ron Kouchi choose as Vice President of the Hawaii Senate?", "answer": "Russell S. Kokubun", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Delphi Community High School is a located in which school district headquartered in Delphi, Indiana?", "answer": "Delphi Community School Corporation", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Rod Strickland is the godfather of an NBA player who won an NBA championship with the cavaliers in which year ?", "answer": "2016", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the person who was taught how to play the helicopter shot by Santosh Lal born?", "answer": "7 July 1981", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Qui\u00e9n co