cted by who, S. Thaman is an Indian film music composer, and composed the music for the film?", "answer": "Santosh Srinivas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What airport was a main base for Air Lithuania and is the third largest airport in Lithuania?", "answer": "Palanga International Airport", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who produced the film with which Andy Muschietti was best known for directing? ", "answer": "Zandy Federico", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which team drafted Ben Hansbrough's older brother in 2009?", "answer": "Indiana Pacers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The actor that played Jim Rockford in \"The Rockford Files\" also starred with Julie Andrews in a 1999 made-for-tv movie based on what play?", "answer": "\"A Winter Visitor\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Hawaiians thought an extinct breed of pariah dog, other than human consumption of the flesh and other edible parts derived from dogs, were what ?", "answer": "spiritual protector", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is the headquarters of the Conference that includes the Texas A&M Aggie baseball team?", "answer": "Birmingham, Alabama", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 2012 film \"Hard Boiled Sweets\" features which character actor best known for his role as an archaeologist in \"Raiders of the Lost Ark\"?", "answer": "Paul Freeman", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the political consultant who has promoted Roger Stone's tweets born?", "answer": "August 27, 1952", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " WWE Vintage is hosted by which person born September 19, 1985?", "answer": "Renee Young", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of the following writers is best known for his biography of Adolf Hitler: John Toland or David James Duncan? ", "answer": "John Willard Toland", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What state has a museum built between 1908 and 1912 that features a room used by Puebloans for religious rituals?", "answer": "Pennsylvania", "type": "bridg