comparison"}, {"question": " John Luke Porter began working for the Confederate States Navy at the oldest and largest industrial facility that belongs to who?", "answer": "the U.S. Navy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of the label with which Dzeko & Torres has had single  is a Canadian independent record label based in Vancouver, British Columbia?", "answer": "Monstercat", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What country was the Bourne and Sleaford Railway and Midland and Great Northern Joint Railway located?", "answer": "England", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Lieutenant Kij\u00e9, is a 1934 Soviet comedy film directed by Aleksandr Faintsimmer, based on the novella \"Lieutenant Kij\u00e9\" by which Soviet writer, literary critic, translator, scholar and screenwriter?", "answer": "Yury Tynyanov", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What platform was used to build both both the midsize Pontiac G6 and a compact executive car manufactured by a Swedish automaker?", "answer": "GM Epsilon platform", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "what does Karsk and Bee's Knees have in common?", "answer": "cocktail", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What United States President crossed paths with Monica Lewinsky and an American model born in 1950 who once posed for 'Penthouse' magazine?", "answer": "Bill Clinton", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Sadma, is an Indian drama movie, released in which year, directed by Balu Mahendra which stars Sridevi, an Indian film actress who has worked in Tamil, Telugu, Hindi, Malayalam and Kannada films?", "answer": "1983", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "On 27 November 2000 album label \"Visible Noise\" released The debut studio album \"The Fake Sound of Progress\", where was the band from ?", "answer": "Pontypridd, Wales", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Natalia Ginzburg and Lytton Strachey, have which occupation in common?", "answer": "writer", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The University System of New Hampshire oversees a coeducational university in Plymouth that has how many undergrad students?", "answer": "4,200", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What American actor know for his striking resemblance to silent film hero Rudolph Valentino played American Old WEst gunfighter Billy the Kid?", "answer": "Anthony John \"Tony\" Dexter", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Do the genuses Bolusanthus and Leucocoryne belong to the same family?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "are both breeds originating in Europe, C\u00e3o de Gado Transmontano and Finnish Spitz ?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What artist that co-founded a band with David Knopfler also played with the group Brewers Droop?", "answer": "Mark Freuder Knopfler", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Was the king of Spain in 1975 given the title \"Marquessate of Samaranch\"?", "answer": "The title was bestowed by King Juan Carlos I of Spain", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American experimental pop band was showcased in London for the Bandstand Busking project?", "answer": "Of Montreal", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What player did Buddy Stephens coach who went on to play for Florida State University, East Mississippi Community College and Auburn University?", "answer": "John Franklin III", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When did Augusta Stanley's husband serve as Dean of Wesminster?", "answer": "1864 to 1881", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What career did the writer of the comedy series The Ex-PM have before turning to comedy full-time ?", "answer": "solicitor", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which airline, that flew only with foreign models, is the largest airline of the Russian Federation?", "answer": "Aeroflot", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which tennis player reached a higher World singles ranking, Allan Stone or Kevin Curren?", "answer": "Kevin Melvyn Curren", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "When was the base where Patrol Squadron Eight was formerly based closed?",