ho was the legal grandson of the Earl of Merica?", "answer": "Gruffudd ap Llywelyn", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who has received more critical acclaim, Conrad Aiken or Paul Heyse?", "answer": "Paul Johann Ludwig von Heyse", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "This American electrical engineer took part with the co-founder of Fairchild Semiconductor in the realization of an object that gave what location its name?", "answer": "Silicon Valley", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What management award was given to former shortstop of the Detroit Tigers, Boston Red Sox, St. Louis Browns and Cincinnati Reds in 1967?", "answer": "Manager of the Year", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Louis MacNeice was part of the Auden Group that included the father of what actor?", "answer": "Daniel Day-Lewis", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Mitchell Report was created by which former Senate Majority Leader?", "answer": "George John Mitchell Jr.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "This 1990 American comedy-drama film that co-starred an American former child actor turned what?", "answer": "lawyer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who has a wider scope of profession, Paul W. S. Anderson or Amanda Lovejoy Street?", "answer": "Paul William Scott Anderson", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "he music of Athens, Georgia, includes a wide variety of popular music and was an important part of the early evolution of alternative rock and new wave, the The city is well known as the home of chart-topping bands like R.E.M., an American rock band that formed in Athens, Georgia, in 1980 by which lead singer?", "answer": "Michael Stipe", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year was the artist who sang \"Future Baby Mama\" inducted into the rock and Roll Hall of Fame?", "answer": "2004", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 2001 FedEx Orange Bowl was played by the team that was led by which 2nd-year coach from the Big 12?", "answer": "Bob Stoops", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What historic house and museum is located in the largest city in the U.S. state of Maine?", "answer": "The Wadsworth-Longfellow House", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of the actors starred in Firangi is also Miss India USA winner on 26 November 2013 while serving as Miss India New England?", "answer": "Monica Gill", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What River is flows through Western North Carolina and East Tennessee that is situated along the Davy Crockett Birthplace State Park?", "answer": "Nolichucky River", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What 1951 film based on a Jacques Offenback opera featured Ann Ayars as Antonia?", "answer": "The Tales of Hoffmann", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the Chief Justice who swore in Sonia Sotomayor born?", "answer": "1955", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Venetian Resort Hotel Casino is a five-diamond luxury hotel and casino resort located on the Las Vegas Strip in Paradise, an unincorporated town and census-designated place (CDP) in Clark County, Nevada, adjacent to the city of Las Vegas, in which country?", "answer": "United States", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the city in which Rana Pratap Nagar railway station is located founded?", "answer": "1553", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which opened first, the Ptarmigan and Tom Mine or the Colomac Mine?", "answer": "The Ptarmigan and Tom Mine", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Martyrs is a 2015 American horror film directed by Kevin and Michael Goetz, it is a remake of which  2008 French-Canadian drama horror film, written and directed by Pascal Laugier?", "answer": "Martyrs", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the actress that played the new Section chief born?", "answer": "1980", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Scottish rock band released the album Twinlights in 1995?", "answer": "Cocteau Twins", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which band is made up of brother, Canterbury or Evermore?", "answer": "Evermore", "type":