o Grande Games in English in 1998, GridIron Master or Elfenland ?", "answer": "Elfenland", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What partially ruined castle is near Dunbeg?", "answer": "Dunstaffnage Castle", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which american professional basketball team is based in the borough of New York City and once had Joshua Malik Childress as a player?", "answer": "Brooklyn Nets", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The \"Extraterrestrial Highway\" runs parallel to what military base?", "answer": "Nellis Air Force Range", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What extraterrestrial creature is featured in a film in which the \"Happy New Year\" actor also appears?", "answer": "alien", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both 1 New York Plaza and 45 Broad Street buildings located in Manhattan?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What star of Someone She Knows also played a character named Mason Wood?", "answer": "Gerald McRaney", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who leaded the 2012 UNLV Rebels football team from their first first winning season since 2000? ", "answer": "Bobby Hauck", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Canadian voice actor voiced Edd a.k.a. Double D from \"Ed, Edd n Eddy\" as well as voicing the same character that Akira Ishida did in \"Mobile Suit Gundam SEED\"?", "answer": "Samuel Vincent", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which company markets Melarsomine as Immiticide in order to treat a small thread-like worm that causes filariasis in dogs, mainly, but also cats, ferrets, bears, sea lions, and coyotes?", "answer": "Merial", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jawad Ahmad is a Pakistani pop singer and musician, and is known for his song \"Main Tenu Samjhawan Ki\" sung by Rahat Fateh Ali Khan?", "answer": "Rahat Fateh Ali Khan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who published the movie in which Cillian Murphy is best known for as Scarecrow?", "answer": "DC Comics", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Tolkien book did Arthur Gardner Rankin Jr. created an animation of?", "answer": "The Hobbit", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Francesco da Mosto, is an Italian architect, author, historian, film maker and television presenter, he explored the country in an Alfa Romeo Spider, which sees him traveling from his home in Venice to which Croatian city on the Adriatic Sea, in the region of Dalmatia, that was historically Ragusa?", "answer": "Dubrovnik", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Congolese Rally for Democracy, also known as the Rally for Congolese Democracy, is a political party and a former rebel group, that operated in the eastern region of the Democratic Republic of the Congo (DRC), and was a major armed faction in the Great War of Africa, or the Great African War, and sometimes referred to as the African World War, or even World War Three, usually it's called?", "answer": "Second Congo War", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the  69th La Liga season inwhich Deportivo La Coru\u00f1a also  won ", "answer": "The 1999\u20132000 La Liga season", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Battle of Vuelta de Obligado was part of a larger naval blockade that lasted how long?", "answer": "five-year-long", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which genus has more accepted species Browningia or Aristotelia?", "answer": "Aristotelia", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which comedy series aired it's second to last season opener with the title \"11 Years Later\"?", "answer": "Will & Grace", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the 2010 Census population of the home to the 15th largest steel producer in 2014?", "answer": "2,864", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who founded the One country, two systems used by the Government of Macau?", "answer": "Deng Xiaoping", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "George Webster Latimer, was a Utah lawyer most known for representing Lt. William Calley Jr. in his court martial from which titled incident?", "answer": "My Lai", "type": "bridge"}, {"ques