key Rooney work in?", "answer": "Film", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Did Darryl Stonum play in the 2012 Holiday Bowl?", "answer": "Baylor accepted a berth in the 2012 Holiday Bowl", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What console was developed by Nintendo that was released in the early 1990s and the Brainies was released on?", "answer": "Super Nintendo Entertainment System", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which mathematician was born first, Pyotr Novikov or Dmitri Egorov?", "answer": "Dmitri Fyodorovich Egorov", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Hobbycraft and it's competitor, High Street, are located where?", "answer": "United Kingdom", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which actress has won multiple awards and nominations for playing a cop out of the 16th precinct?", "answer": "Mariska Hargitay", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Shenzhou City\u00a0and Longchang are located in provinces in what country? ", "answer": "China", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Were both Gasland and When We Were Kings directed by Josh Fox?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who was a MAC Champion and 3-time Division 1 NCAA Qualifier and is an American mixed martial artist who competes in the featherweight division for Ultimate Fighting Championship?", "answer": "Desmond Green", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which actor portrays the German voice of the American actor who played the title character on \"Doogie Howser, M.D.?\"", "answer": "Philipp Moog", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "11oz. is an EP whose title is based on a lager made by which company in the US?", "answer": "Pabst Brewing Company", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Players Club starred which actor who was also known for his role on Good Times?", "answer": "John Allen Amos Jr.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which opera was written by Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart, Martha or Idomeneo?", "answer": "Idomeneo", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Interstate 480 is named for the first American to do what?", "answer": "orbit the Earth", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Quietly Confident Quartet consisted of the freestyler whose career ended after what event?", "answer": "1986 Commonwealth Games", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "With which western series is the star of The Last of the Vikings associated ? ", "answer": "The High Chaparral", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Michaeley O'Brien grew up in a town that had how many inhabitants in 2016 ?", "answer": "2,521", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What are the two largest cities in the congressional district represented by Minnesota congressman John Kline?", "answer": "Burnsville and Eagan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The actor who starred in films like \"Splash\" and \"Forrest Gump\" produced which film that also stars Colin Hanks?", "answer": "The Great Buck Howard", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Sir Brian William Vickers is known for his work on the history of which philosopher who passed away in 1626 ?", "answer": "Francis Bacon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What alcohol is present in both, Monkey Gland and Breakfast martini?", "answer": "The Monkey Gland is a cocktail of gin, orange juice, grenadine and absinthe created in the 1920s by Harry MacElhone, owner of Harry's New York Bar in Paris, France.", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The song \"Just in Time\" was introduced in a musical whose main character is based on what woman?", "answer": "Mary Printz", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which city sports locations for both the Specialty Restaurants Limited restaurant company and the Bombay Stock Exchange? ", "answer": "Mumbai", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What position did this athlete play who played for the Dallas Cowboys between 1998 and 2001 and suffered a shoulder injury before the 1999 San Diego Chargers season?", "answer": "quarterback", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the birthdate of this American baseball infielder, manager, and coach who played 