k about them written by Gabriel Sherman?", "answer": "Roger Ailes", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Chicago Majors was a basketball team based in Chicago, Illinois, the team was owned by who, who was the original owner and coach of the Savoy Big Five, later known as the Harlem Globetrotters?", "answer": "Abe Saperstein", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What town was the 1990s manager of ND \u010crnu\u010de born in?", "answer": "Ljubljana", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the former name of the athlete on the cover of NFL Street 3?", "answer": "Chad Ochocinco", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The actor that played Steve Rhoades in \"Married... with Children\" also co-starred with Jason Bateman in what NBC series that aired from 1984 -85?", "answer": "It's Your Move", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What category of publication can, the American food bimonthly Bon App\u00e9tit and the official periodical of the Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints, called Ensign, be described as?", "answer": "magazine", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Tom Petty and Soyou, share which mutual occupation?", "answer": "singer", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In 2011, what was the population of the city in which Phil Nilsen was born?", "answer": "134,122", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which case considered eminent domain, Kelo v. City of New London or Bivens v. Six Unknown Named Agents?", "answer": "Kelo v. City of New London", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which inner-city suburb is the birthplace of an alleged Australian contract killer missing since May 1985?", "answer": "Brunswick, Victoria", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Was Yakov Protazanov or Marcel Duchamp born in 1881", "answer": "Yakov Alexandrovich Protazanov (Russian: \u042f\u0301\u043a\u043e\u0432 \u0410\u043b\u0435\u043a\u0441\u0430\u0301\u043d\u0434\u0440\u043e\u0432\u0438\u0447 \u041f\u0440\u043e\u0442\u0430\u0437\u0430\u0301\u043d\u043e\u0432 ; January 23 (O.S. February 4),