ped heavy rainfall across the Lesser Antilles in October of which year?", "answer": "1990", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Data Stream Interface is a session layer used to carry this protocol formerly known as what?", "answer": "AppleTalk Filing Protocol", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Bernard Fresson played Scope in a 1976 psychological horror film that was directed by who?", "answer": "Roman Polanski", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Aroostook County town featured Maine State Route 229?", "answer": "Limestone", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Arturo Vega was sometimes called the fifth member of a band that formed where? ", "answer": "Forest Hills, Queens", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "HMS Boadicea participated in which British-US invasion of French North Africa?", "answer": "Operation Torch", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Actress Lucy Gordon had a small role in the 2001 film \"Serendipity\", directed by who?", "answer": "Peter Chelsom", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Hoopoe Starlings are found on an island located in what ocean?", "answer": "the Indian Ocean", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles featured characters in comic book form created by the comic book writer and artist of what nationality?", "answer": "American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Hayley-Marie Coppin has appeared in the UK magazine that launched in what year?", "answer": "2004", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Edward Elwes, was educated at Eton and University College, Oxford, and was ordained in what year, and was Curate of Ashington, Somerset and then Norton St Philip, after a further curacy at Dinder he became Vicar of Over Stowey, a vicar is a representative, deputy or substitute; anyone acting \"in the person of\" or agent for a superior (compare \"vicarious\" in the sense of \"at second hand\")?", "answer": "1873", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Impending Death is a photograph of 1 WTC  after being stuck by an airplane piloted by who?", "answer": "Mohamed Atta", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the population as of the 2010 census of the county in which Pilsen, Kansas is located?", "answer": "12,660", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Tyrone Brown was granted a conditional pardon by the Governor of what state?", "answer": "Texas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What area does WOAD and Ridgeland, Mississippi have in common?", "answer": "Jackson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "USS Oscar Austin was built by the Maine shipyard located on what river?", "answer": "Kennebec River", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In early 2010 PZL-\u015awidnik was acquired by a multinational company formed in what year?", "answer": "2000", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Fedor Fedorov is the younger brother of the retired ice hockey player who is GM of which Kontinental Hockey League team?", "answer": "CSKA Moscow", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Treaty that ended the American Revolutionary war made George Rogers Clark hailed as  the \"Conqueror of the Old Northwest\"?", "answer": "Treaty of Paris", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of these was sold by Commodore, Lambda 8300 or Amiga?", "answer": "Amiga", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "La Harpe is a city in a county that is how many acres in size?", "answer": "322,560", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the City Hall that is built above City Hall station built?", "answer": "1901", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who did the artist born in Houston on March 1, 1965 assist in writing a song for in 2015?", "answer": "Madonna", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is the company, which uses the Reactor physics engine, headquartered?", "answer": "San Rafael, California", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the real name of the convicted Soviet KGB spy in Bridge of Spies?", "answer": "Vilyam \"Willie\" Genrikhovich Fisher", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of Kate Bush's albums were a UK number one album and al