st beds, Psychiatric Institute of Washington or George Washington University Hospital?", "answer": "George Washington University Hospital", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "How long is the river that Fort Cass was located on?", "answer": "147 mi", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What 2014 mixtape is by an individual who wrote for an artist signed to Warner Bros.?", "answer": "\"Only the Poets\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which collection of science fiction short stories by Isaac Asimov was illustrated by an American conceptual designer and illustrator who won an Academy Award for the film \"Cocoon?\"", "answer": "Robot Dreams", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What prime-time host of 12 Olympic Games got his start at station WAER in New York?", "answer": "Bob Costas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both Idlewild and My Morning Jacket American rock bands?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What indoor shopping mall in downtown Rochester, New York was created by B. Forman Co.?", "answer": "Midtown Plaza", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are the films Summer Wars and My Dog Tulip both animated films?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "When was the winner of the ladies' title of The 1988 Prize of Moscow News banned for life by the U.S. Figure Skating Association?", "answer": "1994", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Steven R. Smith's music style, falls best into which nation's music diversity?", "answer": "The music of the United States reflects the country's multi-ethnic population through a diverse array of styles.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Robbie Coltrane is known for his role in the \"Harry Potter\" films in which he is eventually revealed to be a member of which order?", "answer": "the Order of the Phoenix", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Of what nationality is the man who had input into the album Matangi?", "answer": "Australian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Atemoztli, the sixteenth month 