 June 2017", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What industry were both William Styron and Anne Sextona part of?", "answer": "literary", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which tower is taller, the Paramount Plaza or Central Park Tower?", "answer": "Central Park Tower", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Justin Paul Theroux, is an American actor and screenwriter, he is best known for his work with film director David Lynch in Mulholland Drive, released in which year, a neo-noir mystery film written and directed by David Lynch and starring Naomi Watts?", "answer": "2001", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Mike Love and Adam Duritz both of the same nationality?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "When was the writer of a film about a young man who receives a strange creature called a mogwai as a pet born?", "answer": "September 10, 1958", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which musician helped popularize songs by American icons, Peter Hooton or George Thorogood?", "answer": "George Thorogood", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "When was the American actress, voice actress, and comedian born who was known as a cast member of \"Saturday Night Live\" and was a star in the Staten Island Summer film?", "answer": "February 8, 1984", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Takasaki, Gunma is famous as the hometown of a doll that symbolizes what?", "answer": "perseverance and good luck", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Mindaugas Sabutis was born in a city that had this population as of 2011?", "answer": "26,444", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the film based on Elmore Leonard's novel of the same name, featuring \"Pulp Fiction\" actor Ving Rhames?", "answer": "Steven Soderbergh", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who operate the luxury hotel in which the show \"O\" was staged? ", "answer": "MGM Resorts International", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of the bands Seaweed and Blonde Redhead came from Tacoma, Washington?", "answer": "Seaweed", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who composed a form of song in the Carnatic music repertoire in all the '72 Melakarta Ragas?", "answer": "Prashanth Iyengar", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who currently owns the video game development company that co-developed Xenosaga: Pied Piper, along side Namco Mobile and Tom Create?", "answer": "Nintendo", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born first Charles Giblyn or Sean Bridgers ?", "answer": "Charles Giblyn", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The actor who voices the Simpsons character who usually comes as a bystander to disastrous events was born in what year?", "answer": "1957", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Diamond Head starred which Italian-American actor?", "answer": "James William Ercolani", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Christmas Concerto is bya composer that died in what year?", "answer": "1713", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What director did Tom Cruise work for that died on September 20, 2016?", "answer": "Curtis Hanson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the nationality of the person \"For No Good Reason\" is about?", "answer": "Welsh", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the name of the evacuation operation that the RNLB Guide of Dunkirk was used in?", "answer": "Operation Dynamo", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the district created in which  Atwima-Mponua is located?", "answer": "November 12, 2003", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Mad Girl's Love Song\" is a poem written by Sylvia Plath in which year, and was written in the villanelle poetic form and is generally included in the biographical note appended to Plath's novel, \"The Bell Jar\", and was the only novel written by the American writer and poet Platt?", "answer": "1951", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Fregattenkapit\u00e4n Heinrich Lehmann-Willenbrock was a submarine commander in Germany during World War II and the subject of the mini-series called \"Das Boot\" when he was portrayed by which actor? ", "answer": "J\u00fcrgen Prochnow", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Daniel Christmas (born September 10, 1956) is a Canadian Mi\u2019kmaw from the Membertou First Nation in Nova Scotia, Christmas was named to the Senate of Canada by Prime Minister Justin Trudeau, to sit as an independent, a Canadian politician, and which ordinal number, Prime Minister of Canada and leader of the Liberal Party?", "answer": "23rd", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jan Wolkers wrote which film that was directed by Paul Verhoeven?", "answer": "Turkish Delight", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Purple Rain is a song by Prince and The Revolution, it reached number 2 in the United States for how long, behind Wake Me Up Before You Go-Go, a song by the British duo Wham!?", "answer": "two weeks", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Nominated for an Academy Award for Best Supporting Actress for her role as Olive Neal, this actress also made her film debut in what movie? ", "answer": "No Small Affair", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is Gray Wolf Glacier and Mission Mountains located?", "answer": "Montana", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which peoples inhabited this territory where Saint Walpurga was an abbess in the 8th century?", "answer": "the Franks", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Postal 2 (stylized as POSTAL) is a black comedy first-person shooter video game by Running With Scissors, scenes of the game can be seen in the music video of which Black Eyed Peas single, that was released in June 2003 as the lead single from their third album, \"Elephunk\"? ", "answer": "Where Is the Love", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the full name of the record-breaking American sprinter known as Flo-Jo?", "answer": "Florence Griffith Joyner", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which building is planned for the future - 888 7th Avenue or 50 Hudson Yards?", "answer": "50 Hudson Yards", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Dachau Trials and the division of Germany happened due