ox Magazine for hobby seekers?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What 1996 feature  film directed by Danny Devito takes place at Crunchem Hall Primary School?", "answer": "Matilda", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are The Animal World and The Battle of San Pietro both documentaries?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the name of this German thrash metal band, who released Sentence of Death, as their debut?", "answer": "Destruction", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Matt Selman created an action platformer video game based on the animated television series which was released in October of what year? ", "answer": "2007", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who led the real-life Rebellion that the film 'North West Mounted Police' is based on?", "answer": "Louis Riel", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Killing Mr. Griffin starred an actress born October 6 with what nationality?", "answer": "American-Canadian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is the state history museum that presents, what historian Carl L. Becker a century ago, reflects American ideals from the prehistoric to modern eras in 30000 sqft of exhibits ?", "answer": "Kansas Museum of History", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the population as of the 2010 census of the city in which the NBC affiliate WTVA is located?", "answer": "34,546", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "On which issues does this American bi-monthly magazine, for which Merl Reagle produced a bimonthly crossword puzzle for, focus?", "answer": "aging issues", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Acquire and Torres, are which specific form of entertainment?", "answer": "board game", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Cemetery Gates is a song from a Pantera album from what year?", "answer": "1990", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the British award that was won by both Paul Rodgers and Gary Barlow ?", "answer": "Ivor Novello Award", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Samuel Bell Waugh was a 19th-century American portrait paiter whose subjects include an American politician and lawyer who was assasinated when?", "answer": "April 1865", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which band's debut album was released first, We the Kings or Quietdrive?", "answer": "Quietdrive", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Besides Mike Morris, the only other Northeastern University player to be drafted in the first round of the NHL draft was drafted by what team?", "answer": "Dallas Stars", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "This \"Passons\" soap opera character was portrayed at one time by an American actor born in what year?", "answer": "1977", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Do Haplopappus and Malvaviscus fall into the same family of flowering plants?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "When was the  American professional wrestler which led the Latino World Order in 1998 and 1999 born", "answer": "October 9, 1967", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Did both Raine Maida and Josey Scott perform as lead vocalists for Saliva?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In what city are 50 Hudson Yards and the Metropolitan Tower both located? ", "answer": "New York City", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the cover song on the release of Sara Jezebel Deva's second album that was at one time banned in Belgium?", "answer": "Frozen", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The principal building in the village of Guthrie dates back to what century?", "answer": "the 15th century", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Between Ice Princess and Bolt, which was more unsuccessful in the box office?", "answer": "\"Ice Princess\"", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is a Totokia usually made of?", "answer": "wood", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jonathan Goldsmith played \"the most interesting man in the world\" and represented what advertisement campaign?", "answer": "Dos Equis beer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ko Wo