ings of Apple's headquarters that resembles that of a university, with the buildings arranged around green spaces, similar to a suburban business park?", "answer": "Infinite Loop", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Electronic Products and The Wittenburg Door both magazines?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The parody group Boys generally Asian was formed by a YouTuber that had over how many subscribers in 2017?", "answer": "20 million", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What nationality was the player whom the 2003-04 Detroit Pistons selected as their top pick?", "answer": "Serbian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What actor had roles in both \"Good Luck Charlie\" and the 2011 American direct-to-DVD film starring Ashley Tisdale?", "answer": "Bradley Steven Perry", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the company that makes India Kings headquartered?", "answer": "Kolkata, West Bengal.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Donvale Football Club will play in Division 3 of a league based in what suburbs of metropolitan Melbourne?", "answer": "eastern", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Grand Canyon: A Different View has an essay from what American young earth creationist and geophysicist?", "answer": "John Baumgardner", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the full name of the politician Ed Rollins was the national campaign chairman for?", "answer": "Michael Dale Huckabee", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Polish Hunting Dog and Norfolk Spaniel are both dogs?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Where and when was the band that wrote \"Rock or Bust\" formed?", "answer": "Sydney in 1973", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is one of the stars of Norman... Is That You known as?", "answer": "\"King of the Party Records\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Chief Mouser to the Cabinet Office is the title of the official resident cat, of the Prime Minister of the United Kingdom, which tabby cat, with this title, is 