or shareholder is Rallye SA?", "answer": "France", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "William R. Vance, was the seventh mayor of Louisville, Kentucky from 1847 to 1850, during his administration, he conveyed the tract of land that became Cave Hill Cemetery, a Victorian era National Cemetery and arboretum located at 701 Baxter Avenue, Louisville, in which U.S. state?", "answer": "Kentucky", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the film adapted from a book published under the pseudonym Elizabeth McNeill?", "answer": "Adrian Lyne", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " A Time for Miracles chronicles the life story of America's first native born saint who was born in what year?", "answer": "1774", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which director is considered a feminist, Kim Ki-duk or Chantal Akerman?", "answer": "Chantal Anne Akerman", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Iron Maiden's only constant member since their inception was credited for a song on what album?", "answer": "The Number of the Beast", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What country of origin does 17 Carat and Seventeen have in common?", "answer": "Korean", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What class was 6029,a four-cylinder, simple, non-condensing, coal-fired superheated, 4-8-4+4-8-4 heavy goods steam locomotives built by Beyer, Peacock and Company for the New South Wales Government Railways in Australia, used in?", "answer": "The AD60 class", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the home field also know as for the 1981 sooners?", "answer": "Owen Field", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which country is 2MW and Murwillumbah located in?", "answer": "Australia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The wormhoudt massacre occurred during a battle that brought land operations on the Western Front to an end until what date?", "answer": "6 June 1944", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What 147 mile long river is dammed by the Apalachia Dam?", "answer": "Hiwassee River", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Does Yanji have a larger population than Jinzhong?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What was the tag team name of Terry Gene Bollea? ", "answer": "The Mega Powers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Hyland River Provincial Park runs along which 2700km roadway?", "answer": "Alaska Highway", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What role did the maker of the film \"Cradle will Rock\" play in the film \"The Sawshank Redemption\"?", "answer": "Andy Dufresne", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which actor from \"The Cosby Show\" also starred in \"Play'd: A Hip Hop Story\"?", "answer": "Merlin Santana", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The shopping center that incorporates multiple factory outlets in one center is located on which side of the Adelaide Airport?", "answer": "west", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Lynyrd Skynyrd, is an American rock band best known for popularizing the Southern rock genre during the 1970s, at the peak of their success, two band members and a backup singer died in the crash of a Convair CV-240, chartered by the rock band Lynyrd Skynyrd from L&J Company of Addison, Texas, ran out of fuel and crashed in Gillsburg, Mississippi, near the end of its flight from Greenville, South Carolina, to Baton Rouge, in which state?", "answer": "Louisiana", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which year was the 85-86 Man of the Year inducted into the Naismith Memorial Basketball Hall of Fame?", "answer": "1993", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which type of plant has more species:  Mentha or Calodendrum?", "answer": "Mentha", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In 1998, Lopez starred alongside George Clooney in which 1998 American crime comedy film directed by Steven Soderbergh and written by Scott Frank, adapted from Elmore Leonard's novel of the same name?", "answer": "Out of Sight", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Moi, Antoine de Tounens, roi de Patagonie, tells the story of what French lawyer who assumed the title of King of Araucania and 