xas entertainment district?", "answer": "Sixth Street", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Gokula had a soundtrack composed by the composer in what film industry?", "answer": "Kannada", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who murdered the American Olympian Dave Schultz?", "answer": "John Eleuth\u00e8re du Pont", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Detective Phil Fish was played by an actor who was born in what year?", "answer": "1921", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which voice actor starred in both the 2016 film All We Had, as well as the Pixar Film Inside Out?", "answer": "Richard Kind", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Veerse Meer was separated from the North Sea by a series of what?", "answer": "construction projects", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who as an American boy band formed in Orlando, Florida in 1995, that released a song on January 11, 2000 as the first single from their second studio album \"No Strings Attached\"?", "answer": "NSYNC", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Gerhard Thiele and Patrick Baudry, have which occupation in common?", "answer": "astronaut", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which British fascist politician and veterinary surgeon published arguments about controversial topics around the Second World War?", "answer": "Arnold Spencer Leese", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the beginning of the crisis which prompted the Malta Declaration? ", "answer": "2015", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the director of the 1997 American horror film which features the designs of Greek-French production designer Patrick Tatopoulos?", "answer": "Mark A.Z. Dipp\u00e9", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the Texas Longhorns football team head coach who went on to work as a commentator for ESPN?", "answer": "Mack Brown", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jessi Ruth Klein played in many rolls throughout the years. Lucy, the Daughter of the Devil was aired by the Adult Swim Programming block of what channel?", "answer": "Cartoon Network", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "which animation is japanese, Gurren Lagann of The Secret of Kells ?", "answer": "Gurren Lagann", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "A re Tom McCarthy and Jim Sheridan film directors?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which computer was listed the highest selling computer model of all time, Commodore 64 or Aamber Pegasus?", "answer": "Aamber Pegasus", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the middle name of the actor who, along with Seth MacFarlane, Alex Borstein,  Lacey Chabert and Mila Kunis, provides voices for the show Family Guy ? ", "answer": "Benjamin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which character in Disney's Cinderella animated feature was inspired by the actor Jeffrey Stone?", "answer": "Prince Charming", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"'Tis the Fifteenth Season\" is the seventh episode of \"The Simpsons\"' fifteenth season, and the seventh Christmas-themed episode overall, this episode is notable as being the first to make reference to Lisa's Buddhism since she converted in which earlier Christmas episode, which is the sixth episode, of \"The Simpsons\"' thirteenth season?", "answer": "She of Little Faith", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The author of \"The Stranger\" wrote what essay about his life being devoted to opposing the philosophy of nihilism?", "answer": "The Rebel", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed this 2009 British-American mockumentary comedy film to which Wolfgang Held contributed?", "answer": "Larry Charles", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which rapper forms lyrics in the Swahili language, which is primarily spoken in the African Great Lakes Region?", "answer": "E-Sir", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Stanley Brothers were an American bluegrass duo made up of Ralph Stanley, and which bluegrass music lead singer, songwriter, and rhythm guitar player, he formed his band together, with his brother Ralph?", "answer": "Carter Glen Stan