sed by which entity of people?", "answer": "public", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Bowater House was demolished to create what London retail complex?", "answer": "One Hyde Park", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the birthdate of this English actress, who was nominated twice for an Emmy Award and narrated The Hoarder Next Door?", "answer": "30 January 1974", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Chicken Ranch and Ring of Fire both documentary films?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Ol' Brown Ears is Back is a music and comedy record released by The Jim Henson Company, in 1993, the  album consists of 14 songs recorded by whom as Rowlf the Dog, a Muppet character, a scruffy brown dog of indeterminate breed, though part Corgi, with a rounded black nose and long floppy ears?", "answer": "Jim Henson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A 1967 one-act play that is an absurdist drama about 5 people waiting in line for an event, was written by an American playwright, director, and actor, who was born in what year?", "answer": "1939", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which artist who contributed to R Kelly's \"Double Up\" album began his solo career in 2000 ?", "answer": "Nelly", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "USCGC Blackthorn sand in a collision at a bridge spanning what Florida city?", "answer": "Tampa Bay", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which wind-instrument-heavy genre of music did Dolores Janney \"Jenni\" Rivera Saavedra play to garner the title of \"top Latin artist of 2013\"?", "answer": "Banda", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Hera is the goddess of women and marriage in Greek mythology and what collection of beliefs, rituals, and mythology originating in ancient Greece in the form of both popular public religion and cult practices?", "answer": "Ancient Greek religion", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What type of category does Pimelea and Disocactus have in common?", "answer": "genus", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are Bertrand Blier and Chris Carter both American directors?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "(n\u00e9e Bessie; March 29, 1880, From what school did a legendary female pianist and pedagogue, with the former last name of Bessie, born March 29, 1880 in Kiev, Ukraine, Russian Empire graduate?", "answer": "Juilliard School", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which documentary was released first, Feiyu Show or That's Dancing!?", "answer": "That's Dancing!", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Maxwell Braden \"Max\" Mittelman is a voice actor whose roles have in included a charcter who  has grown bored by the absence of challenge in his fight against evil and seeks to find what?", "answer": "a worthy opponent", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Huayin and Ji'an, Jilin both in China?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which documentary was released first, Million Dollar Arm or Wings of Life? ", "answer": "Wings of Life", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Save the Tiger starred an American actor born July 25, 1908 who was nominated for what?", "answer": "Academy Award for Best Supporting Actor", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which city has a greater population, Wanning or Xichang?", "answer": "Xichang", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who was known for being a convicted murder and entrepreneur, but also known for inventing what's known as the dancing tree in computer science?", "answer": "Hans Reiser", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When did an actor in the live action remake of Timon and Pumbaa win a Daytime Emmy Award?", "answer": "2013", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What kind of athlete does Ahmad Khormali and G\u00e1bor Kir\u00e1ly have in common?", "answer": "goalkeeper", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In June, 2016 what was the population of Port Macquarie where the Ngamba traditionally lived?", "answer": "The town with its suburbs had a population of 45,698 in June 2016.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "