ay in?", "answer": "Division I", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What company did Evan Olson record a song for that is also one of the largest chocolate manufacturers in the world?", "answer": "The Hershey Company", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which is a species of flowering plant, Ruscus or Calamus?", "answer": "Ruscus", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the Austrian association football team known as  due to sponsership that is based in Altach, Vorarlberg ,who has their former footballer as their current manager?", "answer": "CASHPOINT SCR", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the release of the song \"Monster\" that was recorded by a South Korea boy band named Big Bang?", "answer": "June 3, 2012", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Uruguayan former footballer is son to Uruguayan basketball player who competed in 1960 Summer Olympics?", "answer": "Gus Poyet", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jerry Maguire is a 1996 American romantic comedy-drama sports film that was produced by what California-based film and television company that was created by James L Brooks?", "answer": "Gracie Films", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What band that was a support act on the initial, first leg of the \"California\" tour was formed in 2003?", "answer": "All Time Low", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Marvel Super Heroes In War of the Gems includes a plot to seek out what six immensely powerful fictional gems?", "answer": "Infinity Gems", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is one physical charactertic of a fuchs?", "answer": "Foxes have a flattened skull, upright triangular ears, a pointed, slightly upturned snout, and a long bushy tail (or \"brush\").", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What role did Hans Morten Hansen played in the form of \"found footage\" mockumentary?", "answer": "Finn", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which company produced more types of products, Voss or Pet, Inc.?", "answer": "Pet, Inc.", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Between Talk Talk and Hunter Valentine, which band was formed earlier?", "answer": "Hunter Valentine", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Michael Benyaer is best known for his role as bob in a Canadian television series that aired starting which year ?", "answer": "1994", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Greenwood Heights, Brooklyn is bordered to the west by a canal that is how long?", "answer": "1.8 mi", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Omo Baba Olowo is the debut album of Davido, who collaborated in production with a British-born Nigerian record producer who was nominated at the 2014 Nigeria Entertainment Awards in what category?", "answer": "Music Producer of the Year", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The year directly after Splash was first broadcasted, what was the name of the syndicated entertainment news show that Charissa Thompson co-hosted in?", "answer": "Extra", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ernie Banks was inducted into which Cooperstown, NY, museum in 1977?", "answer": "National Baseball Hall of Fame", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Eighth Street station is one mile west of which neighborhood in Miami?", "answer": "Little Havana", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year did the American professional stock car racing driver that finished third in the September 5, 2010 Atlanta Motor Speedway was born?", "answer": "1975", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who founded the brewing company that sponsors the Tuborg Image Awards?", "answer": "Carl Frederik Tietgen", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What union was directed by a common monarch and was abandoned in 1523?", "answer": "Kalmar Union", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is is one of the oldest magazines in the country and the first Belgian women's magazine, Femmes d\u2019Aujourd\u2019hui or Better Homes and Gardens?", "answer": "Femmes d\u2019Aujourd\u2019hui", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In what year was the football team for which Gerardo Berodia plays formed?", "answer": "1976", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A Hard Day's Night included the resident in general surgery character who has been portrayed by which actress since Grey's Anatomy began production?", "answer": "Chandra Wilson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which \"MIghty Morphin Power Rangers\" actress also starred in Veritas, Prince of Truth?", "answer": "Amy Jo Johnson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What country are both Mill Creek Valley USD 329 and Alma, Kansas in?", "answer": "United States", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the English-Irish acress who stars in the film Guy X?", "answer": "Natascha McElhone", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Stranger Things stared an Actor who played Nancy Wheeler, what was her name?", "answer": "Natalia Dyer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which airport is the largest hub for American Airlines, Dallas/Fort Worth International Airport or Manhattan Regional Airport?", "answer": "Dallas/Fort Worth International Airport", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Academia Deportiva Cantolao, a Peruvian football club based in the city of Callao, Peru, graduated what former Bayern Munich striker for Bundesliga club 1?", "answer": "Claudio Pizarro", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The We Are Family Foundation was founded by a musician who is famous for which guitar style ?", "answer": "\"chucking\" rhythm guitar", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The film \"Police Academy 6: City Under Siege\" stars a professional football player inducted into the College Football Hall of Fame in what year?", "answer": "1988", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Liberty Park overlooks a memorial located at the World Trade Center site, which is the former location of what?", "answer": "Twin Towers that were destroyed during the September 11 attacks", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Inifinite Love was recorded prior to the phenomenon that was part of the end date of which calendar?", "answer": "Mesoamerican Long Count", "type": "bridge"}, {"question"