ith?", "answer": "Alexei Shulgin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Lichtenberg's Avertissement, is a poster intended to deter the citizens of G\u00f6ttingen, Germany, from attending the performance of Jacob Philadelphia in 1777, it was written by which German scientist, satirist, and Anglophile?", "answer": "Georg Christoph Lichtenberg", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what city did Michael Skinner work for over 20 years as a magician-in-residence?", "answer": "Las Vegas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The literary magazine Okyeame was inspired by which prime minister, having led his country to independence from Britain in 1957?", "answer": "Kwame Nkrumah", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Paul Hindemith and Anton\u00edn Dvo\u0159\u00e1k both German composers?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Bendy Casimir, made his WEC debut on March 6, 2010 at WEC 47, losing via first-round knockout, against which American mixed martial artist who currently fights as a Featherweight in the Ultimate Fighting Championship organization?", "answer": "Ricardo Alejandro Lamas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The actress that played Shirley Partridge in \"The Partridge Family\" also stars with James Stewart in a 1961 western film cased on what novel?", "answer": "\"Comanche Captives\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the birthday of Gerald Strebendt's UFC 44 lightweight opponent?", "answer": "September 21, 1978", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "McKids was a chain of clothing stores marketed to children and operated by an American hamburger and fast food restaurant chain founded in what year?", "answer": "1940", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Steve Mcqueen acted alongside whom in 1974 the Irwin Allen produced action drama disaster film?", "answer": "Paul Newman", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ellen's Energy Adventure is starring a comedian from which country?", "answer": "American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The music tracks from 