 a song that was played in what 1997 Hong Kong romance film?", "answer": "Happy Together", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many BAFTA awards did Irish actor Ray McAnally win including his role in the 1986 film The Mission?", "answer": "four", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Can both War and Peace and Les v\u00eapres siciliennes be arranged as five acts?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the name of the former Arena that was renamed the CotaiArena in the Cotai Strip, located in Macau, China, which is similar to the Las Vegas Strip in America?", "answer": "Venetian Arena", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which masonry fort in the continental United States was  USS \"Fort Marion\"  named for ", "answer": "The Castillo de San Marcos", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Quanta Magazine and Lindy's Sports, are which form of publication?", "answer": "magazine", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Medea de Novara was known for her resemblance of an Empress who passed away in which year ?", "answer": "19 January 1927", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Arnebia\" is a genus of flowering plants. Is \"Colletia\" also a genius of flowering plants?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which women's golf team represents a university formerly referred to as \"Nova.\"", "answer": "NSU Sharks Women's Golf team", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which year was this movie that stars Lee Yeon-hee and was directed by this South Korean film direct who contributed to  \"Volcano High\" (2001) and \"Temptation of Wolves\" (2004)?", "answer": "2006", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which 1990 film written by Alan Dershowitz did Edwin McDonough contribute to?", "answer": "Reversal of Fortune", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "For what contribution did Simon van der Meer won the that is given by he Royal Swedish Academy of Sciences?", "answer": "CERN", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Sugarcubes and SCH, are related to music?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The author of the film \"Jerusalem\", based on a two-part novel, was also the first female writer to win what prize?", "answer": "the Nobel Prize in Literature", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Cecil Wood provided an engine for which New Zealand farmer to build his airplane?", "answer": "Richard William Pearse", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "George Jasper Caster (August 4, 1907 \u2013 December 18, 1955), nicknamed \"Ug\", was a right-handed professional baseball pitcher for 21 years from 1929 to 1948 and again in 1953, He played for which team, from 1945-1946, which American professional baseball team based in Detroit, Michigan?", "answer": "Detroit Tigers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which genus of plant consists of more species, Bruckenthalia or Fothergilla?", "answer": "Fothergilla", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What type of surety was the Earl of Pembroke who participated in the battle at Lincoln castle in 1217?", "answer": "Magna Carta", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the area of the forest on which the mountain which has the WCYB-DT2 was located? ", "answer": "655598 acre", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who currently represents the Minnesota congressional district where Patty Wetterling was a candidate?", "answer": "Tom Emmer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Delta Air Lines Flight 1989 was leaving from which Boston airport when it was thought to have been hijacked?", "answer": "Logan International Airport", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Tripoint is a science fiction novel by an author born in which year ?", "answer": "1942", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which song descended from \"I'll Overcome Some Day\" and used \"O Sanctissima \"?", "answer": "We Shall Overcome", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Firangi lead roles are played by Monica Gill and an actress of what ethnicity?", "answer": "Indian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which camp did the co founder of Wikipedia inaugurate?", "answer": "Wikicamp", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Honorary Consul starred which Mexican and American actress and director?", "answer": "Elpidia Carrillo", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the population of the place as of 2011 where Donald Ray Payne dies on February 25, 2017?", "answer": "87,496", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the capital of the state Fred Mundee went to High School in?", "answer": "Youngstown, Ohio", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "On the Way to the Wedding is a historical romance written by an author whose novels have been translated into how many different languages?", "answer": "26", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The overthrown General in the Battle of Santa Clara lived in what U.S. state for a short period of time before he became a dictator?", "answer": "Florida", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "James Harden previously played for which team?", "answer": "Oklahoma City Thunder", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the 2016 horror film Kim Hwan-hee appeared in?", "answer": "Na Hong-jin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "John Stubbs died in a city with an urban population of what in 2015?", "answer": "29,413", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The duo who did the song \"Hold Each Other\" is from where?", "answer": "New York", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Civil War general was the town in which Francis W. Parker Charter Essential School is located named after?", "answer": "Charles Devens", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which band won an award at the 2006 Meteor Award with their eleventh studio album?", "answer": "U2", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Wong Kar-wai directed which 1994 Hong Kong drama film?", "answer": "Chungking Express", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Neon Lights is a song released on the seven studio album by German electronic music band Kraftwerk, released when?", "answer": "May 1978", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Le Futur Noir is the debut album of the