n as Ghidrah in English markets?", "answer": "Ishir\u014d Honda", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the actor who played the recurring character in Martok born? ", "answer": "March 18, 1950", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In between Blue Peter and Alanis Morissette who's album \"Supposed Former Infatuation Junkie\", was released in 1998?", "answer": "Alanis Nadine Morissette", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the nationality of this stand up comedian and a friend of the guitarist/songwriter Billy Jenkins shown in the documentary spoof, Virus Called The Blues?", "answer": "English", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What song did Fonzworth Bentley co-produce with Kanye West?", "answer": "Champions", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What company owns the magazine that shares a name with the channel that airs the show Oorum Unavum?", "answer": "SRM Group", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Jesuit pope from the Americas established the Syro-Malankara Catholic Eparchy of Gurgaon?", "answer": "Pope Francis", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Strahlen (Rays) for a percussionist (vibraphone and/or glockenspiel) and ten-channel sound recording is a composition by which German composer, widely acknowledged by critics as one of the most important ; but also controversial composers of the 20th and early 21st centuries?", "answer": "Karlheinz Stockhausen", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the current coach of the basketball team in Boulder, Colorado for which Cliff Meely once played?", "answer": "Tad Boyle", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the birth year of the founder of Himalayan Trust, which built the Pangboche school?", "answer": "1919", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Between the Akita and Boykin Spaniel, which dog breed is larger?", "answer": "Akita", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the nationality of the singer of the song sampled in \"Shawty Is a 10\"?", "answer": "Barbadian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What 