ch starred Tony Slattery?", "answer": "Neil Jordan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A member of the girl group \"miss A\" also stars in a South Korean tv drama that airs on what days?", "answer": "Wednesday and Thursday", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Australian rules football player played with the Fitzroy in the Victorian Football League, the West Adelaide Football Club, and the South Adelaide Football Club, or the Panthers in the southern suburbs of Adelaide.", "answer": "Henry Alexander \"Bert\" Rapiport", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The band whose style is typified by the blurring of component musical parts was formed when?", "answer": "2009", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many municipalities are in the Mexican state where the Radiomas is located?", "answer": "212", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "William Z. McFarland, is an American entrepreneur who was the founder and CEO of three companies, McFarland was placed under arrest on which date, and charged with wire fraud in Manhattan federal court related to the organization of The Fyre Festival, was a music festival scheduled to take place on the Bahamian island of Great Exuma over two weekends in April and May 2017?", "answer": "June 30, 2017", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Name a song by LCD Soundsystem?", "answer": "Sound of Silver", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which publication out of The Brown Spectator and Robb Report is aimed at a wealthier audience?", "answer": "Robb Report", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which Austin, TX born singer performed at the 2007 World Music Awards?", "answer": "Ciara", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which star of \"The Last Picture Show\" (1971) also starred in a film based on the the short story \"A Change of Plan\", written by Bruce Jay Friedman?", "answer": "Cybill Shepherd", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the birth year of the actor that stared in Paris by Night and Harry Potter?", "answer": "1940", "type": "bridge"}, {"ques