arm that Wilbur the pig was born and raised?", "answer": "Brooklin, Maine, United States", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the corporate sponsor that had their name in front of the college football bowl game which featured a team in their 106th season lead by a second year coach beat Florida State University?", "answer": "FedEx", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which occurred first, St. Elizabeths Hospital being designated a National Historic Landmark or Sibley Memorial Hospital being a part of Johns Hopkins Medicine?", "answer": "St. Elizabeths Hospital", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who wrote the song on the A-side of the song \"Rain\"?", "answer": "Paul McCartney and John Lennon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Rediscovered is the fifth studio album by English-Norwegian pop group A1, the album was released on which date in Norway, two singles have thus far been released from the album: \"Just Three Words\", featuring singer Annie Khalid?", "answer": "2 November 2012", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Chitwan National Park and Sites of Japan\u2019s Meiji Industrial Revolution: Iron and Steel, Shipbuilding and Coal Mining are located in Europe?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "When was the federation disbanded that governed the multi-sport event held in Tokyo, Japan, from 24 May to 1 June 1958, and replaced by the Olympic Council of Asia ?", "answer": "26 November 1981", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which team that was founded in 1897 prevented the A.C. Milan from retaining their title in the 2004-05 season?", "answer": "Juventus Football Club", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the city that Thomas Edmonds taught at in 1961 founded?", "answer": "1838", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The southern border of the state in the southern region of the United States represented by Frank Alexander McLain forms what ?", "answer": "Gulf of Mexico", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the birthday of the woman who inspired Waylon Jennings to write \"Good Hearted Woman\"?", "answer": "November 26, 1939", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who runs the New York-New York Hotel & Casino that is located in Tropicana in Las Vegas?", "answer": "It is owned and operated by MGM Resorts International.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of Kesha's number-one singles features Diddy?", "answer": "Tik Tok", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the English television presenter of Let's Sing and Dance prior to 2011?", "answer": "Claudia Winkleman", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Mountain Creek is a ski resort that is 47 miles from what double-decked suspension bridge that spans the Hudson River between the WAshington Heights neighborhood of Manhattan in New York City and Fort Lee, New Jersey?", "answer": "The George Washington Bridge", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of the sport analyst of The Experts Network is nicknamed  \"The Iron Man\"?", "answer": "Calvin Edwin Ripken Jr.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What American actor, best known for playing Alex Santiago in the television series \"Resurrection Blvd\" starred in a film directed by James Dodson?", "answer": "Nicholas Edward Gonzalez", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "This American multi-jurisdictional lottery draw game offered in 44 states, the District of Columbia, and the U.S. Virgin Islands is run by which government?", "answer": "the government of New Mexico", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What director had a film in the 1952 Cannes Film Festival and was married to Judy Garland for a short time?", "answer": "Vincente Minnelli", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "K\u00f8benhavn and Vinci are both what?", "answer": "board game", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Order of Saint Michael the Archangel and Maria Vladimirovna, Grand Duchess of Russia have both been involved with which house?", "answer": "Imperial", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the institute founded where Alice Hamilton w