, "answer": "National Geographic", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What type of person does Deirdre Connelly and Andrew Witty have in common?", "answer": "executive", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Live at the Boston Garden: April 5, 1968 was broadcast to quell riots that took place in which cities ?", "answer": "Washington, D.C., Baltimore, Chicago, and Kansas City", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both Billy Milano and Luca Prodan considered American singers?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The 1996\u201397 NBA season was the 51st season of the National Basketball Association (NBA), this season featured the debut of Allen Ezail Iverson, an American former professional basketball player, who played for 14 seasons, in which organization?", "answer": "National Basketball Association (NBA)", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What type of painting work is the illustrator of Chaos Marauders is also known for?", "answer": "fantasy miniature painting", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What American country music singer and guitarist best known for his 1962 hit, Charlie's Shoes, also released the song Forever written by Buddy Killen?", "answer": "Billy Walker", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Hankook Ilbo publishes Korean versions of what magazine started in 1959 owned by Time Inc.? ", "answer": "Golf Magazine", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who's best known work include \"Typee\", a romantic account of his experiences in Polynesian life, and his whaling novel \"Moby-Dick\" that was interpreted as a 2004 French short film directed by Philippe Ramos?", "answer": "Herman Melville", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Eagle Mountain International Church's pastor  married to Terri Pearsons, is part of the ministry started by what man who has been identified with preaching a prosperity and abundance message, commonly referred to as the prosperity gospel?", "answer": "Kenneth Max Copeland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American film great, Sam Wood or Tyler Perry, also specializes in the gospel genre of music?", "answer": "Tyler Perry", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who conducted an opera by Nikolai Rimsky-Korsakov with Yevgeny Akulov in 1962?", "answer": "Aleksei Kovalev", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which director is older, Ringo Lam or Roberto Benigni?", "answer": "Roberto Remigio Benigni", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What nationality was the cartonist and publisher who drew story entitled \"Allah Had No Son\"?", "answer": "American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Tom Powers appeared as Brutus in an adaptation of a William Shakespeare play that was first produced in what year?", "answer": "1937", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Guts Over Fear was a single from which hip hop compilation album from 2014?", "answer": "Shady XV", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Mollo is a French footballer who plays for a football club founded in what year?", "answer": "1879", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the English football club that had played in Runcorn, Widnes, and Prescot during its existence and who footballer Danny Byrne had previously played for?", "answer": "Runcorn F.C. Halton", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Death of a Gentleman is a documentary, released in which year, about the takeover of the governance of cricket by ICC's 'Big Three', it features interviews with which takeover architect, and former England international cricketer, a right-handed batsman and occasional off spin bowler, who currently plays for Melbourne Stars?", "answer": "2015", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "in which armed labor conflict did Charles Everett lively play a major role?", "answer": "The Coal Wars", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what state was William R. Brewster overrun by Confederaqtes at the Emmitsburg Road?", "answer": "Pennsylvania", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When did the team that won the Frauen DFB-Pokal cup competition in 1995 disband?", "answer": "2006", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the 1999 American comedy film featuring William \"Bill\" Lumbergh?", "answer": "Mike Judge", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed the feature film that Janine Turner portrayed Jessie Deighan in?", "answer": "Renny Harlin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which woman was executed first, Karla Faye Tucker or Margie Velma Barfield?", "answer": "Margie Velma Barfield", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 2010 NBA draft included the player from Kentucky who now plays for which New Orleans team being drafted in the first round?", "answer": "Pelicans", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A remix of \"Lush Life\" was released on 26 February 2016 featuring an English rapper who created his own record and fashion label called what?", "answer": "Disturbing London Records", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What did Guinness World Records certify for an young actor known for martial arts in the horror series 'Freakish?'", "answer": "youngest TV director ever", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What 1965 musical film featured a band managed by Brian Epstein?", "answer": "Ferry Cross the Mersey", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is noted for their work on the history of Egypt's largest Christian church?", "answer": "Father Menassa Youhanna", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What third album released in 1973 by the man who played the role as Keith Partridge, the son of Shirley Partridge in the 1970s musical-sitcom \"The Partridge Family\"?", "answer": "Dreams are Nuthin' More than Wishes", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Super High Roller Bowl takes place at a resort and casino that opened when?", "answer": "December 16, 2009", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What boxer that Dave Allen took on in 2016 was British?", "answer": "Dillian Whyte", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In 1986, Oliver Muirhead directed \"A Christmas Held Captive\", which is what type of musical comedy that includes songs, gags, and slap