{"question": "What American biochemist wrote an essay for Grand Canyon: A Different View?", "answer": "Duane Gish", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both Milan Kundera and T. E. Lawrence writers?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In what city is the publisher of tabletop role-playing game Hillfolk based?", "answer": "London", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Paterson Joseph starred in a 2008 British-American drama that had what amount of budget?", "answer": "$15,000,000", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What pre-university college is located in the capital of the Indian state of Karnataka?", "answer": "Surana PU College", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Channel V (styled Channel [V]) is the brand name for multiple international music television networks owned by Fox Networks Group, fully owned subsidiaries of which American multinational mass media corporation based in Midtown Manhattan, New York City?", "answer": "Twenty-First Century Fox Inc.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "AC3D is a 3D design program which has been available since which year, the software is used by designers for modeling 3D graphics for games and simulations - most notably it is used by the scenery creators at Laminar Research on X-Plane flight simulator produced by Laminar Research, and also ships with other software to build and customize aircraft and scenery?", "answer": "1994", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Vogue and Pro Football Weekly, are which type of publication?", "answer": "magazine", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "2004 KV18 was first observed at facilities located in a special land use known as what?", "answer": "\"Astronomy Precinct\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Introduction to Commutative Algebra is a well-known commutative algebra textbook written by Michael Francis Atiyah,who was born on which date, an English mathematician specialising in geometry?", "answer": "22 April 1929", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The same man who released a remix of Rhinna's seventh studio album, made another remix of what song in which one of the creators include Calvin Harris?", "answer": "Iron", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name for the lava, often found with Pele's tears, defined as volcanic glass fibers or thin strands of volcanic glass?", "answer": "Pele's hair", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Faith No More and Birds of Tokyo, have what what in common?", "answer": "rock band", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Ronan Hardiman created the soundtracks to which Irish dance production?", "answer": "Lord of the Dance", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Saving Abel and Sister Hazel both rock bands?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who is considered among the three foremost playwrights of 20th-century American drama, Tennessee Williams or E. B. White?", "answer": "Thomas Lanier \"Tennessee\" Williams III", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which of Bupleurum and Corokia has more species?", "answer": "Bupleurum", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "During the the 1992 Summer Olympics Jos\u00e9 Ortega lost the round of the heavyweight division to a boxer born in what year?", "answer": "1972", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Obadiah Poundage has been used for information on the types of beer made from what?", "answer": "brown malt", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How much did VMware pay to acquire the Atlanta-based provider of enterprise mobility management software?", "answer": "$1.54 billion", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Public Records Act of 1967 was passed during which 1964-1970 Prime Minister?", "answer": "Harold Wilson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which player is from Russia, Marin \u010cili\u0107 or Andrei Olhovskiy?", "answer": "Andrei Stanislavovich Olhovskiy", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which permanent dutch settlement in New Netherland was abandoned by the English in 1676 in favor of the newer Fort Frederick located in Albany, New