ines account for?", "answer": "83%", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which executive prodicer of Mishima: A Life in Four Chapters was a central figure in the New Hollywood wave of filmmaking ?", "answer": "Francis Ford Coppola", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "which was released first \"Do I Sound Gay?\" or \"Walking with Cavemen\" ?", "answer": "Walking with Cavemen", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Cooper is a comic opera, in two acts, by which English composer?", "answer": "Thomas Augustine Arne", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is the executive office of the company of which Young & Rubicam is a member?", "answer": "Dublin, Ireland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What did the Forum Cafeteria contain that were uniquely designed marine vessels?", "answer": "Viking ships", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who co-starred in All the Days Before Tomorrow with the actor known for his roles in Cabin Fever and Grind?", "answer": "Alexandra Holden", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What role did the player that Vince Bartram was an understudy of play during his career?", "answer": "goalkeeper", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Lost in La Mancha and Air Force, Incorporated, are films of which genre?", "answer": "documentary", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Android Cop is a 2014 American science fiction action film produced by The Asylum, the film stars Charles Stanley Dutton, an American stage, film, and television actor and director, best known for his roles as \"Fortune\", in which film?", "answer": "Rudy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Gerard F. Conway, is an American writer of comic books and television shows, he is known for scripting the death of the character Gwen Stacy during his long run on which TV show?", "answer": "The Amazing Spider-Man", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which area were driggers associated with?", "answer": "Cumberland Gap area", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Millennium Force was the first roller coaster to have what kind of system?", "answer": "lift hill", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who wrote the book Lost Girls, based on killings by John Albert Gardner?", "answer": "Caitlin Rother", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the company that owns and operates WOTF-DT originally known as?", "answer": "TeleFutura", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which saxophone hit was both covered by Chet Atkins and used as Benny Hill's signature tune?", "answer": "Yakety Sax", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many members does the band who released the extended play (EP) Signal consist of?", "answer": "nine", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born first, Sigmund Freud or Paul \u00c9luard?", "answer": "Sigmund Freud", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": " Ronald Isley and Ben Gibbard are both what?", "answer": "songwriter", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which  aria from the final act of Giacomo Puccini's opera did  Paul Potts perform ", "answer": "\"Nessun dorma \"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "X2 was directed by the film director who is the founder of what production studio?", "answer": "Bad Hat Harry Productions", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is the mass media company based in that owns Velocity?", "answer": "Silver Spring, Maryland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which band were Mark Stephen Gardener and Andy Bell band members of? ", "answer": "Ride", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the original singer of the song made famous by both Dobie Gray and Uncle Kracker?", "answer": "John Henry Kurtz", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which magazine is published in the U.S., Ranger Rick or OK!?", "answer": "Ranger Rick", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What nationality is the boxer whom Jorge Ahumada fought for the WBC Light Heavyweight Championship?", "answer": "British", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is one common aspect that movies Hot Lead and Cold Feet and Freaky Friday share?", "answer": "comedy", "type": "comparison"}, {"