ed in what California city?", "answer": "San Jose", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ann Winterton and her husband Sir Nicholas Winterton were both MPs for which British party?", "answer": "Conservative Party", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ardtornish House is famous for its gardens and the estate is the location of which abandoned castle?", "answer": "Kinlochaline Castle", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What course Brigadier General Dr. Jaswant Wadhwani lectured in the largest and the Premier Medical School currently located at the Korle Bu Teaching Hospital in Accra?", "answer": "Pathology", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many days did the English football manager born in 1961 manage the 1997-98 Reading F.C. team?", "answer": "seven", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Robbie Rist starred in the film \"Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtles\" in what year?", "answer": "1990", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Australian actor/filmmaker played a former FBI agent convicted of murder charges stemming from his relationship with the Winter Hill Gang?", "answer": "Joel Edgerton", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Zigong and Danjiangkou both located in China?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Are Harper Lee and Rosario Castellanos both poets?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which group of entertainers was associated with the Sands Hotel and Casino, famously run by Carl Cohen?", "answer": "the Rat Pack", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "what does Renault RE30 and Renault in Formula One have in common?", "answer": "car", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the motto of a musical group who performed Dark Adventure Radio Theatre: The Call of Cthulhu?", "answer": "Ludo Fore Putavimus", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What are the mountains that Waynesville, North Carolina is located between that are a physiographic province of the larger Appalachian Mountains range?", "answer": "Blue Ridge Mountains", "type": "bridge"},