rom what ethnic group?", "answer": "Italian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was Johnny Carson's sidekick that had a drunk clip of him drunk on \"The Tonight Show\" shown on The Show with No Name?", "answer": "Ed McMahon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is older, Edgar Wright or Ulli Lommel?", "answer": "Ulli Lommel", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Gerard Way and Varg Vikernes, share which mutual occupation?", "answer": "musician", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Robert William Ray investigated and issued the final reports on the Whitewater scandal, the White House travel office controversy, sometimes referred to as what? ", "answer": "Travelgate", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In the Book of Daniel, the Prophecy of Seventy Weeks, is given to Daniel by which angel, who typically serves as God's messenger, in response to Daniel, praying for God to act on behalf of his people and city of Jerusalem?", "answer": "Gabriel", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which dog breed originated in the United States, Treeing Walker Coonhound or Australian Stumpy Tail Cattle Dog?", "answer": "Treeing Walker Coonhound", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What sports journalist co-wrote \"Chasing Shadows \u2013 The Life and Death of Peter Roebuck\"?", "answer": "Timothy \"Tim\" Lane (born 1952 in Launceston, Tasmania) is an award-winning and veteran Australian sports journalist and sports commentator", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who wrote the novels Are We There Yet and Boy Meets Boy?", "answer": "David Levithan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Jewish Archive was handed by the regime of Francisco Franco to a leading member of the Nazi Party who was born on which day ?", "answer": "7 October 1900", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The work that Ann Bancroft did in the Antartic below 60 degrees latitude was administered by who?", "answer": "Antarctic Treaty System.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Yash Johar founded an Indian production and distribution company that was taken over in 2004 by who?", "answer": "Karan Johar", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Partybaby is an American indie rock band from Los Angeles, California, the group was formed by former The Man, guitarist Noah Gersh, Portugal. The Man, is an American rock band from Wasilla, in which U.S. state?", "answer": "Alaska", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who wrote more novels, Jim Henson or Khady Sylla?", "answer": "Khady Sylla", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Clark Memorandum was written by the undersecretary of which man, who was the 30th President of the United States?", "answer": "John Calvin Coolidge Jr.", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who manages the laboratory which currently has custody of Experimental Breeder Reactor-II ?", "answer": "Battelle Energy Alliance", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the 1982 novel, the subject of which is credited with saving the lives of 1,200 Jews during the Holocaust, including the life of Moshe Taub\u00e9?", "answer": "\"Schindler's Ark\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Berkheya and Conicosia are examples of which taxonomic category?", "answer": "genus", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Maud Solveig Christina Adams is a Swedish actress known for the character in the thirteenth entry in which film series?", "answer": "James Bond", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Dracula II: Ascension is a 2003 direct-to-video American-Romanian horror film, it stars which American actor and martial artist, and is best known for his role as Mowgli in Disney's 1994 live-action adaptation of \"The Jungle Book\"?", "answer": "Jason Scott Lee", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year did one of the judges on \"Your Face Sounds Familiar\" win the Celebrity Big Brother 10?", "answer": "2012", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "John Delaney, who sponsored a bill to make Election Day a federal holiday, will be running for President of what country in 2020? ", "answer": "United States", "type