tlanta Hawks, and the Golden State Warriors", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Auburn is an Antebellum mansion in Duncan Park in Natchez, Mississippi, it was designed and constructed by which person, an accused in the infamous Manhattan Well Murder trial of 1800, the first murder trial in the United States for which there is a recorded transcript?", "answer": "Levi Weeks", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"What Ya Gonna Do Now?\" and \"Bloody Annoying\" are by a singer that is also fouinded what rock band?", "answer": "Blur", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Lyudmil Kirkov and Niki Caro both are or have been what?", "answer": "film director", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What author has won more National Book Critics Circle Awards, Lucy Maud Montgomery or William H. Gass?", "answer": "William Howard Gass", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "When was Kathryn Grayson of the 1946 American musical comedy, Ziegfeld Follies, under contract to Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer?", "answer": "by the early 1940s", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Northcote's head chef was born in what year?", "answer": "1981", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Chick tract that inspired the American short film dark Dungeons was created and published by whom?", "answer": "Jack Chick", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the person who Claude Mongeau succeeded the CEO of?", "answer": "CSX", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American kickboxer based in Scottsdale Arizona has been beaten in world championships by Changpuek Kiatsongrit?", "answer": "Rick Roufus", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which  French professional rally, racing, and rallycross driver was competitive at the 2004 Wales Rally GB along with Petter Solberg?", "answer": "S\u00e9bastien Loeb", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Jiang Tao was a boxer that won bronze at the Asian Games held in which Japanese city?", "answer": "Hiroshima", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which author, Len Deighton or Penelope Fitzgerald, won the Booker Prize?", "answer": "Penelope Fitzgerald", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The 1999\u20132000 UEFA Cup was won with a winning goal by a footballer that was the former captain of what team?", "answer": "FC Barcelona", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the granite dome at the eastern end of Yosemite Valley, where areas were burnt due to the Meadow Fire?", "answer": "Half Dome", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Aniki-B\u00f3b\u00f3 is akin to a children's counting rhyme that has existed in various forms since well before when?", "answer": "1820", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which opera has more acts, Faust or Mignon?", "answer": "Faust", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Il piccolo Marat was written by the composer of what 1890 masterpiece?", "answer": "Cavalleria Rusticana", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Pizzagate conspiracy theory revolved around the Gmail account of what chief of staff?", "answer": "John Podesta", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who authored the book series whose movie version starred Shefali Chowdhury?", "answer": "J. K. Rowling", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which case regarded juveniles as separate types of defendants, In re Gault or Ford v. Wainwright?", "answer": "In re Gault", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What was the nationality of the winner of the second biggest-ranking UK snooker tournament in 2006? ", "answer": "English", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The World Food Championships were moved to the pedestrian mall in what city as of 2013?", "answer": "Las Vegas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What do San Angelo Regional Airport and Abraham Lincoln Capital Airport have in common? ", "answer": "public airport", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "when was the book by J.R.R. Tolkien that Bilbo Baggins is the title character and protagonist originally published?", "answer": "21 September 1937", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Ivan Fesenko and Boris Trakhtenbrot both mathem