on did the Major League Baseball player, who broke Babe Ruth's career home run record when Ed Sudol was the second base umpire, play?", "answer": "right fielder", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where does Jamell Anderson play when he is playing a home game?", "answer": "Ellesmere Port Sports Village", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What type of engine was used in the planes used in the raid led by Colonel James \u201cJimmy\u201d Doolittle?", "answer": "liquid-cooled inline V engine", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the world\u2019s first-ever pilsner type blond lager, the company also awarded the Master Homebrewer Competition held in San Francisco to an award-winning brewer who won the prestigious American Homebrewers Associations' Homebrewer of the Year award in 2013?", "answer": "Pilsner Urquell", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Half Japanese and Balance and Composure, work in the music industry?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Ikemefula Charles \"Ike\" Ibeabuchi defeated a boxer who is a two-time what?", "answer": "world heavyweight champion", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Henry Cabot Lodge Bohler (June 8, 1925 \u2013 August 10, 2007) was a member of the prestigious Tuskegee Airmen during World War II who would later aid the advancement of civil rights for African-Americans living in the rural Southern United States, Tuskegee Airmen formed the 332nd Fighter Group and the 477th Bombardment Group of the ?", "answer": "United States Army Air Forces", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is a road named after the author of February Dragon located?", "answer": "South Australia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Now That's What I Call Music! 58 includes a track that was the debut single for what English singer-songwriter?", "answer": "Zayn", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Still Got Time\", is a song by which British singer and songwriter, and rapper PartyNextDoor?", "answer": "Zayn", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Baoding and Lengshuijiang in the same province in China?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What award-winning journalist did Phyllis Coates play?", "answer": "Lois Lane", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Frankie Valli was in what band with former Royal Teens keyboard and tenor vocalist?", "answer": "Four Seasons", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Passaconaway was sachem of people who primarily inhabited what two present-day states", "answer": "New Hampshire and Massachusetts", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Does Vasek Pospisil have a higher tennis World singles ranking than Michael Stich?  ", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Timothy Carhart starred in the 1992 revival of which Tennessee Williams play?", "answer": "A Streetcar Named Desire", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which former American football player was the starting quarterback for the Cornhuskers in 1997 and now serves as the current head coach of UCF Knight football?", "answer": "Scott Frost", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was the coach of the 1996 Dallas Cowboys team a college coach?", "answer": "University of Oklahoma", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who directed this 2016 American romantic comoedy-drama film starring an American actor, comedian, writer, and producer, best known for his rold as Rodney Ruxx in \"The League\"?", "answer": "Sophie Goodhart", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which country contains both Guangyuan and Xiaoshan District?", "answer": "China", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What English fantasy author born 6 September 1972  wrote the new introduction to The House on the Borderland and Other Novels.", "answer": "China Mi\u00e9ville", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What upcoming American superhero film will be directed by Zack Syder and will feature an appearance of Wonder Woman?", "answer": "Justice League", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Denis Stanley Tomlinson (4 September 1910 \u2013 11 July 1993) was a South Afri