n": "Martellus and Michael Bennett have played for several teams, but what team have they both played for in the past?", "answer": "Texas A&M", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many stores does the sponsor of 7 Eleven Roadbike Phillipines operate?", "answer": "56,600", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A airline headquartered in Wilmington Air Park does what for Amazon Prime Air?", "answer": "contracts through", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "G-Man was published by the company founded in what year?", "answer": "1992", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which dog breed nearly went extinct in the 20th century, the Sloughi or the Saint-Usuge Spaniel?", "answer": "The Saint-Usuge Spaniel", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Was is the premier date of an Indian animated sitcom television series airing on Nickelodeon and Vasantham based on a comic strip published in Lot Pot produced by the founder and CEO of The Art Studio company.", "answer": "16 October 2012", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which national park is situated in the Pyrenees of Huesca province, Aragon, Spain, Ordesa y Monte Perdido National Park or Caldera de Taburiente National Park? ", "answer": "Ordesa y Monte Perdido National Park", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In what year did the singer who starred in the Broadway musical \"Golden Rainbow\" with Steve Lawrence retire?", "answer": "2009", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Camp Winnarainbow, is a circus and performing arts camp, it adjoins which organization, considered to be America's longest running hippie commune, near Laytonville, California?", "answer": "Hog Farm", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which university is located in the city of Ames, Ural Federal University or Iowa State University?", "answer": "Iowa State University", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who is  a Japanese composer, musician, and sound producer known primarily for his work in video games, among other media who composed a 2005 album  based on \"The Five Seasons of Kirite\"?", "answer": "Yasunori Mitsuda", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The group that were the singing voices of the Be Sharps on The Simpson's episode \"Homer's Barbershop Quartet\" have performed at Walt Disney World since what year?", "answer": "1971", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "David Wayne Hull is a leader of a group that originated in what state?", "answer": "Mississippi", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were Larry Baker and Lionel Trilling from the same country?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "How many number one singles as a solo artist does Mark Bryan's former band mate have?", "answer": "seven number-one singles", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which train company has a train that for most of its history has run between New Orleans and Los Angeles, over the nation's second transcontinental route?", "answer": "Amtrak", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year was the man, who founded Moore Capital Management, born?", "answer": "1956", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Is it true that both Cycads and Carpentarias are both plants that grow in different regions?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Luis Llosa and John Ince shared what job?", "answer": "film director", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What bowl game featured a team coached by Mike Leach in 2012?", "answer": "Meineke Car Care Bowl of Texas", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What company formed in 1978 has Simon Arora as its CEO?", "answer": "B & M", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Campanula and Caesalpinia part of the same family?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What sport did both Goran Ivani\u0161evi\u0107 and Thomas Muster play?", "answer": "tennis", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Belle and Sebastian and White Magic, are related to music?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Joker's Daughter was originally a musical collaboration between Greek-English singer/songwriter Helena Costas and producer Danger Mouse, Brian Joseph Burton, better known by his stage name Danger Mouse, is an American musician, songwriter and record producer,born on which date ?", "answer": "July 29, 1977", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Dreams to Dream\" is a song from the 1991 animated feature film An American Tail: Fievel Goes West, based on a short instrumental piece from its prequel \"An American Tail\", released in which year, an American animated musical adventure family comedy-drama film directed by Don Bluth?", "answer": "1986", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which breed of dog has a longer history competing in shows, Gos Rater Valenci\u00e0 or Briard", "answer": "Briard", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What two countries supported the project that Louis Slotin died working on?", "answer": "the United Kingdom and Canada", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Live: In Paradise is a live concert DVD by a musical duo who describe their style as what?", "answer": "Brechtian punk cabaret", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the director of the 1998 comedy film on which the 2016 Romanian comedy film, directed by Paul Negoescu, is loosely based?", "answer": "Kirk Jones", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What prize was won by the the scientist who identified the Hodgkin cycle ? ", "answer": "1963 Nobel Prize", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Faith Goldy was fired for an interview she gave to which neo-Nazi news site?", "answer": "The Daily Stormer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was the husband of the woman who had a biography written by Erika Rosenberg?", "answer": "Oskar Schindler", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which is farther west, Negus Mine or Temagami-Lorrain Mine?", "answer": "Negus Mine", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the name of this American actress born in February 1989, who starred in I Saw the Light with Hank Williams?", "answer": "Elizabeth Olsen", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of the Florida Institute of Technology and University of Waterloo has the larger main campus?", "answer": "University of Waterloo", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Australian Liberty Alliance launched in 2015 with the anti-Islam activist who is director of which organization as a keynote speaker?", "answer": "Sharia Watch UK", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Lesley Barber composed music for an animated television series that is of what nationality?", "answer": "Canadian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is a French filmmaker known for the Holocaust documentary film \"Shoah\", Claude Lanzmann or Shane Meadows?", "answer": "Claude Lanzmann", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What year did the man who replaced Robert Flores on \"SportsCenter\" first become an anchor?", "answer": "1996", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Tonya Suzanne Holly and Ivan Passer, are both a type of director?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Where is the district known as Wah Fu located at?", "answer": "Hong Kong", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Exotica, the first album by Martin Denny was recorded in a studio located in an area most famous for what?", "answer": "Waik\u012bk\u012b Beach", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which one of The Wreckers singers also sang the song \"A Women Needs\"?", "answer": "Jessica Harp", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Both written by George Harrison \"Bangla Desh\" and \"Deep Blue\" were songs intended to raise awareness for what?", "answer": "millions of refugees", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who published the Journey Into Mystery comic in 1960s and the 90s and 2010s?", "answer": "Marvel Comics", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What profession do Claude Lelouch and Danny Leiner have in common?", "answer": "film director", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What tournament did Giovanni Van Bronckhorst lead Feyenoord to in his third season as manager?", "answer": "KNVB Cup", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Marietta, Georgia, the county seat located in Cobb County, Georgia is home to what live hip-hop band that signed with Purple Ribbon Records in 2008?", "answer": "Vonnegutt", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Along side the territorial governor from Virginia, what was the name of the other leaders of the Corps of Discovery?", "answer": "Captain Meriwether Lewis", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both Jean-Luc Godard and Alan Mak Siu-fai from Hong Kong?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "For which film did the actress, who recorded the song Coming Home, receive the Best Actress Academy Award ?", "answer": "Shakespeare in Love\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When did the American singer-songwriter, best known as a solo performer release her debut album?", "answer": "2002", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Montana Meth Project was founded by which businessman born November 20, 1952?", "answer": "Thomas Siebel", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "KTMS (990 AM, \"News Talk AM 990\") is a news/talk radio station based in Santa Barbara, California, and is owned by Rincon Broadcasting LS LLC, it airs talk shows such as who, an American talk show host, author, and conservative political commentator?", "answer": "Sean Patrick Hannity", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The country music artist who released Radio Lover was given what nickname based o the shape of his nose?", "answer": "\"The Possum.\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 1994 Miami Dolphins season, was the franchise's 29th season in the National Football League, on March 23, the NFL approved the transfer of majority interest in the club from the Robbie family to Wayne Huizenga, an American businessman and entrepreneur, and is responsible for six listed companies, of which organization?", "answer": "New York Stock Exchange", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Turner Broadcasting System, Inc., is an American media conglomerate that is a division of Time Warner and manages the collection of cable television networks and properties initiated or acquired by Ted Turner, the original home of Turner's WTBS superstation (now separated into its TBS cable network and Peachtree TV), which today houses the headquarters of what and Williams Street Productions?", "answer": "Adult Swim", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The illustrator of \"Report from Practically Nowhere\" has received how many Grammy Awards?", "answer": "two", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which ocean connects to the Delaware River, a river which has US route 13 running parallel to it before it reaches Claymont?", "answer": "Atlantic", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who were Freedom Riders from Freedom Highways campaign?", "answer": "civil rights activists", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Arrow Rock area was where the historic Santa Fe Trail crossed which longest river in North America?", "answer": "Missouri River", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The winner of the 16th Lumieres Awards tells the tale of nine what?", "answer": "Trappist monks", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What's the name for early electronic hip-hop and music based around Roland drum machines and new wave 1980s sounds?", "answer": "electro", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The wife of Sargent Shriver was the founder of what?", "answer": "Special Olympics", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Bingham was named after the politician who served from what state?", "answer": "Connecticut", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the town in which Berghof is Located in?", "answer": "the \u00d6tztal valley of Tyrol", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "are both movie Celsius 41.11 and The Memory of Justice documentaries ?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who wrote a book named after the demographic cohort following the Lost Generation?", "answer": "Tom Brokaw", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Wealth Partaking Scheme a cash disbursement policy to holders of a card with what acronym?", "answer": "BIR", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Musicians Ara Babajian and Elijah Blue Allman are both what nationallity?", "answer": "American", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Toni Lopopolo is a literary agent whose book publishing career began in 1970 in the publicity department of Bantam Books, where she helped publicize authors such as which English author of romance novels, one of the best-selling authors as well as one of the most prolific and commercially successful worldwide of the twentieth century, with her 723 novels were translated into 38 languages and she continues to be referenced in the \"Guinness World Records\" for the most novels published in a single year in 1976?", "answer": "Barbara Cartland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What role did Jensen Ackles play in the American fantasy horror television series created by Eric Kripke?", "answer": "Dean Winchester", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year was the singer who released the solo album Victim of Romance born?", "answer": "1944", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Brassolaeliocattleya and Codonopsis both hybrids?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which of the creators of Ferb Fletcher was born born December 9, 1960?", "answer": "Jeff \"Swampy\" Marsh", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which terrorist deliberately crashed the plane into the World Trade Center, the photo of which was taken by the freelance photographer Thomas Dallal and named Impending Death?", "answer": "Mohamed Atta", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both Papa Murphy's and Frank Pepe Pizzeria Napoletana in the United States?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who is the founder of the publisher which published Conspiricy X?", "answer": "George Vasilakos", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Rick Heinrichs performed design work on the stop-motion dark fantasy film directed by whom?", "answer": "Henry Selick", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what city did the team that won premierships in both 1992 and 1994 lose in the Grand Final to Hawthorn for the first time?", "answer": "Melbourne", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Maryland's biggest employer is named after a general from which war?", "answer": "U.S. Civil War", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "2017\u201318 Everton F.C. and the 2017\u201318 Premier League both compete in what sport?", "answer": "English football", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Roland West and Debarun Pal are both known for what profession in the film industry?", "answer": "director", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Hexagon Barn is located in the town in which Maine county?", "answer": "Penobscot", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Charles \"Chuck\" Strahl, PC, is a Canadian businessman and politician, first elected for the Reform Party, he was the leader of the Democratic Representative Caucus that left the Canadian Alliance in opposition to leadership of which former Canadian politician, and a member of the Conservative Party of Canada?", "answer": "Stockwell Day", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Paralympic weightlifter Mario Hochberg was born in a socialist state located where?", "answer": "Central Europe", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Mihal Ashminov is currently in the cast of which South Korean cooking program?", "answer": "Please Take Care of My Refrigerator", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "P. Vijay won the National Film Award for Best Lyrics in India for a song performed by who?", "answer": "K. S. Chithra", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What air craft ended production in 1992 and was derived from the same aircraft as the Boeing C-137 Stratoliner?", "answer": "Boeing E-3 Sentry", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who did an actress in That Touch of Mink play on The Honeymooners?", "answer": "Alice Kramden", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Finnish writer was very influential between 1918 and 1939?", "answer": "Olavi Paavolainen", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who coaches the team Lexi Davis' team lost to in the 2016