n 1929?", "answer": "Nobel Peace Prize", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which songwriter, Daniel Gildenl\u00f6w or Wendy James, most notable for work with the pop band Transvision Vamp?", "answer": "Wendy James", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who was an American singer, Bob Dylan or Philip Pullman?", "answer": "Bob Dylan", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What company did the executive who was onboard the September 11th flight to San Francisco work public relations for?", "answer": "Bingham Group", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Noir D\u00e9sir and Balance and Composure are both what?", "answer": "rock band", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Wharfdale is a bounded rural locality, and cadastral parish south of a town situated on the Bogan River between Narromine and what other town?", "answer": "Bourke", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which song by Jon Secada and Shanice was featured on Disney's 33rd animated feature film?", "answer": "\"If I Never Knew You\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What genre is the film in which Tabitha Wady portrays Gemma?", "answer": "teen comedy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Last Mimzy features the actor and comedian of what nationality?", "answer": "American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who created the show that influenced the one which Samanta Tina participated in?", "answer": "John de Mol", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where was both E-40 and Celly Cel from?", "answer": "California", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "John M. Dwyer was nominated for an Academy Award for his work in a film directed by whom?", "answer": "Michael Apted", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was married to the woman known as Jackie O until his assassination in 1963?", "answer": "John F. Kennedy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of this census-designated place with a population of over 25,000, that is the home of the WFTU college radio station?", "answer": "Dix Hills, New York", "type": "bridge"}, 