embly meets?", "answer": "between 1886 and 1894", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Does Egeria or Anigozanthos have more species?", "answer": "Anigozanthos", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which of these Manhattan skyscrapers faces Madison Square Park, The Metropolitan Life Insurance Company Tower or Trump Tower?", "answer": "The Metropolitan Life Insurance Company Tower", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Tim Erixon is a Swedish professional ice hockey defenseman who was selected in the first round of an Entry Draft, which was held on June 26-27, 2009, at what location in Montreal?", "answer": "Bell Centre", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What film did Gong Ji-chul that took place at the Gwangju Inhwa School for the hearing-impaired?", "answer": "The Crucible", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the profession of Neill Blomkamp and Edward Laemmle?", "answer": "film director", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "How many cast and crew members are there for stage production at the Wynn Las Vegas casino resort created by the director of the Cirque du Soleil show that was first performed on December 25, 1993?", "answer": "250", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which actress in Tremor 3: Back to Perfection played was in \"Jurassic Park\"?", "answer": "Ariana Richards", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "On what date was the cosmonaut born that is believed to have landed off-course and been held by the Chinese government?", "answer": "March 31, 1927", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which sport in which Mira Rai consists of running and hiking over trails?", "answer": "Trail running", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which station is located directly below the arena that hosted the 2011 Royal Rumble?", "answer": "MBTA's North Station", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Pingquan and Fenyang, are in which country?", "answer": "China", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the home ground of the team for  which Alfred Chalkley played ?", "answer": "London Stadium", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "R U Professional was a satirical song that partly referenced the 2008 superhero film directed by whom?", "answer": "Christopher Nolan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Republican National Committee is currently led by which former chairwoman of the Michigan Republican Party?", "answer": "Ronna Romney McDaniel", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which HBO series does Chris Coy star in that is set in and around Times Square?", "answer": "The Deuce", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Island Days is a spin-off of an adult game released for Windows on what date?", "answer": "April 28, 2005", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Calhoun Depot  was part of the military raid that took place during which event?", "answer": "American Civil War", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What actor best known for his roles as Peter Waters in \"Crash\" and as O-Dog in the 1993 hood film, \"Menace II Society\", was in a movie based on David Brin's 1985 book?", "answer": "The Postman", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Between WALL-E and The Straight Story, which film was released earlier?", "answer": "The Straight Story", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which plant has more species, Dudleya or Myrsine?", "answer": "Myrsine", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which documentary was produced by more people, Great Old Amusement Parks or The Devil Came on Horseback?", "answer": "The Devil Came on Horseback", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which animator from Canada served as an assistant director on an American animated television series that ran on The WB from September 24, 1999, to July 16, 2000, and on Adult Swim from July 14 to August 11, 2002?", "answer": "Lindsey Pollard", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "David Levien also wrote what film about two friends who earn cash by playing poker?  ", "answer": "Rounders", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born first, Naguib Mahfouz or Ilya Ehrenburg?", "answer": "Ilya Grigorye