o directed the film based on the same person's novel \"Legion\"?", "answer": "William Peter Blatty", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "CKY-DT, VHF channel 7, is a CTV owned-and-operated television station located in Winnipeg, Manitoba, CKY's studios are located on Graham Avenue, adjacent to which was an indoor arena in downtown Winnipeg, Manitoba?", "answer": "Bell MTS Place", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which genus includes more species of flowering plants, Damasonium or Selinum?", "answer": "Damasonium", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who was the winner of the fifth season of the tv baking competition, produced by Love Productions, The Great British Bake off?", "answer": "Nancy Birtwhistle", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Tetracentron and Limnocharis both genuses?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In between  Xinji and Shanghai which one is located in the Yangtze River Delta?", "answer": "Shanghai", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which Champions League Final was played on 22 May 2010 ", "answer": "2010 UEFA Champions League Final", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Pirro Vaso was one of the architects of the structure located in which country?", "answer": "Albania", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which is involved with punk music, Tyson Ritter or Takida?", "answer": "Tyson Jay Ritter", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Polar Golfer is a PC based video game released by WildTangent in which year, it is sometimes bundled with Dell computers, a multinational computer technology company based in Round Rock, Texas?", "answer": "2004", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which animated short film created by Patrick McHale was Over the Garden Wall based on ", "answer": "Tome of the Unknown", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the nationality of The Strictly's choreographer?", "answer": "Australian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 2014 World RX of Argentina  was held at the autodrome in the state that is in what part of Argentina", "answer": "central-west", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "It's Always Sunny in Philadelphia stars which actress who began her career as part of the Groundlings?", "answer": "Kaitlin Willow Olson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the name of the international company set up in 1977 by English composer and impresario of musical theatre whose well-known works include \"The Phantom of the Opera\" and \"Jesus Christ Superstar\"? ", "answer": "Really Useful Group", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What sporting goods and entertainment chain store is headquartered in Fargo, North Dakota and has a store located in the Crossroads Center in St. Cloud, Minnesota?", "answer": "Scheels All Sports", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the Dutch artist who created Metamorphosis II born?", "answer": "17 June 1898", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is the father of the composer of Usher House?", "answer": "J. Paul Getty", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "which former Major League Baseball outfielder was part of those who set a record for most Jewish players on a team at once since the expansion era.", "answer": "Gabriel Stefan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year did Henry I of Castile's grandather sign a peace treaty guaranteeing his successorship to the throne of England?", "answer": "1153", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Is the Peony or the Phygelius native on more continents?", "answer": "The peony", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What was a type of sweet bun found in communities where German dialects together make up the second most spoken first language in Brazil after Portuguese?", "answer": "Schnecken", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was Una Foden confirmed as a judge for the 4th series of \"The Voice of Ireland\"?", "answer": "October 2014", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "19th-century Norwegian violinist Ole Bull was compared to which celebrated Italian virtuoso of the time?", "answer": "Niccol\u00f2 Paganini",