er, singer, and activist born in 1955?", "answer": "\"Cheers\" and \"Frasier\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the club which Johnny M\u00f8lby was most recently the manager of founded?", "answer": "1896", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which artist released an album that made frequent use of a phrase which refers to an old-school subculture of Chincanos & Mexican-Americans associated with zoot suits and flamboyant public behavior?", "answer": "Tom Waits", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were both Joseph Epstein and Mary Renault writers?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Pierre Victor held what rank in the french branch of the Swiss Guards?", "answer": "the last commander", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "which American artist sings \"Nobody's perfect\"?", "answer": "Miley Cyrus", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What album featured the song Innervision by the band featuring Shavo Odadjian on bass?", "answer": "Steal This Album!", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Haydn Bunton Jr. played for what Australian rules football club currently affiliated with the South Australian National Football League (SANFL)?", "answer": "North Adelaide Football Club", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who developed one of the foundations of functional analysis and also taught Hugo Steinhaus?", "answer": "David Hilbert", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which river lies next to the town where Sidney Adams was born in 1904?", "answer": "Nene", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which period in German history came to an end thanks in part to material aid supplied to the Soviet Union by an Arctic convoy?", "answer": "Nazi Germany", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many miles north of Columbus, Mississippi is the base where the 736th Bombardment Squadron was stationed?", "answer": "9", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what county of Massachusetts was Robert V. Bruce born?", "answer": "Middlesex County, Massachusetts", "type": "bridge"}, {"question":