n war drama based on whose 1992 book?", "answer": "Stephen E. Ambrose", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the song originally written to be that is Rod Stewart's most recent top five solo hit?", "answer": "prayer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Black Mountain Side was reviewed as being similar to the John Carpenter film released in what year?", "answer": "1982", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What High Church movement of the Church of England was Edward Hawkins the Provost of Oriel College a committed opponent of from its beginning?", "answer": "Oxford Movement", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In which country did Marek Cholewa first play hockey in the Winter Olympics?", "answer": "Bosnia and Herzegovina", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who did Sam Massell lose to in the Atlanta mayoral election of 1973?", "answer": "Maynard Jackson", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What University of Oklahoma football coach, whom announced his retirement on June 7, 2017, represented the University of Oklahoma in the 2000 NCAA Division I-A football season?", "answer": "Bob Stoops", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What book is the movie that George Clooney win a Golden Globe for producing  adapted from?", "answer": "\"The Master of Disguise\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Finishing the Hat: Collected Lyrics is a book that contains lyrics from a song that was \"freely adpted\" from an ancient greek comedy by who?", "answer": "Aristophanes", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is the university that Anthony M. Esolen previously taught at located?", "answer": "Greenville, South Carolina", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "WHat is the name of this 1993 book by Michael A. Cremo and Richard L. Thompson, in which Cremo argued for the existence of modern man on Earth as long as 30 to 40 million years ago?", "answer": "Forbidden Archeology", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Red Book is an unauthorized edition of the role playing game that was first published in what 