ent ?", "answer": "Iconix Brand Group", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year did the mall near Daniel McLaughlin Therrell highschool open?", "answer": "1965", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Paul Freeman is a hunter of a creature known by what Halkomelem word?", "answer": "\"s\u00e1sq'ets\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "If Thomas Mitchener produced Frank Carter & The Rattlesnakes second studio album, what year would Catherine Marks had to have worked with the band?", "answer": "2015", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is the company headquarters of the airline whose call sign was named after a former U.S. Air Mail pilot?", "answer": "Bridgeton, Missouri", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which actress from the film \"The Postman Always Rings Twice\" became the twenty-second thespian in history to achieve the Triple Crown of Acting?", "answer": "Jessica Lange", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Bethesda Game Studios has studios in which two cities?", "answer": "Montreal, Quebec", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which film depicted patient-inmates of Bridgewater State Hospital, Titicut Follies or The True Glory?", "answer": "Titicut Follies", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Coca-Cola Tigers was founded by the company that was originally intended to do what?", "answer": "patent medicine", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The actor that playes Han Solo in the \"Star Wars\" film series stars with Blake Lively and Michiel Huisman in a film directed by who?", "answer": "Lee Toland Krieger", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In regards to the Lithuanian-born French actor who died on July 3, 2015, what was the film that he starred in in 1966?", "answer": "Balearic Caper", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Tami Steinmetz Center For Peace Research surveys public opinion regarding what conflict that transformed into war in May 1948?", "answer": "Arab\u2013Israeli conflict", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "A Vampire Diaries star received an award for 