at single by an Australian rock band formed in Melbourne in 1983, was performed by American heavy metal band Metallica on their 1998 cover album \"Garage Inc.\"?", "answer": "\"Loverman\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Edgar Wingard was a coach at the private university in what Indiana city?", "answer": "Indianapolis", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "David Charles Hodge earned his bachelor's degree from a college located in what state?", "answer": "Minnesota", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Secret in Their Eyes co-starred the American actor best known for what role on \"House of Cards\"?", "answer": "Doug Stamper", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What dates did the Winter Games that the country that hosted the summers games in 1986 and 2002 hosted occur?", "answer": "January 30 to February 6, 1999", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "WHAT IS A 1997 AUSTRALIAN COMEDY AND A 1997'S LOW BUDGET HIT FILM?", "answer": "The Castle", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What other  movie  did Ezra Miller star in,  in 2015.", "answer": "the comedy \"Trainwreck", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Carry That Weight is part of the medley that is preceded by which song on Abbey Road?", "answer": "Golden Slumbers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Nobel Biocare is stationed next to an airport known as Kloten Airport, what is the airport?", "answer": "Z\u00fcrich Airport", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Back in Business is a 1997 action thriller film starring a former professional football player that was a linebacker for what NFL team?", "answer": "Seattle Seahawks", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "the Poseidon Adventure, starring Jack Albertson, was produced by who?", "answer": "Irwin Allen", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was Pete Mounts son who played basketball on the American Basketball Association born?", "answer": "January 5, 1947", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where in Texas is the company that has a Achievement Hunter as a division located?", "answer": "Aus