erican actor, voice actor, comedian, screenwriter and graphic artist, that moved to the United States in 1958?", "answer": "Phil Hartman", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was born first Henri Kontinen or Richard Gasquet?", "answer": "Richard Gasquet", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who became involved with a cattle and racehorse \"Just A Dash\" to win Australia's most prestigious annual Thoroughbred horse race?", "answer": "Neale John Lavis", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The American author of several books on politics, religion, and culture, wrote the speech, including the phrase, \"Read my lips: no new taxes\" given by what then-American presidential candidate?", "answer": "George H. W. Bush", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which event was won by Clarisse Rasoarizay, in the 8th All Africa Games in Nigeria, for which the newly constructed Abuja Stadium was built; the contestant being a female long distance runner from Madagascar?", "answer": "women's marathon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year was the online newsletter that introduced the Cook Partisan Voting Index founded?", "answer": "1984", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Oranges Are Not The Only Fruit\"  was written by an award winning writer who also wrote a novel about human relationships and physics in what year?", "answer": "1997", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What character was voiced by Lou Romano in the 2006 comedy film produced by Pixar Animation Studios?", "answer": "Snot Rod", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the first South Australian newspaper, who's competition claimed  to be non-religious the \"Adelaide Morning Chronicle\" was established by the draper Andrew Murray during the South Australian Parliament's debate over separation of church and state?", "answer": "The Register", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The horror short story The Raft by Stephen King was also included in what popular skin magazine?", "answer": "Gallery", "type": "bridge"}, {"questio