s notorious for what ?", "answer": "flash flooding", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Beatles album contained the song that was covered in 1976 by Wil Malone and Lou Reizner?", "answer": "Abbey Road", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Red Velvet is a play about the only actor of African-American descent among the 33 actors of the English stage honored with bronze plaques at what theatre?", "answer": "Shakespeare Memorial Theatre", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Julian Edwin Adderley released what record in 1960?", "answer": "Them Dirty Blues", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which component of the Parliment of Canada represented the electoral district, Fredericton, since the year 1988?", "answer": "House of Commons of Canada", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Australian suburban railway network had the song \"Dumb Ways to Die\" composed for them? ", "answer": "Metro Trains Melbourne", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What German sport club based in Hamburg is associated with Ole Bj\u00f8rnmose?", "answer": "Hamburger SV", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who released the 2015 animated short film which is a inspiration Frozen Ever After in Epcot at the Walt Disney World Resort?", "answer": "Walt Disney Pictures", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What city did Al Capone and Edward J. O'Hare both work in?", "answer": "Chicago", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year did the book come out that the film Dev Patel and Jeremy Irons starred in?", "answer": "1991", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How long is the festival wher Mark Trenwith starred in comedy show \"Give Us A Hug\" ", "answer": "31 days and nights", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Stephen Hale reports for which channel headquartered in Atlanta, Georgia?", "answer": "The Weather Channel", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which of the two was of a French background, Louis Jouvet or Stanley Donen?", "answer": "Louis Jouvet", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What was a secret program of the 