rsity at Albany in NCAA Division I men's college lacrosse?", "answer": "head coach", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Miami Springs was founded by an American aviation pioneer who began his career as a bicycle racer and builder before moving on to what?", "answer": "motorcycles", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the granter of the charter of Bradford Grammar School born?", "answer": "1630", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who launched the magazine whose founding editor was Russ Jones?", "answer": "Warren Publishing", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the nationality of the player that has a style similar to that of the captain of the Real Madrid team?", "answer": "Finnish", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Pabst Brewing Company is the holding company for the defunct Pacific Northwest company that was based in what city?", "answer": "Seattle, Washington", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "New Orleans Square was a part of a larger area known as Holidayland,which was located along the western edge of what amusement park?", "answer": "Disneyland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Between Gillo Pontecorvo and Jan \u0160vankmajer, who has more diverse job experience?", "answer": "Jan \u0160vankmajer", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Who directed the 1988 film Bill Murray was in?", "answer": "Richard Donner", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Lyric Suite is a six-movement work usig methods derived from the twelve-tone technique of what Austrian composer, music theorist, and painter who was associated with the expressionist movement?", "answer": "Arnold Franz Walter Schoenberg", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Metropolitan Opera, often called The Met, has had which general manager since August of 2006?", "answer": "Peter Gelb", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was where the two legs of 1933 Mitropa Cup was played built ?", "answer": "between 1929 and 1931", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Sir William Borthwick was master of the king's