": "Miranda Garrison", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Mehrdad Raissi Ardali was a voice actor along with who in the Bee Movie?", "answer": "Jerry Seinfeld", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Clay is a 2008 Hip-hop musical loosely based on Shakespeare's \"Henry IV, Parts 1 and 2\", the central character, Sir John, is based on Falstaff, a fictional character who is mentioned in five plays by who?", "answer": "William Shakespeare", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is a home computer made by Commodore International with a 6502-compatible 7501 or 8501 CPU,  VideoBrain Family Computer or Commodore 16 ?", "answer": "Commodore 16", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The 1992\u201393 NBA season was the Bullets' 32nd season in the National Basketball Association, following the season, which now retired American National Basketball Association basketball player, is the identical twin brother of Horace Grant?", "answer": "Harvey Grant", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which trademarked logo, owned by the New York State Department of Economic Development, was designed by Milton Glaser?", "answer": "I Love New York", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who has written songs for Disney with his wife, as well as composed music for the \"Kick-Ass\" franchise on his own?", "answer": "Henry Jackman", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What was the name of the debut album from the music project of New England native Merrill Garbus?", "answer": "Bird-Brains", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What nationality is the author of the 2015 work Lafayette in the Somewhat United States ?", "answer": "American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who did the injured quarterback of the 2004 Bears season play football for in college?", "answer": "University of Florida", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"Young Girls\" is a song by American singer-songwriter Bruno Mars, it's reminiscent of the individual known professionally, Lana Del Rey's work, the American singer, songwriter, and model, Elizab