 the group of competitive sporting events which primarily involve the use of motorised vehicles, whether for racing or non-racing competition?", "answer": "motorsports", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Witches of Eastwick, based on john Updike's novel, was Directed by which director.?", "answer": "George Miller", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Riga International serves as a base airport for a Hungarian airline whose head office is in what city?", "answer": "Budapest", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Alberta Coal Branch is the name given to a segment of the Canadian National Railway, a Canadian Class I freight railway headquartered in Montreal, Quebec that serves Canada and the Midwestern and Southern United States, having been a Canadian Crown corporation from its founding to its privatization in which year?", "answer": "1995", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which store located at 712 Fifth Avenue did Ellen Steward work at as a fashion designer in the 1950s?", "answer": "Henri Bendel", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What actor who starred in the \"Back to the Future\" trilogy, where he portrayed Marty McFly., hosted an awards show where two networks, A&E and AMC, received their first major nominations that year?", "answer": "Michael Andrew Fox", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The commander of the Totskoye nuclear exercise also command what battle that resulted in the deafeat of Nazi Germany?", "answer": "Battle of Berlin", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what city did Mayumi Raheem win 3 gold medals?", "answer": "Colombo, Sri Lanka", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " Josine Blok has been a professor of Ancient History and Classical Civilisation at what university that is also one of the oldest in the Netherlands", "answer": "Utrecht University", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which band was formed first, Drowners or Pulp?", "answer": "Pulp", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What 1960 film was made by someone blacklisted in the McCarthy era?", "answer": "Never on Sunday", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Yanzhou District and Yizheng, are in which country?", "answer": "People's Republic of China", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which has more species, Phormium or Callicoma?", "answer": "Phormium", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Alan Douglas Ruck, is an American actor, he played Cameron Frye, Bueller's hypochondriac best friend in John Hughes' \"Ferris Bueller's Day Off\", released in which year?", "answer": "1986", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the former American football flanker in the NFL for the Minnesota Vikings born for whom Tucker was traded along with Billy Truax to the Dallas Cowboys?", "answer": "October 14, 1943", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In 2010, Alfred Molina starred alongside Nicolas Cage in an American fantasy film directed by who?", "answer": "Jon Turteltaub", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year did the ferry service for which Corporation Pier station served as a ticket office and waiting room stop operating?", "answer": "1981", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are John Musker and Jason Reitman both directors?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What was the album that produced the single which broke the record for the most weeks spent at number one by a female country artist ?", "answer": "Red", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which film director is older, Jan Troell or Agn\u00e8s Varda?", "answer": "Agn\u00e8s Varda", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "From which country hails the film director, who co-wrote 'Welcome to Dongmakgol' the 2005 critical and commercial hit?", "answer": "South Korea", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which band has more people in it, The Nearly Deads or Spoon?", "answer": "The Nearly Deads", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Moving Day is a 1936 American animated short film produced by Walt Disney Productions and released by United Artists, film was directed by Ben Sharpsteen, includes the