eorgia, United States, and was appropriated by Martha Berry as a Sunday school in 1900. the school grew to become which private, four-year liberal arts college with a Christian emphasis located in Mount Berry, Floyd County, Georgia, United States, just north of Rome?", "answer": "Berry College", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which person Derek Pearsall wrote about was also known as \"the Father of English literature\"?", "answer": "Geoffrey Chaucer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What author of several best-selling books also wrote The Scarlet Slippers?", "answer": "Philip Pullman", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What 1938 Robert Sinclair film starred the first actor to win more than one Academy award?", "answer": "Dramatic School", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Zenobia and Hippocrepis both types of shrubs?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What major airline of the People's Republic of China owns Shandong Airlines?", "answer": "Air China", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which cast member of \"Flying Down to Rio\" was born on July 16, 1911?", "answer": "Ginger Rogers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what language is the text that states that Adi Parashakti is the original creator?", "answer": "Sanskrit", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Laika Entertainment, LLC produced a 2016 film through its Focus Features label, directed by whom?", "answer": "Travis Knight", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Bryant Reeves (born June 8, 1973) is an American retired professional basketball player, Reeves spent his entire career with the NBA's Vancouver Grizzlies, were a Canadian professional basketball team based in Vancouver, in which Canadian province?", "answer": "British Columbia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Glenn Tilbrook and Kyo both musicians ?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In between Jason Kartalian and Fernando Arrabal who describes himself as \"desterrado\"?", "answer": "Fernando Arrabal Ter\u00