": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Onew and Jimi Jamison from the same country?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What was the name of the poem that came out in 1913 by the person who was buried in France but honored by a centaph in the Elmwood Cemetery? ", "answer": "Trees", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Mound is a city in Hennepin County, Minnesota, Mound is the birthplace of which truck, named after Lake Minnetonka, an American producer of toy trucks?", "answer": "Tonka", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In between Volcano Suns and Kongos which one is consisting of four brothers?", "answer": "Kongos", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is a genus of woody vines in the Schisandraceae described as a genus in 1810, Petrophile or Kadsura ?", "answer": "Kadsura", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Gema Simon (born 19 July 1990) is an Australian international football (soccer) player who plays for the Newcastle Jets FC, also known as the Newcastle Jets Women, is an Australian football (soccer) team, founded in which year?", "answer": "2008", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Family Guy: Live in Vegas is a soundtrack album for the American animated television series \"Family Guy\", it  features vocals from which American actress, writer, producer, and comedian?", "answer": "Alexandrea \"Alex\" Borstein", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the largest city in Macomb County and was the headquarters of American Specialty Cars?", "answer": "Warren, Michigan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which was tried first: Goodridge v. Department of Public Health or Dred Scott v. Sandford?", "answer": "Dred Scott v. Sandford", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Ken Loach and Edward F. Cline, are English?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Richard F. W. Davis worked with a Canadian American alternative rock singer, who released what album in 1995?", "answer": "Jagged Little Pill", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What kind of dance did Sneha Kapoor do that comes from the Dominican Republic?", "answer": "Bachata", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What band is widely credited as one of the pioneers of visual kei, and released a compilation box set containing two CDs, a VHS tape and a T-shirt from the \"Violence and Jealousy Tour\"?", "answer": "X Japan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Chicago Shakespeare Theater's permanent home is located on the shore of what lake?", "answer": "Lake Michigan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "101 Park Avenue and 55 Water Street, are located in which state?", "answer": "New York", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which rail network that was established in 2007 and serves a large part of Greater London also manages and serves Kensington?", "answer": "London Overground", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Alan Whitehead is a British musician and businessman whose most successful single in the UK was a cover version of what Paul McCartney song?", "answer": "Ob-La-Di, Ob-La-Da", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": " The 12th Annual Honda Civic Tour was a concert tour headlined by an American pop rock band that originated in what city?", "answer": "Los Angeles", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which South African record producer produced the song Ngud by South African rapper Kwesta?", "answer": "DJ Maphorisa", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What celebrity wears Tieks and stars in \"Mrs. Eastwood & Company\"?", "answer": "Francesca Eastwood", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where were the Olympics where Kevin Romy represented Switzerland?", "answer": "Sochi, Krasnodar Krai, Russia", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Simon Property Group manages what mall in a town known for witch trials in 1692?", "answer": "Liberty Tree Mall", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The fictional character in J. K. Rowling's \"Harry Potter\" series Severus Snape becomes a double-agent on behalf of this secret organisation to fight Voldemort and his followers known as what?",