": "Washington, D.C.", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In which county is the town to which the radio station WCNH is licensed ?", "answer": "Merrimack County,", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Paul Bernard Vogel developed the watch company that is now based in what country?", "answer": "Hong-Kong", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The Devil's Dinner Party is a reality game show hosted by an actor known for his role as Tommy Lascelles in what Netflix drama?", "answer": "The Crown", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which sport do both John Austin and Todd Woodbridge play?", "answer": "tennis", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Kesh temple hymn, one of the oldest surviving literature in the world, describes what aspect of life regarding Acgi?", "answer": "his birth", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What French region was the 1968 Winter Olympics held in? ", "answer": "Auvergne-Rh\u00f4ne-Alpes region", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The actor that played Dale in \"Horrible Bosses\" also appeared in a 2013 3D computer-animated film directed by Dan Scanlon and produced by what studio?", "answer": "Pixar Animation Studios", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "This American television writer and producer, and comic book writer is a showrunner for a popular show based on DC Comics Characters", "answer": "Andrew Kreisberg", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which California irrigation canal formerly provided cooling water for the Rancho Secu Nuclear Generating Station and does not originate at the Kern River, the Calloway Canal or the Folsom South Canal?", "answer": "Folsom South Canal", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": " Davisville Naval Construction Battalion Center was made up of this United States Navy Seabee facility that was  listed on the National Register of Historic Places in what year", "answer": "1978", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were the bands \"Skillet\" and \"Okkervil River\" both formed in Texas?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {