try?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which is a type of cactus, Espostoa or Cryptanthus?", "answer": "Espostoa", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Onizuka Prop Wash Award was named in memory of the student from what Hawaiian city?", "answer": "Kealakekua", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who worked alongside the acclaimed musicologist, music director and composer L. Vaidyanathan on the score and soundtrack of Anupama?", "answer": "C. Ashwath", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What sport do both Michael Irvin and Troy Aikman have in common?", "answer": "football", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Name one journalist that served Maine's largest and principal commercial city?", "answer": "Barbara Ann Walsh", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which castle south-southwest of Montrose is named after the red sandstone it's built from?", "answer": "Red Castle", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was Queen of the Netherlands from 1890 until her abdication in 1948?", "answer": "Wilhelmina of the Netherlands", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Since what year has the award won by Mick Grasso in 1990 been given?", "answer": "1921", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Pearl Vision is currently owned by what company that is based in Milan, Italy?", "answer": "Luxottica", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Stephen J Yohay has invested in Broadway musical hits including which Nazi-themed Mel Brooks show?", "answer": "The Producers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Everyone's Hero is a 2006 American computer-animated sports comedy film directed by Colin Brady, Daniel St. Pierre, and Christopher D'Olier Reeve, was an American actor, film director, producer, screenwriter, author, activist and equestrian, that died on which date?", "answer": "October 10, 2004", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the population rank of the official region of England which has the town of St Helens ? ", "answer": "the third most populated", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Ar