d owned by Key Food Stores Co-op, Inc., which has its headquarters located where?", "answer": "Staten Island", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "62d Expeditionary Reconnaissance Squadron is stationed at an Air Force base in what county?", "answer": "Clark County", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Tiger Shroff starred in a film directed by who?", "answer": "Sabbir Khan", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who currently represents the congressional district for which Jim Meffert was the Democratic nominee in 2010?", "answer": "Erik Paulsen", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How is the 2011 Mumbai bombings connected to the Royal Opera House?", "answer": "blasts occurred", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who wrote an autobiography published by White Mountain Castle Publishing about his adventure in Hawaii?", "answer": "Daniel Keauhou Matsu \"Danny\" Yamashiro", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what year was the creator of the character that appeared in a series of films directed by Stephen Norrington, Guillermo del Toro and Goyer born?", "answer": "1926", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which American author is younger, Nora Roberts or Annie Dillard?", "answer": "Annie Dillard", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which canal is longer, The Central Arizona Project or the Oswego Canal?", "answer": "The Central Arizona Project", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "\"The Tide Will Swallow Us Whole\" is the debut album by a band that announced their hiatus in what year?", "answer": "2010", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year was the director of Snake Eyes born?", "answer": "1940", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Long Flat is a rural village situated on the Oxley Highway and the southern bank of the Hastings River, the village is about 50 kilometres west of which coastal town located on the Mid North Coast of New South Wales, Australia?", "answer": "Port Macquarie", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Manfred Moch was a German trumpet player, he made a name for hims