er": "Football", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Rich Burlew, an American author, game designer, and graphic designer is best known for a webcomic that satirizes tabletop role-playing games and what else?", "answer": "medieval fantasy", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where is the owner of Next big sound provides analytics for online music available?", "answer": "United States", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Olivia Olson played the character Joanna in the 2017 sequel that was directed by whom?", "answer": "Richard Curtis", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Tosca starred the tenor who was of what nationality?", "answer": "Italian", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What role is the twin of Elaine Thompson most notable for playing in the television series \"Casualty\"?  ", "answer": "Charlie Fairhead", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who produces the Mexican telenovela that features \"Saturno\" as its main theme?", "answer": "Giselle Gonz\u00e1lez", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"To Go Home\" is an EP released by a singer-songwriter from what city?", "answer": "Portland", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Glass House was derived from the house designed by whom?", "answer": "Ludwig Mies van der Rohe", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "On Giants' Shoulders was written in 1998 by Melvyn Bragg, the book was assembled after a series of interviews Bragg had with current scientists about the world's greatest scientists such as which English mathematician, astronomer, and physicist (described in his own day as a \"natural philosopher\") who is widely recognised as one of the most influential scientists of all time and a key figure in the scientific revolution?", "answer": "Isaac Newton", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Where does Gamal al-Banna's great-nephew teach?", "answer": "Oxford Faculty of Theology", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Moves and Heavy Metal, are which type of publication?", "answer": "magazine", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In which 2016 film starred one of the voice actors from Fable III?", "answer": "Moonlight", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Saint Vitus and Pentagram had what in common when it came to the music industry?", "answer": "They are one of the first doom metal bands", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both Jingmen and Kangding cities in China?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "How many students did the school, from which Corey Snide would graduate, have in 2005 ?", "answer": "2225", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The 2006 Asia Series was held in what stadium that has an all-seating configuration of 42,000?", "answer": "Tokyo Dome", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "When was the interior of the location of the 1997 MTV Video Music Awards declared a city landmark?", "answer": "1978", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What American actor starred in both \"Westworld\" and \"Sweetwater\"? ", "answer": "Ed Harris", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Robert A. Kotick is CEO of which American video game developer?", "answer": "Activision Blizzard", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Other than Valerie Bowman, who else wrote Regency romance novels? ", "answer": "Georgette Heyer", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who is one of the greatest Irish writers and poets of all time, Theodore H. White or Brendan Behan?", "answer": "Brendan Francis Aidan Behan", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "are The Betrayal \u2013 Nerakhoon and The Square both documentaries ?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What is the name of the paternal grandfather of Lady Margarita Armstrong-Jones ?", "answer": "Antony Armstrong-Jones, 1st Earl of Snowdon", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who has the highest scope of work in Willard Mack or Lewis Gilbert", "answer": "Lewis Gilbert", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In the 2010 census what was the population of the city which the Path 64 Marketplace substation is near ?", "answer": "15,023", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Was 