 the soap opera \"Santa Barbara\"?", "answer": "Leonardo DiCaprio", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "How many years passed between the first hit song by Chuck Berry and the biggest hit by the band The Fabulous Wailers?", "answer": "Their biggest hit was \"Tall Cool One\", first released in 1959", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What year was the band that released \"That Kiss\" formed?", "answer": "2006", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Caner Osman's brother plays for what NBA team?", "answer": "Cleveland Cavaliers", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Park Jung-woo, is a South Korean film director and screenwriter, his third feature is which 2012 South Korean science fiction thriller film starring Kim Myung-min, Kim Dong-wan, Moon Jung-hee and Lee Ha-nui?", "answer": "Deranged", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What position was the top seed in the 2010 China Open - Women's Singles in the Danish professional tennis scene?", "answer": "top", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What award did the penciler who worked on New Man comic books win twice?", "answer": "Eisner Awards", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Oink!, is a video game, for which video game console, and designed by Mike Lorenzen, and inspired by the fairy tale \"The Three Little Pigs\", a fable about three pigs who build three houses of different materials?", "answer": "Atari 2600", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who was a writer on both \"Roc Me Out\" and \"S&M\", songs recorded by Barbadian recording artist Rihanna?", "answer": "Ester Dean", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are both Philippe Perrin and Umberto Guidoni considered astronauts?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which system is most likely to have impacted current computer technology, Atari or Comx-35?", "answer": "Atari", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "What city are both \u0130stiklal Avenue and Yoros Castle located in?", "answer": "Istanbul, Turkey", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Which national pageant included Ashley Renee Litton as a representative from Missouri?", "answer": "Miss USA", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Adriana Lecouvreur and La boh\u00e8me are both what type of opera performance?", "answer": "an opera in four acts", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The Remington Model 31 competed with the Winchester model that was popularly known as what?", "answer": "Perfect Repeater", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "which American Class I railroad was White Horse, formally located ", "answer": "The Great Northern Railway", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What form of play does Nine Men's Morris and Twilight Struggle have in common?", "answer": "game", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Of Stone, Wind and Pillor is an EP by what American heavy metal band from Portland, Oregon?", "answer": "Agalloch", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What agency represents the player who led the Huskies to the 2011 Big East championship?", "answer": "Excel Sports Management", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Matthew Lewis appears in Bluestone 42, a comedy series on what network?", "answer": "BBC Three", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is Wayne Douglas Gretzky's nickname and  how many National Hockey League records does he hold?", "answer": "\"The Great One\"", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Colossians 2 is in what number book of the New Testament?", "answer": "twelfth", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What Armenian-founded manufacturer based in Massachusetts makes James Riley Breckenridge's cymbals?", "answer": "Avedis Zildjian Company", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is a block away from the arena where the Baltimore Blast play their games?", "answer": "Baltimore Convention Center", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is located in the Boston Township of the District of Timiskaming and connected to Highway 112 in Dane?", "answer": "Adams Mine", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Were Patrick McCabe and John Braine of the same nationality?", "answer": "no",