und slab of grewwacke covered in runes on its face and side indicated the Scandinavians came to Minnesota in what century?", "answer": "14th century", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "The same county that one could find the cities of Roanoke and Salem, one could also hear what religious radio broadcast with a Vinton VA license?", "answer": "WKBA", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which magazine was published first, Naval History or Model Railroader?", "answer": "Model Railroader", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "When did the show that Skeet Ulrich is currently starring in premiere? ", "answer": "January 26, 2017", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Are Chris Marker and Yvonne Rainer American?", "answer": "no", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "The retired jersey of Adrian \"Ace\" Custis hangs alongside all-time leader in points for what NBA team?", "answer": "Charlotte Hornets", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "\"My Kinda Party\" is certified quadruple-platinum by the Recording Industry Association of America based on a song originally written and recorded by what artist?", "answer": "Brantley Gilbert", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "While Lobelia is a genus of flowering plants, Asplenium is a genus of what?", "answer": "about 700 species of ferns", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Does Aglaia belongs to Mahogany family and Valeriana belongs to Caprifoliaceae family?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "In what Montana county can you find St. Benedict's Catholic School?", "answer": "Musselshell County", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In 1945, Elmer Lach won a trophy that has been awarded how many times since 1924?", "answer": "92", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Can Fraxinus and Onoclea both be found in North America?", "answer": "yes", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Timothy J. Leiweke was the former president and CEO of a professional sports and commercial real estate company based where?", "answer": "Toronto, Ontario, Canada", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "In what country did Alan Richards play in the TriNoma mall?", "answer": "Philippines", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Joey Scouts are named after the young of what marsupial?", "answer": "kangaroo", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Which Scottish rock band was formed earlier, Cocteau Twins or Big Country?", "answer": "Cocteau Twins were a Scottish rock band active from 1979 to 1997", "type": "comparison"}, {"question": "Kerry Remsen is the daughter of an actor with what ethnicity?", "answer": "American", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Who manages both Northshore Mall in Peabody, Massachusetts and the Liberty Tree Mall in Danvers which are less than one mile from each other?", "answer": "Simon Property Group", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Charlee Johnson was part of a band that signed with a film production label of what company in 2000?", "answer": "Amblin Partners", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "What is the ship that sank in the Baltic sea and is in the novel Salt to the Sea?", "answer": "MV \"Wilhelm Gustloff", "type": "bridge"}, {"question": "Vietnam national cricket team will debut at what competitions at  Kinrara Oval", "answer": "2017 Southeast Asian Games", "type": "bridge"}]